window.AKK_THE_LITTLE_DARLING_WIFE_WHO_IS_A_DIVINE_DOCTOR_SAVED_THE_ENTIRE_FAMILY_OF_THE_DUKES_MANSION_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_THE_LITTLE_DARLING_WIFE_WHO_IS_A_DIVINE_DOCTOR_SAVED_THE_ENTIRE_FAMILY_OF_THE_DUKES_MANSION_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":301,"title":"Chapter 301: It's up to you from now on.","paragraphs":["\"Have you collected any news about the Mo Family?\"","The man from the southern border shook his head desperately: \"No.\"","Mo Jiuye did not believe him at all.","\"The thug from the shipping business said you've been in Yun City for over a month. Don't tell me you've done nothing during this past month?\"","The man from the southern border nodded his head vigorously again.","\"I indeed have done nothing.\"","This man was timid and afraid to die. Mo Jiuye felt that he did not seem to be lying.","\"Why?\"","\"When I set off for Yun City, Master gave me a very special homing pigeon. That pigeon was extremely spiritual and could find my master no matter where he was.","Because I was greedy for the company of beautiful women, I went to the brothel in the prefecture and got drunk. I accidentally let the pigeon get stolen.","My master has a fierce temper. If he finds out I lost the pigeon, he will definitely take my life. That's why I didn't dare go back to the southern border and decided to hide in Da Shun for the time being.\"","Mo Jiuye sneered: \"So then you took over as the head of the shipping business?\"","The man from the southern border nodded: \"I wandered around the prefecture for about a month and found no decent way to make good money there. So I simply came to Yun City.","I heard the commoners on the streets say running a shipping business was a lucrative endeavor without much capital. So I set my mind on getting into that business.\"","Now Mo Jiuye understood everything. This man from the southern border did not intend to continue following Mr. Si Meng. He wanted to stay in Yun City and become a local tycoon.","He did not expect the original head of the shipping business to get exposed. And he got burned because of his association.","Mo Jiuye had one last and most critical question for him.","Of course, Mo Jiuye did not have high hopes of getting any useful information out of him.","\"Do you know where Mr. Si Meng is?\"","\"I don't know. My master comes and goes without a trace. I've only seen him once and didn't even see his real face.\"","\"Then how did he give you instructions?\" Mo Jiuye did not give up questioning.","\"He always passed messages to me through my teacher. As for how my teacher contacted him, I have no idea.\"","After a pause, the man from the southern border added: \"My teacher is my master's top disciple.\"","So far, Mo Jiuye was quite satisfied with his performance. At least it was apparent that if he asked who his teacher was, the man would readily answer.","As for Mr. Si Meng's top disciple, he had already died by Mo Jiuye's hands some time ago. Mo Jiuye had asked him everything he could. As for the man in front of him, Mo Jiuye knew he couldn't get any more useful information out of him.","Mo Jiuye first glanced at He Zhiran: \"Zhiran, go wait for me at the teahouse. I'll take this man to the county government.\"","\"Alright, be safe.\"","He Zhiran felt nauseous for some reason smelling the faint scent of blood on the southern border man.","It was good timing to go back to the teahouse for some water and settle her stomach.","Mo Jiuye did not know his wife was uncomfortable. He directly took the southern border man to the government office.","The officers from the shipping business had also found the original head and captured some of his important subordinates back to the county government office.","The case had nothing to do with Mo Jiuye. Meng Huaining was the person in charge of handling these people. Mo Jiuye bid them farewell and went back to the teahouse with Hu Cong to get He Zhiran.","By this time, Mo Chuhan had also sobered up and was about to get up to go to the county government office to meet with the poisoner.","He Zhiran was persuading him that he would feel dizzy after just having recovered from the poison and should stay to rest for now.","Just then, Mo Jiuye came back. Seeing his eighth brother not listening, he went up and pressed him back down in his seat.","\"Eighth brother, I've already sent the poisoner to the government office. The men from the shipping business were also taken back by the officers. Meng Daren is there handling things, so don't worry. Just focus on recovering.\"","Hearing that things were basically settled at the government office, Mo Chuhan finally felt relieved and asked Mo Jiuye for details about the captured men.","Mo Jiuye told him everything he had gotten out of the southern border man.","Mo Chuhan said indignantly: \"Ninth brother, if we don't get rid of Mr. Si Meng, not only can we not find our missing elders, I'm afraid we won't get to live in peace at home either.\"","This was an indisputable fact. Whether using poison or sorcery, Mr. Si Meng was a top master. Mo Jiuye did not dare let his brothers recklessly go searching.","Although he was also eager to rescue his elders and wanted to live in peace, everything had to be carefully planned before taking action.","\"Eighth brother, let's discuss this thoroughly when we get home before making a decision.\"","Although Mo Chuhan was a bit hotheaded, he was not completely brainless. He naturally understood what his ninth brother was thinking.","He was just feeling unfair for the moment.","\"I know. I'll listen to your arrangements from now on.\"","The two brothers did not intend to keep their conversation from Hu Cong. Hu Cong would be living in Xi Ling Village in the future, so he would inevitably find out about the Mo family's circumstances.","Moreover, they had found so many elders in the family. Hu Cong would see them sooner or later.","Mo Jiuye did not plan on keeping the matter a secret. The Mo men could not live in hiding for a lifetime. Everything would eventually come to light anyway, so they might as well live openly.","Hu Cong knew a little about the Mo family's situation. When he saw Mo Chuhan at the county government office earlier, he was indeed shocked, unable to comprehend how someone already dead could appear again.","After hearing their conversation, Hu Cong had a general guess in his mind.","Having been in court service for many years, he understood very well the virtue of not being too curiously inclined.","Therefore, Hu Cong maintained a calm attitude throughout.","After getting Eighth Brother settled down, the time Mo Jiuye spent out with He Zhiran was about up too.","Since there were no other important matters in Yun City, they went back to Xi Ling Village together.","The Mo family womenfolk were not familiar with Hu Cong. When Mo Jiuye and his wife came back with a stranger, everyone's attention turned to Hu Cong.","Mo Jiuye introduced Hu Cong and his identity to the family. Only then did the wives know that the man was someone who shared the same misery as them.","Hu Cong was even more pitiful than the Mo's. At least the Mo's could take care of each other, while when Hu Cong was exiled, there were only him and his wife with no one to rely on. And now his situation was even more disastrous with him left all alone.","The Mo family greatly sympathized with Hu Cong and were very warm towards him.","However, Hu Cong was still an outsider after all, and there were many women in the family, so it was inconvenient for him to spend the night there. Mo Jiuye took Hu Cong to the head of the Jiang clan and helped rent him a small courtyard to stay at temporarily.","Of course, the money and some daily supplies were provided by the Mo family.","Hu Cong expressed deep gratitude and said he would repay the silver as soon as possible.","On her trip out He Zhiran finally obtained a legitimate reason for the antidote she helped her sister-in-law's prepare. Early next morning, she gave one pill to each sister-in-law.","In addition, she specifically arranged some medicinal tonics, hoping her sister-in-law's could fulfill their wish to have children sooner.","Soon there was more good news.","The little collectibles dealer worked efficiently. He Zhiran had just entered the space when she saw his message.","[I have obtained the crane bamboo you wanted. It can go on the shelf anytime.]"]},{"number":302,"title":"Chapter 302: Just being alive is a Miracle.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran was waiting for his message. As soon as she got the crane bamboo, she could make antidotes for those pharmacists.","[That's great. Please put it up for sale now if it's convenient!]","Little Collector happened to be online at that time. Without saying anything else, he immediately put the crane bamboo up for sale.","This kind of medicine material was prohibited from sale. He changed the name and only hung a price of one yuan. It was equivalent to giving it to He Zhiran for free.","He Zhiran was not an ungrateful person. Although she and Little Collector were in a mutually beneficial relationship, the other party had helped her a lot.","So she took a picture of the dark red bead and sent it to him.","[Take a look at this.]","When Little Collector opened the picture, his eyes lit up instantly.","This was a dark red bead, rarer than the black ones by countless times.","[This is definitely a priceless treasure.]","Facing He Zhiran, Little Collector's words were very real. This dark red bead would definitely be a unique existence if taken to the modern times.","He Zhiran didn't understand the true value of the bead. She had just appraised the price on Taobao, and the minimum price turned out to be 60 million.","This was the highest priced treasure since she started selling antiques.","She would not become complacent because of Little Collector's words of pricelessness. She still adhered to her original principle.","That was to sell all goods at the minimum appraised value, especially since this was something she intended to use to repay Little Collector, there was no possibility of raising the price while sitting down.","[60 million, do you want it?]","[I do, I do! Put it up for sale now!] Little Collector still had the rest of the money left over from preparing to buy the black bead last time. He wanted to get his hands on this priceless treasure at the first opportunity.","Of course, he was also clearly aware that the selling price given by the other party was very low.","[Feel free to ask if there is anything I can help with in the future.]","[Okay, let's help each other out.]","After communicating with each other, they each went to deal with the items they had bought.","He Zhiran was going to prepare the antidote to treat those pharmacists, of course.","After three days of experimentation, the antidote was finally successfully prepared.","The antidote was divided into two types: one was an oral pill with extracts from the gu worm added, and the other was a medicinal bath to completely eliminate the various toxins in their bodies.","Of course, this absolutely could not be done in the space.","Mo Jiuye looked at the dozens of people lying on the ground.","\"Ranran, I found a cave on the mountain that is large enough to accommodate these people. It's a bit late today, tomorrow morning, I'll take you up the mountain and send all those people into the cave. I'll leave the rest to me.\"","He Zhiran thought the same way.","\"Okay, that's settled then.\"","The next morning, the two went to the mountain as agreed. In order to take care of He Zhiran's health, Mo Jiuye's pace could be described as extremely slow. Even if there were more small pebbles on the road, he would have to go forward and kick them away before letting his wife pass.","Since buying this mountain, this was He Zhiran's first time coming up here.","It was better than she had imagined here. Although many trees had been cut down by the villagers of Xi Ling Village, most of the original ecological things were still there.","That was enough. She would turn this place into a paradise orchard in the future.","After walking for about half an hour, the couple came to the cave Mo Jiuye had mentioned.","Although the entrance of the cave was not very big, there was a world inside.","This should be a place where the villagers who went up the mountain to rest often rested. Inside, several small stools were placed, and there were also several large stone beds.","Now that they had bought this mountain, the villagers were very conscious and no longer set foot here. It was very safe to help the pharmacists detoxify here.","He Zhiran first purchased several large wooden barrels in Taobao, poured the medicinal bath water made in the space into them, and finally put all those dozens of people into the cave. The rest was Mo Jiuye's business.","After all, with those big men taking medicinal baths, it would be inappropriate for her to be present.","Mo Jiuye was in no hurry to help these people detoxify, but first sent He Zhiran back home, while bringing several younger brothers from home and Liang Hao up the mountain.","As for finding an excuse to find these pharmacists, it was not something He Zhiran should worry about. She simply went home to play with Rice Ball.","Mo Jiuye went home and found Third Older Brother and Fifth Elder Brother.","Seeing his solemn appearance, Fifth Elder Brother asked, \"Ninth Younger Brother, what's the matter?\"","\"Third Older Brother, Fifth Elder Brother, not only did I find Sixth Elder Brother and Seventh Elder Brother on this trip to the South, I also found brothers who used to live and die together with us Mo men.\"","Fifth Elder Brother was shocked: \"What are you talking about, Ninth Younger Brother?\"","\"Do you still remember when I told you that I found Sixth Elder Brother? At that time, Sixth Elder Brother was infected by a corpse gu, and was being manipulated by Mr. Simeng. The gu worm he was infected with was very special. It was raised with medicine for the purpose of manipulating pharmacists. Those pharmacists were good brothers who fought alongside our Mo Family on the battlefield.\" Mo Jiuye hoped they could understand what he was saying this way.","The two elder brothers did understand what he was saying, and they were very angry.","\"What exactly does the South want to do? Treating the Da Shun soldiers like this is an insult!\" Third Older Brother said indignantly.","Originally, hearing that those brothers were still alive was a good thing, but being so insulted by the Southern people was simply heartbreaking.","Especially the pharmacists, although Third Older Brother and Fifth Elder Brother had not seen them with their own eyes, they had heard about them before. They were simply killing puppets.","Third Older Brother slammed his fist hard on the door frame.","\"These people are really sinister.\"","Although he was angry, there were still questions he had to ask.","\"Ninth Younger Brother, where are those brothers? Did you rescue them?\"","\"I asked them to temporarily settle in a mountain cave. Ranran has already prepared the antidote. I came to find you guys to go help detoxify them,\" Mo Jiuye said calmly.","At this time, he would definitely have to tell the two elder brothers some false reasons, and naturally have to appear calmer.","Sure enough, the expected questions still came.","\"How did you and sister-in-law save them back?\" Third Older Brother asked.","\"Third Older Brother, I used some special methods that I can't tell you about. Anyway, let's call Liang Hao and the others to go up the mountain now to help those people detox,\" he said, knowing his elder brothers didn't like meddling. Otherwise, just saying a few casual sentences like this would definitely not fool them.","Sure enough, Third Older Brother and Fifth Elder Brother showed no intention of pursuing the issue further. They had long noticed that their ninth younger brother and his wife had a lot of secrets now.","Since they knew those brothers were in the mountain cave, Third Older Brother and Fifth Elder Brother did not intend to delay any longer either. The two divided their work to find Liang Hao and the others to go up the mountain together.","He Zhiran had not prepared too many wooden barrels. After taking the antidote, the pharmacists would take turns soaking in the medicinal bath, so the speed of their detoxification would not be very fast.","She waited until late at night before hearing movement outside.","Mo Jiuye knew she would be worried. The first thing he did when he got home was to explain the process of helping the pharmacists detoxify that day.","\"Ranran, the detoxification was very successful. They have all sobered up now, but they are still very weak at the moment. I cooked them some porridge to eat according to what you said. Liang Hao bought some beddings and let them stay in the cave to recuperate for now. Don't worry, Liang Hao and the others will be there to keep an eye on them. If there is any problem, they will notify me immediately.\""]},{"number":303,"title":"Chapter 303: The Fourth Brother can be Treated Today","paragraphs":["Upon hearing that the antidote was successful, He Zhiran finally felt relieved.","After all, the antidote she had formulated had not gone through any clinical trials and was completely based on her own experience and prescribed formula.","\"It's inevitable that they are physically weak now after being poisoned for so long without food. It's already a miracle that they are still alive,\" she said.","As for how Mo Jiuye would settle them, He Zhiran did not intend to worry about it.","In her opinion, the only thing those soldiers wanted most now was to reunite with their loved ones.","\"I've already told them about what happened, and they feel guilty towards their families. They plan to recuperate and then go back to take a look after their health improves,\" Mo Jiuye said.","\"Go back and take a look?\" He Zhiran was a little puzzled.","\"Yes, just go back and take a look. They said they plan to live with the Mo Family in the northwest from now on. Emperor Shunwu is so muddled, they don't want to sacrifice their lives for such a monarch anymore,\" Mo Jiuye explained.","He Zhiran had no objection to these people wanting to come to the northwest to live together with them.","Not to mention that they used to be the Mo Family's subordinates, even if they weren't, more manpower would be needed for future development in the northwest.","This was perfect. Currently, neither Mo Jiuye nor her had any grand ambitions, they just wanted to find all their missing family members in the future and live a life of abundance without deceit.","These people were like the Mo Family's men. Although the Mo brothers looked fine on the surface, after being controlled by others for so many years, they must have suffered irreparable trauma to their spirits and lost confidence in the court.","Moreover, these people had military backgrounds. Without working for the court anymore, it would definitely be difficult for their future livelihoods. It would be better for them to follow the family and live happy days together.","He Zhiran had a heartfelt respect for these military men who had shed blood for the country, whether in modern or ancient times. She could not sit idly by and ignore these fine men who protected their homes and defended the nation.","Of course, she also hoped that those people would be willing to follow the Mo Family on their own initiative, and would not force them.","The Mo brothers had already discussed not telling the women in the family about this for the time being, lest they feel uncomfortable. They would wait until those people had recovered and appeared healthy, so that it would be less distressing to see.","For three consecutive days, the Mo brothers spent their days taking care of their old subordinates on the mountain during the daytime, while He Zhiran focused her efforts on researching treatment for the Fourth Brother.","The Fourth Brother was recovering quite well now, especially with the Fourth Sister-in-Law's attentive care every day. His whole person looked fatter.","With Mo Jiuye not at home, He Zhiran could only simply check his pulse and examine his general condition.","After taking his pulse, she could make a preliminary judgment that the Fourth Brother's body had reached the standard for surgery.","Since this was the case, this matter should also be put on the agenda as soon as possible. He Zhiran considered that her belly would grow bigger and bigger in the future, not only would it be inconvenient to move around, she might not be able to endure the long periods of concentration required for surgery on patients.","The Fourth Brother's condition was special. Not only were his bones shattered, but his skin and flesh were also necrotic in many places. Performing surgery on him was an extremely challenging task that tested the endurance of medical practitioners.","She planned not to let Mo Jiuye go up the mountain tomorrow. Instead, she would first bring the Fourth Brother into her space to do a thorough examination and proceed with surgery immediately if all indicators were qualified.","The next day at dawn, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran once again came to the Fourth Brother's room.","\"Fourth Brother, Zhiran said your condition is good now and plans to give you another injection,\" Mo Jiuye said.","\"Alright, I'll have to trouble my Ninth Brother's wife again,\" the Fourth Brother said, feeling somewhat guilty. He had been paralyzed in bed after being saved by his Ninth Younger Brother and sister-in-law for so long, and had already become a burden to the family.","And now his pregnant sister-in-law still had to help treat him. If it wasn't so he could recover sooner, Mo Xiuyan really wouldn't have felt good about troubling his Ninth Brother's wife.","He Zhiran looked at the Fourth Sister-in-Law who was still standing there.","\"Sister-in-law, please go and boil some hot water for later use. We may need your help to wipe the Fourth Brother's body.\"","This was He Zhiran's excuse to get the Fourth Sister-in-Law away.","After all, she was going to bring the Fourth Brother into her space to use those advanced medical devices for examination. It would be impossible to operate with an outsider present.","Seeing that the sister-in-law had gone out, Mo Jiuye immediately locked the room door.","\"Zhiran, you take the Fourth Brother into your space and I'll stand guard here.\"","He Zhiran responded and brought the Fourth Brother into her space together with her.","Using her mind, she quickly operated the devices to examine the Fourth Brother's body all over.","In order not to make Mo Jiuye, who was guarding the door, worry, she brought the Fourth Brother and the examination results she had just generated out together.","Mo Jiuye had just sent away the sister-in-law who was knocking on the door and was anxiously pacing around in the room. Seeing He Zhiran come out, he went up and asked, \"Zhiran, how is the Fourth Brother's condition?\"","He Zhiran carefully looked through the various examination report forms in her hand.","\"The indicators are all qualified. We can operate on the Fourth Brother today,\" she said.","While feeling happy, Mo Jiuye was still worried about his wife's health.","\"Zhiran, when you help the Fourth Brother with treatment later, try to get me to do the actual work.\"","Do the actual work?","Even with her many years of medical experience, she didn't dare to guarantee that such surgery would definitely succeed, let alone letting someone without medical knowledge do the work. That would be no different from giving the Fourth Brother euthanasia directly.","However, she didn't verbally attack Mo Jiuye's confidence either. In order not to make him worry about her body, He Zhiran obediently agreed, \"Alright, I'll let you do wherever possible.\"","Since the Fourth Brother was still unconscious, surgery would have to be performed in her space.","Both Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran felt it would be safer to conduct it in their own room.","After all, if the husband and wife locked themselves in their own room, outsiders would not be in a position to say anything.","Just as they had made up their minds, there was another knock on the door.","\"Ninth Brother, Sister-in-law, when can I come in?\" the Fourth Sister-in-Law asked impatiently. She knew it was the Ninth Brother and Sister-in-law treating her husband, but she just wanted to stay by his side and watch with her own eyes as they treated her husband.","He Zhiran understood how the Fourth Sister-in-Law felt. If it were Mo Jiuye getting treated, she would also want to stay.","It was just that her treatment methods could not be exposed, so she could only let the Fourth Sister-in-Law feel impatient for a while.","Not only the Fourth Sister-in-Law, upon hearing that she was going to treat the Fourth Brother, all the women in the house had also rushed over.","Old Lady Mo, as the mother, was no less worried than the daughter-in-law.","She held He Zhiran's hand tightly, trembling a little.","\"My child, I know you're unwell with a pregnant body, yet you're still willing to treat your Fourth Brother at this time. I'll remember this in my heart!\" the old lady said, her eyes already welling up with tears.","Seeing the old lady on the verge of crying, He Zhiran hurriedly held her hand in return.","\"Mother, don't worry. If I get tired, I'll rest. I'll definitely try my best to treat the Fourth Brother's injuries,\" she assured.","Old Lady Mo was tactful and would never prattle on endlessly like those talkative women.","She just gently squeezed He Zhiran's hand and ushered all the women away, telling them not to add to the chaos by staying here.","Old Lady Mo's actions actually helped Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran avoid the trouble of having to actively drive people away."]},{"number":304,"title":"Chapter 304: Healing","paragraphs":["Only Fourth Sister-in-Law still stood in place, unwilling to leave.","Mo Jiuye knew that Fourth Sister-in-Law was worried about Fourth elder brother, but it was not good to directly tell her to leave. He simply carried Fourth elder brother on his back towards his own room.","\"Fourth Sister-in-Law, I'm here to help treat Fourth elder brother, so Rangrang can concentrate fully. I won't open the door until the treatment is done, no one is allowed to disturb.\"","Seeing her brother-in-law carry away her husband, Fourth Sister-in-Law woodenly nodded: \"Okay.\"","...","Back in the room, Mo Jiuye locked the door and instantly brought the two people into the space with him.","Rice Ball, who was eating bamboo shoots in the space, saw its owner and immediately threw away the bamboo shoot to run over for a hug.","He Zhiran's mind was completely focused on treating Fourth elder brother at the moment. She had no time to interact with the little guy even though she didn't bear to disappoint it. In the end, she gave it a quick hug and took out a bunch of tasty snacks to keep the silly and cute creature busy playing by itself.","By this time, Mo Jiuye had already efficiently changed into surgical assistant attire and thoroughly disinfected the operating room.","He Zhiran did the same sterile procedures before entering the operating room.","Fourth elder brother's condition was very special. In principle, it would be best to do the fractured leg and dead muscle tissue in two separate surgeries.","But current circumstances didn't allow He Zhiran to do that. She could only do her best to complete everything in one surgery.","It took five hours just to set the bones in Fourth elder brother's comminuted fractures in both legs.","Seeing her working so hard, Mo Jiuye's heart ached badly, but there was nothing he could do to help with this kind of thing.","Finally, after setting the bones, next was dealing with the necrotic muscle tissue.","Mo Jiuye watched closely at his wife's actions. Feeling she was almost done, he promptly took over her work.","Although removing necrotic muscle tissue was not highly difficult, there were still many details that needed attention.","By this point she was quite tired. For the sake of the child in her belly, she didn't dare overexert herself either.","Even letting Mo Jiuye take over, He Zhiran still didn't dare relax her vigilance. She sat by the whole time, watching closely and giving verbal reminders whenever necessary.","The married couple worked busily for the entire day. Fourth elder brother's comminuted fractures in both legs, necrotic tissues, and broken tendons were all finally completed.","Fourth elder brother's condition was very stable after the surgery, but He Zhiran still didn't dare let down her guard. She planned to stay in the space to keep observing before she could completely feel assured.","Moreover, Fourth elder brother needed intravenous supplements after surgery, which would also take some time.","In order not to make the family waiting outside worry, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye exited the space together.","The moment they opened the door to the room, the family members were indeed anxiously waiting out there, as expected.","Seeing the couple come out, Fourth Sister-in-Law rushed up first to grab He Zhiran's arm and asked: \"Sister-in-Law, how is my husband?\"","He Zhiran gently patted Fourth Sister-in-Law's hand: \"Fourth Sister-in-Law, don't worry. Fourth elder brother's treatment was very successful. I just want to observe him a little longer before giving him back to you.\"","He Zhiran couldn't explain much more, she could only use an excuse like this to gloss over.","Old Lady Mo highly trusted her ninth daughter-in-law's medical skills. Although she also felt bewildered that He Zhiran wouldn't let them see Mo Xiuyang, she still chose to stand on He Zhiran's side.","\"Those from Fourth's family, listen to your sister-in-law, she must have a good reason.\" Saying so, she then looked at the others: \"Go back and rest all of you, stop crowding around here.\"","When the head of household had spoken, everyone must obey. The few sisters-in-law handed the specially prepared dinner to Mo Jiuye before turning to leave.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye closed the door again and went back into the space. After exhausting herself for a whole day, her body really couldn't take it anymore at the moment.","Mo Jiuye heated up the food and then went to the kitchen himself to cook some small side dishes that she liked to eat. His cooking skills were very average, but he put a lot of effort into the thoughtful intention, so it still tasted rather good to eat.","Lying in bed to rest, He Zhiran let Mo Jiuye keep watch on Fourth elder brother's condition at all times.","Until almost dawn, feeling that Fourth elder brother would soon wake up and his condition was very stable, only then did she bring him along to exit the space together.","From now on, Fourth elder brother could no longer be brought into the space for treatment. Unable to use syringes for treatment, He Zhiran had to settle for ordering large quantities of the highest grade medicines from Taobao Treasure to consolidate his recovery.","Although these medications didn't help him to recover as fast as post-op iv drips could, they were still much better than ordinary medicine.","Not long after leaving the space, Fourth elder brother slowly regained consciousness.","The surroundings were unfamiliar to him. Ever since returning to Xilin village, because of his physical condition he had been lying in the room he shared with his wife this whole time.","Looking around at the unfamiliar environment, Fourth elder brother's gaze finally fell upon Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran.","\"Fourth elder brother, your treatment was very successful. Rangrang said you'll be able to try walking half a year from now.\"","Mo Jiuye promptly gave him the good news when he saw Fourth elder brother awake.","Even though the environment was unfamiliar, Ninth Younger Brother was here so Fourth elder brother felt it was safe.","\"Ninth Younger Brother, where is this place?\"","\"This is my room. Yesterday, to make treating you more convenient, I brought you here.\" Mo Jiuye explained.","Fourth elder brother was somewhat shocked: \"You mean I was unconscious for a whole day?\"","\"Yes, Rangrang was worried the treatment might be painful for you, so she gave you anesthetic powder. That's why you slept for so long.\"","Hearing this, Fourth elder brother experimentally moved his body a little. Other than the sensation of pain, it seemed like something was tightly wrapped around him. The hard and stiff feeling was very uncomfortable.","Mo Jiuye promptly went up to him: \"Fourth elder brother, don't move. Rangrang went through a lot of effort to set your legs properly.\"","He couldn't ruin his wife's painstaking results with one misstep.","\"Okay, I won't move.\" Fourth elder brother was very obedient. As long as he could stand up again someday, anything was acceptable to him.","Moreover, he had endured such great torment in the basement, so the current pain was nothing in comparison.","He Zhiran looked outside at the lightening sky. She knew Fourth Sister-in-Law must have worried herself sleepless all night.","\"I'll go call Fourth Sister-in-Law over.\" He Zhiran felt it would put Fourth Sister-in-Law's mind at ease if she saw Fourth elder brother earlier.","Indeed, things were just as she guessed. Fourth Sister-in-Law was restlessly pacing circles in the room, her bloodshot eyes clearly showing she hadn't slept all night.","Seeing He Zhiran, Fourth Sister-in-Law became extremely emotional.","\"Sister-in-Law, can I see my husband now?\"","He Zhiran took her hand and walked outside together: \"Fourth elder brother is already awake. We'll have people carry him back in a bit.\""]},{"number":305,"title":"Chapter 305: If you want to go, let's go together.","paragraphs":["Fourth Sister-in-Law excitedly held He Zhiran's hand in return: “That's great, Ninth Younger Sister. It really took a lot of effort from you and Ninth Younger Brother.”","As she spoke, Fourth Sister-in-Law's eyes also involuntarily shed tears.","Seeing her husband's family, the first thing Fourth Sister-in-Law naturally did was to care about them.","Then, He Zhiran handed over several Western medicines that had been ground into powder to Fourth Sister-in-Law, and carefully repeated the method of taking them.","At this time, Mo Jiuye also called several brothers from the family. Everyone carefully carried Mo Xiuyan back to his room.","The treatment for Fourth Brother was temporarily over for the time being. His injury would also take some time to recover. As long as he cooperated well with recuperation in the future, standing up again would definitely not be a problem.","Compared with Fourth Brother, Seventh Brother’s situation was slightly better. His body had multiple superficial injuries, and after a period of conditioning, he had basically recovered.","The current Seventh Brother could already walk a certain distance with someone's support.","It was just a pity that after being locked up in the dungeon of the Prince’s Residence in Southern Xinjiang for many years, his body was not only ravaged, but also suffered from severe malnutrition due to insufficient food supply.","This also needed to be conditioned slowly to recover. At least it was not as difficult to treat as Fourth Brother.","Now that several big events had been completed, Fourth Brother was recovering smoothly, Seventh Brother continued to regulate his body, and those who were poisoned had also removed the poison and would gradually recover after a period of conditioning.","Now, the things that could be done at home were almost all done. It was just that they didn’t know when Nan Rui would bring the Imperial Concubine to come and remove the gu poison.","If they were not worried that there might be fraud on Nan Rui’s side, Mo Jiuye would have arranged to go to the Western Region to investigate a long time ago.","What he thought in his heart was also what everyone in the Mo family thought.","After dinner, Mo Yunfeng called the brothers to Fourth Brother's room together.","\"Now that Father and Eldest and Second Brothers are not at home, I am the oldest son in the family. Today I have gathered everyone together because I want to discuss going to the Western Region to investigate.\" Third Older Brother said righteously.","When he heard that he was going to the Western Region, Mo Chuhan stood up first.","\"Third Brother, I can ask for leave from the government to go to the Western Region.\"","Fifth Elder Brother and Sixth elder brother also responded quickly: “If we are going, then we brothers should go together.”","Mo Jiuye also wanted to go to the Western Region, but he was not as eager as several elder brothers.","\"We can’t leave all the brothers from the family.\"","\"What Ninth Younger Brother said is reasonable. We can’t all leave when there are only women left in the family.\" Third Older Brother agreed.","\"Then I'll go alone.\" Sixth elder brother gritted his teeth and said. He hated the people who harmed the Mo family men to death.","\"No, I'll go alone if someone has to go.\" Eighth Brother was not to be outdone. Among the Mo brothers, he had the highest martial arts skills. At the time to exert strength, he could not shrink back.","\"Old Eight is impulsive. Going to the Western Region is not about fighting. You should obediently stay in Yun City as your county sheriff.\" Fifth Elder Brother reminded.","\"Fifth Brother, how do you know you don't need to fight when going to the Western Region?\" Eighth Brother was dissatisfied.","When Third Older Brother saw that everyone was arguing endlessly, he stopped them and said, \"That's enough, stop arguing. I will go this time. If you don't feel relieved, I can take Liang Hao and the others with me, so there is someone to rely on.\"","Mo Jiuye also wanted to go, but considering his wife’s condition and Nan Rui’s affairs, he couldn’t get away for the time being.","Therefore, when several elder brothers competed to go to the Western Region, he could only be a quail without the right to speak.","Fourth Brother and Seventh Brother also wanted to go, but their bodies absolutely did not allow it. They could only watch enviously.","Finally, after discussing among the brothers, they unanimously decided to let Third Older Brother take Liang Hao and the others to the Western Region and set off early tomorrow morning.","As for those subordinates who were still recuperating in the cave, they would be temporarily handed over to Fifth Elder Brother and Sixth elder brother to take care of them. When their bodies recovered a little, Mo Jiuye would give them some travel money to allow them to go back and visit their relatives.","After leaving Fourth Brother’s room, Mo Jiuye earnestly advised Third Older Brother: “Third Brother, you must remember that going to the Western Region is only to investigate news about Father and Eldest and Second Brothers. As soon as you find a clue, come back immediately to discuss countermeasures.","Mr. Si Meng is a master of raising gu worms, and is also good at using poison. Even if Father and Eldest and Second Brothers really fall into his hands, I'm afraid the situation will not be optimistic. We absolutely cannot rashly try to rescue them.\"","Third Older Brother nodded: “Ninth Younger Brother, don’t worry, I know the pros and cons involved. I won’t act rashly.”","Mo Jiuye was still worried. Although he didn’t catch Mr. Si Meng, he had dealt with him before.","If it wasn’t for his wife’s help, I’m afraid he wouldn’t even be able to escape Mr. Si Meng’s tricks.","Therefore, all he could do now was pray that Third Older Brother would be able to successfully find out the whereabouts of his father and elder brothers when he went to the Western Region, and would not confront Mr. Si Meng face to face.","He Zhiran knew that Mo Jiuye was called by Third Older Brother to discuss going to the Western Region.","If she hadn’t gotten pregnant, she would definitely have undertaken this matter together with Mo Jiuye.","In case Father and Eldest and Second Brothers were in the state of being poisoned by gu, or poisoned, with her presence she could remove it as soon as possible.","She hoped that the Mo family could reunite, but she couldn’t ignore her own flesh and blood either.","Moreover, even if she proposed to go to Southern Xinjiang, Mo Jiuye would not agree.","Therefore, He Zhiran could only stay at home and wait for news at the moment.","When Mo Jiuye returned to the room, he told He Zhiran about the decision just made.","Third Older Brother was a very cautious person, so letting him go was also a good choice.","Even so, He Zhiran was still worried.","She kept thinking about it, and finally helped Third Older Brother, Liang Hao and others prepare a lot of things in case of unexpected events.","Bulletproof vests were a must. They didn’t know what kind of dangers they would encounter when they went to the Western Region. With stab-proof bulletproof vests, it was at least a very big guarantee.","There was also realgar powder, the best weapon to restrain gu worms.","Although Third Older Brother, Liang Hao and others had high martial arts skills, when faced with such unpredictable things, they might not be able to retreat safely. Having realgar powder with them was another greatest guarantee.","He Zhiran also took out a few mini tranquilizer guns and decided to give each person one. If necessary, it could save lives.","Of course, she would also let Mo Jiuye tell them not to take them out unless forced to.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye did not need to consider the excuse for tranquilizer guns too much. They had already given one to each of the women during the exile, so Third Older Brother must be familiar with them.","Finally, she prepared a mini wrist crossbow for each person. This thing could be tied to the arm at any time for contingency needs.","As for anything else, He Zhiran couldn't think of anything more for the time being, so she could only give these things to Third Older Brother and the others for now.","Seeing the items his wife had prepared for Third Older Brother and the others, Mo Jiuye was moved. But since his wife didn’t like him being polite with her, he didn’t say much.","He handed all these things over to Third Older Brother, Liang Hao and others, and explained the usage methods clearly.","As for the source, they tacitly did not ask. Apart from the bulletproof vests, tranquilizer guns and mini repeating crossbows, they had already seen everything else.","Seeing that Third Older Brother had taken these things, Mo Jiuye felt a little more at ease.","As for gu worms, Mo Jiuye didn’t dare to easily hand them over to Third Older Brother. After all, they didn’t know anything about gu, if something went wrong because of it, it would not be worth the loss."]},{"number":306,"title":"Chapter 306: My mother is in critical condition.","paragraphs":["The next day, as soon as Three Lord left with his men, Nan Rui himself drove an unassuming carriage over, without even a guard by his side.","The only conspicuous thing was that a cage with a snow-white homing pigeon was hanging outside the carriage compartment.","Arriving at the Mo family's door, he happened to run into Mo Jiuye who was about to head out. Both got out of their rides to greet each other.","Seeing Mo Jiuye, Nan Rui hurried over and pulled him along anxiously, \"Can you find that master exorcist now?\"","Mo Jiuye could clearly see how urgent Nan Rui was. \"What's going on?\" he asked.","A lot had happened, but Nan Rui didn't have time to explain. He pleaded for Mo Jiuye to help find that gu poison exorcist master for him.","\"Mo Jiuye, my Imperial Consort is in critical condition. If the gu poison isn't lifted soon, I'm afraid she won't make it.\"","\"Pardon my rudeness.\" Hearing this, Mo Jiuye strode over to the carriage and flipped the curtain open.","Inside was an emaciated old woman with eyes closed, unconscious.","Mo Jiuye asked doubtfully, \"Is this Imperial Consort De?\"","When he had tutored Nan Qi in the palace, he had seen Imperial Consort De a few times. While she didn't have the beauty of other consorts, she was better looking than average women.","Plus, Imperial Consort De wasn't that much older than his own mother. Yet now, she looked like a seventy or eighty year old crone.","Nan Rui nodded with difficulty. \"This is indeed my mother. There's a long story, but her condition is very dangerous. Please contact that master now. If the gu isn't removed soon, I'm afraid my mother won't live.\"","Although Mo Jiuye had a lot of questions, he could also see Imperial Consort De's precarious state. Now wasn't the time to overthink Nan Rui's words.","After making sure there were no suspicious presences nearby, he moved aside to let Nan Rui drive the carriage into the yard.","The family rabbits had been giving birth these past days. After breakfast, everyone had gone to help out back, leaving the front yard empty.","Mo Jiuye had Nan Rui carry Imperial Consort De into a wing room.","\"My shabby home is no match for the splendor you’re used to. Please pardon its simplicity, Your Highness.\"","To the Mozi sect members, who had let go of materialism, these environs mattered not. But to the prestigious Prince Rui and Imperial Consort De, it was indeed too shabby. Mo Jiuye felt the need to give them fair warning.","\"No matter. Material trappings have ceased to matter to this prince.\"","Seeing Nan Rui's worried look, Mo Jiuye decided not to delve deeper for now.","\"Rest here for now, Your Highness. I’ll have my family come attend to Consort De shortly. I'm heading out now to look for the master exorcist.\"","Mo Jiuye went to Old Lady Mo's room and gave her a simple rundown of Nan Rui and Consort De's arrival and purpose, asking her to host them for the time being.","He then quickly returned to his room to brief He Zhi Ran on the matter.","He Zhi Ran had been resting well these days. Her discomfort had passed and her only grievance was everyone fretting over her too much, confining her to bedrest.","Hearing the clopping outside earlier, she had peeked out the window and already seen Nan Rui arrive.","To easily assume the gu poison master's identity later, she chose to stay out of sight for now, using her pregnancy as an excuse.","It was reasonable for an expectant mother to refrain from seeing guests.","\"I took a look through the window. Consort De doesn't seem well at all.\" She said.","\"That's right. She looks like she's in her twilight years even though she's only in her fifties. And she's unconscious.\" Mo Jiuye answered.","Without an examination, He Zhi Ran couldn't determine the cause either.","\"It appears the mysterious master exorcist will have to make an early entrance.\" She mused.","He Zhi Ran was thinking that regardless of Nan Rui's motives, since Consort De was already here, she ought to ensure her survival.","With Consort De present, she could keep Nan Rui in check.","\"I'll head out now and wait for you at the foot of the mountain.\" She continued, referring to her storage space.","Mo Jiuye knew she was going to get changed in there.","\"Alright, go carefully. I'll smooth things over with Nan Rui before heading out.\"","After tidying up, He Zhi Ran took the chance while the yard was empty to walk towards the mountainside. Mo Jiuye pretended he was going out and went to the wing room to update Nan Rui.","At this time, Old Lady Mo was already inside conversing with the prince. Their conversation topic was something Mo Jiuye wanted to know more about, so he didn't hurry to leave.","He Zhi Ran could take her time resting in the space anyway. No need to rush to her.","\"You mean Imperial Consort De faked her death to leave the palace?\" Old Lady Mo sounded rather shocked.","She had heard of such death-faking drugs before, but never saw anyone use them. The ingredients were precious indeed.","Mentioning making his mother fake her death distressed Nan Rui somewhat.","\"My mother was tired of palace life. She'd wanted to leave that viper's nest for some time.","When this chance came up to bring Mother out to dispel her gu, I thought I'd make her vanish for good - erase Imperial Consort De from Da Shun Palace, so she can live the rest of her life in peace.\"","Old Lady Mo saw the sorrow on Nan Rui's face and prodded further. \"So you chose to have Consort De fake her death and leave the palace?\"","Nan Rui nodded. \"That's right. I wanted my mother to achieve her wish in this lifetime.","The northwest may not be affluent, but I am still a prince. I naturally have assets on hand. As long as there is money, I believe Mother's life will be the same anywhere.","Moreover, I have no intention of setting foot in that quagmire of deceit and betrayal again. With my company, Mother will live out her remaining years contentedly.\"","\"However, I didn't expect the person cursing my mother with gu to not have activated it for so long. I assumed nothing would go amiss while traveling northwest for a month after her ‘death’.","Yet oddly, around ten days into the journey, Mother suddenly felt pain throughout her body and lost consciousness several times.","My conjecture is that her gu warlock discovered my mother had left the capital with me, forcing me to turn back by agitating the gu worms.","I wavered seeing my mother in such torment, but she insisted even death was preferable to returning there.","Left without recourse, I hurried day and night to Xi Ling Village. Now my mother's already been unconscious for over two days.\"","Hearing this, Mo Jiuye grasped the general picture. He had no intention of prying into the exact details of Consort De's staged death.","\"Your Highness had a rough journey. Please let Imperial Consort De rest here, while I head out now to find that gu master.\""]},{"number":307,"title":"Chapter 307: Of course I did it, your husband.","paragraphs":["When it came to experts in undoing gu spells, no one knew their identity better than Old Lady Mo in her heart. It was none other than her ninth daughter-in-law, He Zhiran. After all, she had personally helped undo the gu spells afflicting several of her sons. She just didn’t know what identity He Zhiran would appear before Nan Rui with. Of course, she also knew this wasn’t the time to ask questions.","What worried Old Lady Mo the most was He Zhiran’s condition. After many years of marriage among the nine Mo sons, they finally had a daughter-in-law who was pregnant. She was afraid He Zhiran doing these things would cause some accident to happen to her body.","She signaled to Mo Jiuye with her eyes, reminding him to take good care of his wife.","Mo Jiuye understood his mother’s meaning. “Don’t worry, Mother.”","Nan Rui didn’t know the hidden meaning behind the interaction between the Mo mother and son. He thought Mo Jiuye might encounter danger while looking for the expert, so he gratefully cupped his fist towards Mo Jiuye.","“As long as the gu in my Imperial Mother can be removed, even if I must trade my life for it, I would not hesitate.”","Mo Jiuye returned the courtesy. “I can only say I will do my best to find someone, but I dare not guarantee I can fulfill your wish.”","At this time, he could not make absolute promises, otherwise it would easily arouse Nan Rui's suspicion.","Mo Jiuye went straight out the door towards the foot of the mountain.","He Zhiran saw he still hadn’t come after a long time, so she entered the space and ate some fruit. By the time she came out, she saw Mo Jiuye striding quickly towards her.","The two returned to the space again, and Mo Jiuye recounted the situation with the Imperial Concubine that he had just learned.","He Zhiran more or less already knew.","“Based on the current condition of the Imperial Concubine, she has been eroded by the gu worms.”","What was called erosion by gu worms was when the spell caster activated the mother gu to torment the person carrying the child gu. If it persisted for too long, the host of the child gu would not be able to withstand the resistance and the gu worms inside the body would spread towards the heart.","This process was very fast, generally not more than five days before the host of the child gu would die.","According to what Nan Rui said, the Imperial Concubine had already been in a coma for two days. That meant the gu worms must be removed from her body within three days, otherwise her life would be in danger.","Three days was ample time for He Zhiran.","Even preparing for major surgery wouldn’t take this long, so Mo Jiuye was in no hurry to bring back news of finding the gu-dispelling expert either.","They could stay outside for one more day, then bring the news back. This way it wouldn’t arouse Nan Rui’s suspicions.","The husband and wife happened to have rare free time, especially outside, without having to worry about their family finding it odd when they couldn’t find them after entering the space.","He Zhiran hadn’t enjoyed the carefree life inside the space for a long time. She first played with her darling Rice Ball for a while before going to the warehouse with Mo Jiuye.","By now, the most abundant things in the warehouse were all kinds of crop seeds and the fruit tree saplings she had stored.","These were all going to be planted in Xi Ling Village after the spring.","Aside from these seeds, He Zhiran had also left a lot of food behind, with even more variety compared to the produce markets in her past life.","There were also the fish in the ponds that she hadn’t taken out to feed her family for a long time. She decisively chose to catch all those fish, then after cleaning them, delivered them into the warehouse for storage.","Anyway, the space came with a preservation function itself, so they would be fresh no matter when they were eaten.","There were also those cows and sheep that He Zhiran had slaughtered batches of using the control panel, before buying more calves and lambs to raise.","She would also need to prepare some to raise outside later. It would be pretty good if there were more adults too.","Mo Jiuye felt distressed for his hardworking wife, who had been enduring bitterness with him all this time without even being able to nurture the pregnancy well like other women.","They finally had some alone time, so he was determined to show off his skills.","He Zhiran didn’t know that Mo Jiuye had secretly used her phone to buy a modern cookbook from the Taobao Mall recently. He would diligently study it whenever he had free time.","After learning for so long, today was finally a chance to show off what he had learned.","He pulled He Zhiran back to rest in the bedroom while he busied himself in the kitchen.","Anyway, the warehouse had all kinds of ingredients, so all he needed to do was display his skills.","He Zhiran woke up from her nap to Mo Jiuye pulling her to the dining table. The scene before her made her stunned speechless.","“Where did all these dishes come from?”","Mo Jiuye grinned as he supported her into her seat. “Of course your husband made them.”","“You made them?” She would never believe that even if she was beaten to death.","There was no way the guy who was burning dishes beyond recognition not long ago could make so many beautifully plated dishes, right?","Mo Jiuye knew she wouldn't believe him, which made it even better as he'd be giving his wife a little surprise.","\"Of course I made them.\"","To prove himself, he put the cookbook he used in front of He Zhiran for her to see.","\"I followed the methods in here to learn.\"","He Zhiran truly didn't know when her sneaky husband had secretly learned cooking. Still, she felt rather touched.","\"Dear husband, thank you for everything you've done for me.\"","Mo Jiuye lovingly stroked her head. \"Silly girl, compared to everything you've done for me, how can this measure up?\"","As he spoke, he picked up a piece of braised pork ribs, her favorite, into her bowl.","\"Try the taste first.\"","Unlike other pregnant women, He Zhiran didn't suffer from severe pregnancy reactions, and her symptoms had only lasted a few days before going away.","Now, her appetite had greatly increased, especially for meat.","Mo Jiuye indulged her preferences, making several meat-focused dishes, which made He Zhiran suddenly feel like her index finger was twitching to dig in.","After eating a piece of the ribs, He Zhiran kept nodding. \"It's really delicious.\"","Hearing his beloved praise his cooking made the corners of Mo Jiuye's lips quirk up instantly.","\"If you like it, I'll make it for you to eat every day from now on.\"","He Zhiran didn't doubt this at all. With how good Mo Jiuye treated her, he was completely capable of doing this.","It was just that this was ancient times after all, and the propriety of men staying out of the kitchen was still valued by people. If Mo Jiuye was cooking meals for her at home, their family would probably feel uncomfortable about it.","Although she possessed a modern soul, she had never forgotten the principle of conforming to local customs when abroad.","Mo Jiuye liked doting on her, so it was enough when it was just the two of them in the space.","Moreover, the meals at home were all handled by her sisters-in-law and Lan Er. They didn't need this big man to get involved at all.","After happily enjoying the delicious meal brought to her by her husband, He Zhiran felt somewhat full.","Thus, she and Mo Jiuye casually strolled around in the space together.","She was relatively casual in the space, wearing an outfit made of pure cotton fabric commonly worn at home.","This was the type of clothes she often wore inside the space, but today they felt a bit tight, especially around her lower abdomen.","Glancing down, her stomach was clearly bigger than a normal three-month pregnant woman's, either because she just ate too much or her little one inside was growing too fast.","Seeing her slightly protruding belly, He Zhiran finally realized that after such a long time, she still hadn’t properly examined herself."]},{"number":308,"title":"Chapter 308: I can't let anything happen to You.","paragraphs":["At this time, she happened to have nothing to do, so she went back to the infirmary and examined it carefully.","He Zhiran was shocked to find that she was actually pregnant with twins.","Seeing her stunned look, Mo Jiuye thought there was something wrong with the child, and asked anxiously,","\"Ranran, is our child okay?\"","\"The child is very healthy, it's just...\"","\"Just what?\" Mo Jiuye couldn't wait to know the result.","\"I'm pregnant with two this time.\" He Zhiran said the result she had just checked. No wonder she always felt something special about her pulse when she diagnosed her pulse.","At this point, Mo Jiuye was petrified.","\"What did you say, Ranran?\"","He Zhiran held up the report form and told him very positively.","\"I'm pregnant with two children.\"","When Mo Jiuye heard her words, there was not a hint of joy on his face, but a frown.","He Zhiran knew he was worried that giving birth to twins would be dangerous.","It was indeed the case that in this medically underdeveloped ancient times, childbirth for women was like going through the ghost gate once, and she was pregnant with two again this time, which made people afraid and worried, right?","But who is she?","She was a military doctor from the 21st century. The space was equipped with all kinds of modern medical facilities. At worst, she could teach Mo Jiuye the cesarean section surgery in advance, or he could help.","\"Don't worry, it's just twins, there must be no problem.\"","He Zhiran said very firmly, as if she could predict the future.","Mo Jiuye still didn't feel as relaxed as she thought.","\"Ranran, twins are not a joke. I would rather not have any offspring than want you to be in danger.\"","He Zhiran could probably guess what Mo Jiuye was going to do.","\"What do you want to do?\"","Mo Jiuye looked very painful, but he still had to say what he should say.","\"Ranran, why don't we not want this child anymore, I can't let you get hurt in any way.\"","Losing his own child was also very painful for him, but thinking of the danger his wife would face in the future, he could only bite the bullet and make a choice.","\"It's not as serious as you think, trust me, our children will be born safely.\" He Zhiran said firmly.","As a doctor, if she couldn't even keep her own children safe, what else could she talk about curing diseases and saving people?","\"But...\"","Mo Jiuye was about to say something more when He Zhiran interrupted him.","\"It doesn't matter if it's twins, you can have a cesarean section.\"","In order to reassure Mo Jiuye, she took him to the infirmary with her and handed him a book on cesarean section.","\"This is the method of cesarean section. You can learn it when you have time. It’s best to have a natural delivery. In case of emergency, use this method.\"","Mo Jiuye's hands holding the book were shaking. He had helped Fourth Brother in the operating room with He Zhiran to treat his leg injury and remove Gu with her many times.","But at the thought of Ranran's body being cut open, his heart ached so much that he couldn't breathe.","Seeing that he was still struggling, He Zhiran shook his arm a few times and said gently, \"Okay, don't be so nervous, believe me, it will definitely be fine.\"","For Mo Jiuye, killing his own flesh and blood was also very cruel. Since his wife said so, he could only choose to compromise for the time being.","\"Okay, then you must take good care of yourself from now on, and never make any mistakes.\"","\"Don't worry!\" He Zhiran assured.","At this moment, Mo Jiuye no longer had the heart to spend the two-person world in the space. Holding the book He Zhiran gave him, he sat on the chair and read it carefully. Whenever he had a question he didn't understand, he would ask from time to time, and He Zhiran would answer them all carefully.","In this way, the two of them spent a whole day in the space before leaving the next morning.","At this time, He Zhiran had already made up her appearance, changing from the original beauty to a white-haired old woman with wrinkles all over her face.","She discussed with Mo Jiuye that she would help Consort De remove Gu at the ghost house at the foot of the mountain where Fifth Brother used to live.","There were usually not many people close to that place, and the old woman He Zhiran pretended to be did not need to be seen by more people either.","He Zhiran didn't have to wait long in the haunted house before Mo Jiuye brought Nan Rui and Consort De over. It could be seen how impatient Nan Rui was to save his mother's life.","Seeing the old woman with wrinkles all over her face standing in the room, Nan Rui knew that this was the highly skilled Gu master Mo Jiuye had found.","In the face of the person who could save his mother's life, he was very respectful, even making He Zhiran feel a little surprised.","I saw Nan Rui take a step forward and kneel directly in front of He Zhiran.","\"Master, as long as you can save my mother's life, let me do anything.\"","He Zhiran didn't expect Nan Rui to kneel down to her.","She didn't dodge it. She could fully accept the courtesy of saving a life. Moreover, no matter what the reason, Nan Rui had done things that were detrimental to the Mo family, so this would be his apology to the Mo family.","\"The Mo family has shown me kindness. I want you to swear that after I remove the Gu from your mother, you will never do anything wrong to the Mo family again in your life.\" He Zhiran deliberately lowered her voice.","She believed in the loyalty of the ancients to their oaths. As long as Nan Rui did not do anything detrimental to the Mo family, there would currently be no one targeting them in the court. In the future, it would be fine to live in peace in the northwest.","Of course, she and Mo Jiuye could also take the opportunity to kill Nan Rui, but neither of them wanted to do that.","If Nan Rui died, Dashun would only have the fake prince Nanqi left. Although they no longer had anything to do with the court, no one wanted to see the situation of one family domination.","With Nan Rui there, it was also a very good restraint for Nanqi to keep him on high alert at all times.","Without even thinking, Nan Rui raised his right hand: \"I swear that I will never do anything detrimental to the Mo family in my life.\"","Moreover, he had already figured it out that after his mother was cured, his wish would be fulfilled. He would take his mother to live incognito for the rest of their lives and never participate in those sinister plots again.","In addition to swearing, Nan Rui also took out a large bundle of silver bills and gave them to He Zhiran.","\"Master, this is the reward for curing my mother. If it's not enough, I can add more.\"","He Zhiran didn't stand on courtesy and glanced sideways at the silver bills in his hand.","The denominations were all one thousand taels each, and she could feel from the texture that there were about one hundred thousand taels.","He Zhiran had no intention of being polite about this. Given Consort De's condition, I'm afraid no one other than her could cure her in this era.","Even if the poisonous insects in her body were removed, her severely damaged body was afraid it wouldn’t last a few more days.","\"Okay, I'll take the silver. I don't want anyone else present when I remove the Gu. Mo Jiuye can stay and help.\"","Nan Rui wanted to stay by his mother's side, but he didn't dare to challenge the authority of the master. In case he displeased her somehow and she didn't help his mother remove the poisonous insects, it wouldn't be worth it.","He looked worriedly at the unconscious Consort De on the bed, saluted He Zhiran again, before leaving the room."]},{"number":309,"title":"Chapter 309: Does He really Have No Ambition","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye saw him leave and instructed, \"When I don't call you, you must not come in and disturb me no matter what.\"","\"Okay,\" Nan Rui replied, and had already closed the door outside.","He Zhiran was not at ease, so she went forward and bolted the door from inside.","The two looked at each other, then brought Consort De with them and flashed into the space.","Consort De's condition was slightly better than what He Zhiran had imagined. After all, she was an imperial consort in the palace, so even if Emperor Shunwu did not favor her, at least she was not mistreated in terms of food and drink.","It was just that the gu worms had erupted on the way here these past few days and she had not eaten much, causing her body to be weaker than an average person’s.","The only tricky thing was that the gu worms in Consort De's body had already eroded into her internal organs and were extremely close to her heart.","Just as He Zhiran had initially judged, if the gu worms were not removed within three days, Consort De's life would be over.","The top priority now was to first remove the gu worms from Consort De's body. As for her aged appearance, it was also caused by the gu worms in her body.","As long as the gu worms were removed, she would surely regain her youthful looks after slowly recuperating.","Mo Jiuye was no stranger to surgery. He knew the gu worms in Consort De’s body were less than a centimeter away from her heart. Removing them would definitely be much more complicated than when his brothers had their gu worms removed.","Therefore, while He Zhiran was carefully examining Consort De, he had already prepared the surgical facilities so that later his wife would only need to do some key procedures. Whatever he could help with, he would definitely not let He Zhiran get too tired.","At this moment, He Zhiran had also changed into surgical scrubs. After accurately locating the gu worms with the equipment, she started wielding the scalpel.","As always, Mo Jiuye was holding a glass container, ready to catch the gu worm as soon as it poked its head out.","The gu worm’s position was quite special, less than a centimeter away from the heart. If this was an ordinary tumor removal surgery, this area could be treated with minimally invasive techniques.","However, Consort De’s situation could not be handled that way. Gu worms were not dead matter like tumors. Once a hole was made in the body, they would still remain in their original position.","If the gu worms sensed any danger, they would immediately destroy other tissues in the body to save themselves.","Therefore, removing Consort De’s gu worm could only be done through conventional surgery.","He Zhiran skillfully used the scalpel to cut open a 10 cm incision below Consort De’s heart. She kept deepening the incision based on the equipment prompts.","Only when she saw the gu worm did she alert Mo Jiuye.","“Get ready to catch the gu worm.”","In fact, Mo Jiuye was already prepared. As He Zhiran peeled back Consort De’s flesh with tools and the gu worm poked its head out a little, Mo Jiuye accurately clamped it with forceps and quickly sent it into the glass bottle.","This was an ordinary gu worm. Unlike puppet gu, once a offspring gu left its host, it was like a child without its mother, thrashing around in the glass bottle.","In order for the gu worm to continue living, He Zhiran decisively took some of Consort De’s blood and poured it into the bottle.","As long as the offspring gu was alive, they still had hope of finding the mother gu.","This was another reason why He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye were willing to save Consort De. As long as the offspring gu was alive, they could use its reactions to search for the location of the mother gu.","This would definitely be easier than her brothers searching the Western Sea.","Mo Jiuye carefully stored away the offspring gu. On He Zhiran’s side, she quickly sutured Consort De’s wound closed before dressing it.","When all the procedures were complete, Consort De was still unconscious.","Taking this chance, He Zhiran administered medical treatments from two fronts, hanging both plasma and intravenous nutrition fluid to speed up Consort De’s recovery.","Worried about He Zhiran’s health, Mo Jiuye helped her change back into the old woman’s outfit as soon as she was done and prepared a sumptuous meal for her.","While Consort De was on the IV drip, He Zhiran took another short nap.","It was not until ten hours later that the two brought Consort De, who was showing signs of awakening, out of the space with them.","When Mo Jiuye opened the door, the sky outside was already dark.","This day had been extremely agonizing for Nan Rui. After waiting five hours, worried about his Imperial Consort Mother’s condition yet not daring to step forward and ask, he was on pins and needles.","Finally, when the door opened, he quickly went up to Mo Jiuye and asked anxiously, “Ninth Young Master, how is my Imperial Mother?”","Mo Jiuye understood his feelings. Back then, when Fourth Brother was having surgery, just watching from the sidelines made him feel tortured. How much more so for Nan Rui who couldn’t even see the person?","“The gu worm in Imperial Consort De's body has been successfully removed, and the master has also treated her body. She will definitely wake up before long.”","Hearing this, Nan Rui trembled as he grabbed Mo Jiuye’s hand in excitement.","“Can I...can I go see Imperial Mother now?”","Mo Jiuye stepped aside to make way for the door. “You can.”","Nan Rui rushed into the room without even remembering to thank He Zhiran.","He knelt by the bed on one knee and carefully examined his mother in the dim oil lamp light.","It could be seen that Consort De’s complexion had a touch of rosy glow to it, and her breathing was extremely steady.","Tears instantly rolled down Nan Rui's cheeks.","“Mother, your gu worm has finally been removed. From now on, your son will take you away to live an ordinary life under assumed names.”","These were Nan Rui’s words to Consort De, but to Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran, they were quite unexpected.","No matter what, Nan Rui was still a prince of the Da Shun Dynasty. To give up the glory and wealth he was born with for his mother was astonishing.","Could it be that he truly had no ambition at all?","This was something Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran did not completely believe.","No matter what he did in the future, as long as he did not secretly harm the Mo family, it was none of their business.","The most important goal of obtaining the offspring gu in Consort De had already been achieved. As for what Nan Rui would do next, they had no intention of getting too involved.","But Consort De’s current condition truly could not be casually moved. It seemed they would have to stay here for some time.","The gu master persona created by He Zhiran could not linger here indefinitely. She planned to take this chance to leave this place.","“The gu worm in Imperial Consort Mother has been removed. This old one should take her leave.”","Hearing her voice, Nan Rui suddenly remembered he had been rude.","He quickly stood up and solemnly bowed to He Zhiran.","“Many thanks to the master for removing the gu worm from my Imperial Mother. I plan to stay in the northwest from now on. If you ever need me for anything, please let me know.”","It could be said that Nan Rui’s tone was very sincere. He Zhiran did not sense even a hint of perfunctoriness from him.","“This old one has remembered Prince Rui’s words. I definitely won’t stand on ceremony with you if I have any needs.”","As He Zhiran spoke, she was also sneering inwardly.","Nan Rui wanting to stay in the northwest was unexpected for both her and Mo Jiuye. Could it be that he really planned to live an obscure life from now on?"]},{"number":310,"title":"Chapter 310: I promise to have two babies.","paragraphs":["Everyone says it's easy to go from frugal to extravagant, but hard to go from extravagant to frugal.","Nan Rui was once a prominent prince in the Great Shun Dynasty. If he hid his identity and stayed in the northwest, he would be just an ordinary person.","Even if he had plenty of money, could he really get used to living a simple life like the common people?","Could it be that he didn't enjoy the scheming and plotting in the royal court?","No matter what, it was Nan Rui's own business and had nothing to do with them.","\"Alright, if anything comes up I'll ask Master Mo Jiuye to help you.\"","As he finished speaking, He Zhiran immediately turned and walked towards the door.","Mo Jiuye quickly followed.","\"I'll walk the master out.\"","Nan Rui also wanted to go, but looked back at the still unconscious Imperial Concubine on the bed before following them.","How could He Zhiran let Nan Rui come along?","\"Prince Rui, please stay behind. This old man has some matters to discuss with Master Jiu.\"","Since he put it that way, it would be improper for Nan Rui to insist on following.","\"If that's the case, I won't see you off. Have a safe journey.\"","His polite attitude made He Zhiran momentarily feel that this was no prince at all, but a gentle and refined scholar.","But then again, Nan Rui's image at court had always been that of a literary man absorbed in poetry and prose.","Seeing Nan Rui turn back to the Imperial Concubine's bedside, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye left one after the other.","Once they reached the foot of the mountain where no one was around, they slipped into the space.","He Zhiran changed back into his original attire before returning home with Mo Jiuye.","The two of them had been out for a whole day and night, worrying old Mrs. Mo sick.","She even cursed her foolish ninth son several times. His wife was pregnant, a delicate condition, yet he still went out to undo a curse, and was gone for so long!","Even if it was just for show to find someone for Nan Rui, he shouldn't have stayed out overnight as a healthy young man. How could a pregnant woman endure it?","Just as old Mrs. Mo was getting more and more upset, the two people she had just complained about came back hand in hand.","The moment old Mrs. Mo saw He Zhiran, half her anger dissipated.","She hurried forward, first shooting Mo Jiuye a fierce glare.","Mo Jiuye was of course very familiar with his old mother's looks - she was warning him that she would deal with him later...","But very soon, old Mrs. Mo's expression became extremely gentle.","She looked He Zhiran up and down and, seeing nothing wrong with her, finally relaxed.","\"Jiuye, hurry and take your wife back to rest.\"","He Zhiran knew her mother-in-law was worried about her, so she explained on Mo Jiuye's behalf, \"Mother, my husband took good care of me. Nothing happened, please don't worry about me.\"","Old Mrs. Mo's tone was much gentler with her daughter-in-law.","\"That's good as long as you're alright. Ever since you married into the Mo family you haven't had an easy time - either traveling around destitute or helping search for your elders.","Now that things are finally settled, and you're expecting the Mo family's only grandchild, yet this boy still doesn't know to cherish his wife and took you out overnight.\"","In old Mrs. Mo's mind, her son had to be a pillar when outside, and a loving husband and father at home. And now his wife had just gotten pregnant, helping the Imperial Concubine detox was unavoidable, but this wretched son didn't know to take care of his wife at all!","He Zhiran knew her mother-in-law was eager for a grandson, but she and Mo Jiuye had rested in the space - the most suitable place for nurturing a child and extremely comfortable.","She continued to make excuses for Mo Jiuye with a smile, \"Mother, my husband took great care of me. Also, I have good news to tell you - I'm expecting twins this time! When they're born, whether they're boys or girls, you can hold two grandchildren at once.\"","She spoke lightly, but it made old Mrs. Mo and Mo Jiuye equally nervous. Twins could easily threaten the mother's life...","\"You said you're having twins?\"","At this moment old Mrs. Mo could only hope she had misheard.","But Mo Jiuye shattered her fantasy.","\"Mother, it really is twins. We've had it confirmed by a doctor.\"","Old Mrs. Mo was dumbstruck, staring at He Zhiran's belly for a long time unable to utter a word.","She thought that she'd rather the Mo family have no heir than let such a good daughter-in-law be in danger.","\"This child...\" can't be kept.","Old Mrs. Mo didn't finish her sentence before He Zhiran interrupted her.","\"Mother, I'm a doctor myself. I guarantee I can safely deliver both children.\"","He Zhiran knew that her mother-in-law, like Mo Jiuye at first, was worried about any danger to her.","Mo Jiuye knew his mother was also concerned for He Zhiran's safety. Since he had already promised his wife to keep the children, he had to stand united with her.","\"Mother, He Zhiran says she has a way to safely give birth. We have to believe her.\"","Seeing her foolish son still thinking so naively, old Mrs. Mo almost wanted to punch him.","Just as the mother-in-law was about to lose her temper at her son-in-law, He Zhiran quickly stepped forward.","Old Mrs. Mo's outstretched hand froze in midair before falling back to her side.","\"Listen to me this time. You can always have more children later, but I can't let such a good daughter-in-law be in danger.\"","Seeing this, He Zhiran could only patiently explain,","\"Mother, trust me. I know a medical technique. Even if delivery is difficult, don't worry. I guarantee the safety of both mother and children.\"","Old Mrs. Mo was stunned for a moment, then asked, \"You're sure you won't be in danger?\"","Although she didn't know what medical technique her daughter-in-law was referring to, she was clearly aware He Zhiran was capable.","After thinking it over, she finally decided to trust her capable daughter-in-law regarding the children.","\"Alright then. Mother won't worry any more. You must protect yourself well.\"","\"I understand, Mother. Not only will I protect myself, I will protect your grandchildren as well,\" He Zhiran said with a playful smile.","Seeing this, old Mrs. Mo's taut expression also gradually relaxed.","She urged Mo Jiuye, \"Quickly take your wife back to rest. You're a grown man yet don't even know how to take care of your wife.\"","Mo Jiuye now felt as if he had received an imperial pardon. He nodded vigorously, \"Mother, I'll take He Zhiran back to rest right away.\"","With that said, he pulled He Zhiran towards their room without looking back - afraid that if he walked too slowly his mother's piercing gaze would stab him...","Old Mrs. Mo took a deep breath and returned to her own room.","At dinner that night, He Zhiran realized the news that she was expecting twins had spread to the whole family. Her sisters-in-law were as concerned as her mother-in-law, treating her like an animal needing special protection. They directly handed her her bowl and chopsticks, as if afraid any big movements would harm the children.","This enthusiasm made He Zhiran a little overwhelmed, and she kept thanking her sisters-in-law.","Seeing this, old Mrs. Mo also knew she felt uncomfortable with all the attention, and saw her daughters-in-law were still piling food onto He Zhiran's plate. She quickly spoke up, \"You girls are too enthusiastic.\""]},{"number":311,"title":"Chapter 311: Carrier Pigeon","paragraphs":["The sisters-in-law's hands stopped scooping up dishes, and they looked at each other in dismay before looking towards He Zhiran's bowl, which was already piled high with various dishes, threatening to spill over the sides.","Only then did they laugh and return to their seats.","Second sister-in-law said loudly, \"Hahaha, look at us sisters-in-law, afraid our two nephews won't eat enough, constantly putting dishes in Ninth Sister-in-Law's bowl.\"","Her timely words defused the embarrassment of the other sisters-in-law.","He Zhiran was now eating everything given to her. Not only did she finish all the dishes, she also ate two large bowls of rice.","After eating so much, she had visibly gained some weight, taking on a different kind of beauty.","Poor Mo Jiuye, in the prime of his youth, could only watch this feast longingly with a nosebleed...","That night after returning to the space, He Zhiran washed up and immediately fell asleep.","Mo Jiuye looked at her longingly, wanting to touch her but afraid of disturbing his wife's rest. Left with no choice, he could only go to the bathroom to forcibly cool down.","The next morning, Mo Jiuye pretended to take He Zhiran out for a walk. The two went directly to the haunted house at the foot of the mountain.","Nan Rui's carriage contained quite a bit of rations and ingredients. The haunted house also had simple stoves left by Fifth Brother, so mother and son would not go hungry.","The Consort De had regained consciousness but her body was still very weak. She couldn't eat the hard biscuits Nan Rui took out.","Nan Rui was waiting for Mo Jiuye to come and ask him to help buy some ingredients.","\"Ninth Young Master, you're finally here.\"","Hearing him say this, Mo Jiuye thought something had happened to the Consort De.","\"Is there something wrong with the Consort De?\"","Seeing Mo Jiuye's tone had misunderstood, Nan Rui quickly explained, \"No, my mother has woken up, it's just that I don't have any suitable food for her here. I wanted to trouble you to help me buy some nourishing ingredients.","Also, if it's convenient, could you help bring over my mother's personal servant from the largest inn in Yun City?\"","In order not to make Mo Jiuye wary, he had ordered his personal attendants and mother's servants to all remain in Yun City.","He had come to Xi Ling Village alone, disguised as an ordinary merchant. Now he didn't even have someone to help him.","Although he had already prepared himself for the possibility of having to do everything himself in the future, after all he had just started and was not yet used to it.","Especially now, he really felt a bit flustered.","Not to mention taking care of his mother's daily needs, he simply could not serve her well enough.","These were all issues that needed to be resolved immediately.","Seeing that Mo Jiuye did not respond immediately, Nan Rui thought he was still resentful about what had happened before.","So he hurried to the carriage, took out the white dove from inside.","Mo Jiuye had wanted to ask Nan Rui why he had brought a white dove to the northwest, but at that time the Consort De's life was in danger and Nan Rui was extremely anxious, so he had endured and not asked.","Now, without waiting for Mo Jiuye to inquire, Nan Rui was already holding the cage and coming over to explain:","\"This dove is also considered a gift to thank you for helping me find an expert to treat my mother.\"","Then, Nan Rui took out two more silver notes and gave them to Mo Jiuye, afraid he would think the previous five hundred taels were too little.","\"And take this too.\"","The reason he gave Mo Jiuye more silver notes again was because he thought of the unpleasant things Emperor Father had arranged when the Mo family was exiled, as well as the schemes his elder brother had done behind the scenes, resulting in the Mo family leaving for exile empty-handed.","Now they had just settled in the northwest, they must be in need of money.","Knowing Mo Jiuye's pride, if he directly said he wanted to help them, they probably wouldn't accept it. It was just right to take this opportunity of asking him to buy things to help the Mo family a bit.","Actually Nan Rui didn't know that Mo Jiuye had changed.","He was no longer as rigid as before, having already learned to be flexible and know when to advance and when to retreat from He Zhiran.","What's more, his wife had saved the Consort De's life. Apart from these silver notes, even ten or a hundred times more would not be excessive.","He took the silver notes with no intention of returning them, focusing all his attention on the white dove.","\"Is there anything special about this white dove?\"","Seeing that Mo Jiuye did not decline the silver notes he had given, Nan Rui happily bent down to open the cage and took out the white dove.","\"Don't look down on this thing. It's that mysterious man's treasure. He used this white dove to send me a letter before.\"","Speaking of delivering letters, Mo Jiuye remembered what had happened a few days ago. The Southerner who had seized the shipping company said that Si Meng's carrier pigeon was lost, which was why he didn't dare to go back and became the boss there instead.","Could it be that the white dove in Nan Rui's hand was the one the Southerner had lost?","\"May I ask, Prince Rui, why are you so certain that this is the dove that sent you letters, and how did you obtain this white dove?\"","Nan Rui spread the wings of the white dove while still holding it.","\"Look here, there is a golden feather in this white dove's wing.","After I left here before the new year, on the way I saw a Southerner holding a cage with a white dove.","Coincidentally, the dove stretched its wings at that moment, and I recognized it at a glance as the one the mysterious man used to send me letters.\"","Hearing Nan Rui say this, Mo Jiuye could confirm that this was indeed the dove the Southerner had lost.","Before he could speak, Nan Rui continued:","\"At that time I thought this white dove might be useful to you, so I had my attendant rob it from the Southerner.","Unfortunately, that Southerner knew how to use poison. My attendant was unable to catch him.","Luckily, I obtained this white dove.\"","As he spoke, Nan Rui had already put the white dove back in the cage, then pushed the cage towards Mo Jiuye, signaling him to take it.","This white dove could be a clue for Mo Jiuye to find Si Meng. He solemnly thanked Nan Rui, then picked up the cage.","Thinking they were about to leave, Nan Rui anxiously said, \"My mother's appetite is poor now. I hope you can help me buy some nourishing ingredients, and also, if it's convenient, help bring over my mother's personal servant.\"","Mo Jiuye had no intention of leaving immediately. He and his wife had come mainly to check on the Consort De.","\"My wife and I came to visit the Consort De.\"","Hearing this, Nan Rui hurriedly moved to the side.","\"Great. My mother is awake inside.\""]},{"number":312,"title":"Chapter 312: Unknown Creature","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye pulled He Zhiran with him into the room.","Consort De had indeed woken up, but she didn't look to have much energy.","When Mo Jiuye was young, he would often go into the palace and had met Consort De a few times, so the two weren't complete strangers.","Consort De narrowed her eyes slightly to size up the newcomers, and said with difficulty: \"You are Young Master Mo Jiuye, right?\"","Mo Jiuye didn't have any bad impressions towards Consort De, so he clasped his hands in salute towards her: \"Greetings to Consort Mother.\"","Consort De slowly raised her hand: \"There is no Consort anymore, from now on I'm just an ordinary woman. If Young Master Mo doesn't look down on me, just call me Aunt Mei!\"","Mei was Consort De's maiden name. She and her son would be living ordinary lives under assumed names from then on, so she didn't want to reveal her surname and had Mo Jiuye address her as Aunt Mei instead.","Mo Jiuye didn't refuse, and spoke again calling her: \"Aunt Mei.\"","Consort De blinked showing that she was very happy, then looked towards He Zhiran.","\"This is the young master's wife?\"","Mo Jiuye pulled He Zhiran to his side: \"That's right, my wife.\"","He Zhiran also properly performed a blessing gesture towards Consort De, while carefully observing her condition.","Consort De's complexion was a little more rosy compared to when they had first met, and the corners of her lips still showed some signs of dryness.","\"Aunt Mei, I learned some medical skills since I was young. Why don't I take your pulse and have a look?\"","Consort De sized up He Zhiran for a while, then softly said: \"Alright, I'll have to trouble the young mistress then.\"","Hearing someone so much older address herself as young mistress, He Zhiran felt a little embarrassed.","\"Aunt Mei, just call me by my given name.\" Given Consort De's current condition, she estimated that she and Nan Rui would be staying here for a while. An elderly shouldn't have to keep addressing her as young mistress.","Mo Jiuye added: \"Aunt Mei, I usually call my wife Rangrang, you can call her that too.\"","Consort De lightly nodded: \"Alright, Rangrang it is then.\"","The original owner had attended banquets at the palace with her family before getting married. She was known as one of the top great beauties in the capital.","If Consort De hadn't heard that she was engaged to Mo Jiuye since young, she even thought of asking for an imperial decree to make her the Consort to Prince Rui.","Although Nan Rui was quite a bit older, he didn't have an official consort yet at that time and only had two concubines living in his residence.","It was a pity that his son didn't have such good fortune.","He Zhiran didn't know what Consort De was thinking. She picked up Consort De's wrist to take her pulse.","The results were better than she had imagined. Although Consort De had been eroded by gu worms for many years, possibly due to recuperating treatments at the palace, her health was recovering quite well.","Based on the current situation, eating some supplemental medicinal dishes on a regular basis would be good.","Her aged complexion would also gradually recover somewhat as her health improved.","Seeing her get up, Nan Rui asked: \"Young Mistress Jiu, how is my Imperial Mother's health?\"","He Zhiran smiled and said: \"Aunt Mei's condition is not bad. As long as she recuperates slowly, her health will definitely recover.\"","Nan Rui didn't know how skilled He Zhiran's medical techniques were. In any case, since someone said the Imperial Mother was in good health, he felt much more relieved.","The room was quite small to begin with. Nan Rui asked about his mother's condition, so Consort De could naturally hear it too.","No matter ancient or modern times, elderly people feared death. Consort De was no exception.","After waking up and finding out the gu worms in her body were gone, she had thought her health would immediately recover. But other than not feeling that bone-gnawing pain, things were still the same.","She started worrying that her end was near, feeling heartache that her son would have no kin by his side in the future.","Just now when she heard He Zhiran say there was nothing major wrong with her health, she suddenly felt relieved all over.","With this sense of relief, when He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye were about to leave, Consort De actually sat up wanting to go out to see them off.","He Zhiran knew that part of it was Consort De's mentality. It was probably because she had just said her health was fine which uplifted Consort De's spirits, giving her the energy to sit up.","Even so, she couldn't let Consort De get out of bed to send them off.","\"Aunt Mei, your health is still a little weak. You should be resting in bed.\"","Seeing his mother get up, Nan Rui felt happy but was also worried for her.","\"Mother is right, you just rest here. I'll go send Young Master Jiu off.\"","Ever since leaving the palace, Nan Rui had switched to calling her Mother instead of Imperial Mother! From then on, there would no longer be any Consort in this world!","After getting Consort De to settle back in, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran took their leave.","It was very easy for them to buy supplies for Nan Rui. He Zhiran's online shopping tools and personal space could get it done, providing anything they needed.","On the way back to the village, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye entered her space. She first wrote out a few medicinal diet recipes to help Consort De recuperate. Ingredients that were already in her space warehouse were directly taken out, those that weren't purchased online.","Aside from these, there was also grain and some food for Nan Rui to eat.","After preparing all of this, the two then headed back home.","While no one else was around, He Zhiran put all of the ingredients into the carriage. Mo Jiuye just had to go to Yucheng to bring Consort De's personal palace maid over.","With Mo Jiuye gone, she was bored by herself and went into her space to study that homing pigeon. Just now when she and Mo Jiuye were together, Rice Ball had behaved very obediently.","Unexpectedly, as soon as she entered her space, she discovered the little guy closely inspecting the cage with the homing pigeon.","That homing pigeon really seemed to have some spiritual nature, constantly flapping its wings to protest at Rice Ball.","He Zhiran was afraid Rice Ball might accidentally play this homing pigeon to death. She hurriedly used her mind to take out some fresh bamboo shoots to exchange for the cage.","But Rice Ball was being stubborn today. Usually when seeing the tender and delicious bamboo shoots, it would be shaking its butt eagerly to find its owner begging for a treat.","Yet now it was different. Rice Ball didn't have any interest stirred up by the bamboo shoots at all. It kept staring fixedly at the homing pigeon, and even more peculiarly, it didn't make any sounds towards the animal like it normally would with other creatures.","He Zhiran quickly picked up on Rice Ball's abnormal behavior, and hastily snatched the cage back from its embrace.","\"Rice Ball, don't be naughty.\"","Unhappy at having its toy taken away, Rice Ball turned its butt towards its owner, persisting in trying to hug that cage back.","Rice Ball would always put its owner as the first priority, yet today it was only interested in this homing pigeon.","Since the little guy was acting abnormally, He Zhiran didn't dare be too harsh and stood by to observe Rice Ball's condition.","She then saw that after Rice Ball got the cage as it wished, it continued staring fixedly at the 'unidentified creature' puffing itself up inside.","The homing pigeon also refused to back down with both eyes tightly fixed on the black and white furball in front of it.","As she was observing, she noticed the homing pigeon's beak suddenly transform.","Its originally pointed beak gradually changed shape into a curved blade, and its originally black eyes also turned crimson.","How was this still some homing pigeon!","It was clearly a miniature snow sculpture!","Except He Zhiran had never heard of snow sculptures existing in such a tiny size before.","Just then, Rice Ball finally reacted. It let out a few wolf howls towards the 'unidentified creature' in the cage.","\"Awoo...\"","She then saw the previously ruffled up unidentified creature immediately fold its wings close. Its eyes and beak also reverted back to their original appearances."]},{"number":313,"title":"Chapter 313: Eagle with Golden Wings","paragraphs":["He Zhiran could see that the rice ball had completely conquered whatever was inside the cage, be it a pigeon or something else.","Not only that, the mysterious white creature kept nodding at the rice ball.","The rice ball was no longer so stiff now. It trotted over to its owner like it was showing off.","After He Zhiran calmed down the rice ball, she looked at the mysterious creature.","It looked no different than when she first saw it - still a well-behaved little white pigeon.","If not for the rice ball bringing out its other side, He Zhiran might not have noticed anything unusual about it at all.","Now that the rice ball had revealed its true nature, He Zhiran was naturally more wary.","She made sure to keep some distance from the cage as she observed it.","But to her surprise, the little thing in the cage started acting cute towards her.","Its little head bobbed up and down nonstop, and its wings flapped open and closed - clearly trying to curry favor.","He Zhiran was a little stunned.","She brought the rice ball over and asked it, \"Baby, did you tame it?\"","The rice ball nodded its round head vigorously and made murmuring sounds.","Now He Zhiran could confirm that this mysterious creature had accepted her or the rice ball as its master.","And from her observations, it seemed more likely that it had chosen her as the master.","Because even though the rice ball had been by her side for so long, the little thing hadn't so much as glanced at it.","Sure enough, as He Zhiran continued observing, the little thing started fluttering its wings at her again.","Compared to how it acted with the rice ball, it was who knows how many times more gentle.","He Zhiran tentatively reached her hand towards the cage. The little thing became even more obedient.","Its snowy white body rubbed against the edge of the cage, as if inviting He Zhiran to pet it.","He Zhiran opened the cage according to the little thing's wishes.","The little thing immediately fluttered out and circled He Zhiran, chirping happily.","He Zhiran could now fully confirm it meant no harm to her, so she reached out her palm tentatively to pet it.","Seeing this, the little thing even leaned in towards her voluntarily.","He Zhiran stroked its head first, then slowly stroked its body.","The little thing seemed to love the feeling. It leaned towards her even more.","Taking the chance, He Zhiran slowly spread its wings open, wanting to take a look at the golden feathers inside.","The little thing cooperated fully, spreading its wings open for He Zhiran to see the single golden feather clearly.","In her past life, she had accidentally read a book mentioning a very rare snow sculpture. Its whole body was snowy white, but under its wings on both sides was one golden feather each.","People called this kind of snow sculpture the Golden Winged Roc.","But the Golden Winged Roc was massive in size. Even in its youth it couldn't be as small as the creature before her eyes.","To identify what the little thing was, He Zhiran decided to ask the little collector for help. She hoped he could search online in the modern world for her.","So she took out her phone and took photos of the little thing from every angle using Taobao's photo uploading function.","The photo function came with a valuation - and the valuation for the little thing shocked He Zhiran.","Taobao valued the little thing at over seven figures, which showed how precious it was.","He Zhiran didn't dwell too much on the creature's monetary value. What she lacked least right now was money. She would never sell the little thing for profit.","She opened up the chat with the little collector and sent the photos she just took.","[Hello, could you please help me identify what species this little thing is?]","Perhaps the little collector was busy. He Zhiran had to wait around ten minutes before she saw his avatar blink.","[I asked animal experts just now to help appraise the photos. This is a very rare type of eagle called the Golden-winged Sculpture.","These eagles look no different from pigeons normally. When faced with danger, they transform into giant rocs, with a golden feather under each wing.","The most unique part is their beak, which has two layers. The outer layer extends into an eagle's beak shape when carrying things or encountering danger.","According to experts, Golden-winged Sculptures are basically extinct in modern times. They only know about them from documents.]","Right after, the little collector said: [Don't tell me this Golden-winged Sculpture is in your hands?]","He Zhiran: [Yes, I do have one.]","Little collector: [I can buy it from you at a high price.]","He Zhiran: [I'm sorry, this Golden-winged Sculpture is very important to me, I can't sell it to you.]","Little collector: [Since that's the case, I won't insist.]","What He Zhiran cared about more right now were the Golden-winged Sculpture's special traits.","[Did you find out anything special about these Golden-winged Sculptures?]","Little collector: [The experts said Golden-winged Sculptures recognize masters. Don't let their small size fool you, their combat power is extremely strong. But without their master's orders, they won't act on their own.]","After the little collector's introduction, He Zhiran couldn't wait to test the Golden-winged Sculpture's ability to recognize masters.","As thanks, she listed a large diamond she bought from a foreigner.","The little collector's previously somewhat dejected mood was instantly replaced with joy at obtaining this large diamond.","Seeing that he was satisfied, He Zhiran closed the chat.","She turned around, held out her palm towards the Golden-winged Sculpture and beckoned.","Seeing her hand, the Golden-winged Sculpture fluttered its wings and jumped right on, chirping happily twice.","He Zhiran continued testing.","She pointed at the dried chili peppers hanging outside the warehouse and said, \"Little one, help me bring that over.\"","The Golden-winged Sculpture let out another cry, then quickly flew to the designated spot, picked up a dried chili pepper in its beak, and flew back.","As He Zhiran took the chili pepper, she also noticed the Golden-winged Sculpture's beak had turned into an eagle's.","But very quickly, the Golden-winged Sculpture's eagle beak retracted back.","He Zhiran could now confirm this little thing had accepted her as its master.","Although this little thing used to belong to Mr. Si Meng, now that it was hers, He Zhiran wouldn't fuss too much about a spiritual creature changing owners.","What worried her most now was whether the Golden-winged Sculpture, after being tamed by the rice ball as her pet, could still find its original master - that was uncertain.","To verify this, she tried communicating with the Golden-winged Sculpture.","\"Little one, can you still find your previous master?\"","The Golden-winged Sculpture just stood there blankly staring at her, clearly having no idea what she was expressing.","Now He Zhiran was completely stumped. She had hoped the little thing could lead her to find Mr. Si Meng, but now it seemed that if she let it out, it would only fly back to its new master, which was her."]},{"number":314,"title":"Chapter 314: Are you sure you can keep up with a very fast bird","paragraphs":["He Zhiran helplessly looked at the rice ball sitting to the side leisurely eating bamboo shoots.","\"Stinky rice ball, you have really made a terrible mistake.\"","When the rice ball saw that his master was complaining about him, his movements of eating bamboo shoots suddenly froze. He then looked at her blankly, appearing extremely aggrieved.","He Zhiran's heart instantly softened and the tone of her voice became much gentler.","\"Baby, this golden-winged sculpture is very important to me. I want to find its original owner through it. Now that you have tamed it, what should I do?\"","The rice ball's dark eyes rolled around. He got up and walked towards the golden-winged sculpture.","It was seen that the little guy gesticulated towards the golden-winged sculpture. The golden-winged sculpture once again became the same ruffled appearance as before.","Facing He Zhiran again, it no longer had the earlier fawning manner and had an appearance of avoiding strangers.","Soon, after the little thing took a few steps back, it flapped its wings and flew very high, wanting to get as far away as possible from the person and bear.","In the space, He Zhiran was not worried at all about losing the golden-winged sculpture. When needed, she only needed a thought to recall it.","Anyway, there was a lot of food in the space and there was no need to worry about the golden-winged sculpture starving to death.","As for using it to find clues about Mr. Si Meng, it would have to wait until Mo Jiuye came back to discuss and make a decision together.","...","He Zhiran looked at the time displayed on the clock in the infirmary. She had already been inside for several hours. She estimated that Mo Jiuye would be back soon too.","Therefore, after hugging the rice ball, she flashed out of the space.","Mo Jiuye returned earlier than she had expected. He had even sent those items and the palace maids serving Consort De to the haunted house.","Seeing He Zhiran come out from the space, he knew that she had gone in to check on the white dove.","Before he could ask, He Zhiran said first, \"Have you heard of the golden-winged sculpture?\"","Mo Jiuye didn't even need to think before answering, \"No.\"","He Zhiran explained the characteristics of the golden-winged sculpture in detail and told Mo Jiuye that it was not at all some white dove, but a very rare golden-winged sculpture.","No matter where his wife had learned this information from, Mo Jiuye's main goal was to find Mr. Si Meng through the golden-winged sculpture.","\"Ranran, let the golden-winged sculpture out. Will it go to find its original owner?\"","He Zhiran nodded, \"I think it should be like this. The loyalty of the golden-winged sculpture to its owner is extremely strong.\"","Since Mr. Si Meng's whereabouts were uncertain, only this golden-winged sculpture would likely be able to find him.","Mo Jiuye pondered deeply before saying, \"Ranran, I plan to prepare tomorrow and follow the golden-winged sculpture out to look for clues.\"","In fact, He Zhiran hadn't thought of a better way either.","Hoping that the golden-winged sculpture would find Mr. Si Meng was probably the only way out, as Mo Jiuye said.","It's just that she had just seen it in the space earlier that the flight speed of the golden-winged sculpture was especially fast. Even with Mo Jiuye's superb qinggong, his stamina probably could not compare with such a naturally flying animal.","\"Are you sure you can keep up with the speed of a bird that flies extremely fast?\"","Mo Jiuye also did not dare to fully guarantee this. His qinggong was not weak and was even considered one of the best in the Da Shun Dynasty.","It was just that people do get tired at times. If the golden-winged sculpture kept flying without stopping, he really might not be able to keep up.","If there were high mountains, big rivers and such, he might directly lose track of it.","After thinking it over, neither of them could come up with a good plan.","To put it bluntly, the most reliable approach would be to bring the golden-winged sculpture with them in July when they headed to the western border.","Because at that time, Mr. Si Meng would very likely appear there. Releasing the golden-winged sculpture within a fixed range, Mo Jiuye would definitely be able to keep up with its speed.","To play it safe, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye immediately decided that they could not recklessly let the golden-winged sculpture out. Once it got lost, this clue would be completely broken.","It seemed that even with this golden-winged sculpture in hand, they could not do anything in advance.","Third Brother had already taken people rushing to the western border. It was believed that it would not take long for them to bring back some news.","They could make a decision when that time came, so it would not be too late.","...","Time flew, and March arrived in the blink of an eye.","The weather in the northwest was much warmer than that of the north. The little ice and snow that was originally there had long since melted away.","Fourth Brother's surgery was very successful. Although he still could not walk with his legs, his hands that had their tendons reconnected could slowly move after the surgery.","This gave Fourth Brother hope. He looked forward every day to recovering sooner, as he could not be a cripple of the Mo family.","After recuperation, Seventh Brother's health had also basically recovered. Apart from still looking somewhat thin and frail, he had no obstacles at all to moving around.","Consort De's health had also recovered very well. Nan Rui indeed had no intention of returning to the capital.","He felt that though the Xi Ling Village place was a bit remote, it was a suitable place to recuperate.","Without having to face those deceitful things every day, as long as taking good care of Mother was alright, he had no rush to leave either and temporarily settled down in that haunted house for now.","When he had nothing to do, Nan Rui would also bring Consort De to walk around the Mo family.","Facing the Mo family brothers, he did not put on any airs at all. Seeing the Mo brothers busying about, he would also actively go over to help.","As for Consort De, she would go chat with Old Madam Mo.","The two were of similar ages and were once prominent family daughters, so they talked very happily.","There was another person who had been running over to the Mo family most diligently recently, and that was Meng Huaining.","He was slowly revealing his intentions in front of Old Madam Mo bit by bit.","Old Madam Mo had also vaguely revealed her own feelings. In short, this pair also had great progress.","He Zhiran was now over four months pregnant with twins. Because of this, her small belly was already bulging high and her figure had also become increasingly plump.","Fortunately, the two little ones took very good care of her and never made trouble. This made her pregnancy a lot more relaxed.","Seeing that there were still more than twenty days before it was time to start planting crops again when the farmers were free, they had to hurry and start working on the house at the foot of the mountain.","He Zhiran spent two days' time drawing house structure diagrams in the space.","If nothing unexpected happened, this place would be where they permanently lived in the future, so it definitely had to be built to be comfortable and practical.","Although there were many people in the family, they had always gotten along harmoniously without any intrigue happening between the women.","Even so, He Zhiran was a modern person after all and did not want to live the life of a big family.","This was also why she and Mo Jiuye had bought such a large piece of land in the first place.","Now they could basically confirm that Old Master Mo and the brothers in the family were all alive. It would be appropriate for the yard to have an area for each small family.","Calculating it this way, with two elders and nine brothers, they needed courtyards for at least ten units.","He Zhiran planned to build these ten courtyards all according to the pattern of traditional Chinese quadrangle courtyards from her previous life. After all, this was the countryside, so there was no need to differentiate between interior and exterior courtyards. As long as it was comfortable to live in, that was good.","Of course, the most important thing was the facilities and layout inside the rooms.","It was without doubt that glass would be used for all the windows. She had previously purchased a large amount of glass with Henry in the space, enough to use when building the new house.","There were also heating facilities inside the rooms.","After coming to the northwest, He Zhiran had chatted with surrounding villagers when free and asked around about their heating facilities for passing the winter. Most of them mainly used kang stove-beds, and those better-off families would also light up one or two braziers for heating."]},{"number":315,"title":"Chapter 315: We're going to build a yard like this at the foot of the mountain.","paragraphs":["Thinking of the radiators and geothermal energy in her previous life, He Zhiran felt they were more suitable for the winter here.","Not only beautiful, but also safe and clean.","It's just that the kind of person who could install floor heating was difficult for her to find.","She could only talk about some general principles. To really implement it, she still needed a knowledgeable person to do it.","There was also the indoor toilet and plumbing she designed, she could only talk about some of it. To really make it, she also needed a professional.","Just as He Zhiran was troubled by these difficulties, Mo Jiuye recommended someone to her.","This person was Hu Cong.","Hu Cong had lived in Xi Ling Village for some time, and felt more accustomed to the environment and local conditions here than the fishing village.","Not long ago, Meng Huaining had finished reviewing all the cases of the shipping company, and confiscated all the assets of the shipping company. As a result, Hu Cong also received a sum of compensation.","He bought a small courtyard in Xi Ling Village, and bought some acres of land. He had already planned to live here for the long term.","Mo Jiuye went to Hu Cong's house with He Zhiran. At this moment, Hu Cong was making something out of wood boards in the yard.","That thing was not yet fully formed, at first glance it looked a bit like a large syringe.","Seeing them coming, Hu Cong hurriedly got up to greet them.","\"Young Master Mo, what brings you here today.\"","Mo Jiuye had originally planned to get right to the point, but unexpectedly, He Zhiran bypassed him and picked up the wooden object Hu Cong was making to examine it.","At first glance, she had roughly guessed what it was for.","So she tentatively asked, \"Brother Hu, is this a seeding tool you're making?\"","Hu Cong didn't expect that the thing he had racked his brains over for several days, and hadn't even fully taken shape yet, He Zhiran was able to see its purpose at a glance.","He replied enthusiastically, \"It's indeed for sowing seeds. The seeds are placed inside, push the switch at the back, and a small amount of seeds inside will flow out. This will save a lot of manpower when sowing seeds.\"","In her previous life, although He Zhiran had seen farmers sowing seeds, it was already a very technologically advanced era at that time. The farming tools people used were basically fully automated.","Although such manual farm tools were rare, some older generations still used them.","Therefore, similar objects were something He Zhiran had seen before. They were more delicate and convenient than the ones Hu Cong designed.","So she pointed to the seeder Hu Cong had just made and said, \"Brother Hu, look here, if the holes were a little smaller, even fewer seeds would be lost, saving a lot more.","Also here, you can install something to help provide power, which will save even more effort.","And...\"","He Zhiran made several suggestions for improvement in a row, and Hu Cong's eyes got brighter and brighter as he listened.","\"Young Lady, I didn't think of what you said. I'll modify it according to your method later. I believe the improved seeder will definitely be more useful.\"","If Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran weren't there, Hu Cong would have wanted to get started immediately.","He Zhiran only understood some principles. The improvement methods she gave Hu Cong still required him to figure out how to implement them.","She could also see that Hu Cong was eager to improve the seeder, so as not to waste his time, she signaled Mo Jiuye to take out the drawings she had made for him to see.","Seeing Mo Jiuye take out some sheets of paper from his arms, Hu Cong asked in surprise, \"Young Master, what is this?\"","Mo Jiuye spread out a layout drawing of a courtyard for Hu Cong to see.","\"Brother Hu, take a look. This is a layout my wife drew of the courtyard. We plan to build such a courtyard at the foot of the mountain.\"","Hu Cong was no stranger to building courtyards. When he was in the capital, many prominent families needed to build some special structures, and they would ask him for advice.","Hearing that it was a layout of the courtyard, Hu Cong took it over.","The drawing appeared before his eyes, giving Hu Cong another big surprise.","He had no other hobbies in his life, only liking to study some things he had never seen before, such as some tools, or housing construction, and so on...","The courtyard He Zhiran drew first attracted Hu Cong's attention in terms of structure.","Not to mention the details, just looking at the structure of the house, it not only saved land, but was also very practical. Such a courtyard, in Hu Cong's eyes, was very suitable for a family to live in.","\"Young Master, may I ask which expert designed such a courtyard?\"","Even the drawing skills amazed Hu Cong.","In fact, He Zhiran's drawing skills weren't that great either. She wasn't used to using the ancient brush, so when drawing the drawings, she bought pencils on Taobao.","This would not arouse anyone's suspicion either. She could simply say that she sharpened charcoal to draw with.","As for some drafting tools, they also came from Taobao. With so many handy tools, the effect was naturally better than the ancient people using soft brushes.","Seeing that his wife's drawings were approved by Hu Cong, Mo Jiuye inexplicably felt a sense of pride rise up.","First he looked at his wife, then said, \"It was conceived by my wife.\"","Hu Cong had just looked up to He Zhiran for pointing out improvements to his seeder making.","Now Mo Jiuye said the drawings were also from this young lady's hand.","Hu Cong instantly developed a heart of admiration.","It seems the saying that there are people beyond people and heavens beyond heavens is not false at all. If Lady Mo wasn't a daughter, just her talents, how many good men would she surpass?","After admiring for a while, Hu Cong continued to look at the details on the drawings.","He Zhiran had indeed added details of the rooms when making the drawings.","Such as the cesspool in the backyard, the plumbing in the rooms, as well as the floor heating, etc.","No matter how smart Hu Cong was, he wouldn't recognize these things that he hadn't even thought of.","After looking for a while, he still didn't understand what these were.","\"May I ask Lady Mo, this looks like a deep pit, what is it for?\"","He Zhiran looked at where he was pointing, it was the cesspool she had designed in the backyard, farthest from the house.","Speaking of cesspools, it started with the indoor plumbing and flushing toilets.","He Zhiran pointed to the locations of the bathrooms and kitchens in the rooms, and carefully explained the principles she knew to Hu Cong.","At first, Hu Cong didn't quite understand having a toilet inside the house. Later, after listening to He Zhiran's detailed explanation, he felt this in-house toilet design was simply perfect.","He Zhiran had only talked about the structure connecting the toilet to the cesspool, and hadn't gone into the details yet.","Even so, it had already piqued Hu Cong's great interest.","He slowly digested the principles explained by He Zhiran, and continued to ask about other things.","He Zhiran also explained the principles of floor heating, plumbing and other pipelines. Hu Cong listened like an attentive student, with a level of concentration that couldn't be described in words.","Not only that, he also had the potential to ask when he didn't understand. Any parts he didn't get, he would ask over and over again."]},{"number":316,"title":"Chapter 316: You Can Take your Time.","paragraphs":["Just a layout diagram of a siheyuan piqued Hu Cong's interest entirely.","He stared at the blueprint in his hand, increasingly lamenting his own inferiority.","He really didn't know how this woman came up with such ideas. If he hadn't had the good fortune to see this blueprint, he might not have known in his whole life that houses could be built like this, with such convenient and practical facilities inside.","After pondering for a long time, Hu Cong awkwardly opened his mouth to ask Mo Jiuye, \"Young Master Mo, do you know if you have found a good craftsman to build this courtyard?\"","This was something Mo Jiuye should have taken the initiative to mention, but Hu Cong beat him to it.","However, knowing Hu Cong as he did, it was not at all strange for him to do something like this.","\"I came to find Brother Hu because I want you to be the general contractor for the construction of this courtyard. What does Brother Hu think?\"","When Hu Cong heard this, he couldn't hide the delight on his face at all.","He didn't even hesitate for a moment, just kept nodding his head.","\"Good, good, good! As long as Young Master Mo trusts me, I am willing to be the general contractor for the construction of this building.\"","The general contractor was the master craftsman of this era, responsible for the overall structure and supervision of the construction.","In Da Shun, there weren't many people with such abilities.","Hu Cong was one of them. When he was in the capital city, those officials and nobles felt honored to be able to hire him as the general contractor for their family constructions.","It was just a pity that Hu Cong was stubborn and inflexible. For any house he built for others, it had to be a structure that he was satisfied with himself, otherwise he would not agree to it.","As a result, he had offended many people of power in the capital city.","Now it was very obvious that even if Mo Jiuye didn't say it outright, he would take the initiative to participate in the Mo family's housing construction.","It could be said that this was the first time in Hu Cong's life that he had taken such initiative.","Seeing that Hu Cong agreed, Mo Jiuye was also very happy. After all, he understood Hu Cong's reputation in the construction industry of the capital city.","He quickly handed over all the design drawings to Hu Cong.","\"Brother Hu, take a look at these details drawn by my wife.\"","Hu Cong nodded and took over the drawings. The first one was a detailed drawing of a flush toilet.","When He Zhiran was explaining it to him earlier, he had already started thinking in his mind what a flush toilet should look like.","Now, seeing such a vivid design drawing, Hu Cong suddenly felt enlightened.","How could he not have thought of that? A flush toilet could be built like this - it was simply perfect.","The materials used for the floor heating were all made of iron pipes, and the connections between the iron pipes, as well as the thing called a faucet, were ingeniously designed.","In short, these design drawings could be said to open a new door again for Hu Cong's attainments in the construction industry.","The more he looked at these drawings, the more enthusiastic he became, to the point where he had ignored the two people next to him completely.","Seeing this, Mo Jiuye laughed and said, \"Brother Hu, just keep the drawings here and you can study them slowly.\"","Hearing his voice, Hu Cong realized that he had been rude.","\"I'm sorry, Young Master Mo. When I see something fresh, I can't take my eyes off of it. I hope you and Young Mistress Mo won't take offense.\"","\"No problem at all. Brother Hu, since you've agreed to be the general contractor for our Mo family's building, there are still many details that we need to make clear in advance.\"","He Zhiran was not at all worried that such architectural methods would leak out at all.","In her heart, these were all things created by the wisdom of future people for the purpose of making people's lives better.","Although she had brought such good things to Da Shun ahead of time, she never selfishly thought that they were her things.","Her purpose was simple - as long as her family lived comfortably.","As for when these architectural structures would leak out, she wouldn't care at all. Whoever had the ability to build them out could go build them.","What she wanted to discuss with Hu Cong was the remuneration for hiring him as general contractor.","\"Brother Hu, as long as you build ten courtyards with the same design as the drawings for me, it would be even better if you can contact the porcelain kilns and blacksmiths to produce ceramic toilets and iron pipes. Of course, I won't let Brother Hu work hard for nothing, I will definitely pay you more.\"","Money and the like was never lacking for He Zhiran. As long as Hu Cong did a good job, giving him ten thousand taels would not be a problem at all.","Hu Cong's willingness to undertake the Mo family's housing construction had nothing to do with remuneration.","He simply wanted to take on the challenge of building such an odd courtyard design for the first time.","\"The remuneration doesn’t matter at all. I’m quite familiar with the blacksmiths in the city, and can help contact them to produce those iron pipes and hardware. As for ceramics, I’ve heard there’s a porcelain kiln on the east side of Yun City, so I can also go over there to inquire.\"","\"The only requirement I have is that all the laborers for the construction must listen to my arrangements alone. Of course, if the young master and mistress Mo are dissatisfied with anything, feel free to let me know.”","Mo Jiuye already had some understanding of Hu Cong’s requirements when building houses for others, even if Hu Cong didn’t mention it outright.","Back when Hu Cong was in the capital city, he had a construction team under him. Whenever he went to build houses for officials and nobles, he would bring those people along.","It was said that those people only listened to Hu Cong's arrangements.","If He Zhiran had to summarize his way of working, she could describe it using the modern term \"contractor\".","The employer would contract the project to him at a fixed price, and after Hu Cong finished building the house, the employer only needed to come inspect it.","This was very beneficial for both parties. For example, the employer didn't have to watch over things all day, only needing to come take occasional looks. This saved a lot of time.","As for Hu Cong, there was no need to elaborate - not only could he earn more profits, the most important thing was that the workers all listened to his arrangements. Those who did well could stay, those who didn’t could be dismissed with one sentence from him.","With this level of control, those workers would also be more diligent, saving him a lot of trouble as well.","This was simply a win-win situation.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye had no objections to this whatsoever.","Many construction materials had already been stockpiled at home during the winter. What remained for Hu Cong to worry about were those novel gadgets in He Zhiran’s drawings.","At present, the two parties only needed to negotiate the price.","\"Brother Hu, it's not the same as the capital city here in the northwest. The people you once trained can't come here to work, so we can only ask the nearby villagers to help with the construction.\"","Hu Cong nodded. \"That's true.\"","His requirements weren’t high. He only hoped that these people would fully listen to his commands.","Mo Jiuye went on, \"When the time comes, I will explain things clearly to the hired laborers beforehand and have them all listen to your directions. As for the issue of wages, Brother Hu can first take a look at the drawings for the things needed and the complexity of the project, then let me know after considering it carefully.\"","With this said, what else did Hu Cong not understand?","Mo Jiuye understood his usual way of building houses for others back in the capital city, and likewise chose to hire him in the same fashion here in the northwest.","The two parties only needed to negotiate the price now."]},{"number":317,"title":"Chapter 317: Your Satisfaction is guaranteed.","paragraphs":["Hu Cong felt very comforted in his heart.","He actually understood the truth that times change.","Now in the northwest, no one would appreciate his skills like they used to in the past. Perhaps only the Mo family would.","Especially He Zhiran's design drawings, he was very interested. If he didn't take the lead and participate in the construction, he would probably regret it for the rest of his life.","Therefore, even if Mo Jiuye did not agree to give all the projects to him, he would still choose to participate.","It's just that he might feel a little uncomfortable in his heart.","After settling the matter, the two talked with Hu Cong about some details.","He Zhiran was also very wealthy. She directly gave Hu Cong 10,000 taels of silver bills. For ordinary commoners, this was definitely an unimaginable number.","For the current Hu Cong, it could also be described as an astronomical figure.","After all, he had been exiled to the northwest, and usually he could only rely on his skills to earn some money to make ends meet.","Although this money was not completely for him, for the current Hu Cong, it was still a huge sum.","When Hu Cong received so much silver, he was indeed a little stunned.","\"Ninth Lady, what is this for?\"","He Zhiran explained with a smile, \"Since I have entrusted the whole matter of building the house to Elder Brother Hu, I won't interfere in anything anymore. In the future, some of the materials needed will also have to be taken care of by Elder Brother Hu personally, so the silver also includes some purchases of materials and labor.\"","Of course, before coming to find Hu Cong, He Zhiran had initially calculated the cost.","The cost of labor was very cheap in this era. For labor-intensive work like building a house, it only cost fifteen to twenty wen a day.","Their family was building ten yards, which was not a small project, and certainly required a lot of manpower.","If they could recruit a hundred people to work every day, with the highest price of twenty wen per day, the labor cost would only be two taels of silver per day.","The bricks, tiles and wood they needed had already been prepared before the New Year, and the number of porcelain toilets needed was not very large either. One hundred taels of silver would be enough.","The only thing that might be more expensive was the iron pipes used for floor heating. Ancient materials were scarce, and not much iron ore was mined and often controlled by the court. Therefore, the price of iron was relatively high.","Even so, it was estimated that a few thousand taels would be enough.","The remaining miscellaneous items would not cost much silver at all.","If Hu Cong could plan these expenses well and help the Mo family build the house, he could earn at least four thousand taels.","Since He Zhiran was able to calculate it clearly, Hu Cong, as a professional, could naturally calculate it even more clearly.","\"Since that's the case, I won't stand on ceremony. I will definitely do my best to complete the Mo family's house and ensure your satisfaction.\"","\"Good. Elder Brother Hu can start preparing in the next few days. As for the labor, you can discuss it with the village heads of the surrounding villages.\"","With the labor of Xiling Village alone, it would definitely not be enough, not to mention that many young and strong laborers could not come out to work when it was time for the spring plowing.","Contacting people from several villages would definitely find some families with more adult men who would be willing to come out and work for money.","\"Okay, leave these things to me.\"","Hu Cong thought the same way. As long as there was silver, there would be no worry about not being able to hire people.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye knew that Hu Cong was eager to study her design drawings, so after finishing the discussion, they bid farewell and left.","Now, the matter of building the house in the family was handed over to Hu Cong to handle, which also relieved them a lot. They could focus on preparing for the spring plowing.","Hu Cong acted quickly. He locked himself in the room for two days and thoroughly studied He Zhiran's drawings.","He first contacted the porcelain kiln to produce the toilet bowls, and then contacted several iron shops in Yuncheng to produce the iron pipes for floor heating.","After all these things were arranged, he went to find the village heads of the surrounding villages to hire people to help build the houses.","Although it was about to be the spring plowing season, as He Zhiran had expected, families with more manpower were indeed willing to spare one or two to come out and work.","After all, few people were willing to give up this kind of work to earn money on the spot.","On He Zhiran's side, she was equally busy.","In the past few days, she and Mo Jiuye rented a large yard not far from the pier in Yuncheng.","She stored all the fruit trees cultivated in advance in the space there.","The plants or seeds produced in the space were not particular about soil and climate. Therefore, the varieties of fruit trees she had prepared were very complete.","There were apples, tangerines, oranges, honey peaches, cherries, and even tropical mangoes and durians.","In short, everything she could think of was prepared.","With so many varieties and quantities of fruit trees, a lot of manpower would be needed as well.","The manpower of Xiling Village and surrounding villages was helping their own family build houses, which did not stump Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran at all.","The two asked Meng Huaining for help to find some labor in the city.","The common people living in Yuncheng had no farmland, so there was no busy farming season.","Moreover, the wages He Zhiran paid were also very high, thirty wen per person per day. Even for doing work in the city, it was not so much.","Meng Huaining sent people to spread the news, and many people scrambled to sign up.","Even if it was just a little thing for the Mo family, Meng Huaining did not dare to be sloppy at all.","He specifically sent all his subordinates to find out about the temperament of those who signed up. Those who were slippery were ruled out without exception.","After careful selection, he finally helped the Mo family hire one hundred people.","That large tract of mountain, He Zhiran planned to plant all kinds of fruit trees, so the project was naturally not small.","The hired people first transported the fruit trees from that yard in Yuncheng to Xiling Village, and then carried out the planting.","So, after busy working for ten days, these fruit trees were completely planted.","Now on the hillside, it no longer looked as messy as before, but neat rows of various fruit trees.","The pear blossoms and peach blossoms had bloomed one after another, bringing a different beauty to the mountain.","Of course, after the Mo family planted so many fruits trees that villagers had never seen before on the mountain, it naturally aroused a lot of discussion among the villagers.","Even the Mo family themselves were a little puzzled at first.","When He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye were doing this, they had already figured out an excuse.","The reason why they rented a yard close to the pier was to continue using the foreigners as scapegoats.","Although this excuse was a bit shabby, it was still better than being asked questions they couldn't answer properly."]},{"number":318,"title":"Chapter 318: Everyday (Part 1)","paragraphs":["The villagers of Xi Ling Village would often go down to the foot of the mountain to watch from time to time.","They were very law-abiding, knowing that piece of mountain had already been bought by the Mo Family, and would not rashly go up.","They just wanted to see what flowers could bloom in this season.","At the same time, they would also gather in groups of three or two, saying that the Mo Family was not in vain as nobles from the Capital city, spending so much silver to buy a piece of mountain, and it turned out to be for planting trees.","After all, they did not recognize these fruit trees, thinking they were just some special trees that could bloom...","He Zhiran did not care about the thoughts of those villagers. She and Mo Jiuye had already started preparing for the spring plowing.","Of course, she could only make suggestions and move her mouth now.","Mo Jiuye was always around her, not allowing her to have too much movement.","The neglected land had been cleared once before the frozen soil, and now it only needed to be plowed to plant.","The rabbits raised at home were increasing day by day. In addition to being busy making cold rabbit dishes every day to supply Tang Mingrui, the sisters-in-law were making doll pendants.","Lan Er and Yu Er also quickly integrated into the Mo Family's life.","They competed with each other to do housework every day, and in their spare time they would go to help Mo Hanyue take care of those pet rabbits.","There was a lot of work, and the Mo Family women couldn't keep up. They would give some of it to the women of the Xie Family and Fang Family to do together, still paying them wages according to their work, just like when making dolls.","Therefore, they really couldn't help with the farm work.","Eighth Brother had to go to the yamen every day, and Third Older Brother took Liang Hao and the others to the western border and had not returned yet.","Although Seventh Elder Brother's health had improved a lot, his strength was still not as good as that of his other brothers.","According to He Zhiran's intention, he had to recuperate for at least a few more months.","Sixth elder brother's body was basically free of impediments, and he followed Mo Jiuye and Fifth Elder Brother every day, busy with odd jobs, completely living the life of a farmer.","Such a life was not unfamiliar to the Mo family at all.","Doing things with their own hands and having adequate food and clothing every day, although it was more tiring, being together as a family made them feel more fulfilled.","The laborers Meng Huaining helped find in Yun City came in handy after finishing planting the fruit trees.","Although they were not as familiar with farming as those countrymen, who would begrudge the daily wage of thirty wen, in order not to displease their employer, they worked very hard.","He Zhiran, with her big belly, was not allowed by Mo Jiuye to work hard, so she could only tell him some methods and let him direct those people to do it.","The spring ploughing on the Mo Family's side went on vigorously.","When those indigenous villagers of Xi Ling Village saw them planting some crops they had never seen before, some kind people came to advise Mo Jiuye.","For example, the new Village Chief Zhao.","He pulled Mo Jiuye and earnestly said, \"Ninth Brother, at worst I have been farming for half my life. Our land in the northwest is barren, and the climate is bad too. Not everything planted will be productive.","I can see that the Mo Family is not lacking in silver, but with so much land under cultivation, there should at least be some harvest in the autumn.\"","Mo Jiuye knew that Village Chief Zhao meant well for his own family.","\"Village Chief Zhao, don't worry. My wife and I have asked carefully about these seeds, there is no problem planting them here at all.","Moreover, these seeds are high-yielding seeds, and the yield will definitely be considerable in the autumn harvest.\"","When they first came to Xi Ling Village, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran felt that the Zhou family and Zhao family were pretty good. Since they lived in the same village, they naturally wouldn't hide any good seeds they had.","But if people didn't recognize stuff, they didn't have to be eager to recommend it.","Whether it was good or bad had to be proven by the facts and yield.","Seeing that his words were completely unheeded, Village Chief Zhao could only sigh and say, \"If that's the case, just try it!\"","What else could he say? It was others' land, they could plant whatever they wanted, he was just giving a kind reminder, and there was nothing he could do if they didn't listen.","After Village Chief Zhao left, Xie Tianhai and Fang Chuanzhou came together by appointment.","In order to make a living, the two found a private school in Yun City to work as teachers, so they rarely appeared in the village on weekdays.","If it wasn't the spring ploughing season when the private school gave them a few days off, they wouldn't have come to find Mo Jiuye at this time either.","From their understanding of Mo Jiuye, they were very clear in their hearts that the Mo Family would never do anything without certainty.","Just like the problem Village Chief Zhao was worried about just now.","In Fang Chuanzhou and Xie Tianhai's view, no matter how rare the things planted by the Mo Family were, there would be no problems.","Just as they said themselves, they were all high-yielding crops, and the yield would be very high.","Therefore, the reason Xie Tianhai and Fang Chuanzhou came to find Mo Jiuye today was that they wanted to ask for some seeds.","Xie Tianhai was a relative of the Mo Family, so it was easier for him to speak up.","\"Ninth Brother, we were thinking of buying some of these high-yielding seeds from you, what do you think?\"","Xie Tianhai had also followed the local customs, calling Mo Jiuye \"Ninth Brother\" like the villagers.","He didn't hold back with the villagers, let alone the Xie Family and Fang Family.","\"No problem, my wife said that currently the high-yielding seeds available are corn, sweet potatoes and potatoes. Which do you plan to plant?\"","Anyway, his wife's space-produced seeds were not picky about seasons, and could be planted together without any problem.","Xie Tianhai and Fang Chuanzhou had tasted all three items at the Mo Family.","In their hearts, these were all good things, especially potatoes, the stir-fried dishes tasted extremely good.","\"If possible, I'd like to buy some seeds of all three from you.\"","As for the price, Xie Tianhai and Fang Chuanzhou didn't think too much about it.","Now both their families had income, and it was no longer the time when they lacked silver. They had heard that the Mo Family's seeds were all obtained from foreigners, so the price would naturally not be too low.","It didn't matter if the seed prices were a little higher. If the yield went up, what was there to worry about losing money?","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran thought the same way, they could help people who had good relations with their family, but they couldn't help without a bottom line.","For example, these seeds basically cost them nothing, but they couldn't give them away for free.","The price was also discussed in advance between him and his wife.","\"Uncles, we still have surplus seeds at home. The price of corn seeds is 50 wen per jin.","Sweet potatoes and potatoes are 25 wen per jin.\"","Hearing the prices Mo Jiuye quoted, Xie Tianhai and Fang Chuanzhou both felt a little embarrassed.","Even if they didn't understand business, they knew that things bought from foreigners would not be cheap.","The prices the other party quoted now were probably at the expense of their own profits to take care of them.","\"Ninth Brother, you selling us seeds is good enough already, don't lose money to accommodate us!\"","The seed prices Mo Jiuye reported were indeed not high, but they were still much higher than the cost price. He smiled and explained, \"I bought a lot at the time, so the price is cheaper without losing money. Uncles can go home and get whatever you need.\""]},{"number":319,"title":"Chapter 319: Everyday (Part 2)","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran saw that they were not just bragging. Only then did the two feel relieved.","Even so, they were sincerely grateful.","Seeds so precious and unavailable in Dashun were given to them without profit. This was an enormous favor.","\"Alright, alright. I'll take my family to get the seeds in a bit. We'll remember this favor, uncle.\"","Fang Chuanzhou also said, \"Yes, I also represent the Fang family to thank you.\"","Mo Jiuye did not care whether they expressed gratitude or not. Good seeds from his wife's space could bring the commoners a life of food and clothing. It was also accumulating blessings for their unborn children.","Moreover, he and He Zhiran were not lacking in money. Even if they did nothing in the northwest, they had enough money to last several lifetimes.","After some polite conversation, Mo Jiuye sent the two men away and went with the hired laborers to demarcate the planting areas.","Although their farmland was substantial, they grew many types of crops.","Xi Ling Village had no paddy fields. Other than rice, any economically valuable, delicious grain or vegetable was planted.","Especially chili peppers - unavailable in this period. Chili peppers could be used to cook many delicacies, so they had to plant a lot.","Thus, the Mo family planted 20 mu of just chili peppers this year.","For other crops, the focus was still grain. Of course, they grew a complete variety.","At this time, Mo Hanyue was not idle either. During breaks from raising pet rabbits, she read the pharmaceutical books He Zhiran gave her many times.","Recently, He Zhiran helped exchange one-year medicinal plant seeds for her on the interface.","The little girl got up before dawn every day. She asked for 3 mu of family land to reclaim her own medicine field.","She did not need family help. She would cultivate this medicine field completely by herself.","Because sister-in-law said that to grow medicinal materials well required getting one’s hands dirty. Only this way could she quickly understand the growth habits of these herbs.","In fact, these medicinal seeds all came from the space. They did not need much care at all. He Zhiran deliberately made Mo Hanyue work hard to temper her endurance but did not say so outright.","The young miss was good in every way, just a little pampered.","He Zhiran hoped Mo Hanyue would become tougher through the hard work of cultivating the medicine field.","Her good intentions did not escape old Lady Mo. In Beijing, the family had only one daughter who had been spoiled beyond recognition.","But now things were different. The entire family had been exiled and gone through so many hardships and dangers on the way that survival was a blessing in itself, let alone living the pampered life of a young miss!","Thus, old Lady Mo highly approved of He Zhiran’s approach. Even though she felt bad that her daughter worked hard every day, she showed no intention of helping.","Initially, Mo Hanyue cried from exhaustion, but she persisted.","By the time the family farmland was finished planting, her medicine field was also fully cultivated.","Through this effort, she also tasted the sweetness of success.","The Mo family's land was vast and they hired many laborers, so their planting progress was even faster than other families in the village.","After the busy spring planting, there were only crops to maintain, which was not urgent. They could ask fellow villagers for help later and just pay them some fees. The family themselves only needed to provide little support.","In the mountain cave, the former subordinates were still cared for every day by Fifth Elder Brother and Sixth elder brother. After a period of recuperation, although their health had not recovered to initial levels, they could move freely again.","They wanted to stay here and live with the Mo family, but also missed families back home.","Today, they asked to return home for a visit. If possible, they would bring their families here to live together.","Of course, like the Mo family's other sons, they did not want the court to know they were alive.","With such an incompetent emperor, they never wanted to protect him again in this life.","If not for Mo Jiuye rescuing them from southern borderlands, they would have lived like walking corpses for the rest of their lives, or even perished under enemy abuse until their bodies were mangled mess.","They hated Mr. Si Meng for turning them into medicine men, and hated Emperor Shunwu more.","Because Mo Jiuye told them that after news of their deaths in battle reached Beijing, Emperor Shunwu not only failed to provide for their families, but even accused the incompetent in court.","If Duke Mo's Family had not secretly sent money to support them, they dared not imagine how difficult life would have been.","Thinking of this, the men would be filled with righteous indignation and miss families more strongly.","Mo Chongyuan could understand the feelings of these officers and men. At first, when he recovered his memories and connected these events, he also felt equally outraged and aggrieved.","With so many people returning home, road expenses would inevitably be high. Moreover, they had been away from home for years and were returning from the dead. They couldn’t just show up empty-handed.","His younger brother gave family money every month.","Although he and his wife had saved up some private money, funding these people's travel expenses was a drop in the bucket.","Helpless, Mo Chongyuan could only discuss with Mo Jiuye. He had no choice since he, the elder brother, was useless and could not earn enough money.","When he found Mo Jiuye, he was arranging to build a large rabbit shed with people.","Additionally, He Zhiran had bred large quantities of poultry and livestock in her space. They required housing too.","The family had plenty of wasteland, not all of which was reclaimed yet. He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye had discussed reserving these lands for building rabbit sheds and other uses.","Of course, rabbit raising was presently the most mature family business, so building rabbit sheds was given top priority.","The location chosen for the rabbit shed was at the mountain base. That area of land was used to build farms.","This was a properly designed rabbit shed by He Zhiran.","The brick and tile rabbit shed was divided into large compartments. The cages were neatly arranged around four sides.","Future rabbits in the shed would be classified by size, variety, etc.","The rabbit shed occupied a large area. It looked like no small project. The advantage lay in ease of construction. Anyone basically familiar with housing procedures could complete it.","When the Mo family got busy, it was a month, and now late April. The weather was getting warmer.","Fruit trees on the mountain had completely taken root. Because they were space products, they thrived regardless of soil or climate. All fruit trees displayed vigorous vitality.","Their growth was as good as mature fruit trees in the space. Come autumn, there would be a steady crop of various fruits.","Field crops were similar. After the busy spring planting, Xi Ling villagers no longer as busy as before and looked to work for the Mo family to earn some money."]},{"number":320,"title":"Chapter 320: This time I will make your Mohism never turn over.","paragraphs":["The Mo Family was building houses where Hu Cong was in charge. Now that the foundations of the houses had taken shape, the busiest time had passed.","Although Hu Cong wanted to take care of these villagers as well, there was no shortage of manpower. If he used people from Xi Ling Village, others would lose the chance to work.","Therefore, Hu Cong was in a very difficult position.","How could Mo Jiuye let him be in such a difficult position?","The Mo Family's farms happened to need more workers too.","After discussing with the patriarchs of both families, 20 people from each family came to help with the work. The wages remained 30 wen per day.","With such high wages compared to building houses, the Zhao and Zhou families knew the Mo Family was taking care of them. Therefore, they would definitely work hard for the Mo Family.","As for the Cui Family, without Cui Wen's support, many people had entered the academy. Those remaining in the family were basically useless.","When they heard that the Zhao and Zhou families were helping the Mo Family farm, not only did they not have to leave the village, but could also earn high wages, they became very jealous.","Apart from the 30 wen they could earn per day, if not for the Mo Family, their backer, the Cui Family, would not have fallen either.","Anyone could see that the new County prefect had a good relationship with the Mo Family. If not for the Mo Family, he would not have driven the Cui Family to desperation.","Now, their backbone was gone, most of their good farmland had been sold, and all they had left was a small piece of land and a worthless courtyard.","This year had just begun, yet some of them were already going hungry.","The more the Cui Family people thought about it, the more upset they became. So they gathered to discuss how to make trouble for the Mo Family.","They were not stupid. They knew it was useless to ask the Mo Family for work. So they gave up on that idea.","But they could not swallow this anger.","After discussing back and forth, they finally decided on the best approach - they would stop at nothing to cause trouble for the Mo Family!","Humph! So what if the Mo Family was close with the County prefect?","So what if they had a catcher at home?","I will make sure the Mo Family can never recover this time...","The next day at noon, a Cui Family man who looked extremely honest mixed among the workers building houses for the Mo Family.","The Zhao and Zhou family members were helping the Mo Family farm. They did not recognize this person, so they would definitely think he was a newcomer.","Helping the Mo Family had another benefit - free lunch.","The Cui Family man sneaked to the temporarily erected stove and added a package of white powder into the pot when no one was paying attention.","He thought he was flawless, but was caught red-handed by Mo Jiuye who had not come to check the progress of the house construction for a long time.","Mo Jiuye had just come over when he saw someone sneaking behind those workers.","He originally came because he heard the flush toilet was installed and wanted to take a look. But he discovered something wrong instead.","Unfortunately, he was some distance away. Not wanting to reveal his lightness skill before these commoners, he could only quicken his steps like an ordinary person. So he was a step late in stopping it.","Even so, there was no way for the Cui Family poisoner to escape.","Seeing that man try to leave after doing the dirty deed, Mo Jiuye dashed forward and grabbed his collar.","\"Who are you?\"","The Cui Family man was afraid of getting caught. Being grabbed, his whole body shivered in fear.","He turned his head and saw Mo Jiuye's eyes as cold as frost, staring at him closely.","\"Mo... Mo Jiu, what do you want to do?\"","Mo Jiuye smiled instead of getting angry, \"I want to ask what you wanted to do.\"","The Cui Family man would not admit that he came to poison them.","He struggled hard to break free, but how could his strength match Mo Jiuye's?","The more he struggled, the greater the strength on his collar. Eventually, he gave up.","\"Don't get me wrong. We are from the same village. I just wanted to help since your family is building houses and pays such high wages. Who wouldn't be envious?\"","Of course Mo Jiuye did not believe this lame excuse.","He probably did not even believe it himself.","Mo Jiuye was too lazy to quibble with this kind of person. Still holding onto his collar, he brought the Cui Family man to where there were more people.","Hu Cong had just finished arranging the tasks at hand when he saw Mo Jiuye bringing over an extremely unfamiliar man.","He went up and asked, \"Young Master Mo Jiu, who is this?\"","Mo Jiuye snorted coldly and threw the Cui Family man on the ground. \"This man added something to the hot soup. I caught him red-handed.\"","Hu Cong was shocked to hear this. In Beijing, it was nothing unusual for powerful households to resort to poisoning.","But in such an infertile place like the Northwest, and looking at this man dressed like an ordinary farmer, how could he have such nasty thoughts?","There were over a hundred workers building houses here. If that was some potent poison, it would be over a hundred lives!","The more Hu Cong thought about it, even the usually gentle man could not help but kick the Cui Family man a few times.","\"Speak! Who exactly are you? Why did you try to poison us‍?\"","Seeing no way to escape, the Cui Family man could only try to defend himself.","\"I did not poison anyone. I really just wanted to help. With the high wages your Mo Family pays, who wouldn't be envious?\"","He had to admit, his words sounded quite reasonable. If Mo Jiuye did not catch him red-handed, some might actually believe him.","Mo Jiuye had no time to quibble with such a person. He called over some workers to bring the poisoned soup over, then told Hu Cong, \"Big brother Hu, please arrange for the lunch to be remade. I'll bring this man to the yamen now.\"","For someone raised in an official's household since childhood, the first thought when encountering issues was to find the authorities to resolve it.","Especially since they wanted to live safely in the Northwest, they had to do things properly in front of outsiders.","Hu Cong acted decisively. Since such a big incident happened under his watch, he had to pay attention to it.","Soon, Mo Jiuye brought over the family carriage, together with Fifth Elder Brother.","Fifth Elder Brother used a small porcelain bottle to hold some of the poisoned soup, while Mo Jiuye tied up the Cui Family man and threw him onto the carriage.","He Zhi Ran also found out about the incident at home. Knowing Mo Jiuye could handle things properly at the yamen, she gave up on following along.","And even if she wanted to watch the excitement, her clingy husband who stared at her all day not to wander around would definitely not agree.","Many Cui Family members were poking their heads out at their doorways, looking towards the foot of the hill, wondering why the person they sent to poison had been gone for so long without returning - could something have happened unexpectedly?","Just as the Cui Family people were distracted, they saw the Mo Family carriage racing towards the village entrance."]},{"number":321,"title":"Chapter 321: Trial of Poisoning Cases","paragraphs":["The Cui family people looked at each other, and a bad premonition arose in their hearts.","The clan elder looked around at everyone behind him and called over a teenager, telling him to go down the hill on the pretext of chopping firewood and take a look.","Of course, the news they would get would surely make the Cui family people even more worried.","...","Mo Jiuye and Fifth Elder Brother drove the carriage and soon arrived at the county government.","They happened to run into Mo Chuhan who had just finished lunch and was taking people out on business.","Seeing his brothers come at this time, Mo Chuhan instinctively felt something was up.","\"Fifth Elder Brother, Ninth Younger Brother, why are you here at this time?\"","Mo Jiuye was the first to jump off the carriage. Without saying a word, he dragged the Cui family member who had poisoned the soup out of the carriage and threw him heavily on the ground.","\"Eighth Elder Brother, this is a Cui family member. He actually dared to put poison in the workers' soup!\"","When Mo Chuhan heard this, he was also furious. He walked over and kicked Cui Xing viciously.","\"You really are shamelessly audacious. Do you know what crime poisoning is? Severely, it's punishable by death.\"","This kick landed right on Cui Xing's waist. It was no light kick. Cui Xing yelped in pain.","The clerks who were following Mo Chuhan also heard the brothers' conversation. Very cleverly, they came over, picked Cui Xing up, and walked towards the yamen.","Someone shouted, \"Go invite the magistrate to hold court and try this poisoning case!\"","Seeing someone had gone to fetch Magistrate Meng, Mo Jiuye said to Eighth Elder Brother, \"Eighth Elder Brother, go to the medicine hall and ask a doctor to come.\"","Mo Chuhan had been a catcher in Yun City for several months. He was extremely familiar with everything here. Without Mo Jiuye telling him, he already knew which doctors were better.","\"Alright, I'll go now.\"","With Little Sister Nine's amazing medical skills at home, they never needed to ask for an outside doctor when the family got sick.","Mo Chuhan thought the poisoned workers at home were already showing symptoms. Little Sister Nine alone couldn't handle it, so Ninth Younger Brother was anxious for him to fetch a doctor.","Poisoning is no trivial matter. If not handled properly, it can cost lives...","Indeed, Mo Chuhan did not listen carefully to his younger brother’s words. When Mo Jiuye asked him to invite one doctor over, the location he meant was the county yamen, and the number was one. But Mo Chuhan didn’t catch that at all.","He went into town and brought over all the famous doctors from several medicine halls to Xi Ling Village.","But that’s for later.","Fifth Elder Brother tied the carriage in the horse yard outside the yamen entrance, and followed Mo Jiuye inside.","Upon hearing it was the Mo family members, Meng Huaining ran to the court hall faster than a rabbit.","When Mo Jiuye and Fifth Elder Brother saw him, he was still straightening his magistrate hat that had tilted.","Seeing them, Meng Huaining enthusiastically walked out from behind the desk and stood in the middle of the hall to talk with them.","\"Fifth Elder Brother, Ninth Elder Brother, what exactly happened?\"","If outsiders heard this form of address, they would have thought these few were blood brothers meeting.","Mo Jiuye and Fifth Elder Brother were still quite furious at the moment, so they didn't engage in small talk with Meng Huaining.","\"Magistrate Meng, I saw this man put poison into those workers' food with my own eyes.\"","Inside the yamen, Mo Jiuye felt it would be better not to address Meng as Brother Meng.","Meng Huaining also understood this was not the time to bond with his future uncle.","He turned around, walked behind the desk, and his expression immediately became grave.","With a resounding crack of the startling block, Meng Huaining said, \"Bring him in to stand trial!\"","Immediately, rows of clerks wielding fierce-looking staffs marched into orderly positions on both sides.","Seeing this battle array, Cui Xing was already scared stiff, even having trouble kneeling steadily.","Meng Huaining asked sternly, \"Who is the man kneeling in the court?\"","Accompanying Meng Huaining, the clerks' staffs rhythmically struck the ground.","Never having seen such a scene before, Cui Xing curled up trembling on the ground, repeatedly knocking his head on the floor towards the magistrate.","\"This... this lowly one is Cui Xing from Xi Ling Village.\"","Meng Huaining struck the startling block again. \"Cui Xing, speak. Why did you poison the Mo family workers?\"","If this was in Xi Ling Village, Cui Xing would still have a ray of hope.","Even if Mo Jiuye actually didn’t see anything and was just bluffing, as long as he adamantly denied it, the other side would have nothing on him.","But it was different in the court. The common folk of Yun City all said this man was Honorable Magistrate from High Heaven, and no case stumped him.","Cui Xing had seen with his own eyes Mo Fifth Elder fill a porcelain bottle with the poisoned soup.","With just a doctor's examination, the poison added would surely be discovered.","Cui Xing knew there was no escaping this. Rather than suffer torture before confessing, he might as well speak out early and suffer less himself.","\"Your Honor, this lowly one is guilty. But it wasn't my idea alone...\"","Meng Huaining shouted sternly again, \"Speak!\"","\"It was my clan elder and some clansmen. They were jealous the Mo family nowadays is living so well, so they wanted to add difficulties for them.","Later, we all gathered to discuss, thinking to put poison in the Mo family workers' meals. That way, the compensation money would make the Mo family go bankrupt.\"","Hearing this, wasn't it perfectly clear to everyone present the motive behind the Cui family's poisoning?","Nothing more than jealousy that the Mo family in Xi Ling Village was better off day after day, while decline crept up on the Cui family.","The usually composed Fifth Elder Brother became angrier the more he thought about it.","The Mo family people only wanted to live peacefully in Xi Ling Village. Who would have thought in an inconspicuous rural village, there would be so much deceit?","In fury, Fifth Elder Brother strode forward to grab Cui Xing by the collar and growled, \"What poison did you put in the soup?\"","Seeing someone violently lay hands on him again, Cui Xing panicked and quickly said,","\"I don't know what poison it was. My clansmen obtained it. Anyway, it was potent enough that the Mo family wouldn't get far after eating it.\"","Fifth Elder Brother knew Cui Xing wouldn't dare conceal anything now. Since he said he didn't know, he likely truly didn't know.","He flung the man back to his former spot and turned to look towards the entrance.","\"I remember there is a medicine hall nearby. Why hasn't Eighth Younger Brother returned with a doctor yet after going to fetch one?\"","At this time, Mo Chuhan was already leading over a dozen doctors rushing swiftly towards Xi Ling Village...","Hearing Mo Chuhan had gone to find doctors, Meng Huaining was in no hurry to send more people.","Since the Cui family members all took part in the poisoning, naturally they wouldn't be let off easily.","He sent Prefect Shi to interrogate Cui Xing on how many clansmen took part, who the ringleader was, what all they did, and so on.","At the same time, he dispatched clerks to swiftly travel to Xi Ling Village and surround the Cui residence. Regardless if they were involved or not, until there was a definite conclusion, not a single person could be let escape.","While Prefect Shi took Cui Xing aside for questioning, Meng Huaining also had tea brought for the Mo brothers in the back hall.","After waiting for about an hour, Prefect Shi had finished transcribing all the records, but there was still no sign of Mo Chuhan returning...","Mo Jiuye and Fifth Elder Brother really could no longer sit. Both were worried Mo Chuhan might have run into some difficulty.","The two stood up at the same time and told Meng Huaining they were going to look for Mo Chuhan.","Feeling something was off by now, Meng Huaining sent a few clerks along with the brothers in their search."]},{"number":322,"title":"Chapter 322: Do bad things and run Away","paragraphs":["Neither Mo Jiuye nor Fifth Elder Brother expected that Mo Chuhan would bring a group of doctors back to Xi Ling Village. At present, their search range was still limited to within Yun City.","It could be said that Mo Chuhan bringing a group of doctors back to Xi Ling Village happened by coincidence.","He had just entered the village when he saw over a dozen members of the Cui Family rushing over in a panic.","Seeing the bundles they were holding in their hands, it was obvious they wanted to flee after committing a crime.","Without saying a word, Mo Chuhan stepped forward to block the path of the dozen or so people.","After living in Xi Ling Village for a long time, it was inevitable that there would be occasions to run into members of the Cui Family. The dozen or so people in front of Mo Chuhan were not strangers to him.","\"You want to run after doing bad things?\" He said sarcastically.","After exchanging glances with each other, the members of the Cui Family were somewhat at a loss.","Back when the Mo Family had just arrived at Xi Ling Village, it was this Mo Chuhan who first jumped into the Li Family’s yard. His agile skill was something a few people had witnessed with their own eyes.","In the face of Mo Chuhan, no one wanted to stand out. If they said the wrong thing, they would definitely suffer a beating.","The most important thing now was that there were many of them and only one of him. Even if Mo Chuhan wanted to catch them, it was impossible for him to grab everyone.","As for the doctors Mo Chuhan had brought back, they had failed to keep up with his pace and were still behind, not yet arriving at Xi Ling Village.","With this in mind, the members of the Cui Family wanted to escape by their own means.","When Mo Chuhan was not looking at him, one person took large steps and ran towards the village entrance.","Mo Chuhan did not give chase at all. He quickly bent down to pick up a small stone from the ground and threw it at the escaping person.","It was seen that the person stumbled over something in front of him as if he had tripped over something. With a cry, he fell forward flat on his face.","Seeing this, the other members of the Cui Family thought it was their chance. They scattered and ran towards the village entrance.","Mo Chuhan picked up a few more pebbles and threw them out accurately, hitting each person's ankle.","None of the Cui Family members were spared, and they all fell to the ground.","The most miserable was the Cui Family's only elder. He was older in age and did not have the quick feet like those younger ones. Mo Chuhan was closer to him and threw the stone with greater force.","Therefore, he fell with even greater force. His remaining few teeth were all knocked out.","Mo Chuhan ignored the cries of the Cui Family and efficiently took off their belts to tie them up one by one.","The commotion at the village entrance was not small. The remaining members of the Cui Family who had not escaped had a guilty conscience and did not dare to come out and see what was going on.","The Zhou and Zhao Families were different. Since the Cui Family had been taught a lesson to behave themselves, there had not been any major disturbances in the village for a long time. Now there was some excitement to watch, so idle people ran out to watch.","Coincidentally, the patriarchs of both the Zhou and Zhao Families were present.","Mo Chuhan said to both of them, \"Please help watch these people for a while. I will go to the foot of the mountain to take a look and will be back soon.\"","Now that Mo Chuhan was a government officer, the Zhou and Zhao Family members would naturally not be ambiguous about watching the people he had caught.","Moreover, they were reluctant to let slip the opportunity to show off their power in front of the Cui Family.","\"Alright. Constable Mo, go ahead with your work. We will keep an eye on them.”","After Mo Chuhan gave his thanks, he rushed towards the foot of the mountain.","He wanted to see what the poisoning situation of those workers was.","As a result, when he arrived at his family's home site, what he saw was completely different from what he had imagined.","The workers were orderly doing their own work, showing no signs of poisoning at all.","That’s not right. Didn’t younger brother say that the Cui Family members had poisoned their soup?","How come these people were fine?","Just as Mo Chuhan was puzzled, Hu Cong, who was directing from up high, discovered his arrival.","Hu Cong immediately walked over, \"Eighth Young Master, didn't you go to your post today?\"","Mo Chuhan was completely baffled.","\"Elder Brother Hu, my younger brother said that the Cui Family came here to poison people. Is that true?\"","Hu Cong didn’t know what Mo Chuhan had misunderstood. He nodded slightly and said indifferently, \"That is indeed the case. The poisoner has already been sent to the yamen by the young masters.\"","Mo Chuhan was still confused.","\"But these people are clearly fine without any signs of poisoning!\"","Only then did Hu Cong realize that Mo Chuhan had misunderstood something.","\"Fortunately, Ninth Young Master came just in time to catch the poisoner on the scene, otherwise a great disaster would have occurred.\"","Shouldn’t it be a disaster? Just now, He Zhiran couldn't help coming over to take a look.","She determined on the spot that there was arsenic in the soup.","Who doesn’t know what arsenic is? That’s an extremely toxic poison.","Hu Cong knew Mo Chuhan had an irritable personality. He was afraid that he would act impulsively and hurt someone, causing unnecessary trouble. Therefore, he did not say it clearly.","Anyway, Mo Jiuye had already taken some of the poisoned soup to the yamen. Although the sale of such a toxic poison like arsenic was restricted in Da Shun, ordinary doctors would be able to identify it.","When the time comes, the yamen will ask the doctors to identify it, and the Cui Family members can be convicted accordingly.","After listening to Hu Cong’s words, Mo Chuhan came to his senses as if awakening from a dream.","Just now when younger brother told him to invite a doctor to come over, it was to go to the yamen instead of here.","Fortunately, he had misunderstood, otherwise he would have given those sinister Cui Family members a chance to escape.","Knowing that he had made a false alarm, Mo Chuhan was about to rush back to the county government immediately.","He had just walked to the village entrance when the doctors he had found and the officers sent by Meng Huaining arrived as well.","The dozen or so Cui Family members who had just been caught showed signs of trying to escape again. It was obvious that they were involved in the poisoning incident. Now there was no need for Meng Huaining to issue another order. Mo Chuhan directly instructed that two officers stay to guard the Cui Family while the rest escorted those few escaping Cui Family members back to the yamen.","After leaving the county yamen, Mo Jiuye and Fifth Elder Brother went separate ways to look for Mo Chuhan.","He asked around a medical hall in the city and was told that Constable Mo had indeed been there to invite doctors, saying he was going to Xi Ling Village to save people.","Mo Jiuye understood in his heart that it must be his rash eighth brother who had misunderstood something and brought those doctors back to the village.","So he quickened his pace towards Xi Ling Village, hoping to catch up with him on the way back.","Halfway there, he happened to meet Mo Chuhan and the others who were escorting those Cui Family members back to the county yamen.","The two brothers escorted those Cui Family members back together.","By now, it was nearing dusk. The yamen would normally not handle official business during this time.","But since it was the Mo Family’s business, let alone dusk, even if it was the middle of the night, Meng Huaining would still go all out.","There were no doubts about the case itself. After getting doctors to identify it, it was confirmed that the poison in the soup was arsenic.","As for the source of the arsenic, Meng Huaining soon inquired it out.","This stuff had been given to them by Deputy Magistrate Cui, to get the Cui Family members to help out with some shady business whenever needed.","After Deputy Magistrate Cui’s downfall, there was no use for this stuff, so it was left with the Cui Family in Xi Ling Village.","Today, they actually wanted to use such a deadly poison to kill those workers. It can be seen how malicious their intentions were.","Fortunately, the incident was discovered in time by Mo Jiuye, otherwise a great disaster would have occurred.","Even so, Meng Huaining would not let the Cui Family members off easily.","The Yun City he governed would never allow the existence of such malicious people."]},{"number":323,"title":"Chapter 323: The Most thoughtful Gift to Mo Hanyu","paragraphs":["After an overnight interrogation, the Cui family confessed that except for some women and children who were not involved, most of the rest of the clan were more or less involved to some degree.","Meng Huaining felt that not only was the former Cui County Magistrate extremely evil, but the Cui clan itself was rotten to the core.","Therefore, he severely sentenced the Cui clan.","Three days later, the entire Cui clan, all were exiled to the Western Regions to mine, and were forbidden from leaving for the rest of their lives.","The yamen runners received the order and immediately went to Xiling Village, capturing all the Cui family members, only waiting for Meng Huaining to finalize the documents in three days before sending them away.","All the Cui clan's land and houses were confiscated, once again giving the Mo Family an opportunity to expand their assets.","This time, Mo Jiuye was not considering his own family.","The manor sites and wasteland at the foot of the mountain were already enough for his own family to use. He intended to help his subordinates who had returned home to visit relatives acquire some land and property, which was also a compensation from the Mo Family to these brothers who had followed him through life and death for many years.","Living in the countryside, one must follow local customs. Spending every day doing some farming and weaving, plus the cleverness of his sisters-in-law, would also lead them to earn money together.","In short, it would not be a bad thing for everyone to live together in a village like this.","Upon hearing that Mo Jiuye wanted to buy up the Cui clan’s assets, Meng Huaining agreed without hesitation.","Moreover, he offered the lowest price possible.","Unexpectedly, the Cui clan’s single evil act ended up benefiting the Mo Family.","Now in Xiling Village, apart from the original Zhao and Zhou native families, there were the Mo, Fang and Xie families.","Surely there would be no more troublemakers like the Cui clan coming to make trouble while living in Xiling Village in the future.","The storm caused by the Cui clan passed very quickly, and the Mo Family’s various construction projects were still progressing vigorously.","After more than ten days of hard work, the rabbit sheds were finally completed.","Everyone worked together to move all the original rabbits from the family into the new rabbit sheds.","The new rabbit sheds were dozens of times larger than the original ones. Even though the original female rabbits were already frantically breeding, they still only took up one fifth of the rabbit sheds.","He Zhiran had originally planned to use the foreigners as an excuse a few more times to purchase some rabbits from the shop to breed.","Later, she discovered that those female rabbits had big bellies again, and the number of adult female rabbits in the family was increasing. She believed that the ideal breeding quantity would be reached before long.","Of course, with the expansion of the rabbit sheds’ scale, He Zhiran had new plans.","The sisters-in-law had said before that rabbit fur dyed in colors would definitely look very beautiful if made into cloaks or clothes.","He Zhiran had never forgotten this point.","Those beautiful angora knitwear in modern times were not only good-looking but also kept warm well. If they could be produced successfully, it would be a huge source of income.","He Zhiran was already raising a large group of angora rabbits in the shop space, which happened to have just reached adulthood today, and some were even pregnant with bunnies.","It was time to bring them into the open.","Coincidentally, Mo Jiuye was free today, so the two of them drove the carriage into the city, took out all the rabbits together with their cages from the shop space, and put them in the rented yard.","As usual, Mo Jiuye brought his brothers from the family to hire ox carts to transport them home.","Although this was more troublesome, this method was still quite useful. The family members were also used to the couple buying things from foreigners...","The return of the angora rabbits once again delighted the women of the family.","Especially after the sisters-in-law heard that angora fur could be made into beautiful clothes, they liked it even more.","Now the number of rabbits raised in the family was increasing. Just slaughtering the male rabbits every day to make chilled rabbit meat was an extremely tiring job, relying solely on the fifth elder brother and his wife.","The fifth elder brother and his wife had already learned a lot of rabbit raising skills after this period of time, and now they were even more knowledgeable than He Zhiran who led the way.","In the future, the fifth elder brother couple would continue to be in charge of the rabbit sheds, but they would have to hire more people to help.","This way, the fifth elder brother and his wife would not have to be too busy and could have some time of their own to do other things.","Whether to continue expanding the scale in the future would depend on Tang Mingrui’s business situation.","Speaking of Tang Mingrui, he was indeed worthy of becoming a big merchant in the future.","In just a few months, through cooperation with the Mo Family and his own business sources found outside, he now had accumulated a large amount of capital.","When he heard that the Mo Family was expanding the scale of rabbit breeding, he was even more excited than the Mo Family people.","It should be known that the chilled rabbit meat produced by the Mo Family was no longer just being sold to the restaurants in the prefectural city.","As the quantity of chilled rabbit meat gradually increased, he had also contacted several restaurants in other cities and signed long-term sales contracts with them.","The expansion of the Mo Family's rabbit breeding scale gave him countless times more profit.","Recently, he had been running to the Mo Family very diligently. The chilled rabbit meat could only ensure freshness if it was freshly made every day.","It should be said that Tang Mingrui now had silver in his hands. This kind of going to collect goods personally could be completely handled by hiring people, but he still insisted on doing it himself.","Over a period of time, the threshold of the Mo Family's door was almost worn out by him.","Not only that, Tang Mingrui often did not come empty-handed, bringing more or less some small gifts he had collected when he went out.","Although everyone had gifts, after several times, He Zhiran noticed something wrong.","On the surface Tang Mingrui had prepared gifts for all the Mo Family members, but upon closer inspection, the gifts he prepared for Mo Hanyue were given the most thought.","For example, the first time Tang Mingrui brought gifts to the Mo family, it was just after the new year.","He went to other cities to do business, and the local specialty there was osmanthus cake.","Although the name of the cake was osmanthus cake, there were also several flavors.","The osmanthus cakes Tang Mingrui bought for the other Mo family members were all the basic white sugar flavor, while the one box for Mo Hanyue contained three flavors.","Not only that, the osmanthus cakes in that box were also divided into different shapes, which made one reluctant to eat them.","And a few days ago, Tang Mingrui gave everyone in the Mo Family a bolt of cloth.","Although the cloth seemed to be of considerable value, the one given to Mo Hanyue was particularly special.","When the Mo Family was in the capital city, they were also a prestigious household. Naturally they recognized fine goods.","Everyone recognized at a glance that the cloth Tang Mingrui gave to Mo Hanyue turned out to be Shu brocade.","This was an extremely rare fine fabric. Even the Imperial Consorts in the palace had to curry tremendous favor from the Emperor. Only when the Emperor was happy would he bestow enough fabric for them to make a set of clothing."]},{"number":324,"title":"Chapter 324: We'll never talk about it again.","paragraphs":["Tang Mingrui generously gave Mo Hanyue a piece of Shu brocade directly.","Old Lady Mo was a very perceptive person. Through these two gifts, she and He Zhiran both caught some clues.","Tang Mingrui was interested in Mo Hanyue!","Of course, with such a precious thing, the Mo family would never accept it.","Although Tang Mingrui's Shu brocade was not given, his actions could be seen clearly by the observant.","Not only Old Lady Mo saw it, He Zhiran and several sisters-in-law also saw it clearly.","Tang Mingrui purely wanted to give Mo Hanyue a gift, so he used this method.","Second sister-in-law had a hard time keeping things to herself. After dinner, she took the women of the family together and started gossiping in front of her mother-in-law.","\"Mother, have you noticed that Young Master Tang is very nice to Hanyue?\"","Although Old Lady Mo had been exiled to the northwest, that kind of deep-rooted ideology could not be completely transformed all at once.","In her opinion, no matter how excellent Tang Mingrui was, he was still a businessman, while Meng Huaining was different. Even if he did not become an official, he still came from a scholarly family.","Comparing the two, she still valued the literati more.","Old Lady Mo did not look down on Tang Mingrui, she just preferred her daughter to marry a literatus if she had a choice.","Of course, she didn't want to be the kind of mother who made all the decisions for her children. If Mo Hanyue didn't like Meng Huaining and liked Tang Mingrui instead, she would also choose to approve their relationship.","Old Lady Mo had originally wanted to discuss it with He Zhiran, but she didn't expect her second daughter-in-law to speak up first.","She first glanced at Mo Hanyue, whose face was flushed red, and gently said, \"Hanyue, didn't you say your rabbit might give birth to babies tonight?\"","After going through some things, Mo Hanyue was no longer as childish as before.","She knew that as a young lady, it was inappropriate for her to join in the discussion of such matters.","However, she also didn't want to marry someone she didn't like.","Before leaving, she whispered in Old Lady Mo's ear, \"Mother, your daughter has no romantic feelings for Young Master Tang.\"","Since she took the initiative to say it, it saved Old Lady Mo the trouble of asking.","Old Lady Mo now thoroughly understood her daughter's mindset.","After Mo Hanyue left, Old Lady Mo solemnly said to her daughters-in-law, \"I know Hanyue's situation well. From now on, be polite to Young Master Tang when he comes, and don't have any other ideas.\"","This could also be considered giving everyone an explanation. Whether it was Mo Hanyue's refusal or her own unwillingness as a mother, she had made her attitude clear.","There were many women in the family, and they were all Mo Hanyue's sisters-in-law. It was inevitable that they would worry about the only young miss in the family.","Letting them know her attitude early on would prevent the daughters-in-law from being overzealous and causing any misunderstandings.","He Zhiran was the most perceptive. After hearing her mother-in-law's words, she immediately understood her meaning.","\"Mother, don't worry. From now on, we will keep our mouths shut about this.\"","The other sisters-in-law also nodded in agreement after seeing the ninth sister-in-law say this, indicating that they would do the same.","Only the silly second sister-in-law still felt that after Mo Hanyue rejected Tang Mingrui, she might not be able to find someone from such a good family in the future.","After all, the Mo family's circumstances were not what they used to be. Although their lives were still quite affluent, how many people would not mind that they were exiled criminals of the court?","\"Mother, I think Young Master Tang is a good man, why don't you consider it?\"","Old Lady Mo usually treated the nine daughters-in-law equally.","The only exception was this stubborn second daughter-in-law who didn't understand what everyone else could see clearly.","Thinking that she spoke without thinking, the old lady was somewhat angry.","She frowned and scolded, \"If you don't understand, go back and ask the other daughters-in-law later.\"","The eldest sister-in-law quickly pulled the second sister-in-law's sleeve and said, \"Second sister-in-law, eldest sister will explain it to you later.\"","The second sister-in-law nodded blankly, \"Okay.\"","Now, the women of the family all understood the mother-in-law's attitude, and tacitly stopped mentioning Tang Mingrui.","The next morning, as usual, Tang Mingrui came with a carriage to pick up goods.","Coincidentally, Meng Huaining also came on the pretext of catching up with Mo Jiuye, and the two arrived at the Mo family one after the other.","Tang Mingrui was a businessman, so naturally he would pay his respects when seeing an official.","Meng Huaining did not know Tang Mingrui's feelings. He knew that this person had business dealings with the Mo family and was on good terms with them.","Therefore, he did not put on any official airs in front of Tang Mingrui, and treated him as casually as he did the Mo family.","He and Tang Mingrui were led into the yard by Mo Jiuye. By chance, Mo Hanyue was wearing a face veil and holding a hoe. She came out from inside with Yu Er and Lan Er, planning to go take care of her medicinal fields.","After all, Tang Mingrui was a businessman, so he acted much more generously than Meng Huaining.","He took the initiative to greet her, \"Miss Mo, are you going to work in the fields?\"","When Mo Hanyue saw the righteous Meng Huaining, she was thrilled in her heart.","She was just about to greet him when she saw Tang Mingrui had already strode towards her.","Having heard her second sister-in-law's words yesterday, she more or less knew Tang Mingrui's feelings.","Although she didn't dislike Tang Mingrui, she didn't have any romantic feelings for him either.","Especially in front of the man she liked, Mo Hanyue was somewhat at a loss for a moment.","After all, she was a young lady from a prominent family, and etiquette was not taught to her in vain.","She quickly sorted out her thoughts and bowed slightly to the two men standing side by side.","\"Good morning, Master Meng, Young Master Tang.\"","When Meng Huaining saw the girl he had been thinking about, he was overjoyed.","He was just about to return the greeting when he saw Tang Mingrui had already taken out an exquisite little purse from his arms.","Tang Mingrui stepped forward again and presented the little purse to Mo Hanyue.","\"Miss Mo, these are ginseng seeds I happened to come across while doing business. I know you like growing medicinal herbs, so I brought them for you to plant and see.\"","In fact, He Zhiran could provide as many ginseng seeds as needed, and they were high-quality varieties produced in her space.","The main reason she didn't give them to Mo Hanyue for planting was that ginseng had a long growth cycle, and there would be little to see in the short term.","Tang Mingrui didn't know about this. He only knew that Mo Hanyue liked to grow medicinal herbs, so he wanted to give her the best.","Seeing Tang Mingrui give Mo Hanyue a gift as soon as he arrived, Meng Huaining suddenly felt a little unhappy.","Just as he was thinking about how to step forward and strike up a conversation, Mo Hanyue spoke.","\"Thank you, Young Master Tang. Ginseng seeds are too precious, Hanyue cannot accept them.\"","Cannot accept!","Yes, she could not accept his things.","Seeing Mo Hanyue reject the gift, Meng Huaining instantly felt relieved.","Tang Mingrui was not discouraged and continued to hold out the purse.","\"This is not worth much money. I just happened to come across it and bought it. Miss Mo, please accept it!\"","Mo Hanyue took a step back.","\"Thank you for your kindness, Young Master Tang, but I've just started learning to grow medicinal herbs. I shouldn't ruin something so good.\""]},{"number":325,"title":"Chapter 325: Isn't He Dead","paragraphs":["Tang Mingrui had asked Mo Hanyue to marry him several times, but even someone as experienced with all kinds of people as Tang Mingrui felt somewhat embarrassed as Mo Hanyue rejected him repeatedly. His hand holding the money pouch didn't know whether to move forward or to pull back.","Just then, Old Lady Mo came out from the room. She had heard the commotion in the yard and after watching for a while, she decided to come out to help her daughter defuse the situation. However, before she could say anything, Meng Huaining, who had remained silent all this time, came up to her.","Meng Huaining was very respectful. He bowed deeply to Old Lady Mo and said, \"Good day, Old Lady Mo.\"","Old Lady Mo nodded benevolently, \"What brings Mister Meng to our humble abode today?\"","Meng Huaining clenched and unclenched his fists hidden in his sleeves. After a long while, he finally steeled his resolve and said, \"This junior wishes to ask for Mo Hanyue's hand in marriage. I pledge to make her my only wife in this lifetime and never take a concubine, even if I remain childless.\"","God knows how much courage Meng Huaining had mustered to say those words in front of so many people.","He had originally planned to get more familiar with Mo Hanyue first, to make the young lady like him more before sending a formal letter to his family asking his sister-in-law to come and help propose the marriage. That would also show how much he valued Mo Hanyue.","But after seeing how obvious Tang Mingrui's intentions were today, if he continued that tactic of slowly boiling the frog, he was afraid the bride would be snatched away by someone else.","From Old Lady Mo's understanding of Meng Huaining's character, he was not the rash type.","Moreover, she could also see that the young man was about to send someone to their home with a formal proposal.","Meng Huaining's words really caught Old Lady Mo off guard. However, since she had approved of her daughter marrying Meng Huaining in the first place, she naturally could not reject him now.","\"Since Mister Meng is interested, we can sit down to discuss this.\"","Old Lady Mo's words were like giving Meng Huaining a huge reassurance.","Meng Huaining quickly cupped his fists, \"Old Lady, please give me three days. I will prepare the betrothal gifts and send the best matchmaker in the city to your home with the official proposal.\"","Time was tight, so asking his sister-in-law to come help was probably not feasible. Hiring the best matchmaker in the city would surely not shortchange Mo Hanyue.","Moreover, Old Lady Mo did not reject him outright, which meant she did not oppose the marriage.","Therefore, he must not give the Mo family any chance to reconsider.","When Meng Huaining was speaking just now, he had sneakily glanced at Mo Hanyue.","The young lady was now hiding bashfully behind her sisters-in-law, knowing it was improper for her to be present during such discussions but unable to tear herself away as she wanted to listen in on what would happen next.","Meanwhile, Tang Mingrui was dumbfounded.","What was going on here? The girl he liked was getting proposed to by someone else?","Moreover, from Old Lady Mo's smiling expression, she seemed to highly approve of it.","Did this mean... he had no chance at all now?","Even so, Tang Mingrui was unwilling to admit defeat without even putting up a fight. That was not his style.","After organizing his thoughts, Tang Mingrui stepped up beside Meng Huaining.","But just as he was about to say something, from the corner of his eye he caught Mo Hanyue looking at Meng Huaining bashfully yet eagerly.","Even if Tang Mingrui wanted to fight for her, upon seeing Mo Hanyue's gaze, he could only retreat.","That was clearly a look of admiration, unfortunately not directed at him.","In this situation, if he insisted on barging forward, he would only embarrass himself.","Therefore, he changed what he had originally wanted to say.","\"Congratulations, Mister Meng and Miss Mo.\"","Meng Huaining smiled mildly, \"Thank you for your well wishes, Master Tang.\"","Seeing the matter was settled, Mo Hanyue quietly slipped away from the crowd.","Tang Mingrui also tactfully took his leave. Seeing that Mo Hanyue had gone, he discreetly tucked the pouch containing the ginseng seeds into his clothes, pretending nothing had happened today.","His main purpose in coming today was to collect the goods. Not only had the Mo family produced a large quantity of Cold Rabbit Snacks today, they also had over a hundred rabbit pendents.","Plus the two dozen or so pet rabbits from Mo Hanyue, he was taking them all away.","Tang Mingrui knew when to advance and when to retreat. Since he and Mo Hanyue no longer had a chance, he saw no need to linger.","The sooner he took away the goods to earn more money and bring his business to greater heights, that would become his sole goal going forward.","To spend more time at the Mo residence, Meng Huaining had already arranged all the matters at the yamen yesterday.","But with how things had developed, since he had already proposed to Mo Hanyue, he had to rush back immediately to prepare betrothal gifts and other matters.","Thus, not long after Tang Mingrui's departure, Meng Huaining also hastily took his leave.","After Meng Huaining left, Old Lady Mo called all the family members into her room.","In the Mo family's minds, Mo Hanyue's marriage was the biggest event in the household. Everyone held their breaths waiting for Old Lady Mo to speak.","\"Hanyue is grown up now, at the age to be married off. She and Mister Meng are fond of each other, so as her mother I must do right by her. Do any of you have any objections?\"","He Zhiran secretly laughed to herself.","She thought: You've already agreed to it, what objections could we possibly have?","Besides, it's a case of a willing couple, who would object?","While Old Lady Mo's actions today felt unfamiliar to He Zhiran, the other sisters-in-law thought it was perfectly normal.","Back in the capital, the Mo family had also been a prestigious and powerful household. As the lady of the house, Old Lady Mo naturally had her dignity and authority.","After many years of running the household, ever since they were exiled, she had put away her stern side.","Yet today, the aura she used to have as the lady of the house in the capital emerged once again, showing how much Old Lady Mo valued her daughter's marriage.","The Eldest Sister-in-law slowly stood up and said, \"There are feelings between Hanyue and Mister Meng. This is a rare good match. Mother's judgement has always been spot on. I believe their future will definitely be a happy one.\"","The Seventh Sister-In-Law also stood up and echoed, \"That's right, Mother. Hanyue clearly has great fortune. It looks like us sisters-in-law need to start preparing her bridal outfits.\"","Seeing that both daughters-in-law spoke in agreement, Old Lady Mo instantly beamed happily.","\"Wonderful, wonderful. It's time our Mo family had a joyous occasion to liven things up.\"","Then she added, \"The reason I called you here today is to discuss Hanyue's wedding date.\"","Everyone, including the Mo brothers, was puzzled by this statement.","The Fifth Elder Brother stood up and asked, \"Mother, isn't the wedding date always decided by the groom's side? Besides, our Hanyue isn't some old spinster who can't find a match. Why are we in such a rush?\"","After the Fifth Elder Brother voiced the question, everyone looked to Old Lady Mo, equally confused.","In the Great Shun Dynasty, after a marriage was agreed upon, the groom's side would take both parties' birth dates to a fortune teller to select auspicious wedding dates based on their eight characters.","These matters were all handled by the groom's family, while the bride's side simply had to wait for them to finalize the wedding day and inform them.","So why was Mother bringing up the wedding date with them?","\"Mother, are you worried that since our family is down and out now, Mister Meng might go back on his word, and Hanyue won't be able to find such a good match again in the future?\"","Other than that, Mo Jinnian could not think of any other reason for his mother's actions."]},{"number":326,"title":"Chapter 326: What good intentions do you have","paragraphs":["Old Lady Mo was well aware of these traditional rules. She had her own considerations for acting this way.","\"It's already April,\" Old Lady Mo said, her gaze gradually drifting away, tinged with a hint of sadness.","She continued, \"Yun Feng took people to the western border to gather information and hasn't returned yet. Your fathers and brothers are currently missing, their fate unknown.","According to the information we've received, Mr. Si Meng is expected to appear in the western border in July. I am worried that by that time, if we still can't successfully rescue your fathers and brothers, their chances of survival will be slim.\"","Old Lady Mo had kept these words hidden in her heart, never speaking them in front of the children, fearing it would shatter their confidence.","But today, while discussing her daughter's marriage date, she had no choice but to bring it up for explanation.","He Zhiran, being perceptive, instantly guessed her thoughts upon hearing a few words from her. However, it was not something she could speak of openly.","However, just because she didn't mention it didn't mean others wouldn't.","Even Second Sister-in-law, who was usually outspoken, had her mind working today. The first thing that came to her mind was her missing husband. In front of everyone, tears uncontrollably streamed down her face.","She stood up, choked with emotion, and pleaded, \"Mother, my husband and father will surely come back safely. Please don't entertain such thoughts.\"","Even Big Sister-in-law shed tears, but unlike Second Younger Siblings, she didn't say anything out loud. She silently prayed in her heart that her husband, father-in-law, and Second Younger Siblings would return safely like the other missing brothers.","Old Lady Mo also had the same thoughts, but she had experienced more in life, making it easier for her daughter-in-law to accept reality.","She gently wiped the corner of her eye and said, \"I'm just worried. The situation hasn't reached its final stage yet, and no one knows what the outcome will be.\"","Old Lady Mo asked Second Sister-in-law to sit back down and spoke again, \"If by July, we receive any unfortunate news, Hanyue's marriage will be delayed because of it.","We can't let Hanyue's lifelong happiness be delayed because of those unwritten rules.\"","As a wise old woman, she didn't believe that once news of the deaths of the Mo father and son arrived, after Hanyue finished mourning for three years, Meng Huaining would still be waiting for her in the same place.","Therefore, today she wanted to make a change in her daughter's marriage.","Mo Jiuye never liked those worldly rules, and besides, he was confident that he could safely rescue his father and brothers.","Of course, regardless of his mother's thoughts, he chose to support her.","\"Since that's the case, Mother, do you have any plans?\" Mo Jiuye sighed and asked.","\"Meng Huaining has already said that he will come to propose in three days. He doesn't have any elders in Yuncheng, so I can make the decision on the wedding date,\" Old Lady Mo said.","\"Since you have a plan, we'll follow what you said,\" Mo Jiuye agreed.","It was rare for his mother to want to take charge, and as a son, he naturally wanted to fulfill her wishes.","Moreover, after getting to know Meng Huaining during their time together, he understood that he was a dependable person. As long as Hanyue could marry such a person, he, as her older brother, would be at ease.","He Zhiran had no objections, and she started to contemplate what kind of dowry would be appropriate for her younger sister-in-law.","Although Old Lady Mo still held some authority in the family, she had relinquished the stewardship to He Zhiran since they began their exile journey.","During this period, no matter what decisions He Zhiran made, her mother-in-law never raised any objections, showing her trust in He Zhiran.","Moreover, the family's financial resources were under He Zhiran's control. Although she would allocate some to her brothers and sisters-in-law on regular occasions, it was only a small portion.","Furthermore, the Mo family had not split, and they all lived together as one big family. Naturally, it was He Zhiran's responsibility as the head of the household to handle the dowry for her younger sister-in-law's marriage.","He Zhiran's spatial storage was filled with abundant resources, and she would not be stingy when it came to Mo Hanyue's dowry.","However, the dowry had to be carefully considered.","First, they had to take into account the betrothal gifts from the groom's side and provide a corresponding dowry based on their value.","They could also consider the financial strength of the bride's family. If the bride's family was wealthy, they would naturally not mistreat their married daughter.","However, even though they were considered free now, they had come into exile with no money. It was well-known that they had left the capital penniless. After arriving in the northwest, they engaged in some small businesses, but their visible income was limited.","If the dowry He Zhiran provided exceeded the apparent range, it would inevitably raise suspicions among others.","Especially those precious treasures that had been taken from the national treasury, they couldn't be shown off casually.","Therefore, He Zhiran had her own plan.","The dowry for a daughter's marriage usually consisted of gold, silver, and other valuable items.","Recently, she had seen two village weddings in Xiling Village, and she noticed that the bride's family also sent furniture and other objects as part of the dowry. Presumably, only well-off families could afford to do so.","After careful consideration, He Zhiran had a rough idea in mind and was waiting to see what kind of betrothal gifts Meng Huaining would bring before making a final decision.","The matter of Mo Hanyue had been discussed and the whole family had reached a consensus.","Life in the Mo family resumed its previous tranquility, and everyone busied themselves with their own affairs.","After a few days of renovation, the rabbit shed was back on track. Hired help took care of it every day, so Wu Ge and Wu Sao had a lot of free time.","However, they still couldn't rest assured and took turns guarding the rabbit shed. Wu Ge even checked on it at night because they were worried about wild animals coming down from the mountain and mixing in with the rabbits. Additionally, they had to guard against thieves.","Although the Cui family no longer existed, the fact that the Mo family built the rabbit shed was not a secret. People from other villages also came to help build the house. Who could guarantee that these people had no ill intentions or would reveal this information to someone with ulterior motives?","Therefore, Mo Chongyuan patrolled the rabbit shed at night to prevent anyone from coveting their rabbits.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye also had this in mind.","They both felt that Wu Ge's nightly inspections were not a long-term solution, and it would be best to come up with a permanent solution.","He Zhiran, who had lived two lives, naturally had a more insightful mind than Mo Jiuye.","She looked at the spoiled rice ball in front of her and suddenly had an idea in her mind.","In the open space, a hundred or so shiny black German Shepherd puppies suddenly appeared.","When Fentuan saw the sudden arrival of many new animals not far away, he immediately abandoned trying to please his owner and ran over with his short little legs.","He Zhiran realized that this little guy enjoyed making those small animals submit to him.","The cows and sheep in the space had already bored him; he considered giving them some respite and no longer enforcing rules every day.","The appearance of so many new and exciting animals once again piqued Fentuan's interest.","He Zhiran knew that it would have this kind of effect, so she stood quietly there, watching Fentuan's performance.","Of course, this was also something she was happy to see come to fruition."]},{"number":327,"title":"Chapter 327: Tuanzi Is Awesome Today","paragraphs":["In order to allow these German Shepherd puppies to grow up quickly, He Zhiran spent a high price to buy them in the operating table.","In just five days, those German Shepherd puppies would grow to adult size. By then, they could be released to guard the yard.","A single rabbit hutch alone could not use so many German Shepherds to supervise. He Zhiran was also prepared in advance.","There would be more and more industries in her home in the future, such as the cattle and sheep she wanted to raise, as well as some poultry.","Some crops planted in the fields also needed protection when they matured. For example, melon fields, which also saved the trouble of building melon sheds and hiring manpower to supervise them.","Seeing so many new animals, Rice Ball jumped for joy.","It waved its furry paws to command those German Shepherd puppies to form formations, while selling cute to its owner to show off its achievements.","He Zhiran was already unable to withstand Rice Ball's cute offensive in the first place. Now seeing it commanding the puppies there with a straight face, the feeling of satisfaction brought by happiness instantly overflowed.","However, what she wanted this time was not for these German Shepherds to be so well-behaved. She wanted them to learn how to guard the property at home.","\"Rice Ball, you have to teach them to guard the house. Only then can they be considered qualified.\"","Rice Ball saw its owner issuing orders to it. It tilted its little head to look at her, then immediately made a few whimpering sounds, and turned to look at those German Shepherd puppies.","I saw its furry little paws waving a few times, and I saw those little puppies who were still standing there neatly just now rushing towards the direction of the sheep herd instantly, while uttering a series of milky calls.","The sheep that were leisurely eating grass originally saw a group of black puppies rushing over and immediately started to flee in all directions.","However, after Rice Ball issued the next order, the puppies quickly surrounded the escaping sheep, and the circle became smaller and smaller.","One hundred German Shepherd puppies surrounded the sheep tightly. As soon as a sheep wanted to escape, a dog would immediately stop it.","He Zhiran knew that this was the first step Rice Ball trained these dogs. She continued to watch the changes.","Sure enough, after Rice Ball made another strange cry, the puppies changed again, barking and rushing towards the sheep herd to attack.","Just as He Zhiran was a little worried about the safety of the sheep herd, Rice Ball issued another order again, and those dogs obediently returned to their original places.","The sheep were unharmed.","This is how Rice Ball trained those dogs countless times back and forth before finally stopping.","It trotted over to its owner with its short legs as if showing off, constantly making hmm hmm sounds.","He Zhiran knew that the little guy had successfully completed his task.","Her belly was already very noticeable now. She slightly leaned to the side and sat on the grass, gently stroking Rice Ball's fluffy head.","\"Rice Ball is so good today, I will reward you with delicious food.\"","As she spoke, He Zhiran's thoughts had already moved, and she prepared Rice Ball's favorite milk bowl for it, as well as many tender bamboo shoots, small apples and more.","With delicious food in front, the little guy suddenly felt that the owner was no longer fragrant, and joyfully pounced over to enjoy it.","Of course, those new little puppies are also a great help for her in the future, and they must not be neglected.","He Zhiran took out some ingredients from the warehouse and processed them into nutritious and delicious dog food on the operation table.","Not only that, she considered that the puppies were growing up and also purchased a large number of pet vitamins and other nutritional products in Taobao Treasure.","Seeing the food, the puppies ran over with joy. Their ravenous appearance was something Rice Ball simply couldn’t compete with.","Now that the problem of guarding the house has been solved, just wait for these puppies to grow to adulthood in five days, and find a chance to take them out.","He Zhiran looked at the time. She had been in the space for some time. She simply tidied up a bit and appeared in her room.","Her figure had just appeared when Mo Jiuye came back.","Nan Rui was with him.","Ever since Nan Rui came to Xiling Village, he had been living in the haunted house at the foot of the mountain. He basically would not appear in front of people unless he wanted to ask her to help Consort De check her body.","It was rather rare today that he actually came with Mo Jiuye.","The guest comes, and He Zhiran naturally would not forget the proper etiquette.","\"Greetings to King Rui.\"","Nan Rui quickly waved his hand: \"The Ninth Lady is too polite. I am no longer a prince, and there is no such person as Nan Rui in the world. Just call me Uncle Rui when you see me in the future.\"","He Zhiran was not a sentimental person to begin with, let alone like too many rules. Since Nan Rui said so, she simply said, \"Okay, I won't call you King Rui from now on.\"","The reason Nan Rui came this time was that he had something very important to say.","He originally planned to talk to Mo Jiuye alone, but Consort De could see clearly that the real decision maker in the Mo family was Mo Jiuye’s wife. Therefore, he first found Mo Jiuye and said he had something to discuss with them.","Mo Jiuye didn't think too much. Things that can be discussed with his wife are basically related to medical treatment.","During this period, He Zhiran went to help Consort De check her body every few days. As they contacted more, they found that Nan Rui and his mother really had no intention of harming the Mo family, and their grievances against them gradually eased.","\"Does Uncle Rui want my wife to help see a doctor?\"","Mo Jiuye didn't want Nan Rui's arrival to delay his wife from nourishing the fetus, so he asked straightforwardly.","Nan Rui was still thinking about how to bring it up when he took the opportunity to say, \"My mother and I have been living here for almost a month. We both like the environment here very much and plan to settle down here.\"","\"Settle down here?\" This was unexpected for Mo Jiuye.","In Dashun, the northwest was barren land, and the climate was not as good as that in the capital. Especially Xiling Village, it was not a particularly good place in the local area. He didn't know why Nan Rui would choose to settle down here.","Especially since he didn't believe that a prince who had enjoyed glory and wealth could get used to the life of ordinary people.","Seeing his doubt, Nan Rui was not surprised at all.","\"My mother and I didn't expect where we would settle down in the future. After living here recently, I feel that the people here are very simple. My mother also gets along well with Old Lady Mo. She won't feel lonely on weekdays, so I intend to live here for a long time.\"","Hearing Nan Rui say this, doubts arose in Mo Jiuye’s heart again.","Xiling Village did not belong to the Mo family. If Nan Rui wanted to live here for a long time with Consort De, he could directly choose a site to build a house, or buy a suitable yard from the villagers. There was no need to come and discuss it with him.","Seeing that Mo Jiuye still did not respond, Nan Rui continued: \"I see that your Mo family's yard is well built, and I also know that Hu Cong is helping to manage it. I came to find you two today to ask if you can ask Hu Cong to help build me such a yard.","Of course, I can buy the site from the government myself.\""]},{"number":328,"title":"Chapter 328: Where I live now is fine.","paragraphs":["This was the crux of why Nan Rui had come to find the Mo Jiuye couple.","In the past few days, the shape of the courtyard Mo Jiuye's family was building could be vaguely made out. The site of the courtyard was chosen to be next to a mountain and water, and its design was the most sensible yet warm one he had seen. If in the future he could live in such a place with his mother, spending his days writing poetry and painting, it would be a comfortable life.","He Zhiran immediately understood Nan Rui's intention upon hearing his words. She first thought that he must have already spoken to Hu Cong.","\"Has Brother Nan Rui already asked Brother Hu Cong?\"","Hearing this, Nan Rui appeared somewhat embarrassed as he pursed his lips.","\"Yes, I did mention this matter to Hu Cong, but he said the building method was researched by Consort De, he only helped with the construction. Whether I could also build such a courtyard would have to be asked after Consort De's opinion.\"","So that was how it was.","It was never going to be a secret that the quadrangle courtyard was designed by He Zhiran, the structure was very simple, and anyone knowledgeable could understand it at a glance.","Only the water supply, drainage and heating was known to Hu Cong alone, outsiders would not be able to learn even if they saw it.","Hu Cong was a down-to-earth person. He believed these were He Zhiran's property, and if the owner wanted to profit from them, it would be theft for the secret to leak through him.","Therefore, when Nan Rui approached him, he directly referred the matter to the Mo Jiuye couple.","He could help with the construction, but must have the homeowners' consent.","This was why Nan Rui had come to consult with the Mo Jiuye couple.","Xiling Village did not belong to the Mo family, so Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran naturally had no objections to Nan Rui building a house here.","\"Have you picked a location to build the house?\"","Asked this, Nan Rui smiled awkwardly.","\"The place I'm staying now is quite nice, at the foot of the mountain with a clear environment. I heard you bought that land, may I ask if you could transfer it to me?\"","He Zhiran rejected this without a second thought.","\"I'm afraid not, Nan Rui. I already have plans for that place, selling it to you would foil them.\"","That was the site He Zhiran had chosen for cattle and sheep pastures, with the haunted house's location being the cattle shed. If not for Consort De recovering her health there, Mo Jiuye would have demolished the building long ago.","They thought there was no hurry to demolish it with many matters at hand, they could bring it up with Nan Rui when the time really came.","They did not expect he had taken a liking to that place and wanted to purchase it.","He Zhiran would not compromise her plans for the sake of propriety.","Nan Rui was not annoyed at the rejection. He felt awkward making the request in the first place, seeing the Mo family's plans.","It would feel odd for an outsider to live amidst the large tract of land they bought.","While he truly liked the place, especially the lush unknown fruit trees on the hill that flowered and bore fruit, giving a sense of carefree joy just from looking at them.","Nan Rui also thought being close to the Mo family would make moving around more convenient in the future.","He never harbored high hopes of succeeding in buying the haunted house, just felt somewhat reluctant to give up without trying.","Since they disagreed, he would naturally not insist.","\"In that case, I will go look around the village, to see if there is a suitable place to build a house.\"","In any case, he was determined to live here from now on.","\"Very well, just look for a suitable location in the village. I will let Hu Cong know, if he is willing to help build your house, we have no objections.\"","He Zhiran did not oppose it herself, but could not make decisions for Hu Cong either.","Hearing He Zhiran say this, Nan Rui also felt somewhat relieved.","Seeing her reject his purchase of the house so decisively, he thought they would not be as accommodating as imagined.","He did not expect they would readily agree to help with the construction.","\"Since it is so, I will not disturb you further, and go look around the village right away to see if there is a suitable place.\"","As for Hu Cong's side, he was confident he could persuade him.","After leaving the Mo family, Nan Rui went straight to the Zhao Family Village Chief's home.","Although he had never lived among the common people, through recent observations, he also understood many matters.","To buy property in the village, asking the Village Chief for help was most appropriate.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran did not fret over Nan Rui purchasing a house site, what concerned them most now was their daughter Mo Hanyue's marriage.","It had to be said, Meng Huaining was truly impatient to bring a wife home.","They agreed on three days, yet he came asking for her hand in marriage after only two.","Meng Huaining was not low-key at all this time. Not only did he bring the matchmaker from Yuncheng, he also hired a band with drums and gongs. The thundering sound could be heard clearly from the village entrance.","Villagers came out one after another to watch the spectacle, but did not dare approach too closely, only craning their necks to see.","The County Prefect's face was gleaming with joy, behind him were people carrying chests draped in bright red silk banners, clearly indicating he had come to propose to some young lady.","The villagers went through all the unmarried girls in Xiling Village, but could not think who the County Prefect wanted to marry.","As the matchmaking procession had not gone far, they did not dare discuss loudly, only whispering to those next to them.","\"Look, the County Prefect is headed towards the village, in the direction of the Zhou family. Could it be he wants to propose to a Zhou girl?\"","\"That's impossible. The Zhou family doesn't have any outstanding girls. Look how refined the County Prefect is, which ordinary family could catch his eye?\"","\"How can you say that? The Zhou family has no special girls, but the Zhao family does?\"","Just as the two were on the verge of arguing, someone shouted, \"Look quickly, the matchmaking procession is going towards the Zhou family!\"","The Zhou family members rushed towards their home upon seeing this.","Their clansman was so tight-lipped, marrying the County Prefect without a word, leaving them anxiously guessing.","The crowd followed Meng Huaining's procession from a distance, eyes fixed on his movements.","Seeing he was close to the Clan Elder's home, someone could no longer restrain their elation.","\"Look, the County Prefect is going to the Clan Elder's home. Their granddaughter is sixteen this year.\"","The Zhao family looked on enviously, thinking the Zhou family's ancestors must be blessed for one of their girls to be chosen by the County Prefect.","But before they could rejoice too long, they saw the procession pass by the Clan Elder's home and stop at the Mo family's door.","Everyone looked at each other in dismay.","\"The County Prefect has gone to the Mo family.\"","\"It really is the Mo family.\"","\"Does the Mo family have a daughter of marriageable age?\"","\"Don't know...\""]},{"number":329,"title":"Chapter 329: Upper Beam","paragraphs":["It was also no wonder that those people did not know. When Mo Hanyue first came to Xi Ling Village, she had always followed the sisters-in-law around, wearing ordinary coarse cloth clothes that did not stand out at all in the crowds.","After settling down here, she basically never went out the front or back door, and when she recently went out to take care of the medicinal fields, she was also afraid of tanning her skin and had wrapped herself up tightly.","The Mo Family people also did not deliberately mention to outsiders that there was an unmarried daughter in the family, so the villagers were unaware that the Mo Family also had a marriageable daughter.","Seeing that the county magistrate had gone to the Mo Family in such a high-profile manner, even if they were still unclear about the Mo Family’s situation, they could not help but believe the facts.","Meng Huaining did not know that his high-profile proposal had aroused countless guesses among the villagers. At this moment, he was so nervous that his forehead was sweating.","When he arrived at the Mo Family’s door, Meng Huaining waved his hand to signal the drums and music to stop. He then walked into the Mo Family’s yard, followed closely by the smiling matchmaker he had invited.","The betrothal gift boxes were also carried into the yard in an orderly manner by the yamen runners.","It just so happened that today was the day that the roof ridge was going to be installed at the Mo Family's new house. All of the Mo Family members had gone there to watch it, even 8th elder brother who had an official position at the yamen had taken leave to be at home today.","Other than 4th elder brother who had limited mobility, there was no one else at home.","Having already heard the commotion outside, Mo Xiuyan unfortunately still could not get out of bed and walk around. He could only call out loudly from his room, \"Who is it?\"","Meng Huaining knew that the roof ridge of the Mo Family's new house was being installed today. He had deliberately come a day earlier to propose specifically in order to join in the lively event.","He often visited the Mo family and was not unfamiliar with where the Mo family members lived.","Based on where the voice came from, he could judge that it was Fourth Elder Brother speaking. Since he had limited mobility, it was normal for him to call out.","So Meng Huaining immediately knocked on Fourth Elder Brother's door, and said, \"Fourth Elder Brother, it's me, Meng Huaining. I came today specifically to propose marriage to Young Lady Mo.\"","Although Fourth Elder Brother had not participated in the discussions about Mo Hanyue’s marriage matter, his wife had told him everything she heard. Thus, Fourth Elder Brother also knew about this matter.","Although he did not have much interaction with Meng Huaining, if mother looked favorably upon this person, his character must be good.","\"Elder Brother Meng, please come in,\" he called.","Meng Huaining did not stand on courtesy and pushed the door to enter.","He first cupped his fists towards Fourth Elder Brother: \"Am I disturbing Fourth Elder Brother's rest?\"","Fourth Elder Brother waved his hands: \"No, no, Elder Brother Meng please sit.\"","Meng Huaining had come to propose, and had no intention to stay long since he was here merely out of courtesy to meet Fourth Elder Brother.","\"Fourth Elder Brother, where have all the family members gone?\" he asked.","Fourth Elder Brother had gone through this process himself when marrying his wife in the past. He personally went to deliver the proposal gifts and felt somewhat nervous and impatient at that time too.","Therefore, he could empathize with Meng Huaining’s current mood.","\"They have all gone to the new house over there, today is the roof ridge installation ceremony.\"","Meng Huaining cupped his fists again: \"Many thanks to Fourth Elder Brother for informing me, I will go over now to find everyone.\"","At this moment, he wished that he could immediately finish the proposal so that his heart would feel at ease.","After speaking, Meng Huaining directly led a few men to follow him to the Mo Family's new house.","The new house was quite some distance from the rented yard in the village, and the scene there was exceptionally lively. Even with Mo Jiuye's good hearing, he did not hear the drums and music of the proposal party.","Fifth Elder Brother had already hung the firecrackers. Sixth Elder Brother stood below with a lit match, just waiting for the auspicious timing to light the firecrackers.","The female family members were all crowded around Old Lady Mo at the front, waiting to watch the roof ridge installation ceremony.","Mo Jiuye stood at the back of the women, holding He Zhiran's hand with one hand and supporting her by the waist with the other, for fear that something might happen to his wife amidst the dense crowd.","Eighth Elder Brother stood at the back of the group responsible for maintaining order. When he turned around, he saw Meng Huaining coming over with some yamen runners.","He knew Meng Huaining had been busy over the last few days preparing to propose to his little sister. He had not even appeared much at the yamen, so Eighth Elder Brother was unclear why he had rushed over today.","Eighth Elder Brother walked over: \"Elder Brother Meng, why did you come today?\"","He remembered not inviting him to the family’s roof ridge ceremony!","Although Meng Huaining often visited the Mo family, he had never been to the Mo family's new house here. As soon as he walked in, he was attracted by the unusual shapes of so many different buildings. If he wasn’t still thinking about finalizing the big matter in his heart, he would definitely have walked around to take a careful look at these exotic houses.","Seeing his future older brother-in-law personally coming up to welcome him, Meng Huaining strode forward a few steps. \"Eighth Elder Brother, I've come today to propose marriage.\"","While the two were talking, Sixth Elder Brother had already lit the firecrackers hanging from the roof ridge over on his side. The deafening loud bangs drowned out the sound of everyone talking, so Meng Huaining and Eighth Elder Brother stopped chatting and both looked towards the roof ridge.","The roof ridge ceremony was not complicated. After setting off the firecrackers, Hu Cong said a few auspicious words to the Mo family. Then he instructed the workers to symbolically tap the roof ridge a few times with hammers, and the ceremony was considered completed.","In ancient times, the roof ridge ceremony required entertaining relatives and friends. The Mo family was no exception.","Although they had not been here long, they got along well with villagers from both the Zhou and Zhao families. They naturally also invited over the Fang and Xie families to liven things up.","As for Tang Mingrui, Old Lady Mo had seen that he had feelings for Mo Hanyue, and did not intend to get too close with him. Thus she did not notify him.","Similarly, she knew from Mo Chuhan that Meng Huaining had been extremely busy over the past two days preparing for the proposal. So she did not extend an invitation either.","What they didn't expect was that Meng Huaining had gotten ready much quicker than anticipated and rushed over to propose formally today.","With the ceremony over, a banquet was prepared for noon. The Mo family women were about to head to the kitchen to help out.","As soon everyone turned around, they saw Meng Huaining standing behind the crowd.","Not waiting for the Mo family to speak, Meng Huaining took the initiative to walk up and offer sincere congratulations.","“Congratulations, congratulations!”","After some polite remarks, Meng Huaining eagerly got to the point of his visit.","“I’ve already brought the proposal gifts today and invited a matchmaker. Old Lady Mo, when would it be convenient for you to propose marriage to Young Lady Mo?”","Meng Huaining was just asking a question he already knew the answer to. He knew the procedure for roof ridge ceremonies generally arranged the banquet at noon. The Mo family people should not be too busy at this time.","Eager to finalize her daughter's marriage matter as soon as possible, Old Lady Mo made a gesture of invitation and said, \"Official Meng, let's go speak of this in our home.\"","This was her daughter’s lifetime event, all of the elder brothers generously made way to participate.","Seeing that mother had agreed with Meng Huaining to go back home and discuss the proposal, several people followed along.","Mo Jiuye assisted He Zhiran and walked behind the group.","Back at the Mo family home, they directly went to Old Lady Mo’s main hall. Only then did Meng Huaining formally instruct those yamen runners to carry the betrothal gift boxes inside. He stood up respectfully and handed over a stack of papers to Old Lady Mo.","\"Esteemed Elder, please look over this list of proposal gifts I've prepared for Young Lady Mo.\"","Old Lady Mo casually flipped through them. They were all fine items. To call them fine items was to say they were good by Yun City standards. In the eyes of honored officials in the capital, they would not count for much."]},{"number":330,"title":"Chapter 330: Proposing marriage","paragraphs":["Old Lady Mo was very clear in her heart that Meng Huaining was clean as an official, and his family was also being suppressed by Emperor Shunwu. It was already not easy for him to prepare such a generous betrothal gift.","There must have been help from his clan, otherwise with Meng Huaining's salary, it would have been impossible to prepare a betrothal gift of this standard.","She was marrying off her daughter, not selling her daughter. No matter the amount, the betrothal gift represented the groom's sincerity. When the time came, she would carry the gift back along with her daughter's dowry.","As long as her daughter was well taken care of, nothing else mattered.","Moreover, Old Lady Mo had long seen through worldly possessions. The amount was just a token of his feelings.","If she really wanted her daughter to live in splendor and wealth, she could have married her to Tang Mingrui. Tang Mingrui's business was currently thriving, much more well-off than Meng Huaining.","Old Lady Mo had a kindly look on her face as she gently placed the list of betrothal gifts on the table next to her.","\"Meng is very thoughtful.\"","Meng Huaining saluted with clasped hands again, \"I hope the gift does not displease you, Old Lady.\"","He knew clearly in his heart that since Old Lady Mo did not raise any objections, it meant his prepared betrothal passed muster.","The matchmaker also understood the circumstances. It was time for her to make her entrance.","With a big smile, she came forward and introduced herself first.","\"Old Lady Mo, gentlemen, I am the official matchmaker of Yuncheng. Everyone calls me Matchmaker Liu. Today I have the fortune to be here on County Prefect Meng's invitation to propose to Miss Mo on his behalf.\"","Old Lady Mo smiled back, \"We are very grateful, please have a seat.\"","Matchmaker Liu did not stand on ceremony and sat down in a nearby chair. She then sang praises of Meng Huaining, as was customary.","Old Lady Mo had seen similar scenes many times, so she let the matchmaker talk.","After a long while, Matchmaker Liu finally got to the main point, \"Since Old Lady Mo does not have any objections, how about letting me take Miss Mo's birth date and time so I can select an auspicious date for the happy couple?\"","Speaking of wedding dates, Old Lady Mo had no intention of fully listening to the matchmaker because she was anxious.","\"Can we set the date ourselves?\"","Her words sounded like she was asking, but she was actually informing the matchmaker that she would set the wedding date herself.","The matchmaker was clearly surprised. She had been in this business for so many years, yet this was the first time she encountered something like this.","However, she was perceptive. She could see that Old Lady Mo had a domineering character and an imposing manner that she did not dare provoke.","Moreover, Prefect Meng had already said as long as the marriage could happen, everything else was fine. She need not insist on following every custom at the expense of someone's happiness.","\"Ohoho...that's not bad either. Does Old Lady have some good dates in mind?\"","These past few days whenever Old Lady Mo had free time, she would consult the lunar calendar. She had already picked out several good dates.","Most importantly, all these dates were before July.","\"If this marriage takes place, I plan to have Meng take Han Yue as his wife before July.\"","Old Lady Mo said this to Meng Huaining. For matters like this, only Meng Huaining's agreement carried any weight.","Meng Huaining did not know that Old Lady Mo would disregard custom and take the initiative to suggest potential wedding dates. Although he did not know her reasons, he believed that given Old Lady Mo's experience and wisdom, she would not make such a request without good cause.","Of course, he also was not in the habit of prying into other's private affairs. Besides, the issue of wedding dates was not a problem for him. In fact, the earlier he could take his beloved as his wife, the better.","Meng Huaining stood up solemnly, \"Since you are the elder, Old Lady, whatever you decide shall be.\"","Seeing that the concerned party had spoken, the matchmaker also stood up.","\"The old lady does have good foresight. I was about to say the same thing. This year is a leap year, so only the first half has auspicious days. The second half is not suitable for weddings.\"","Her words were pleasing to hear and set the Mo family members and Meng Huaining at ease.","Old Lady Mo nodded satisfactorily and asked, \"Since Matchmaker Liu puts it like that, are there any good dates before July this year?\"","As someone in this line of work, Matchmaker Liu had memorized the auspicious Yellow Calendar dates like the back of her hand.","\"Right now it's April. April 26 is on the Yellow Calendar. There's also May 8, June 12...\"","Old Lady Mo laughed to herself when she heard the dates the matchmaker listed. They were the same ones she had found in the Yellow Calendar.","Since the matchmaker's opinion aligned with hers, there was nothing more she needed to question.","The only thing left was to use the bride and groom's birth charts to determine if they were incompatible. As long as the result was not terribly ominous, they could choose a good date to make up for it.","This was Matchmaker Liu's first time seeing a family so anxious to marry off their daughter. She could also see that the County Prefect was very happy to do so.","Thus, she no longer offered her own opinion and quietly sat to the side, using the birth years and times on the bride and groom's charts to calculate their compatibility.","The Mo family and Meng Huaining also did not say anything more, silently waiting for the matchmaker's conclusion.","After scribbling away for a long time, Matchmaker Liu's expression grew happier and happier.","She put the charts down and excitedly stood up.","\"Congratulations to you, Prefect Meng, and to you, Old Lady. The charts of the bride and groom are naturally matching. It's simply a marriage made in heaven.\"","She paused, then continued animatedly, \"In all my years as a matchmaker, this is the first time I've seen such compatible charts. This union will go smoothly at every turn. Even if no special date is chosen, there will be no issues.\"","At this, everyone revealed looks of joy. Meng Huaining was especially thrilled and exclaimed \"Wonderful!\" three times.","Of course, the matchmaker's words gladdened all those present. But Old Lady Mo still wanted Meng Huaining to have the final say on the decision.","At least this would not violate too many customs, since the wedding date was ultimately the groom's choice.","\"Prefect Meng, when do you think would be good to take Han Yue as your wife?\"","Meng Huaining wanted to make Mo Hanyue his wife as soon as possible. The date he favored most was April 26.","However, it was already mid April. There were only ten days until that date, which would be too rushed to adequately prepare for the wedding and slight Miss Mo.","Moreover, his wedding required his elders to come preside over the ceremonies, which was impossible to arrange within such a short timeframe.","After thinking it over, he tentatively asked, \"What does Old Lady think about June 12?\"","He had many considerations. First, he needed to purchase a residence in Yuncheng. A married man could not keep living with his wife in the government offices.","After securing a residence, it would need redecorating to make it comfortable for his beloved.","With this timeframe, he would also have enough time to notify his elders to come preside over his wedding ceremonies without too much rush.","Overall, this was the most suitable timeframe.","Old Lady Mo would have no objections as long as it was before July.","\"Good. We'll go with what Prefect Meng suggests–on June 12, come and take Han Yue as your wife.\""]},{"number":331,"title":"Chapter 331: Dowry","paragraphs":["<Old Lady Mo>'s words had just fallen when <Mo Hanyue> walked in, her face flushed red.","\"Lord <Meng>, may <Mo Hanyue> make a request?\"","At this remark, everyone present except for <He Zhiran> was somewhat shocked.","What family's daughter would personally step forward to make requests about her own wedding?","<Mo Hanyue> really had no other option, so after thinking it over, she decided it would be best to speak out before the wedding.","Very quickly, <Old Lady Mo>'s face darkened as she said in a displeased tone: \"Hanyue, your wedding matters will be handled by your mother and eldest brother. What reason does a young lady like you have to step forward yourself?\"","Heaven knows it took <Mo Hanyue> an enormous amount of courage to come here. Now that she had already spoken, she had no reason to back down.","She stubbornly lifted her chin and said, \"Mother, <Mo Hanyue> has been learning medicine and herbology from <Ninth Sister-in-law> for over half a year now. I've just started trying to plant medicinal fields, and I hope that after we marry, Lord <Meng> can agree to come back here every day to help me tend to my medicine fields.\"","<Ninth Sister-in-law> said that no matter what you do, you have to see it through to the end and not give up halfway.","She truly enjoyed medicine and herbology, especially watching the medicinal plants she sowed with her own hands grow a little more day after day. That gave her a sense of satisfaction she had never felt since she was little.","Although she was also fond of <Meng Huaining> and willing to marry him, if that meant she could no longer continue doing what she loved, she would rather not marry for her whole life.","<Mo Hanyue> had just recently thought this through clearly.","Because <Meng Huaining> had brought up their wedding, she started thinking about the future.","Among the nine sister-in-laws in her family, apart from <Ninth Sister-in-law> who had her own will, the other eight sister-in-laws spent their days following routine in that kind of hopeless way.","That wasn't the life she wanted. She wanted to be like <Ninth Sister-in-law>, to have her own skills and through her own hard work, create more value.","At first, <Meng Huaining> thought that <Mo Hanyue> coming here meant she was unwilling to marry him!","He was so frightened his back was already drenched in cold sweat.","He didn't expect that the young girl's request would be this small.","He instantly felt relieved. Seeing that the future mother-in-law was about to scold her, he quickly stepped forward.","\"That's no problem. I was planning to get a residence anyway. If Miss Mo feels that West Ridge Village is suitable, I don't mind building a courtyard here just like the new Mo manor.\"","This was also one of <Meng Huaining>'s small intentions.","Today when he went to the foot of the mountain, he saw the new Mo manor. Its structure was very different from the norm, and it made people feel very comfortable after seeing it.","Moreover, he had no family or friends in Yuncheng, so he might as well satisfy his delicate wife.","If he happened to be very busy with work, <Mo Hanyue> would have her family to look after her, so he wouldn't need to worry either.","In fact, <Meng Huaining> hadn't seen the completed new Mo manor.","If he had, he certainly wouldn't have tried to find so many reasons to build a house here. Just the word \"comfortable\" alone would have made him choose to do so without hesitation.","Speaking of building the same courtyard, everyone in the Mo family knew that the beautifully unique new manor was all <He Zhiran>'s contribution.","Therefore, everyone's gazes landed on <He Zhiran> at the same time.","<Nan Rui> wanted to build the same kind of house and <He Zhiran> didn't object, so she was even less likely to have any objections to this future in-law wanting to build one.","\"Since Brother Meng has this intention, why don't we Mo family build it? We'll consider it one of Hanyue's dowries.\"","Over the past few days she had been thinking about what would be an appropriate dowry for <Mo Hanyue>.","She had just seen the betrothal gifts <Meng Huaining> sent, which were definitely sky-high in Yuncheng. This showed how much he valued <Mo Hanyue>.","Since this was the case, the Mo family couldn't lose etiquette either.","She had also asked the villagers about it. When the big families in Yuncheng married off their daughters, they would often send gifts like shops, houses, or manors as part of the dowry.","Since <Meng Huaining> liked living here, they might as well send him a courtyard just like the Mo family's.","Then later, preparing some jewelry and other items would complete <Mo Hanyue>'s dowry.","Although she had plenty of these kinds of things in her space, after all they were still 'dirty items'. If they accidentally caused unnecessary trouble it wouldn't be worth it, so <He Zhiran> planned to buy some different styles on Taobao Treasures.","Anyway, there was still around two months until their wedding date, plenty of time for her to prepare.","From <Old Lady Mo>'s understanding of her daughter-in-law, the Ninth Daughter-in-Law was generous and reasonable. Now that she was running the household, she naturally wouldn't shortchange <Mo Hanyue>'s dowry. The old lady never imagined that her daughter-in-law would offer to build an identical house with one remark.","One had to know, although the house didn't look like much from the outside, the construction costs were extremely high. Especially the glass used for the windows, which was purchased from foreigners. How could the prices be low?","Moreover, there was only so much of the stuff. Once it was used up, getting more wouldn't be easy.","The family had nine daughters-in-law. Even if the Ninth Daughter-in-Law was generous, it was hard to guarantee the other daughters-in-law wouldn't feel unhappy about something like this.","She couldn't disregard the other daughters-in-laws' feelings just for the sake of her own daughter's dignity.","\"This...\" Wasn't it a bit too extravagant?","<He Zhiran> knew what the mother-in-law was thinking. She was worried that <Mo Hanyue>'s dowry being too abundant might upset the other daughters-in-law.","<He Zhiran> had considered this before she spoke.","She thought that there was only this one young sister in the family. The amount of silver she had could be described as enough to rival a nation. She wouldn't care at all about the dowry she was giving <Mo Hanyue>.","Moreover, she didn't plan to withdraw this money from the public accounts.","\"Mother, my husband and I have already discussed it. Hanyue's dowry will be paid from our private funds, and won't touch the Mo family's public accounts.\"","Ever since settling down in West Ridge Village and starting to raise rabbits, <He Zhiran> had recorded the family's income and expenditures in a small notebook.","On the last day of every month, she would gather the family and make the account book public, and distribute wages to everyone. Of course, the wages were allocated based on work, so no one would have any objections.","<Old Lady Mo> knew the couple had a lot of money, but that was their personal assets. How could she tear down the east wall to mend the west, using her son's money to help her daughter?","But she wasn't an ignorant country woman who had never seen the world either. Now that the daughter-in-law had already spoken in front of the future son-in-law, there was no way she could kick the ball back.","\"Since that's the case, Mother has also saved up some private funds. I'll take it out to build Hanyue a house too!\"","The filial children in the family would all give her some of their wages every month, and she earned some herself from making dolls with the daughters-in-law. <Old Lady Mo> did have some savings.","But to build a courtyard like that, she was still worried it might not be enough. Thus, <Old Lady Mo> didn't speak with much confidence."]},{"number":332,"title":"Chapter 332: A Banquet","paragraphs":["He Zhiran knew that the old lady Mo was impartial in handling matters, so she hurriedly said, \"Mother, no matter who provided this silver, in short, one siheyuan courtyard is considered as part of Hanyue's dowry.\"","When Mo Jiuye saw this, he also echoed, \"That's right, Mother. This is nothing difficult. As long as Hanyue lives well in the future, we can really feel at ease.\"","His words were already very obvious, with the intention of threatening Meng Huaining.","As the elder brother, if his only younger sister was not treated well by her husband’s family in the future, he would absolutely not stand idly by.","Meng Huaining could naturally hear Mo Jiuye's implication.","He was marrying the girl he liked, so he would definitely treat her well for a lifetime, there was no doubt about this. He didn't need to guarantee anything either. He would prove it with actions in the future.","The most important thing now was the issue of their future home.","\"Old Madam, Ninth Brother, Ninth Sister-in-law, I can handle the matter of the house myself. I know you treat Lady Mo well, but such a heavy dowry is too much,\" said Meng Huaining.","He had never thought about what kind of dowry his future wife would have, after all, he was not clear about the Mo family's current situation.","On the surface, it seemed that the Mo family was not lacking money at the moment, but it was all earned by raising rabbits after going to Northwest.","Building such a nice house did not cost a small amount of money. He was marrying the girl he loved. The good days in the future were what he would strive for. He had never thought about the dowry.","This was also Meng Huaining's heartfelt words.","Mo Jiuye knew best that his wife had racked her brains these days to prepare a dowry for Hanyue. How could he possibly let Meng Huaining snatch it away now that his wife had finally decided on the dowry to give to the young aunt?","\"The dowry is decided by the bride's family. Hanyue's dowry has been set. Brother Meng does not need to feel pressured,\" said Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye gave others the impression that he was the type who had the final say. Therefore, Meng Huaining felt that it would be futile no matter how much he argued.","\"Since this is the case, I will not stand on ceremony with Ninth Brother.\"","At worst, he could set up a few more shops in the city for Mo Hanyue to offset the dowry.","Mo Hanyue did not know Meng Huaining's thoughts. Seeing that her goal had been achieved, she shyly lowered her head and said nothing more.","When Old Lady Mo saw the embarrassing atmosphere, she quickly said, \"Alright, today Mister Meng and Hanyue’s engagement has been settled. It is a joyous event. Coincidentally, the topping-out ceremony for our family’s new house is today. Everyone who comes to the Mo family today shall stay for the meal.\"","With this, she clearly told everyone present that the matter was settled and no one needed to say any more.","The Mo brothers were very perceptive. Hearing their mother's words, they quickly got up and invited everyone to take a walk around the new house while waiting for the banquet to begin.","Since her wish was fulfilled, Mo Hanyue did not want to appear too much in front of Meng Huaining either. She took the opportunity to go help her sisters-in-law.","What the Mo family did not expect was that the villagers had successively brought gifts before the topping-out banquet even began.","Their gifts were some homemade chickens, ducks and other items. The richer families gave fabrics, while the poorer ones also gave baskets of eggs.","For the villagers of Xi Ling Village, these were considered grand gifts. The Mo family would definitely remember each of these favors.","The villagers' arrival was unexpected. Fortunately, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran had prepared more ingredients. They hurriedly notified the kitchen to increase the quantity.","When it struck noon, tables and chairs brought by the villagers were placed all around the new house. After Old Lady Mo said a few words of thanks, everyone sat down around the tables.","At this time, Nan Rui also came with Consort De.","He had already given his gift early in the morning. He came now only wanting to show his support.","Moreover, he had also decided to live in Xi Ling Village in the future. He could not always stay indoors. It was necessary to get acquainted with these villagers. Today was a good opportunity.","Meng Huaining had not seen Nan Rui before, but with his perception he could determine that these two people had extraordinary bearings and were definitely not ordinary merchants or commoners.","Also, seeing the old woman being very familiar with Old Lady Mo, he could ascertain that the two families were deeply connected.","Whether the visitors were of high status, since the Mo family did not take the initiative to introduce them, he would not probe.","The Mo family had many secrets. Just the fact that so many deceased brothers had successively come back to life was something difficult to accept.","Especially at the beginning, when he came here at Fei Nanyu's request to tell him the news that the eighth young master of the Mo family was alive, Fei Nanyu had thought he was lying.","On the contrary, later when he found that he had fallen in love with the Mo family's girl, he knew that it would be best if those nobles in the capital were unaware of these secrets of the Mo family. So he deliberately concealed it.","Now when he sent messages to Fei Nanyu, he only said that the Mo family had settled in Xi Ling Village and were participating in farm work, and had accepted such a life. There was nothing else.","Meng Huaining did not recognize Nan Rui, but Xie Tianhai and Fang Chuanzhou also recognized him.","Having been officials at court for many years, they frequently saw Nan Rui face to face.","When the two of them turned around today, they saw that familiar face.","The two were instantly scared into a cold sweat, and even hoped they had made a mistake in recognizing the person.","However, they did not recognize the wrong person.","Nan Rui had brought Consort De to the banquet scene. He first scanned the surroundings. Although he had been living in Xi Ling Village for a long time, he had never met Xie Tianhai and Fang Chuanzhou face to face before. He had also instructed the Mo family not to reveal that he was here.","Today he chose to appear completely because he had made up his mind to live an ordinary life like the Mo family in the future. Therefore, he was no longer hiding his presence.","Just as Xie Tianhai and Fang Chuanzhou were about to kowtow to Nan Rui, Mo Jiuye reached out quickly to stop them.","Mo Jiuye whispered, \"Uncles, pretend you don't know that person. I will slowly explain it to you later.\"","Hearing Mo Jiuye say this, they immediately understood, although they were still a little apprehensive.","However, they were also scheming people. They would not show it too obviously.","The two quickly adjusted themselves, no longer looking in Nan Rui's direction, but sitting down with the villagers instead.","Seeing this, Nan Rui nodded gratefully to Mo Jiuye, then was called over by Old Lady Mo to dine at her table.","With the guests seated, Mo Chongyuan thanked everyone on behalf of the Mo family again before the banquet officially began.","Because Meng Huaining was present, the villagers were somewhat restrained. Facing such good food, they did not dare to praise loudly, and could only silently lower their heads to eat.","Xie Tianhai and Fang Chuanzhou were not afraid of Meng Huaining, but they saw that Prince Rui was somewhat reserved. So after hurriedly eating some food, the two left in a hurry.","As for why the Prince was here, it was not their position to inquire. Thus, the two took their curiosity away with them."]},{"number":333,"title":"Chapter 333: Furniture","paragraphs":["The banquet at the Liang's residence continued until the early hours of the morning, and the guests gradually took their leave.","He Zhiran had accomplished all that he had set out to do on this trip, and since the Mo family was busy dealing with the aftermath, he no longer had any reason to stay. He bid his subordinates and the matchmaker farewell and departed.","The Mo family was kept busy until nightfall, utterly exhausted by the time they finally went back to rest.","The next morning, Hu Cong asked Mo Jiuye to go with him to survey the land at the foot of the mountain.","Now that they needed to build another courtyard residence of the same style to give to He Zhiran's younger sister, the original plans would require some modifications.","Fortunately, the vacant land west of the courtyard complex was space that Hu Cong had intended to reserve for future workshops. Since there was ample room, losing the area for one courtyard residence was not an issue.","Once they determined the location, the couple went that very day to inform Hu Cong and explain their desire to build another identical courtyard residence there, hoping that the speed of construction could be faster, ideally completed at the same time as the Mo family's courtyards.","Having already mastered the techniques for building courtyard residences, and with excess materials still available, Hu Cong saw no issue with an expedited timeline.","Thus, he readily agreed.","Thanks to the plentiful labor and prepared materials, there was no reason for delays to the construction timeline of the courtyard residences. Hu Cong estimated everything could be completely finished within another month.","Without modern harmful substances like formaldehyde, newly built houses in ancient times could be moved into as soon as some furniture was made after construction was complete.","Speaking of furniture, He Zhiran felt they could begin preparations on that front as well.","Most modern furniture was custom-made, which meant tailoring pieces to fit the size and layout of the intended space.","The style could be uniform, but the dimensions had to be appropriate - that was the crux of bespoke furniture.","Moreover, He Zhiran found the ancient furniture impractical and not very aesthetically pleasing.","Thus, she also planned to personally design the furniture.","Though calling it design was rather shameless given her lack of talent in that area.","Either way, originating distinct items in this era that also came from her hands meant she could brazenly claim to have designed them.","After settling on the arrangements, He Zhiran returned to her workshop and sketched out on paper all the furniture designs she could think of that seemed reasonable.","Nan Rui still had not moved out of the haunted house, and construction on the cattle shed Mo Jiuye planned to build could not yet begin, so there were relatively fewer matters to handle over the last couple days. This left him free to accompany his wife.","Oblivious to Mo Jiuye's desires, He Zhiran sat engrossed at the desk in her workshop, wholly focused on sketching furniture blueprints, while Mo Jiuye surrounded her, preparing various freshly cut fruits piece by piece and feeding them to her.","Gazing at his wife's cherry-like red lips parting open and closed, Mo Jiuye couldn't help swallowing.","By his tally, it had already been over two months since his wife discovered her pregnancy, which meant two months of abstinent celibacy for him.","He even felt an urge to hold his wife in intimacy again as they once had. But seeing her protruding belly, he endured...","Unaware of Mo Jiuye's lust, He Zhiran had unknowingly designed many modern-style pieces of furniture.","She had considered some ancient conventions as well, aiming for a perfect blend.","For instance, the exterior and color of the wardrobes could not be as novel as modern ones, made of natural wood, but the structure leaned more modern.","The sliding doors were designed nearly flush with the ceiling's height, with small built-in drawers inside for knickknacks.","And there was the bed in the bedroom. He Zhiran disliked ancient step-up beds where entering and exiting would be inconvenient for the occupant at night.","Thus, she designed a modern wood-frame platform bed, with storage space underneath and ornately carved headboard in an antique style.","There were also desks and chairs, similarly of a minimalist modern style, giving an overall refined and elegant appearance.","Of course, there were also a few lazyboy recliners, non-existent in this era, which would require a skilled artisan to figure out.","After a cold shower, Mo Jiuye returned to see his wife carefully reviewing the fruits of her labor blueprint by blueprint.","The furniture styles were nothing novel to Mo Jiuye. Between his wife's online store and the odd furnishings of the clinic, he had long become inured to eccentric designs.","He had worried initially that basing the furniture on those styles would be too unconventional, and nearly advised against it for fear of dampening her enthusiasm.","But now things were well, the furniture perfectly suited his aesthetic - the more he looked, the more pleasing it was to the eye.","\"Wife, this bed is great, very similar to the one in your workshop, yet the antique style of the headboard doesn't seem out of place.\"","Having earned such an evaluation, He Zhiran felt her efforts had not been in vain.","\"Since you find it suitable, there's no issue.\"","In short, this would be the furniture used for their new home.","As for whether others would like this style, that depended on their own taste.","If they found it unsuitable, they could opt for furniture in the style of this era.","After reviewing the blueprints again and mutually agreeing there were no problems, the couple left the workshop.","The first person they thought of for producing novel furniture was still Hu Cong.","This was because He Zhiran had seen with her own eyes the wooden seeders he invented. She had examined the craftsmanship closely at the time and noted the intricate workmanship.","Although Hu Cong was currently busy helping the Mo family build houses and had taken on Nan Rui's business, he had always been receptive to fresh ideas.","Just like with the furniture drawings He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye showed him today - once again expanding his horizons.","Moreover, he fully appreciated the aesthetic appeal and practicality of these designs.","By now, Hu Cong had quietly made a decision that after finishing the Mo family affairs, he would buy a plot of land in the village like Nan Rui and build a similar courtyard residence for himself. And if He Zhiran permitted it, he also planned to use her furniture designs to furnish it.","Taking advantage of the family gathered for dinner, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye showed the new furniture sketches and asked if any of them needed such novel furnishings.","The sisters-in-law had always been supportive of everything He Zhiran created. Even without seeing the drawings, they would have no objections. Moreover, they truly found the little sister-in-law's designs ingeniously unique. Placed in a room, the pieces not only looked beautiful but seemed highly practical.","Though the women had made up their minds, they would not voice opinions before the old matriarch spoke first.","Thus, all eyes uniformly fell on Old Lady Mo.","Having lived most of her life, Old Lady Mo was long accustomed to those rules and proprieties. Even during her banishment to the northwest frontier, she still clung to those ingrained old customs, especially regarding furnishings, which were considerably strict in prestigious households.","Wardrobes inside the rooms had to be opened from the top and carved with lotus patterns, said to attract wealth.","And she had slept most of her life on a step-up bed, an essential barrier of modesty between man and wife."]},{"number":334,"title":"Chapter 334: They asked for the whereabouts of Xiling Village.","paragraphs":["Just like most aristocratic families in the capital city, when the master and his wife show courtesy to each other like Zhou Gong, the maids and servants would be waiting outside the door. After the master finishes, he would call them in to serve them. Under such circumstances, the master inside the bed could lower the curtain. If anything was needed, the servants just needed to pass it in through the curtain.","Although now that the Mo family has come to Xi Ling Village to live, they are not bound by so many rules and etiquette, those rules are still unshakable in the mind of the conservative old lady. Of course, she would not interfere with things that her children couldn't accept just because she herself couldn't accept them.","She saw that her daughters-in-law were all waiting for her to comment. She said indifferently, \"I'm old now and cling to the past. I still prefer the original style of furniture. If you like them, feel free to use them.\"","With the mother-in-law's word, the sisters-in-law could no longer hold back.","The second sister-in-law hurriedly grabbed He Zhiran’s arm, \"Sister-in-law, I like these new styles of furniture. Let's use this kind of furniture for the new house.\"","The third sister-in-law said excitedly: “Sister-in-law, I really like the furniture you designed. They will look very good when placed in the room in the future.”","The eighth sister-in-law pushed Mo Chuhan next to her and said, \"Dear, we also want this kind of furniture.\"","Mo Chuhan nodded, \"Well, whatever you say.\"","In fact, even if his wife hadn’t said so, Mo Chuhan would have chosen this new style of furniture anyway.","If he were say who in the family he most admired now, it would be his ninth sister-in-law. Everything she came up with was surprisingly good, beyond everyone's imagination.","Seeing this, the fifth, sixth, and seventh sister-in-laws also asked their husbands for opinions. Everyone agreed that they would choose the new style furniture for their future new houses.","Only the fourth sister-in-law, her husband was still recuperating in the room. She couldn’t wait to borrow the drawings and went back to ask her husband Mo Xiuyan’s opinion.","Needless to say, Mo Xiuyan also liked the new style furniture.","As for Mo Hanyan, the little girl was still a little shy, and only said, “I’ll leave it to ninth brother and sister-in-law to decide.”","The meaning was obvious. She also wanted the new style furniture.","So in the Mo family, only old Lady Mo’s new house didn’t need the new style furniture. He Zhiran was clear on this.","There was plenty of timber in her space. She could go in at night to chop and then process it into finished wood using the console. Then she would find a chance to deliver it to the yard they rented in the city.","This would not only save costs, but more importantly, also save Mo Jiuye the trouble of purchasing.","The couple were go-getters. That night, they chopped a large amount of pear wood in the space. The next day, they got up early and said they were going into the city to buy wood before heading to Yun City.","The carriage arrived smoothly at the yard they rented in the city.","With a thought, He Zhiran arranged all the finished wood processed in the space and placed it in the yard.","It was impossible to buy wood in such a short amount of time. In order not to arouse suspicion from the family, the couple planned to walk around the streets.","There were many pedestrians on the street. Mo Jiuye parked the carriage properly and led He Zhiran around, strolling leisurely.","Although desolate compared to other places, Xi Bei was still relatively prosperous in Yun City.","As they walked hand in hand along the busiest street, shop assistants were soliciting business in front of the shops on both sides. Some commoners were also selling goods produced by their families on the roadside.","There was an endless stream of pedestrians coming and going. Only two men caught Mo Jiuye’s attention.","When those two walked, they looked around, occasionally inquiring the stall owners by the roadside.","It was common for there to be outsiders coming and going anywhere, but the meticulous Mo Jiuye noticed a big problem.","Although the two men wore Da Shun people's clothes with their hair coiled up in a bun like the Da Shun people, and wore kerchiefs like the commoners, the shoes under their cheongsam gave away their identity.","Mo Jiuye was very familiar with the South Border. He knew that the South Border people believed in witch gods, and witch gods were born on the first night when the moon was in a crescent shape.","Therefore, South Border people used the crescent moon as a symbol for the witch god. They would embroider crescents on clothes, hats or even shoes and socks.","It was precisely because Mo Jiuye discovered this that he realized those two men had unnoticeable crescent moons embroidered on their shoes.","Seeing her husband staring at those two nondescript men, He Zhiran asked, \"Dear, is there something wrong with those two?\"","Mo Jiuye replied in a low voice, \"They are from the South Border.\"","\"South Border?\" He Zhiran was obviously very shocked.","It should be known that the South Border was far away from Xi Bei, and Xi Bei was where the most barren areas of Da Shun were located. For them to come to Da Shun, they must have had some purpose other than just visiting such a place.","The two walked over to the stall owner the South Border people had just asked about earlier, acting as if nothing had happened.","He Zhiran took some coins out of her space and asked the man softly, \"Brother, what did those two ask you just now?\"","The stall owner happily took the coins and whispered: \"They asked about the whereabouts of Xi Ling Village.\"","Upon hearing this, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran immediately became vigilant.","For South Border people to ask about Xi Ling Village, they could think of no other reason than to find the Mo family.","Looking at those two men, they were already walking in the direction of Xi Ling Village.","He Zhiran knew that with her bulky body now, Mo Jiuye would be neglecting her safety if he kept worrying about her. Following those two men carefully would be difficult.","\"Dear, follow them first. I'll go to the government office to find eighth brother and ask him to hurry over with the carriage to take me back.\"","If she hadn’t mentioned the eighth brother, Mo Jiuye would never feel assured letting her go back alone. Moreover, the government office was near, which made him feel more at ease.","\"Alright, there are many people on the street. Don't wander around yourself. Go to the government office to find eighth brother. I may also need help.\"","There was no time to delay. Mo Jiuye exhorted her for a bit before tightly following those two South Border men.","He Zhiran did not wander off but went straight to the government office.","She happened to arrive just as Mo Chuhan was returning from patrolling with a group of people.","\"Sister-in-law, weren't you with ninth brother buying wood? Why did you come here alone?”","He Zhiran felt it was inappropriate to talk about this in front of so many officers.","\"Eighth brother, let’s talk over there.”","Mo Chuhan knew something was wrong. Otherwise, the meticulous ninth brother wouldn’t have left the ninth sister-in-law alone. He dismissed the officers and walked with He Zhiran to the side of the government office.","\"Sister-in-law, what on earth happened?”","\"Eighth brother, just now in the market, we discovered two sneaky South Border men. They were asking about the location of Xi Ling Village. My husband was worried there would be trouble at home, so he secretly followed them.”","When he heard the words South Border men, Mo Chuhan instinctively clenched his fists.","The person he hated most now were the South Border people because the perpetrator who had persecuted countless Mo men was Mr. Si Meng from the South Border.","Moreover, not long after the ninth brother and sister-in-law had just rescued three elder brothers from the South Border, South Border men suddenly appeared in Yun City asking about the whereabouts of Xi Ling Village. This couldn’t help but make him extremely vigilant."]},{"number":335,"title":"Chapter 335: Two People from Southern Xinjiang","paragraphs":["<Mo Chuhan> although was angry, he had not completely lost his senses and could not leave his pregnant younger sister alone here.","Besides, he also believed in his ninth younger brother's skills to easily handle two <People of Southern Frontier>.","<He Zhiran> knew things were not as simple as <Mo Chuhan> thought.","If those two <People of Southern Frontier> were really sent by Mr. <Si Meng>, even if their martial arts skills were not great, they would at least be people who knew how to use poison.","Otherwise, with Mr. <Si Meng>'s vigilant personality, he would not have sent people this far to the northwest without some special skills.","Therefore, she hoped Eldest Brother would hurry and catch up to <Mo Jiuye> and <He Zhiran>'s footsteps. If those two <People of Southern Frontier> tried any tricks, it would be safer with her there too.","The two fetched a carriage and rushed in the direction of <Xi Ling Village>.","Seeing his sister-in-law's belly was so big, Eldest Brother did not dare drive the carriage too fast, he could only keep the pace smooth and steady.","Fortunately, those two <People of Southern Frontier> were walking to <Xi Ling Village> on foot without using any lightness kungfu, so their speed was ordinary.","The carriage quickly caught up to them.","At this time, they were on the road to <Xi Ling Village>, with farmland from nearby villages on both sides. The villagers were all busy at this time, so the road was deserted.","Hearing the sound of horse hooves, <Mo Jiuye> looked back and saw it was Eldest Brother driving the carriage to catch up.","He lightly leapt up and sat next to Eldest Brother.","<Mo Chuhan> pointed to the two people not far ahead and asked, \"Is it them?\"","<Mo Jiuye> nodded lightly, \"Mm, it's them.\"","Hearing this, <Mo Chuhan> handed the reins to <Mo Jiuye>.","\"I'll go catch them.\"","Even if Eldest Brother had not caught up now, <Mo Jiuye> was already planning to take action.","This was the most sparsely populated area on the road to <Xi Ling Village>.","Therefore, <Mo Jiuye> did not stop Eldest Brother's actions, but still gave a reminder, \"Be careful of their tricks.\"","Although Eldest Brother was the most rough and impulsive among the brothers, he had also suffered losses from <People of Southern Frontier> before, so he would naturally be more vigilant.","\"Don't worry, I'll be careful!\"","It had to be said, Eldest Brother's martial arts skills were indeed the best among the brothers. <He Zhiran> lifted a corner of the carriage curtain, and in the blink of an eye, he was behind the two <People of Southern Frontier>.","The <People of Southern Frontier> seemed to also sense something wrong and were about to turn around to respond, but Eldest Brother reacted even faster. He kicked and sent one man flying, then swiftly grabbed the other man who was just about to reach into his clothes to take something out.","<Mo Jiuye> also noticed the Southern Frontier man's gesture to take something out and worried Eldest Brother would be in danger, so he immediately stopped the carriage at the roadside and flew over.","The two brothers moved as swift as lightning, not giving the <People of Southern Frontier> any chance to react.","Almost at the same time, each brother controlled one man.","It was somewhat unbelievable that the <People of Southern Frontier> were captured so easily.","Especially when facing <Mo Jiuye>'s handsome face that seemed to be frosted over, they froze in place.","The older <Person of Southern Frontier> quickly eased his nervousness.","\"Who...who are you? Committing violence in broad daylight, I will report this to the officials!\"","When it came to reporting to officials, Eldest Brother almost laughed out loud.","He was in a hurry to catch up with Ninth Younger Brother and had not changed out of his <Da Shun> government officer uniform.","\"I am the official. If you have any grievances, just say it.\" As he spoke, he deliberately straightened his chest to make the 'official' character on his chest clearer.","The <People of Southern Frontier> had only seen a portrait of <Mo Jiuye> and were not familiar with <Mo Chuhan>.","After recognizing <Mo Jiuye> earlier, tension appeared in their hearts for a moment, making them overlook <Mo Chuhan> who had made the first move against them.","With this reminder, the two finally noticed that this person was wearing the uniform of a <Da Shun> government officer!","\"So what if you're an official? We didn't break any laws.\"","Seeing the man was still stubborn, <Mo Chuhan> found it even more amusing.","However, like <Mo Jiuye>, he also had no intention of wasting words with them.","The two brothers tacitly knocked out one man each without giving the <People of Southern Frontier> a chance to react.","Seeing this, <He Zhiran> also got out of the carriage and had the brothers carry the <People of Southern Frontier> onto the carriage.","She knew clearly that although this place was rarely visited by people, they could not guarantee no passersby would show up in broad daylight.","Besides, the things they wanted to inquire were quite sensitive matters, so they had to be more prudent.","<Xi Ling Village> was not far away now. <Mo Jiuye> supported <He Zhiran> to sit outside the carriage compartment while <Mo Chuhan> followed alongside the carriage using lightness martial arts.","Entering <Xi Ling Village>, the carriage slowly drove into the courtyard they were renting.","It happened that Fifth and Sixth Eldest Brothers were chopping firewood in the front yard. Seeing Ninth Younger Brother had returned, and Eighth Eldest Brother who should have been at his government job had come along too, they immediately sensed something was amiss.","Fifth Eldest Brother put down his ax and came over to ask, \"Eighth Brother, how come you came back too? No errands at the yamen?\"","<He Zhiran> knew <Mo Jiuye> did not plan to interrogate the two men at home, and it was not possible to bring her along, so she directly returned to her own room.","<Mo Jiuye> lifted a corner of the carriage curtain to show Fifth and Sixth Eldest Brothers.","\"Fifth Eldest Brother, Sixth Eldest Brother, we discovered two <People of Southern Frontier> inquiring about <Xi Ling Village>'s whereabouts, so we captured them and brought them back.\"","When it came to <People of Southern Frontier>, the Mo brothers could be said to harbor the same enmity.","Heaven knows how much they detested <People of Southern Frontier>, moreover, <People of Southern Frontier> coming to <Yun City> to inquire about <Xi Ling Village> was undoubtedly targeting their Mo family.","\"Ninth Younger Brother, how do you plan to deal with these two?\" Fifth Eldest Brother asked.","\"These two were knocked unconscious by Eighth Brother and me. They will wake up soon. I plan to take them to the mountain cave to interrogate them.\"","Sixth Eldest Brother agreed, \"Good, no time to delay. Let's go over now.\"","After the brothers discussed, they silently brought the two men to the mountain cave that was previously used by those medicine men to recuperate injuries.","<Mo Jiuye> was already prepared against the tricks of <People of Southern Frontier>. As soon as the brothers threw the two men on the ground, he went over to search them.","These two were quite rich, he actually found a thousand taels worth of silver notes on them.","Apart from that were a few thumb-sized porcelain bottles. There was definitely something like poison powders stored inside.","<Mo Jiuye> took away those items without worry that his brothers would be in danger. He walked forward and fiercely kicked the two men a few times. The two <People of Southern Frontier> gradually woke up.","When they saw the four formidable men before them, their bodies instinctively tried to shrink back.","Sixth Eldest Brother and Eldest Brother simply did not give them a chance to react. In one swift movement, they pressed the two men down firmly.","\"Don't struggle if you don't want to suffer torment.\"","The two <People of Southern Frontier> were indeed obedient. Hearing Eldest Brother's shout, they did not dare to move at all, continuing to pretend to be ostriches.","In fact, they had already quickly thought up ways to escape in their minds.","The older <Person of Southern Frontier> saw that the people in front of him did not continue to act. His eyes darted around before reaching into his clothes.","As a result, when he touched around, there was nothing there. The self-defense drugs they brought had been taken away..."]},{"number":336,"title":"Chapter 336: What did he send you here for","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye smiled ambiguously as he walked up with the porcelain bottle he had taken from them in his hand.","\"Were you looking for this?\"","\"Uh...\"","\"This is...\"","Seeing the thing that was protecting their lives in someone else's hand, the two felt extremely troubled.","Mo Jiuye sneered and put away the porcelain bottle in his arms. Then he went straight to the point and asked, \"Who sent you to Yuncheng?\"","As he was asking, Mo Chuhan had already drawn out his waist saber and held it against the neck of the older Nanzheng man.","The Nanzheng man was so frightened that cold sweat streamed down. Although they had some martial arts skills, they had just felt that the skills of the people in front of them were far above theirs, especially Mo Jiuye, who was once the war god of Da Shun. They simply had no chance to make a move.","If they did not admit their Nanzheng identity, there might still be a ray of hope for survival.","\"Good sir, spare me... We are commoners of Da Shun, not Nanzheng people!\"","It had to be said that when this older Nanzheng man spoke, there was really no accent that could be heard at all. He sounded completely like a person of Da Shun.","Even so, no one would believe his words.","Mo Chuhan moved the saber against his neck again. The Nanzheng man could already feel a hint of chill. If the saber moved a bit more, it would probably draw blood.","\"Good sir, spare me... I really am not a Nanzheng person.\"","Mo Chuhan snorted coldly, \"Humph! Still being stubborn when facing death. I will let you experience a fate worse than death.\"","As he spoke, he had already shifted the position of the big saber in his hand. It went straight to cut off one ear of the older Nanzheng man.","\"Ahhhh!\" The Nanzheng man yelled out in pain. He reached up to cover where his ear used to be, looking at Mo Chuhan in horror.","At this time, Mo Chuhan had already raised his saber again, aiming at his other ear.","Seeing this, the Nanzheng man pleaded incessantly, \"Good sir, spare me... I will tell you everything I know.\"","Hearing him say this, Mo Chuhan did indeed stop his movement.","Unexpectedly, taking advantage of the few seconds when he paused, the Nanzheng man actually rushed straight towards his big saber.","It was too late for Mo Chuhan to dodge. The big saber stabbed right into the Nanzheng man's chest without deviation.","Seeing this, Mo Jiuye was afraid that the other Nanzheng man would also commit suicide. He dashed over like lightning and controlled the man.","Fifth Brother and Sixth Brother also followed Ninth Brother's footsteps and surrounded the surviving Nanzheng man.","Now the surviving Nanzheng man could not commit suicide even if he wanted to. He was increasingly terrified. At one point, he even wanted to cover his ears, but his hands and feet were all under control so he could not move at all.","\"What exactly do you want to do?\"","Mo Jiuye sneered, \"As long as you are willing to answer my questions, I promise you will die without pain.\"","\"Can I not die?\" The horrible death of his companion was still fresh in his mind. As a survivor, who would be willing to die if they could live properly?","\"No.\" Mo Jiuye's reply was very decisive.","Hearing this, the survivor's body shuddered. At the same time, he felt a stream of warmth between his legs...","Mo Chuhan turned his head in disgust, \"How foul.\"","Fifth Brother and Sixth Brother had also never seen such a scene before. They did not expect that someone could actually lose control of their bladder because of fear.","Fifth Brother said impatiently, \"Ninth Brother, hurry up with the interrogation.\"","Before his voice fell, Mo Chuhan had already raised his saber again, the blade tip pointing at the Nanzheng man's face.","The Nanzheng man was so frightened that his face lost all color. \"Don't kill me, I'll talk, I'll tell everything.\"","After saying this, he looked at them again, thinking that they did not refute him, which meant they agreed not to kill him.","Mo Jiuye did not care about this person's thoughts at all. He asked in a deep voice, \"Speak, who sent you here?\"","\"It... it was Mr. Si Meng.\"","\"I knew it was him!\" Mo Jiuye gnashed his teeth and said. Then he exchanged glances with his brothers.","The brothers all hated Si Meng. Hearing his name, they clenched their fists.","Mo Jiuye took a deep breath and continued to ask, \"What did he send you here to do?\"","\"His treasured pet went missing. He sent us to look for it.\"","Speaking of Si Meng's treasured pet, the first thing that came to Mo Jiuye's mind was the golden eagle in his wife's space.","His wife had told him that the little thing usually looked like an ordinary white dove. But when it needed to carry out tasks or encountered danger, it would reveal an eagle-like mouth.","It seemed that Si Meng cared a lot about the little thing.","But now was not the time for him to think about those things. He needed to ask for some useful information.","\"Where is Si Meng now?\"","This was the key point that the Mo brothers desperately wanted to know.","\"I don't know...\"","\"Dare to say you don't know, I'll take your life right now!\"","Before the Nanzheng man could finish speaking, Mo Chuhan's big saber was already pointing at the top of his head. If he continued to say he didn't know, he would surely be split in half.","The Nanzheng man was so frightened that tears came out. He pleaded over and over, \"Good sir, spare me... I really don't know about Si Meng's whereabouts.\"","From his reaction, it was not difficult to see that he was not lying.","Mo Jiuye still had other questions to ask. He was afraid Eighth Brother would kill the man on impulse, so he could only remind him.","\"Eighth Brother.\"","Hearing Ninth Brother's reminder, although Mo Chuhan did not move the saber away, he also had no intention of striking down. It still remained above the Nanzheng man's head.","Taking this chance, Mo Jiuye came forward to ask, \"If you don't even know about Si Meng's whereabouts, how do you take orders from him? \"","In order to survive, the Nanzheng man had racked his brains to think.","He hoped that he could analyze and find out about Si Meng's whereabouts to give them an explanation.","After thinking it over, he decided to lay bare everything he knew.","\"I was arranged by my master to gather intelligence within Da Shun's territory. My master once said that if Si Meng asked us to do something, we must obey.\"","Hearing this, Mo Chuhan couldn't wait to ask, \"Who is your master?\"","\"My master is Nanzheng's Empress Yun Li.\" The Nanzheng man answered very readily, apparently not intending to lie.","Speaking of Yun Li, she was the one killed by Mo Jiuye. He actually had a lot of questions to ask.","The Nanzheng man in front of him could not leave this place alive anyway, so he had no misgivings.","\"Isn't Yun Li already dead?\"","The Nanzheng man was obviously very surprised to hear this. \"You said my master is dead?\"","Mo Jiuye sneered, \"She died by my hand long ago.\"","The Nanzheng man was shocked. No wonder his master had not given him any tasks for so long.","But at the moment, he felt that the most important thing was still his own life. Therefore, he did not dare to actively inquire about the details.","Seeing that he said nothing, Mo Jiuye continued asking, \"Since your master is dead, how did Si Meng order you to act?","Also, how many eyes like you did Yun Li arrange within Da Shun's territory?\""]},{"number":337,"title":"Chapter 337: My own wife, I love dearly by myself.","paragraphs":["The man from Southern Xinjiang answered very honestly: \"As far as I know, there were only the two of us. We had been in the capital all along. Whenever there was new information, we would send a homing pigeon to deliver a letter back to Southern Xinjiang.\"","Hearing this, the several Mo brothers also came to understand one thing.","In the past whenever the Mo Family troops went on campaigns, by the time they reached the borders, the other side would already know very clearly which Mo Family general was leading the troops and the size of the forces.","Without a doubt, there were Southern Xinjiang spies in the capital.","The brothers had submitted petitions to Emperor Shunwu on multiple occasions, urging him to pay attention to this matter and send more people to uncover the Southern Xinjiang spies.","At that time, in order to get the Mo Family to protect his regime, Emperor Shunwu still took their words seriously to some extent.","But despite sending many people to investigate, nothing was ever found.","They didn't expect that these two spies from Southern Xinjiang would be caught by chance in the northwest.","Thinking of this, the Mo brothers hated the men before them even more.","However, the brothers all knew that before taking revenge, they still had to get to the bottom of what they wanted to know.","Mo Jiuye continued asking: \"Yun Li has been dead for so long. Didn't you notice anything amiss with the homing pigeons?\"","What he meant was, with Yun Li having died such a long time ago, it was impossible they hadn't sent any messages back and forth.","And from the looks of this man from Southern Xinjiang, he didn't seem to have noticed anything wrong with that.","\"Our mistress often leaves the palace. She has trusted palace maids in the palace. We mostly send letters through them. If the mistress isn't there, the maids will bring the messages directly to the Emperor.\"","Now the issue made sense. Besides, for the Mo brothers, who was responsible for receiving messages on the Southern Xinjiang side was of no importance anyway.","Mo Jiuye kept pressing: \"How does Mr. Si Meng give you orders to do things? Where do you hide out in the capital?\"","\"We live in Yong'an Alley in the capital. There's a big tree in front of our residence. We put a bird's nest in the tree where Master or Mr. Si Meng would leave us notes whenever they had tasks for us.","As long as we're in the capital, we check it every day to see if there are new assignments.\"","As native residents of the capital, the Mo brothers were extremely familiar with Yong'an Alley.","It was called Yong'an or \"Perpetual Peace\" Alley because it was built by Yong'an, the only non-royal Prince in Da Shun’s founding.","Prince Yong'an had no descendants. Before his death, he took all his wealth and transformed the area into countless housing units for homeless commoners to live in.","After hundreds of years of wind and frost, it had become the most chaotic part of the capital.","These two really knew how to hide. With the messiness of Yong'an Alley, no wonder Emperor Shunwu had sent so many people who failed to find them.","Of course, this also had to do with their disguises and intentional concealment.","Mo Jiuye felt he had seen enough to know that given Mr. Si Meng's prudence, even his disciple didn't know his whereabouts, let alone these two men who were temporarily utilized.","But he still had to ask everything clearly.","\"Did Mr. Si Meng ever say how you should deliver the pet to him after finding it?\"","The man from Southern Xinjiang shook his head. \"He didn't say how to deliver it to him. If we find that pet, we must bring it back to the capital to raise temporarily while awaiting his next order.\"","\"He ordered you to do things for him. It's impossible he didn't give you any benefits in return, right?\" Mo Jiuye kept pressing.","Hearing his words, the Southern Xinjiang man's gaze inadvertently fell on the slightly bulging spot on Mo Jiuye's chest.","\"It's the purse you took. Inside was the method he gave us for quickly raising Gu worms.\"","When Mo Jiuye had searched the two men earlier, there was indeed an inconspicuous little purse that he had casually squeezed, thinking it contained cash, so he didn't examine it closely.","Now that the man from Southern Xinjiang mentioned that purse, he took it back out from his bosom.","Indeed inside the purse was not money but a piece of paper covered in writing.","Seeing that it did record things related to Gu worms, it meant this man from Southern Xinjiang wasn't lying.","Mo Jiuye pondered briefly, feeling he couldn't think of any other questions.","So he nodded at the elder brothers who were raring for revenge.","The elder brothers immediately understood his meaning.","Although this man from Southern Xinjiang didn't personally persecute the Mo Family men, he did play an instigating role. Therefore, some torture was necessary.","At this point Mo Jiuye had already formed an idea in his mind and had no interest in following the elder brothers to torture this man from Southern Xinjiang.","After signaling to them, he walked out of the cave amidst the screams of the Southern Xinjiang man.","He guessed that it was very likely Mr. Si Meng was hiding in the Da Shun capital, otherwise he wouldn't have thought to send two spies stationed in the capital to the northwest to look for the Golden-winged Sculpture.","If these spies did manage to find the Golden-winged Sculpture, they would certainly bring it back to the capital. Wouldn't it be very convenient then for Mr. Si Meng to retrieve his beloved pet?","The more he pondered, the more plausible it seemed. At the same time, the notion to hurry to the capital and investigate also arose in him.","But this was no trivial matter that required careful planning.","As the screams grew fainter, Mo Jiuye was lost in thought, pondering his plan. Unknowingly, he had arrived at the foot of the mountain.","He Zhiran was worried the two men from Southern Xinjiang were stubborn and the Mo brothers wouldn’t be able to get any useful information out of them. So she had slipped away without notice when her family wasn't paying attention and come here alone.","As a result, she happened to run into Mo Jiuye walking down the mountain, lost in thought.","\"Ranran, what are you doing here?\"","Seeing his wife, Mo Jiuye rushed over to her at first notice and carefully held onto her.","Seeing his nervous manner, He Zhiran felt a warmth in her heart.","Even in modern times, she really hadn’t seen any husband treat his pregnant wife so carefully and tenderly.","\"I'm fine. Don't worry. Besides, you've seen those pregnant village women still working hard with the men!\"","\"I don't care what others do. When it comes to my wife, I worry for her myself.\"","Having been doted on like this from the time she became pregnant until now, He Zhiran was already used to it. Her previous words were pointless.","\"Did you manage to ask anything useful?\" She changed the topic.","Mo Jiuye supported her as they walked, recounting what they had asked.","He Zhiran’s first reaction was the same as Mo Jiuye’s - they both felt Mr. Si Meng was likely in the capital.","At the same time, He Zhiran also guessed Mo Jiuye’s thoughts.","\"Are you thinking of going to the capital?\"","Mo Jiuye heavily nodded. \"I do have this plan.\"","He Zhiran knew her husband was not the rash type. Since he had made this decision, he must have considered it thoroughly.","Besides, Mr. Si Meng was currently the Mo Family’s biggest enemy. If they could find him earlier, Grandpa and Eldest and Second Brother could also reunite with their families sooner."]},{"number":338,"title":"Chapter 338: Let's talk about this.","paragraphs":["Only is, Si Meng Sir not only poison technique fierce, in hand also domesticates these many gu insects, Mo Jiuye if meets him, can do the safe and sound?","This is she most cares about the issue!","Now she is pregnant, even if on own initiative propose to follow the husband together, he is also impossible to agree.","Does not have herself at side, He Zhiran total feels Mo Jiuye meets Si Meng Sir's odds of success are not big.","But she also knew, this matter even if involves dangerously, Mo Jiuye also will decide goes.","Looks like, she also needs to prepare well that is, most basic, gives the husband to use to protect life the thing to need complete.","\"This matter do not worry first, that two southwestern person appearances just arrived Northwest, even if Si Meng Sir in capital city wait for their news, knows is impossible too quickly, we also some time, lets me think how can help you.\"","Mo Jiuye knew, daughter-in-law than him clever, situation also has many can dissolve the Si Meng Sir method, therefore has not rejected.","\"Good, this matter we discussed slowly.\"","Now he had the delicate wife, soon can also become two child's fathers, he does not think has any flash.","Returns to the family, two people then entered the space.","He Zhiran first has thought of that only golden eagle, that small thing already by Rice Ball docile returned to primitive consciousness, thinks certainly in heart recognizes the master still to be Si Meng Sir.","Does not know Rice Ball whether has the skill to let it recognize Mo Jiuye is the master.","Thus, Mo Jiuye leads it together goes to the capital city to look for Si Meng Sir, will be easier.","Thinks to want immediately to carry out, this is the He Zhiran disposition.","She called in the bamboo forest sleepy Rice Ball, first was the flattery gave it some delicacies, said: \"Rice Ball, can you let that only golden eagle recognize him is the master?\"","Rice Ball black slick eyes looked at Mo Jiuye, immediately revealed an arrogant appearance.","However quickly, it also hugged He Zhiran's small leg.","He Zhiran knew, the little fellow this appearance is asking for a reward to oneself.","She has extended the hand to touch the head of Rice Ball, the gentle voice said: \"Treasure is clever, finished the matter to certainly have the reward.\"","The Rice Ball round brains in master leg rub gently, then strides the small short leg to run toward that golden eagle.","Does not know is the space regarding biology nourishing function or how, that only golden eagle looks like compared with just arrived the He Zhiran hand is more plump.","The small thing sees Rice Ball to run over, suddenly makes one vigilant the condition.","Obviously Rice Ball often bullied it frequently.","Rice Ball seems the interest rises suddenly, intentionally made one to bare fangs and show claws the appearance to the golden eagle, has gotten angry the golden eagle suddenly to explode the feather, the curved mouth blade has extended suddenly, the wing the following golden feather also occasionally revealed.","Very obviously, the small thing vitality heavy by Rice Ball, if not in the cage, feared that already started to attack.","Rice Ball sees the small thing to explode the feather, also happily toward it shakes the buttocks.","That appearance, making He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye who stood watches unable to smile.","They contacted were long with Rice Ball, all knew its disposition, made it do any matter, looked like the child, oneself played enough only then can carry on.","Really, when Rice Ball golden eagle startling begins to send out the anger roar the noise, it only then became serious.","Only sees Rice Ball to wield two fluffy small claws, to the golden eagle symbolic, the mouth likely the human talked fluently issues one string \" correct correct correct \" calling out sound.","The golden eagle initial also in resisting, gradually was actually defeated, quickly has then put away the eagle general sharp mouth, crawls in situ, the vision when Mo Jiuye looks. The god likely flatters!","Mo Jiuye by this startled dull.","He asked He Zhiran: \"Ranran, Rice Ball this succeeded?\"","He Zhiran has not replied him immediately, but opened the cage to put out the golden eagle.","The golden eagle came out from the cage, fluttered the wing to fly toward Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye very coordinated has raised an arm, the golden eagle steadily fell above.","Mo Jiuye heart inexplicable rising sense of achievement, he happily said: \"Ranran, you quickly have a look, this small thing should recognize me is the master.\"","His words fell, the golden eagle called one likely the coordination very much, making Mo Jiuye more happy.","Rice Ball sees itself to complete the task successfully, not only has not obtained the master's praise for a long time, the attention falls above that small thing unexpectedly, suddenly feels wronged to hug He Zhiran's thigh, that appearance must many wronged have many wronged.","How He Zhiran is possibly makes own heart treasure wronged, hurriedly sat in the lawn to appease.","\"Rice Ball clever, you are most.\"","The words arrived, she had already taken away a small jar honey as the reward to give it.","Sees the honey, the Rice Ball mood finally has cheered up, released the master thigh, hugged the small jar to roll the crawling to run.","Mo Jiuye at this moment is trying to communicate with the golden eagle.","He casually pulled off a leaf, integrates an aura to throw toward the distant place.","\"Little White, takes back the leaf.\"","The golden eagle does not know itself also has a name called 'Little White', but it can distinguish, is the master issues the instruction to oneself.","The Mo Jiuye sound falls, the golden eagle then opens the wing to fly fast toward that leaf, subsequently in the space port whirlpool falls back to the Mo Jiuye arm again, while is biting that leaf the eye wink does not wink looked at Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye has extended the hand before it, the small thing then spits the leaf in his palm.","\"Ranran, Little White really has the spirituality.\"","He Zhiran smiles: \"You decided to call it Little White?\"","\"If not reveal that golden feather, it is only the snow white entirely pigeon, called Little White to be very good.\"","Mo Jiuye very optional, he thought calling Little White to speak smoothly, simply has called.","He explained a sentence, then could not wait to excavate the Little White other attainments.","Finally two people discovered, Little White can only listen to Mo Jiuye a person's speech, so long as is not the instruction beyond the scope, it can achieve.","Mo Jiuye has touched the Little White smooth small brains: \"Little White, can find Si Meng Sir depends entirely on you.\"","Through a moment ago test, Mo Jiuye understood Little White's skill.","It can seek the person through the smell.","It happens to, just obtained the card case that Si Meng Sir has given from that two southwestern person searches, had this, he can let Little White seek the Si Meng Sir whereabouts in capital city.","At the same time he also guessed, Little White after all was Si Meng Sir raised for many years the pet, it also possibly also remembered the past master.","Depends entirely on these two points, he thinks the hope is very big to seek Si Meng Sir.","The Little White matter does, He Zhiran looked at the time, already approached nightfall, to prevent the family member to knock on a door the nobody to respond, two people can only leave the space temporarily.","Five elder brothers they just came back from the mountain at this time, happen to meet the Mo Jiuye couple.","He Zhiran already saw that two southwestern person, therefore the brothers several speech time has not hidden the truth from her."]},{"number":339,"title":"Chapter 339: Never a Safe Day","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye asked: \"Have all the bodies been taken care of?\"","Eighth Brother answered, seemingly a little disappointed: \"This guy, I just chopped off one of his arms and he got scared to death. There wasn't even enough time to dispose of the bodies before taking revenge...\"","Mo Jiuye couldn't help but chuckle: \"That kind of person is clearly afraid to die. If he's dead, then he's dead.\"","Fifth Elder Brother knew what Mo Jiuye wanted to ask: \"We threw those two bodies in the back mountain.\"","Speaking of the back mountain, Mo Jiuye had never been there before.","From what those villagers said, it was the place the Barbarians came from when they lacked food and clothing, going over the front mountain and entering Xi Ling Village.","Since his elder brothers had already been there, Mo Jiuye felt it necessary to inquire about it.","\"Fifth Elder Brother, when you went to the back mountain, did you discover any suspicious traces or special markings?\"","Based on many years of combat experience, when Mo Jiuye had led troops and wanted to sneak into the enemy's interior first, he would send scouts ahead to scout the route and leave markings.","According to the villagers of Xi Ling Village, the Barbarians would come to harass them once every year or two. It would be impossible without leaving markings in those deep mountains.","The elder brothers had all heard about the Barbarian harassment.","Therefore, when the meticulous Fifth Elder Brother went to the back mountain, he made a point to observe carefully.","This was also something he was eager to tell Ninth Younger Brother about.","\"Ninth Younger Brother, I discovered traces of burning wood there, and in addition, animal furs and bones. I guess someone must have recently been there, hunting game to survive. As for other markings and such, I really didn't find any. Besides, we were afraid of worrying our family by coming home late, so we didn't linger there for long.\"","Sixth Elder Brother also stepped forward and said: \"We guessed that it was quite likely Barbarians wanting to come raid Da Shun, but they discovered plenty of game there and gave up on the idea.\"","Mo Jiuye nodded: \"That's not an impossibility. After all, those who come to raid are Barbarian commoners, what they want is just something to eat. If they can find something to fill their stomachs, they probably wouldn't want to take the risk and come here.\"","He paused, then continued: \"In any case, we must be vigilant. This year there is little rain, and there may be a drought. If it weren't for the river in our village, and everyone working hard to carry water to irrigate the fields, I'm afraid even the crops would be doomed.\"","\"Here we are only separated from the Barbarians by one mountain. If they have nothing to eat, it's very likely they will come in groups to harass us.\"","Now the new house had just begun to take shape, and various industries were also being prepared.","Especially since he had planted so many crops, and there were over a thousand rabbits.","Before long, poultry and livestock like chickens, ducks, cows, and sheep would also begin to take shape on a large scale for raising. It would be a pity if they couldn't take care of them and they were stolen.","\"Don't worry Ninth Younger Brother, starting tomorrow, we brothers will take turns going over there to keep watch. If anything happens, we'll be able to discover it in time.\"","If it was up to letting the elder brothers take turns keeping watch, Mo Jiuye didn't have that intention at all.","In his view, why use an ox knife to kill a chicken?","The dogs trained in his wife's space were completely capable of doing it.","Of course, in the next few days Fan Tong would first need to issue orders for them to get used to it, then they would naturally take the initiative to patrol on their own.","He Zhiran's thoughts were the same as Mo Jiuye's. Amidst the brother's discussion, her consciousness had already entered the space.","Just now when they had Fan Tong tame Xiao Bai, she hadn't paid attention. Not a single one of those dogs had appeared, they must have been manipulated by the little guy to go establish rules somewhere.","Her consciousness searched around in the space, and sure enough, all those dogs were sitting neatly in a row at the foot of the mountain, not daring to move an inch.","If it weren't for several elder brothers present, He Zhiran would have laughed out loud.","Fan Tong was really not bored in the space.","As for those dogs, they had grown a lot bigger. She estimated after another two or three days, they would be able to officially start work after leaving the space.","...","The original plan was for Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran to use the morning to buy lumber as a cover, prepare it, then arrange for transport back home.","Unexpectedly, they had run into two Southerners in Yun City, and as a result, delayed their plans.","It was Old Lady Mo who first remembered this at dinnertime.","\"Jiuye, how did things go with buying lumber in the city?\"","The old lady had long since refused to worry about matters in the household. Now she only wanted to contribute some effort like her daughters-in-law.","It was just that she felt something was off with the sullenness today. Mo Chuhan, who usually loved to tell everyone about handling cases at the yamen when he got home, was unusually quiet today.","Old Lady Mo guessed that something must have happened today, which was why she brought up the matter of buying lumber.","The elder brothers hadn't intended to tell their family about capturing the two Southerners. After all, it wasn't a pleasant matter.","But they understood their mother's disposition very well. If she hadn't noticed anything amiss, she wouldn't have asked questions at the dinner table.","Mo Jiuye had originally planned to prepare everything and tell them when setting off for the capital.","Since his mother had asked, he simply told her some of it.","\"Mother, the lumber has been prepared. I was planning to arrange for transport back home this afternoon, but unexpectedly, we ran into two Southerners in Yun City asking about the whereabouts of Xi Ling Village...\"","Mo Jiuye informed his mother about today's events. This way, he wouldn't need to explain his trip to the capital again.","Of course, he didn't give details on how those two men died, only saying that the elder brothers had already taken care of it cleanly.","After hearing his story, not only his sisters-in-law, but even the usually composed Old Lady Mo was no longer calm.","\"That Si Meng is truly relentless. As long as he's around, my Mo family will never have a peaceful day.\"","Seeing his mother's state, Mo Jiuye knew that she was also thinking of a way to go to the capital and look for this person.","He took the opportunity to say: \"Mother, I'm planning to go to the capital in a few days. I don't want to give up even the slightest clue.\"","When Ninth Younger Brother said he was going to the capital to find Si Meng, the elder brothers stood up, ready to fight.","\"If we're going, we brothers are going together,\" said Eighth Brother.","Even Seventh Elder Brother, whose health hadn't fully recovered, was anxious.","\"That's right, going to the capital is no trivial matter. Ninth Younger Brother can't go alone. If we're going, we brothers should go together.\"","\"No, with our sensitive identities, it would draw too much attention with more people. I plan to go investigate alone first.\" Mo Jiuye strongly disagreed.","Old Lady Mo did not approve of this. Before the other sons could object, the old lady spoke up.","\"Jiuye, that Si Meng is extremely skilled at covering his tracks, clearly a sly man. Not only that, he also wields many crooked skills. Without someone watching your back, I'm afraid it won't do.\"","Fifth Elder Brother also agreed: \"Mother is right. The others can stay home, Fifth Elder Brother will accompany you there.\""]},{"number":340,"title":"Chapter 340: It's absolutely fine to take care of a home.","paragraphs":["The other few brothers were anxious when they saw Fifth Elder Brother take care of everything for him and Ninth Younger Brother.","\"That won't do. We brothers should go together,\" Eighth Brother said urgently.","\"In case there is news about father and two elder brothers, there are many of us brothers who could leave at any time,\" Sixth elder brother said.","Just when Seventh Elder Brother wanted to say something, Old Lady Mo spoke again.","\"Alright, stop arguing. I'll decide this matter. It will be Jiuye, Chongyuan and Jingnian, three people going. Chu Han stays at home working, and Yuan Ce, your health hasn't fully recovered yet, so stay and take care of the family.\"","Old Lady Mo had the final say, and Mo Jiuye could not refute.","The Seventh and Eighth brothers at home felt very frustrated, but they knew clearly in their hearts that mother had always been uncompromising. Things she decided would not be changed.","But it also made sense to think about it. There were so many women in the family. If all the men left, it would be a great loss if danger was encountered.","He Zhiran had not expressed her opinion all along, because she felt that her mother-in-law's arrangement was very reasonable and spoke to her heart.","The other sisters-in-law and Mo Hanyue were extremely nervous, but they knew clearly that they had no say in this kind of thing. They could only pray in their hearts that the brothers going to the capital would return safely.","The trip to the capital city was already on the agenda. He Zhiran had to speed up preparing supplies.","After dinner, she entered the space and did not rest for a moment, preparing a large number of self-defense items for the brothers.","Bulletproof vests were essential. There was not only the unpredictable Mr. Si Meng in the capital city, but also Emperor Shunwu.","In case they encountered a battle, this thing could save lives.","There were also some special weapons, such as mini pistols, tranquilizer guns, stainless steel daggers, mini crossbows, grenades.","When in danger, these weapons could not only save lives, but also do great things if necessary, such as grenades that could flatten a place...","In addition to these, the most important thing was realgar to prevent gu worms and some antidotes.","Speaking of antidotes, there was a little bit of extract left from the dead gu worm last time. He Zhiran added some precious medicinal materials and made it into a universal antidote pill according to the book.","With antidote there had to be poison. Although it was not a good thing, it could come in handy at critical moments.","In addition, there were sufficient banknotes. She had already raised several thousand-mile horses in her space that could serve as their means of transportation.","As for how to explain the source to the two elder brothers, it was not something He Zhiran should consider. Mo Jiuye would naturally have a way to explain clearly.","Although the items were prepared, Mo Jiuye did not intend to leave immediately.","According to the time calculation, those two Southerners should have just arrived in the northwest. Whether they could successfully find the golden eagle would take some time.","The cunning Mr. Si Meng would also plan the time for them to return to the capital to check the results.","Therefore, he planned to set off a few days later.","He might as well take advantage of these few days to transport the timber back from the city.","This kept him busy for three days. All the little puppies in He Zhiran’s space had grown to adult size, and they were trained by Rice Ball to be more obedient than military dogs. Once they were released, they could directly guard the house.","Of course, there had to be a proper reason for the appearance of so many dogs.","Now He Zhiran didn’t need to worry about things like this. Mo Jiuye had already figured out the excuse.","That was, they were bought from herders in other cities through some channels.","In fact, he and He Zhiran were just being paranoid. They didn't know that the family had long been used to such strange phenomena.","Especially those simple-minded sisters-in-law in the family, they not only did not feel strange, but also secretly admired the ability of the ninth younger brother and his wife in their hearts.","After the dogs were brought home, Mo Jiuye arranged for some of them to patrol the mountain.","Preventing the Barbarians from invading was one aspect, and the main reason was that many of the fruit trees planted on the mountain had bloomed and fruited, and it was hard to prevent some people with impure thoughts from coveting them.","With the dogs guarding, even though they couldn't drive bad guys away, at least they could send a signal to the family.","Also, rabbits sheds and farmland were assigned a certain number of dogs to guard and patrol.","The Mo brothers were all military men. Although their army did not raise military dogs at the time, the Southern Borders had an extremely powerful military dog team.","In their understanding, those military dogs were even more fierce than wolves, and many Da Shun officials had suffered losses from those military dogs.","And so, the Mo brothers were very interested in these seemingly well-trained dogs.","Seventh Elder Brother was the one staying at home to guard, so he took the initiative to take over the management of these dogs.","It only took a day before Seventh Elder Brother went happily to find Mo Jiuye.","“Ninth Younger Brother, have these dogs received any training before?\"","When Mo Jiuye heard Seventh Elder Brother ask this, he couldn’t help laughing to himself.","Weren’t they trained?","They were trained by a chubby rice ball.","Although he was sarcastic in his heart, he couldn’t say that when answering Seventh Elder Brother.","“Seventh Elder Brother, these dogs have indeed been trained by someone. Guarding the house is definitely no problem.”","\"Not only can they guard properly, I see they are more capable than the military dogs raised by Southerners,\" Seventh Elder Brother praised again.","Mo Jiuye was interested and raised his eyebrows. \"Oh? How capable?\"","He had seen Rice Ball establish rules for those dogs in his wife's space, but he hadn't seen the abilities of these dogs himself. Hearing what the Seventh Elder Brother said, he also wanted to understand in detail.","When Seventh Elder Brother thought of the scene he saw today, he felt amused.","\"Today I saw at the foot of the mountain that those dogs seem to have a leader. As long as the leader barks, they will line up in neat rows and then go up the mountain orderly.","Also, those dogs watching the crops maintain the same distance between each other. As soon as strangers approach, they will surround them collectively.","The ones guarding the rabbits shed are even more amazing. They can even help catch escaped little rabbits.\"","Mo Jiuye was also shocked to hear this. He didn't expect dogs could be trained like this.","\"Hehe... Maybe the dog trainer has some special means. This is great. We will feel more at ease in the future.\"","Seventh Elder Brother nodded. \"Yes, it really is. Now that you and Fifth Elder Brother are going to the capital, I alone can keep the family safe more easily.\""]},{"number":341,"title":"Chapter 341: Find a pet, send it to the Nine Kingdoms","paragraphs":["Three days' time, Mo Jiuye tried to arrange the things that needed to be done by himself at home.","The next day, the three brothers got up before dawn, fully armed and ready to go.","The three rode on the thousand-mile fine steeds raised by He Zhiran's space, whipped up their horse whips and galloped away.","After Mo Jiuye left this time, He Zhiran couldn't do many things without getting his hands dirty.","For example, communicating some details about the house and furniture with Hu Cong, and she also had to keep an eye on the growth of the crops at all times.","He Zhiran's move really worried the old lady Mother He.","She specifically called Lan Er to accompany her all day.","He Zhiran knew that if she didn't let Lan Er accompany her, the old lady would probably not feel at ease, so she had to reluctantly accept it.","Although she felt that there was nothing wrong with her body, who knows if there will be any accidents?","Lan Er is attentive and observant, and it's good to have her by my side.","Time passed bit by bit, and in the blink of an eye, Mo Jiuye and his brothers had been away from Yuncheng for more than half a month.","The brothers whipped their horses and, if nothing unexpected happened, they should have arrived in the capital by this time. I wonder if everything went smoothly for them?","Although He Zhiran spent every day busy, she was inevitably worried about him when she was alone at night.","She stroked Rice Ball's furry head with one hand in the space, and put the other hand on her bulging belly and whispered softly.","\"Kids, do you think they've already arrived safely in the capital?\"","At this time, the only one who could answer her was Rice Ball.","\"Hmm hmm hmm...\"","\"I hope they come back safe and sound.\"","\"Hmm hmm hmm...\"","...","The capital.","Yong'an Alley.","At night!","Mo Jiuye and his three brothers were standing under a tall and sturdy tree.","\"Ninth Brother, this should be the big tree the Southerners talked about.\"","\"In that case, the yard where they are hiding is right in front of us.\"","Hearing the two elder brothers analyzing there, Mo Jiuye did not respond.","Because he could feel that Little White, who was carrying the cage, was a little uneasy and kept walking around.","He took off the black cloth covering the cage and asked softly, \"Little White, did you find anything?\"","Little White fluttered its wings lightly twice, then let out a not very loud chirp.","Through contact with Little White, Mo Jiuye knew that it was confirming what he said.","Before entering the capital, Mo Jiuye had let Little White smell the purse obtained from the Southerners, and told it to remind him as soon as it detected the smell.","Little White's recent behavior was obviously to alert him that there might be a similar smell nearby.","Mo Jiuye looked around and eventually his eyes fell on an inconspicuous place in the treetops.","In the moonlight, you can see a bird's nest there.","If it was an attentive person, he would definitely find something wrong with the bird's nest.","Normal bird nests are usually built on sturdy tree trunks, while that bird's nest is at the top of the tree.","Mo Jiuye handed the cage to Fifth Elder Brother, then used qinggong to lightly leap up and landed on the tree trunk closest to the bird's nest.","He did not rashly remove the bird's nest, because he was not sure if Mr. Si Meng would come, and once he moved things here, it would inevitably arouse the other's suspicion.","He just probed towards the bird's nest, trying to make himself see more clearly.","After all, it was night time, and the inside of the bird's nest was pitch black. No matter how good Mo Jiuye's eyesight was, he couldn't see the situation clearly.","So he took out the mini flashlight that his wife had prepared for him from his arms.","The flashlight was not the kind of strong light. When the switch was turned on, a soft yellow light would appear.","The reason why He Zhiran prepared such a flashlight for Mo Jiuye was because the light from this flashlight was not very conspicuous. Seen from a distance, it would only be regarded as a small night pearl or something.","Although it was such illumination, it was enough for Mo Jiuye.","Using the flashlight, he observed the inside of the bird's nest.","The inside was clean and tidy, even the grass used to make the nest was neat and tidy, without any sloppy traces. It was obvious that this bird's nest was man-made rather than natural.","This was already within Mo Jiuye's expectations, and he didn't find it strange at all.","However, in his opinion, this thing could not be flawless. Although it was man-made, it was not guaranteed that a bird would take advantage of it and stay there for a while.","So Mo Jiuye probed closer to the bird's nest again, reaching out into it.","This time, there really were new discoveries.","There was a thin partition at the top of the bird's nest. If he hadn't put his hand in, it would have been invisible to the naked eye.","Mo Jiuye carefully put his hand in and touched something like paper.","He took out the paper and looked at it under the light of the flashlight.","There was only one line of small words on it—","Take any pet found to the Ninth Prince's Mansion.","Mo Jiuye narrowed his ink-colored eyes, then put the note back in its original place and jumped off the tree.","\"Ninth Brother, what's going on?\" Seventh Elder Brother asked.","\"There was a note in the bird's nest that read: Take any pet found to the Ninth Prince's Mansion.\"","\"What?\"","\"The Ninth Prince's Mansion??\"","Fifth Elder Brother and Seventh Elder Brother were equally incredulous.","Speaking of the Ninth Prince, the Mo brothers were no strangers.","The Ninth Prince was the only prince in Da Shun who was of the same generation as Emperor Shunwu. He was also Emperor Shunwu's foster brother.","He was similar to the current Prince Rui at that time. He never participated in the struggles in the court. Therefore, he dispelled many suspicions of Emperor Shunwu. Since they were brothers, Emperor Shunwu did not kill him but conferred him the title of the Ninth Prince and let him stay in the capital.","The Ninth Prince usually lived a low-key life. Even when there was turmoil in the court, he was nowhere to be seen.","Emperor Shunwu also had some fraternal feelings towards him. Usually the stipend he gave was enough for the Ninth Prince to live a life of luxury and leisure.","The note just now could basically be determined to have been written by Mr. Si Meng. What the brothers did not expect was that the Ninth Prince, who usually kept a low profile, was actually colluding with Mr. Si Meng.","It seemed that Da Shun would soon face a bloody storm.","For the Mo brothers, this was too unexpected. Of course, they knew clearly in their hearts that this had nothing to do with them.","\"Ninth Brother, should we plan to go to the Ninth Prince's Mansion to look for someone?\" Fifth Elder Brother asked.","Although the Ninth Prince looked aloof from the world on the surface, after all he was still a prince. The guards in his mansion must be strict. If they wanted to go there to look for someone, they had to be fully prepared.","\"We must go to the Ninth Prince's Mansion, but we have to do so only when we are sure we can succeed. If we rashly go there and startle the snake, allowing him to escape, it would be a great loss.\" Mo Jiuye analyzed.","Sixth Elder Brother also echoed, \"That's right. It was hard to get a clue. We must find the person.\"","Mo Jiuye did not respond immediately. He looked at the cage in Fifth Elder Brother's hand.","He took the cage and lifted the black cloth cover."]},{"number":342,"title":"Chapter 342: Why didn't you go to the Nine Kings House earlier","paragraphs":["\"Xiaobai, the success depends on you,\" said the master.","Xiaobai seemed to understand the master's words and responded with a soft call.","Fifth Elder Brother and Sixth Elder Brother didn't understand Ninth Younger Brother's actions. They didn't believe that Xiaobai's response was merely a single call.","They were even more skeptical that Xiaobai, who was originally Mr. Si Meng's beloved pet, could become Ninth Younger Brother's companion just by being tamed by Fan Tuan.","After all, Xiaobai had spent more time with Mr. Si Meng, and if they were to meet the original owner, there was a possibility that Xiaobai would recognize him as the master again.","Mo Jiuye was unaware of the concerns in the minds of his two older brothers. At this moment, he was calculating the time.","They had rushed from the northwest to the capital city, using fast horses and pushing themselves for half a month.","If those two men from the southern border successfully arrived in the northwest and found Xiaobai, they would undoubtedly make their way back to the capital city at the fastest speed.","Of course, Mo Jiuye was calculating for the shortest possible time.","Even if those two men from the southern border reached the northwest, it was unlikely that they would immediately find Xiaobai. Therefore, he planned to delay the time a little further so as not to arouse suspicion.","\"Fifth Elder Brother, Sixth Elder Brother, let's temporarily suspend our actions these few days. We'll find a place to settle down and observe the situation at the Ninth Prince's residence.\"","Sixth Elder Brother obviously didn't consider as much as Mo Jiuye did.","\"Ninth Younger Brother, since we've already found a clue, why don't we go to the Ninth Prince's residence to search for the person?\"","Mo Jiuye explained his calculations to his two older brothers, and Fifth Elder Brother agreed, \"Ninth Younger Brother makes sense. We finally have a lead, so we mustn't act rashly.\"","In the end, the three brothers decided to hide temporarily in the courtyard of those two men from the southern border.","After all, they were already dead and would never be able to return. It was much safer than exposing themselves by going to inns or renting houses.","Of course, they also had to be cautious of Mr. Si Meng's spies discovering their location, so they would minimize going out or engaging in other activities.","Mo Jiuye and his brothers had handsome features and were tall and robust, making them very conspicuous in a crowd.","Moreover, many people in the capital city recognized them, so it was necessary for them to keep a low profile.","Of course, they could send someone out to buy some food ingredients.","When Mo Jiuye left home, He Zhiran had prepared some makeup tools for him. Although his skills were not proficient enough to completely change a person's appearance, he could still manage a simple disguise.","The three brothers didn't use the main entrance but instead used light footwork to leap over the walls into the courtyard.","Under the moonlight, they could see that the courtyard was not large but very tidy. In the center, there was a water well, and in front of the main entrance, there were two main rooms.","There were smaller rooms on the east and west sides, one empty and the other a kitchen.","Fifth Elder Brother and Sixth Elder Brother simultaneously pushed open the doors of the two main rooms. The layout of the rooms was basically the same, with a bed facing the door, a round table in the center, and wardrobes on either side.","Because they were afraid of being discovered, the three brothers didn't plan to light the oil lamps. Instead, they relied on the moonlight to feel their way in.","After making sure there was no danger, Fifth Elder Brother spoke, \"Ninth Younger Brother, you can have one room to yourself, and Sixth Brother and I will stay here.\"","\"Okay.\"","After days of traveling, Mo Jiuye was indeed tired. He responded and each of the brothers went to rest.","Mo Jiuye lay in bed, unable to fall asleep immediately. He was carefully considering the matter of investigating the Ninth Prince's mansion.","According to the confessions of the people from South Jiang, they had not encountered Mr. Si Meng, which means they were not familiar with his appearance.","However, since Mr. Si Meng arranged for two people to do things in secret, it was inevitable that he would observe them closely. Therefore, there was a high possibility that Mr. Si Meng knew what these two individuals looked like.","If that was the case, even if they sent Little White to the Ninth Prince's mansion, their identities would likely be exposed.","Even if he tried to disguise himself, the physique of him and his brothers was completely different from those two people from South Jiang.","Since that was the situation, there was no need for them to conceal their identities.","If someone from the Ninth Prince's mansion came to take Little White, they could seize the opportunity to sneak into the mansion. If it happened to be Mr. Si Meng himself who came to retrieve Little White, they would do whatever it takes to capture him on the spot.","Of course, they also needed to be cautious of the power of the Ninth Prince's mansion. If the Ninth Prince could collude with Mr. Si Meng, it must not be as simple as it seemed on the surface.","However, there was also the possibility that the Ninth Prince, like Nan Rui, had some leverage that Mr. Si Meng held, which made him willingly cooperate.","Regardless, these were all matters concerning the court of the Dashun Dynasty, and as long as it didn't harm the interests of the people and the Mo family, Mo Jiuye wouldn't care about the struggles between those in power.","Perhaps it was due to not having a good rest for a long time, Mo Jiuye's mind became more and more chaotic as he thought, and he gradually fell asleep without realizing it.","Mo Jiuye was always a light sleeper, so when a faint light seeped in through the window paper, he sensed the slight sound of footsteps.","He sat up abruptly and asked in a deep voice, \"Who's there?\"","As he spoke, Mo Jiuye quickly pushed open the door.","\"Ninth Brother, it's me.\"","\"Fifth Elder Brother, why are you up so early?\"","Fifth Elder Brother raised the bucket in his hand.","\"I couldn't sleep, so I got up to fetch water and cook. I saw that there's still some food in the kitchen, so let's have a simple meal.\"","Mo Jiuye had originally wanted to sleep a little longer, but seeing that Fifth Elder Brother had already woken up, he dismissed that thought and helped prepare breakfast together.","In the Mo family, Mo Jiuye was the youngest son, and his older brothers always took great care of him, never letting him do any work.","Fifth Elder Brother was still accustomed to this.","\"Ninth Brother, you don't need to bother. I can handle it alone.\"","It wasn't that he looked down on Mo Jiuye, but now that Mo Jiuye was married, it was fine for him to take care of some external matters. As for these household chores, he was afraid that Mo Jiuye would only become busier the more he helped.","Mo Jiuye didn't know Fifth Elder Brother's thoughts. Instead of obediently going back to rest, he entered the kitchen to prepare breakfast.","There was quite a bit of food stored in the kitchen, but the few large cabbages piled up in the corner had completely rotted. Apart from that, there were no other vegetables.","Fortunately, there were several pieces of dried salted meat and a string of dried radishes hanging from the ceiling beams.","Mo Jiuye had become very cautious now. Before cooking, he took out the miniature toxin detector his wife gave him and checked all the ingredients to make sure there were no problems before starting to cook.","Fifth Elder Brother thought that Ninth Brother was just being polite by entering the kitchen and wouldn't do much.","As he entered carrying the firewood, he found that Mo Jiuye had already washed the rice and put it in the pot, while the dried radish and salted meat were soaking in water.","Without waiting for him to say anything, Mo Jiuye took the firewood he had chopped and quickly placed it inside the stove, igniting it.","\"Fifth Elder Brother, I'll prepare breakfast,\" he said.","Fifth Elder Brother was somewhat astonished at his skilled movements.","However, in order to not discourage Ninth Younger Brother's enthusiasm, he had already prepared himself to consume a meal of dark cuisine.","Regardless of whether the dish Ninth Younger Brother made was edible or not, he was determined to finish it..."]},{"number":343,"title":"Chapter 343: Fei Fu","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye did not know that his cooking skills were criticized by his elder brother. He was still carefully preparing breakfast there.","Half an hour later, Sixth Elder Brother, who was sleeping soundly, woke up too. As soon as he came out of the room, he smelled a scent of delicious food.","\"Fifth Elder Brother, I haven't eaten the meals you cooked for a long time. Your cooking skills seem to have improved.\"","Fifth Elder Brother stood in the yard with an embarrassed look on his face.","\"It's not me who cooked this meal, it's Ninth Younger Brother.\"","When he lost his memory, he lived alone for so long, especially in the haunted house under the West Ridge Village, he had always been self-reliant. He thought he was the best cook among the brothers.","He didn't know when Ninth Younger Brother had attained such skills, which immediately surpassed him.","When Sixth Elder Brother heard that the fragrance came from Ninth Younger Brother's hands, he also felt incredible.","In fact, Mo Jiuye was able to make such a tasty breakfast all thanks to the seasonings his wife had brought him.","He Zhiran thought that with the brothers rushing to the capital city, they would inevitably eat in the open air and spend nights in the wild, passing through jungles or high mountains. So she put some seasonings in small bottles for Mo Jiuye to bring.","As a result, the brothers were in a hurry on the road and didn't have the heart to go hunting. These seasonings were not used up, and now they have become the capital for Mo Jiuye's excellent cooking skills.","The door of the kitchen opened.","\"Fifth Elder Brother, Sixth Elder Brother, breakfast is ready.\"","Fifth Elder Brother and Sixth Elder Brother looked at each other and rushed into the kitchen like a gust of smoke.","In fact, with such ingredients, Mo Jiuye couldn't prepare any big meals either, just white rice porridge and a dish of radish pickles with some salted meat added.","Since He Zhiran joined the Mo family, they had delicious food every day. Fifth Elder Brother and Sixth Elder Brother were used to that taste.","After travelling on the road for so long, they had always eaten casually. Missing the taste of home cooking was one reason. More importantly, today's delicious breakfast was made by Ninth Younger Brother.","If Fifth Elder Brother hadn't seen Mo Jiuye make breakfast with his own eyes, he would never have believed that Ninth Younger Brother had such cooking skills.","How could Mo Jiuye not understand what was on his brothers' minds?","He said smugly, \"Fifth Elder Brother, Sixth Elder Brother, what are you still dazing around for? Eat quickly!\"","Fifth Elder Brother and Sixth Elder Brother nodded dully and picked up their bowls and chopsticks.","After eating a few bites, Sixth Elder Brother couldn't help asking, \"Ninth Younger Brother, when did you acquire such cooking skills?\"","Mo Jiuye smiled awkwardly, \"It was taught by Ranga. I made it according to her method.\"","It was not surprising then. Everyone in the family witnessed Ninth younger sister-in-law’s capabilities. It was no wonder that Ninth Younger Brother had received her true teachings.","Seeing his cooking skills appreciated, Mo Jiuye was thinking that he would disguise himself and go to the market to buy more ingredients today, so that he could show off his skills in the future and thoroughly impress his two elder brothers.","After breakfast, the sky was already bright. Mo Jiuye went back to the room to dress up a bit.","He put on the fake beard given by his wife, and thickened his eyebrows...","Although not as good at makeup as his wife, he looked even uglier, but his two elder brothers wouldn't recognize him if they didn't look closely.","With the approval of his two elder brothers on his outfit, Mo Jiuye then left the yard.","In the capital city, there were basically no places he was not familiar with, so Mo Jiuye wandered the streets with ease.","Since he went out, it would not be as simple as just shopping for groceries.","He intended to take a look around the Ninth Prince's Mansion, hoping to find something.","On the way from Yong'an Alley to the Ninth Prince's Mansion, he had to pass the original Duke of Protector’s mansion.","Mo Jiuye's heart was inevitably sad when he arrived there.","It was still bustling with traffic outside the door, but the original Duke of Protector’s mansion was gone.","Mo Jiuye thought Emperor Shunwu would at least seal the mansion temporarily. Unexpectedly, the gate had been changed here.","On the towering red lacquered gate, a brand new plaque was hanging with the two large characters “Fei Residence”.","The first person Mo Jiuye thought of was Fei Nanyu. He heard from Meng Huaining that Fei Nanyu was highly valued by Nan Qi and was treated as his right-hand man.","Of Emperor Shunwu's three sons, Nan Heng died upstream of the Salt Lake, Nan Rui was now living incognito in West Ridge Village, and currently only one prince Nan Qi was left in the capital.","Besides, Nan Qi had also accumulated many cronies over the years, and he should be extremely comfortable now.","With Nan Qi's current status, giving his confidant a good mansion would be easy.","Mo Jiuye didn't want to reminisce here. He paused briefly and was about to leave.","Unexpectedly, he had just turned around when the door opened.","Fei Nanyu looked solemn, exuding an aura of superiority, followed by servants and several guards.","Mo Jiuye pretended to pass by here on his way to the Ninth Prince’s Mansion, but his speed was extremely slow.","He heard someone talking to Fei Nanyu behind him.","\"Sir, Prince Qi is going too far. He asked you to personally prepare the birthday gift for the Ninth Prince. Isn't this a waste of your talent?\"","Fei Nanyu raised his hand to stop the servant's words.","\"Don't talk nonsense. The fact that His Highness does this can fully demonstrate his trust in me.\"","The complaining servant was silenced and immediately shut his mouth.","Mo Jiuye walked not far from Fei Nanyu, and did not hear them speak again.","In fact, he didn't know that Fei Nanyu's dialogue with the servant just now was deliberately staged.","Recently, Emperor Shunwu had already revealed his intention to establish Nan Qi as the Crown Prince in the court. Those who used to fawn on Nan Heng were much more low-key now.","Especially the matter of Nan Qi being established as the Crown Prince, even if they wanted to object, they couldn't find a suitable reason.","After all, Prince Heng had been missing for more than half a year, and Prince Rui was even more useless. It was said that he had disappeared as well after Imperial Consort De passed away.","The emperor did not seem anxious at all about losing this son. The current situation in the court was that Prince Qi’s family dominated, and it had become an indisputable fact that he would become the next emperor of Great Shun.","Therefore, most of those ministers who used to fawn on Prince Heng had now defected to Prince Qi’s camp.","Prince Qi was now more arrogant. In He Zhiran's words, he became conceited...","Fei Nanyu, who had been most trusted before, had become less trusted under the provocation of some people with intentions.","However, Prince Qi knew clearly that Fei Nanyu was very talented and he was reluctant to abandon such a person.","The reason why he took the former Duke of Protector’s mansion for Fei Nanyu was to constantly remind Fei Nanyu of what happened to the Mo family on the surface.","Fei Nanyu was so smart that he could naturally see through Prince Qi's purpose.","He pretended to be ignorant and thanked Prince Qi profusely for giving him such a good mansion.","As the only heir of Great Shun, how could Prince Qi possibly not have anything good in his mansion?","Besides, what Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran had taken away was the national treasury, and they didn't touch his private treasury as the Prince.","It was obvious that Prince Qi was creating difficulties for Fei Nanyu.","Not long ago, Fei Nanyu found that the guards beside him were secretly reporting his whereabouts to Prince Qi. When he went out just now, he found that the guard was also following him. So he deliberately had that conversation with the servant."]},{"number":344,"title":"Chapter 344: Marriage by Decree","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye continued to walk ahead of Fe Nanyu and his group, neither too close nor too far. He pondered over their recent conversation.","Normally, the task of preparing gifts could be entrusted to the steward of the mansion.","To Mo Jiuye's surprise, Nan Qi had asked Fe Nanyu to personally handle the preparations. If one applied a little bit of thinking, this matter would appear suspicious.","Mo Jiuye knew Nan Qi quite well. He wasn't an upright gentleman. When Mo Jiuye served as his tutor, Nan Qi didn't even bother to study properly unless he could outperform Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye had always played his part as a courtier, deliberately underperforming in his exams to allow Nan Qi to feel superior.","Now, with the presence of the outstanding Fe Nanyu by his side, it would be difficult for Nan Qi not to feel threatened if Fe Nanyu didn't restrain his brilliance.","It seemed that Fe Nanyu was walking on thin ice these days.","However, Mo Jiuye couldn't understand Fe Nanyu's intentions. Since Fe Mama was already a witness, why didn't they reveal the truth and restore Fe Nanyu's true identity as a prince?","Of course, these were just Mo Jiuye's thoughts. He couldn't involve himself in these power struggles.","Furthermore, Fe Nanyu seemed to be doing well at the moment, but who knew what he would become if he were to ascend to that position?","Although Mo Jiuye didn't want to interact too much with Fe Nanyu, he heard that the Ninth Prince would be celebrating his birthday soon, probably in the near future.","If Mo Jiuye could infiltrate the Ninth Prince's mansion through Fe Nanyu, wouldn't it be safer than his brothers risking their lives to deliver a message to Xiao Bai?","After careful consideration, Mo Jiuye decided to pay a visit to the Fe mansion in the evening and meet Fe Nanyu.","Setting aside the uncertainties of Fe Nanyu's future, finding Mr. Si Meng was the most important thing for now.","With his mind made up, Mo Jiuye no longer hesitated. He quickened his pace and headed straight towards the Ninth Prince's mansion.","Even though the Ninth Prince was no longer favored by Emperor Shunwu, he still held the title of a prince. Therefore, his mansion was quite luxurious and not far from the palace.","When Mo Jiuye used to attend court, he would pass by there.","He initially intended to go directly to the Ninth Prince's mansion, but unexpectedly, another incident occurred on the way.","A group of people on horseback approached from the direction of the palace, led by a eunuch who held a yellow imperial edict high in his hand. They were coming at full speed.","Judging by the smirk on the eunuch's lips, it was clear that something good was about to happen to someone.","Behind the group of people on horseback, there were numerous commoners following on foot.","Although the eunuch rode on horseback while the commoners walked, it didn't take long for them to fall far behind.","Despite this, the onlookers among the commoners remained undeterred and continued to move in the direction of the eunuch, whispering among themselves.","\"I heard that the Emperor has arranged a marriage between Princess Yu and the eldest son of Minister Hao's family. Those people must be going to deliver the imperial edict to Minister Hao's residence.\"","Upon hearing Minister Hao's name, Mo Jiuye immediately halted his steps.","Minister Hao was his father-in-law.","The eldest son of Minister Hao's family was his own dear elder brother-in-law.","Although his wife rarely mentioned her family, the fact that his father-in-law and mother-in-law risked pursuit and gave chase to the exiled convoy to provide Ran Ran with money clearly showed that they cared deeply for Ran Ran.","Since it concerned his father-in-law's family, it was necessary for him to take a look.","Speaking of Princess Yu, Mo Jiuye was not unfamiliar with her.","She was the youngest daughter of the Ninth Prince's family and had been showered with endless love and favors since childhood.","The only headache was that Princess Yu was arrogant and haughty. Everyone in the capital knew that she was insolent and didn't care about anyone except the Emperor's children.","Although the Ninth Prince usually kept a low profile, he made an exception for his daughter. Not only did he not stop Princess Yu from causing trouble, but he also always stepped in to help her out whenever she got into trouble.","It could be said that the Ninth Prince appeared in public the most when he was dealing with his daughter's affairs.","A woman as domineering and arrogant as her marrying his eldest nephew, Minister Hao's family would probably have no peaceful days in the future...","Mo Jiuye didn't know why Emperor Shunwu would arrange a marriage between these two individuals with such disparate backgrounds.","To figure out the situation, he mingled in the crowd that went to watch the commotion and approached someone to inquire.","\"Excuse me, sir. Do you happen to know how the marriage between Princess Yu and Eldest Young Master He came about?\"","Surprisingly, Mo Jiuye asked the right person.","The man had a natural inclination for gossip and happened to have some knowledge about the matter. When he saw someone asking, he immediately felt a sense of superiority and explained quietly as they walked:","\"Eldest Young Master He of Minister Hao's family just passed the imperial examination and was parading through the streets when Princess Yu saw him.","Everyone in the capital knows that Princess Yu likes handsome and refined men, and Eldest Young Master He resembled Pan An, catching Princess Yu's eye at first glance.","The Ninth Prince's love for Princess Yu is well-known throughout the capital. If she wants the stars, the Ninth Prince would never deny her the moon.","Since Princess Yu took a liking to Eldest Young Master He, the Ninth Prince will find a way to make it happen.\"","As he spoke, the man shook his head and sighed:","\"It's a pity, Eldest Young Master He is so outstanding. The latter half of his life might be difficult...\"","Mo Jiuye understood the reason and couldn't help but worry for his eldest nephew.","Marrying Princess Yu was like marrying an ancestor. Minister Hao's family would probably have a tough time ahead.","At the same time, he thought of He Zhiran.","If she were in the capital and encountered such a situation at home, what would she do?","Based on his understanding of his wife, He Zhiran would definitely find a way to stop this marriage. Even if it was an imperial decree, it wouldn't be acceptable.","Since he stumbled upon this matter, he couldn't just stand by and do nothing.","Of course, he was also aware that he currently couldn't prevent the imperial decree from being issued.","After all, it was only a marriage decree, and Princess Yu wouldn't immediately become part of the family. He still had time to resolve this matter.","Lost in thought, Mo Jiuye arrived at Minister Hao's residence before the commoners did.","At this moment, the gates of the residence were wide open, with horses parked to the side.","Two young servants knelt in front of the gate, facing the courtyard.","Mo Jiuye knew that at this point, the imperial messenger had already begun reading the imperial decree.","He had arrived relatively quickly, and there weren't many onlookers in front of Minister Hao's residence. He easily found a good spot to stand where he had a clear view.","There was a stone wall blocking the view outside the gate, but it didn't hinder Mo Jiuye's hearing.","He could hear the eunuch inside saying, \"Congratulations, Young Master He, receive the imperial decree!\"","According to reason, receiving a marriage decree is a joyous occasion for high-ranking officials, but Mo Jiuye couldn't detect any hint of joy in his eldest uncle's tone.","\"I humbly thank the Emperor for his grace.\"","The tone was so uncomfortable and repressed, as if his father-in-law's family was deeply disappointed with this marriage arrangement.","The official delivering the decree knew full well that this was not a favorable match, but as a servant of the Emperor, he had to stand in the Emperor's position. Even though he sympathized with Minister Hao's family in his heart, he couldn't show it."]},{"number":345,"title":"Chapter 345: How can This be good","paragraphs":["The imperial envoy, who was astute, neither expressed sympathy for the He family nor intended to witness their embarrassment any longer. After exchanging a few auspicious words, he beckoned for his men to leave.","As soon as these people departed, the two kneeling servants at the door immediately stood up and entered the courtyard, closing the main gate behind them.","Shortly after, Mo Jiuye heard a faint sobbing sound coming from within the courtyard.","\"Madam, what are we going to do?\"","Madam He's voice was very soft, and if it weren't for Mo Jiuye's exceptional martial arts and keen hearing, he wouldn't have heard it at all.","He was indeed curious about the reactions of his in-laws to this matter. Therefore, he quietly left the crowd, circumvented the side of Minister Hao's residence, and leaped up a tall tree to get a glimpse inside.","Minister Hao and his wife and son all hung their heads, sighing deeply.","\"The imperial decree has ordered the marriage. What else can I do?\"","He Yuanming spoke and turned to his despondent son.","\"So many excellent young ladies were introduced to you by your mother, but you refused them all. Now, you've caught the attention of Princess Yu, and the whole family is implicated.\"","Madam He, displeased with her son being blamed, said somewhat unhappily:","\"It's all because of you. You insisted on sending Ziming to participate in the imperial examination. If not for that, how would he have ended up parading in the streets and caught the attention of Princess Yu?\"","\"You... I sent Ziming to participate in the imperial examination because I didn't want his talent to go to waste. How can you blame me for this?\"","He Ziming, seeing his parents about to argue, quickly stepped between them.","\"Father, Mother, please stop arguing. The imperial order is hard to defy. Since I must marry Princess Yu, I can simply live separately, sparing you both from suffering.\"","Upon hearing their son's words, Madam He burst into tears.","\"How can that be? No matter how arrogant Princess Yu is, she is still a junior in front of your father and me. She will have some considerations. If you live separately, I'm afraid you won't have a single good day.\"","Madam He thought that as a mother-in-law, she could at least have some deterrent effect.","Listening to the conversation between his in-laws and his wife, Mo Jiuye made a silent resolution to help them.","He quietly left Minister Hao's residence and headed once again towards the direction of the Ninth Prince's Mansion.","Perhaps due to the imperial decree for Princess Yu's marriage, the usually low-key Ninth Prince's Mansion was surprisingly bustling today.","Although the main gate was not fully open, people were constantly coming and going through the side entrance, and servants were busy back and forth.","If Mo Jiuye didn't know about the connection between Mr. Si Meng and the Ninth Prince's Mansion, he might have mistaken it for the Ninth Prince deliberately keeping a low profile.","Now, however, he didn't think so. The Ninth Prince's Mansion's actions were clearly intentional.","Whether intentional or unintentional, in any case, Mo Jiuye would not dare to underestimate the Ninth Prince.","After observing at the front gate for a while to avoid raising suspicion, he planned to walk around the walls of the Ninth Prince's Mansion.","Arriving at the backyard of the Ninth Prince's Mansion, Mo Jiuye could faintly hear the sound of a qin.","This place was much quieter compared to the front courtyard, and although the sound of the qin was not loud, it was clear to Mo Jiuye, who possessed martial arts skills.","He had never dabbled in music theory, and in the past, he would occasionally listen to his mother and sisters-in-law playing the qin at home.","Even so, he could sense a hint of resentment intertwined within the melody, and the tune was different from what he usually heard.","As Mo Jiuye pondered, a sudden discordant sound rang out, indicating that a string on the qin had snapped.","And just like that, the qin music ceased.","Mo Jiuye was curious. Based on his understanding, places like the Ninth Prince's Mansion were usually inhabited by servants or guards.","Yet here, he heard the sound of the qin being played, and the skill of the musician seemed impressive.","Unusual circumstances often imply something sinister, so Mo Jiuye decided to investigate further.","After surveying the surroundings and confirming that no one was watching, he leaped onto the wall of the courtyard.","There was a tree's shade that conveniently concealed his body, so he didn't have to worry about being discovered.","Mo Jiuye focused his gaze on the courtyard and took a closer look.","It was different from what he had imagined. The ground was covered in weeds, and amidst the thickest patch of weeds was a small courtyard.","Inside the courtyard, a tall figure dressed in white robes, with white hair and a bamboo hat, sat in a daze in front of an ancient qin.","Although Mo Jiuye hadn't personally seen Mr. Si Meng's appearance, he had questioned people who described him as having white hair.","Therefore, he could conclude that the person before him was undoubtedly Mr. Si Meng.","Fortunately, he still had his wits about him and refrained from rashly taking action upon encountering his enemy.","Because he noticed numerous black-clad guards lurking in the shadows around the courtyard.","It was evident that these people were here to protect Mr. Si Meng.","If he acted recklessly, he might be caught, and if he startled the snake in the grass, he likely wouldn't get a second chance.","Mo Jiuye suppressed his impulses and leaped down from the wall.","He was certain that Mr. Si Meng wouldn't leave the Ninth Prince's Mansion unless he obtained the Golden Winged Eagle.","As long as the man was present, Mo Jiuye needed to devise a foolproof plan to capture him as quickly as possible.","Lost in thought, Mo Jiuye arrived once again at the entrance to the Fei Mansion.","Suddenly, an idea sprang to his mind.","...","Under the cover of night, dressed in black night attire, Mo Jiuye left Yong'an Lane.","He returned to the most familiar place and observed his surroundings before leaping over the east courtyard wall.","The courtyard was pitch black, unlike the scenes he remembered when the Mo family lived there.","Mo Jiuye was familiar with everything here. He surmised that Fei Nanyu likely resided in the main courtyard, so he quickly made his way toward his target.","To his surprise, the main courtyard was equally dark, but a faint light emanated from the study just beyond the courtyard wall.","Mo Jiuye cautiously moved toward the study because he could sense many unfamiliar auras around it, indicating the presence of guards.","He held his breath and circled around to the back of the study, gently poking a hole in the paper covering the window to peer inside.","Fei Nanyu remained oblivious, reclining on a soft couch with slightly narrowed eyes. He wasn't in a deep sleep but seemed lost in thought.","In the quiet of the night, Mo Jiuye's black attire didn't attract attention, especially since he had intentionally suppressed his presence to avoid detection by the surrounding guards.","Fei Nanyu was a person who knew nothing about martial arts. If he didn't cause some commotion, it was highly likely that Fei Nanyu would never notice his presence.","Today, in front of the Fei residence, Mo Jiuye had already suspected that there were spies planted by Nan Qian around Fei Nanyu. Therefore, he didn't want to be discovered when he arrived tonight. No matter what, he couldn't trouble Fei Nanyu.","Hence, with a swift movement, he arrived at a hidden spot and observed that there was possibly only one guard behind the study window.","Mo Jiuye leaped into the air and swiftly knocked out the guard with a hand chop before placing him in a safe position. Only then did he break into the study through the window."]},{"number":346,"title":"Chapter 346: How did you come to the capital","paragraphs":["\"Who?\"","Fei Nanyu jerked up into a sitting position. Although he didn't have any martial arts skills, having the window suddenly opened was still enough to startle him.","Mo Jiuye was afraid he would call out to the attendants outside, so he quickly removed the veil from his face.","\"Mr. Fei, it's me.\"","Hearing the familiar voice, Fei Nanyu was still somewhat incredulous.","But in the lamplight he could clearly confirm that the person before him was indeed Mo Jiuye.","\"Master Mo, how did you come to the capital?\"","For Fei Nanyu, Mo Jiuye showing up in the capital city was an extremely improbable thing.","What's more, he had left Yuncheng without Meng Huaining sending him any messages.","Even so, he was still very curious what Mo Jiuye's purpose was in coming to the capital this time.","Mo Jiuye did not intend to beat around the bush.","\"Mr. Fei, I came to the capital because of some family matters. Coming to find you this time, I was also hoping to ask your help with something.\"","Fei Nanyu had always had a good impression of Mo Jiuye. Seeing that he seemed somewhat anxious, he quickly agreed:","\"If there's anything I can help you with, just go ahead and tell me.\"","\"I heard that it's the Ninth Prince's birthday in a few days?\" Mo Jiuye asked.","\"That's right, in three more days.\" After a pause, Fei Nanyu asked somewhat uncertainly: \"Does your trip to the capital have something to do with the Ninth Prince?\"","Recently Fei Nanyu had also noticed some unusual signs.","The usually low-key Ninth Prince wanted to hold some kind of birthday celebration. This could be said to be completely different from his past style.","He had already warned Nan Qi to send people to pay more attention to the Ninth Prince Estate's activities, but he still hadn't received any feedback from Nan Qi's side.","And now Mo Jiuye had suddenly come to the capital, also targeting the Ninth Prince Estate. This made Fei Nanyu have to think more deeply about it.","Especially today, the Emperor had also issued an edict marrying off the Ninth Prince Estate's Jade Princess to Master He, the eldest son of the prominent He family.","Although Minister He was known for being honest in his official duties, he was also an official who held real power.","Given the Ninth Prince's reclusive personality, even if he doted on his daughter, he wouldn't stoop to asking the Emperor to help marry the Jade Princess off to such an influential aristocratic family.","This easily made people suspect he was courting the important ministers at court.","He had already reminded Nan Qi to send more people to pay attention to the Ninth Prince Estate's activities. But he still hadn't received any feedback from Nan Qi's side.","Now that Mo Jiuye had suddenly come to the capital with the Ninth Prince Estate as his target as well, Fei Nanyu had to think more deeply about this.","\"Master Mo, would it be possible for you to tell me why you're inquiring about the Ninth Prince's matters?\"","Mo Jiuye had already anticipated that with Fei Nanyu's meticulous personality, he would definitely ask about the reason.","He was very clear about Fei Nanyu's identity. There was no conflict of interest between them, at most just some sentiment of gratitude.","What's more, Mo Jiuye felt that telling him his purpose would not negatively impact Fei Nanyu in the slightest in the future, and might even serve to give him an early warning.","Therefore, Mo Jiuye did not intend to conceal anything.","\"I won't hide it from Mr. Fei. My Mo family was plotted against by a man named Simeng from Southern Borderlands, leading to our decline to our current state.","Not long ago in Yuncheng I discovered two suspicious people. After capturing them and interrogating them, they said this Mr. Simeng was in the capital city. Therefore, I secretly came to the capital wanting to find out the whereabouts of this enemy.","Based on some clues, I can confirm that this Mr. Simeng is currently within the Ninth Prince Estate.\"","The name Simeng was very unfamiliar to Fei Nanyu.","But he had never had a good impression towards people from the Southern Borderlands to begin with. Hearing that Mr. Simeng was from the Southern Borderlands, and was even the main culprit behind harming the Mo family, he quickly determined that this Simeng must not be simple.","Although his true identity had not yet been revealed, in Fei Nanyu's heart, this Great Shun's rivers and mountains would sooner or later be his. He could not allow such a dangerous figure to remain in the capital city.","What's more, this person was able to hide in the Ninth Prince Estate. This showed that the Ninth Prince was also not as simple as he seemed on the surface.","If the Ninth Prince really harbored ulterior motives, he could make good use of Nan Qi's hand to eliminate him.","\"Master Mo's meaning is that you hope I can find a way to sneak you into the prince's estate on his birthday celebration day?\"","Dealing with smart people was less trouble. Mo Jiuye nodded. \"That is my intention.\"","Fei Nanyu did not ask about Mo Jiuye's specific plan, because he believed that with Mo Jiuye's capabilities, hiding within the Ninth Prince Estate to search for someone would be extremely easy.","When the time came, he could also secretly do something.","\"In three days, Prince Qi will bring me to attend the birthday banquet. You can pretend to be my attendant and follow me in. Whether or not you can find that Simeng you mentioned will depend on your own abilities.\"","As for how Mo Jiuye would take action, Fei Nanyu did not ask further.","Mo Jiuye cupped his fist: \"Then, I will have to thank Mr. Fei. I will come find you on the night before the banquet.\"","Fei Nanyu nodded. \"Alright.\" As he spoke, he looked at Mo Jiuye. It had already been several months since they last met. He heard the northwest was bitterly cold, but he couldn't see any signs of hardship on him.","\"Were you doing well in the northwest?\"","\"Thank you for your concern. Everything was fine for us in the northwest.\"","Speaking of the northwest, Mo Jiuye couldn't help but once again feel grateful to Fei Nanyu.","\"Thank you, Mr. Fei, for thinking of my Mo family and sending Master Meng there to take care of us.\"","Although Fei Nanyu's purpose in sending Meng Huaining to the northwest was not as simple as it seemed on the surface, Mo Jiuye sincerely thanked him from the bottom of his heart.","He understood clearly that for a person to rise to power, it would be impossible without some shrewdness.","If Meng Huaining had not gone to Yuncheng as county magistrate, his family would not have been able to live such a smooth life. Not only that, his family had also gained such an outstanding brother-in-law.","In fact, Fei Nanyu knew clearly in his heart that with Mo Jiuye and his wife's intelligence, it was impossible for them to not guess one of his purposes in sending Meng Huaining to Yuncheng.","Yet the other party had sincerely thanked him. He instantly felt somewhat ashamed.","\"It was a coincidence. Master Mo need not take this matter to heart. As a pillar of Great Shun, yet meeting such injustice and decline, this is the most Fei can do.\"","Looking into Mo Jiuye's sincere eyes, Fei Nanyu instantly changed his original intentions.","Even before coming to the capital, he would often hear the common folk discussing things like the Mo family men had established new merits for Great Shun again.","Thus, ever since he was little he had a very good impression towards the Mo family. Especially after arriving at the capital, he discovered that the Mo family had truly suffered unjust treatment from his so-called father whom he had not acknowledged yet.","Because of this, he had felt many times that the Mo family men's contributions were not valued enough.","Even Nan Qi, whom he assisted every day, was the same. He would often reminisce to Fei Nanyu about the heroic deeds of the Mo family men.","After hearing these kinds of words so many times, with Fei Nanyu's meticulous personality, he naturally investigated further. The results proved everything was true, and thus his respect for the Mo family grew even deeper.","Now, his good impression of the Mo family had already taken firm root.","Especially in recent days, despite Meng Huaining not sending him any news about the Mo family, he did not have the slightest suspicion."]},{"number":347,"title":"Chapter 347: Is Sister Fei Still a Fei","paragraphs":["That is to say, in Fei Nanyu's heart, if even people like the Mo family could not be trusted, then there would be no trustworthy people under this sky.","Mo Jiuye did not know that Fei Nanyu had already regarded his Mo family as his own people. The first thing he would do when he took power one day would be to help the Mo family clear their name and allow them to return to the imperial court.","With such loyal people to assist him, the dynasty would become even more stable.","Mo Jiuye never imagined that the future emperor had already noticed the Mo family. He thought that since the matter was already settled, he should leave early.","However, before he could speak, Fei Nanyu took the initiative to speak first.","\"Mama Fei is still surnamed Fei in the end.\"","Mo Jiuye raised his eyebrows. He did not know what Fei Nanyu wanted to say to him, and he did not want to discuss more about his origins.","After all, the Mo family had completely lost hope in the imperial court, and did not want any more involvement. Knowing too much would not be good.","Fei Nanyu could naturally see Mo Jiuye’s thoughts. The other party simply did not want to know these things.","But since he had chosen to say it out, his purpose was to get Mo Jiuye to see him in a different light, while at the same time showing the difference between himself and those royals.","Whether Mo Jiuye wanted to know or not, he said to himself:","\"Mama Fei was soft-hearted in the end. Nan Qi is her nephew by blood after all.","After settling down in the capital, I asked her if she was willing to testify for my identity. She hesitated at the time and asked if I would kill Nan Qi.","I said it was not up to me whether I would kill Nan Qi or not, that would depend on His Majesty’s verdict.","Perhaps Mama Fei felt safe and thus had compassion for Nan Qi. Now I have hidden her away and she is very safe, she just can't help for the time being.","With her attitude like this, I dare not rashly bring her out to testify, in case she bites back, it would not be worth it.\"","In fact, Fei Nanyu had another reason for telling Mo Jiuye these things.","There were not many people he could trust around him, and he felt an urge to confide his troubles to someone he trusted after keeping it bottled up for so long.","At this moment, he told the whole story in one breath, feeling much more relaxed in his heart. At the same time, he also hoped to get a little response from Mo Jiuye.","Now that Fei Nanyu had said so much, if Mo Jiuye did not respond at all, it would seem too impersonal.","\"Since Mama Fei is unwilling to come forward, have you ever thought of finding Concubine Yuan?\"","Concubine Yuan was Fei Nanyu’s birth mother. She must want her son back by her side more than anyone else now.","Speaking of Concubine Yuan, a look of loss appeared on Fei Nanyu's face.","He gave a cold laugh, \"Heh... it was she who ordered someone to switch me with Nan Qi. Now I don't even know how to face this mother I've never met.\"","Mo Jiuye could understand this to some extent.","From what he knew, it was Concubine Yuan’s carelessness back then. She did not even look at her child after giving birth and ordered someone to switch the babies. Now Fei Nanyu had finally survived to this day and found out about his origins, yet he still had to work under that impostor.","No matter who it was, they probably could not forgive this.","He did not know how to comfort Fei Nanyu, so he just walked over and patted him on the shoulder.","\"Things will come to light one day.\"","From the Mo family’s standpoint, he hoped Fei Nanyu could recognize his ancestry while Emperor Shun Wu was still alive, so as to avoid any harm Nan Qi might inflict on the Mo family.","Fei Nanyu smiled bitterly. \"I hope so!\"","Mo Jiuye did not actually want to get too involved in this matter. Seeing that it was getting late, he said,","\"It's getting late, I should leave now.\"","Fei Nanyu was also very cautious. Seeing that he was about to leave, he pointed to the window Mo Jiuye had come in through earlier and said,","\"You should leave through here again. There are people sent by Nan Qi to monitor me among the guards outside. Don't let them discover you.\"","Mo Jiuye nodded. \"Alright, I’ll come here to find you again the night after tomorrow.\"","With that said, he leapt lightly out of the window and left the Fei residence without a trace.","Back at the courtyard where the Southerners lived, Fifth Brother and Sixth Brother were anxiously waiting.","Hearing the sound, they asked in unison, \"Is that Ninth Brother?\"","Mo Jiuye knew that his two elder brothers were worried about him, while also caring about the outcome of the matter.","\"It's me, Fifth Brother, Sixth Brother, let's go inside to talk.\"","Upon entering the room, Mo Jiuye did not even have time to change out of his night clothes before telling his two elder brothers about what was decided tonight.","Hearing that they could sneak into the Ninth Prince's Mansion with Fei Nanyu on the occasion of the Ninth Prince's birthday celebration, Fifth Brother and Sixth Brother both scrambled to be the one to take on the adventure.","\"Ninth Brother, let Fifth Brother go.\"","\"Ninth Brother, let Sixth Brother go.\"","Mo Jiuye shook his head. \"No, I must be the one to go this time.\"","In order to convince his two elder brothers, Mo Jiuye continued to explain, \"It has been confirmed that Master Si Meng is in the Ninth Prince's Mansion. The key to capturing him alive is the Golden-winged Sculpture.","The Golden-winged Sculpture has accepted me as its master. I can fully command it to lead me to find Master Si Meng.","Besides, I suspect the Ninth Prince may have some handle over Si Meng. Just like Nan Rui, those of royal blood are immune to exotic poisons, but it’s hard to guarantee Si Meng won't target those close to them.","I’ve been learning some techniques to dispel curses from Ran Ran, and she also prepared some antidote pills for me. If necessary, I can still help.\"","\"But... Si Meng is too dangerous. We don't want you to take risks alone,\" said Fifth Brother somewhat reluctantly.","Mo Jiuye knew that the purpose of bringing his two elder brothers with him to the capital was so that they could support each other.","He was not someone who liked to show off. Whenever his brothers could work together, he would never stand on ceremony.","\"Tomorrow, let’s go out together, brothers, and take another look at the terrain around the Ninth Prince’s Mansion. When the time comes, I’ll go in with Fei Nanyu while you two wait outside ready to meet us. Once we succeed, we’ll bring Si Meng out together.”","Seeing that Ninth Brother had said so much, Fifth Brother and Sixth Brother naturally could not object anymore. After all, Ninth Brother had abilities that they did not.","\"Alright, let's make a good plan tomorrow then.\"","The next day, Mo Jiuye disguised all three brothers before leaving the courtyard. After making sure their original looks could not be seen, they headed out.","The three brothers lingered around the Ninth Prince's Mansion for a long time before finally deciding that Fifth Brother and Sixth Brother would split up and stand in two different locations.","Although in two locations, they could still see each other. If anything unexpected happened, the two could quickly regroup.","Mo Jiuye's position upon leaving the prince’s mansion was also visible to both elder brothers.","The three brothers all took this matter very seriously. Even after returning to the courtyard, they were still discussing it, doing their best to leave nothing to chance.","...","Finally, it was the time Mo Jiuye had agreed upon with Fei Nanyu. He changed into his night clothes again and appeared in the study room.","At the same time, the snow-white Golden-winged Sculpture stood on the roof of the study, ready to obey its master’s orders at any time."]},{"number":348,"title":"Chapter 348: No Doubt on My Head","paragraphs":["Fei Nanyu had been waiting for some time and hurried over when he heard the window open.","\"Young Master Mo, you're here?\"","Mo Jiuye jumped into the study room.","\"Mr. Fei, how are the preparations coming along?\"","Fei Nanyu closed the window behind him and invited Mo Jiuye to sit at the desk.","\"Everything has been arranged. Tomorrow I will accompany Nan Qi to the birthday banquet and you can disguise yourself as a guard to enter the Ninth Prince's mansion with me.\"","Mo Jiuye had intended to do just that. He gratefully thanked Fei Nanyu for helping.","\"Thank you for your assistance, Mr. Fei.\"","\"Young Master Mo is too kind. I will call for a guard later whom you can knock unconscious.\"","Mo Jiuye naturally understood Fei Nanyu's implication.","\"All right.\"","Fei Nanyu looked outside at the darkening sky then opened the door and called out, \"Shadow, come here!\"","At the same time, Mo Jiuye swiftly hid behind the door and held his breath.","In a flash, a man dressed in black appeared inside the study.","Before the man could react, he felt a sharp pain at the back of his neck and collapsed to the ground.","Fei Nanyu quickly closed the door.","He stared contemptuously at the figure sprawled on the floor.","He made no attempt to hide this from Mo Jiuye either.","\"Two of my guards were sent by Nan Qi to spy on me. This was one of them.\"","Having spent a long time around Nan Qi, Mo Jiuye knew his palm strike would keep Shadow unconscious for at least two hours.","Therefore, he conversed openly with Fei Nanyu.","\"Nan Qi is indeed deeply suspicious. No matter how much he trusts someone, doubts will emerge after enough time. However, he has one good trait - his suspicions do not last too long.\"","Glancing at Shadow's lifeless form, he continued,","\"For example, after placing someone under surveillance for a period without discovering anything amiss, he will come to trust them even more. When that happens, Mr. Fei, you'll have more freedom to maneuver.\"","Although intelligent, Fei Nanyu had not kept Nan Qi's company as long as Mo Jiuye. His words offered a glimmer of hope.","Fei Nanyu was not serving Nan Qi with pure intentions. If he were under constant surveillance, acting cautiously all the time, how could he ever achieve his goals?","It seemed he would have to display even more loyalty before Nan Qi's spies in the future to quickly win their trust.","\"Thank you for the reminder, Young Master Mo. I will be careful.\"","Seeing Fei Nanyu's composure, Mo Jiuye inevitably worried for him.","\"But with us having knocked him out, how will you explain this to Nan Qi?\"","Fei Nanyu sighed helplessly.","\"I'm accompanying Nan Qi to the Ninth Prince's birthday banquet tomorrow. He specifically instructed Shadow to pose as my attendant given my status as his advisor. Without that, I likely wouldn't even get through the front gate let alone bring more than one companion.","So I could only target Shadow. Tomorrow, whether Nan Qi interacts with you or not, you two would have at least seen each other. I'll be by his side the entire time without arousing suspicion. After leaving the prince's mansion, Shadow's sudden disappearance will make Nan Qi doubt his loyalty instead of suspecting me.\"","Hearing Fei Nanyu's explanation, Mo Jiuye felt somewhat reassured.","It wasn't that he was overly sentimental. Fei Nanyu was already helping him tremendously - he couldn't allow the other to end up in an even more difficult position because of him.","\"In that case, I'll do my best to leave seamlessly so Nan Qi won't doubt you.\"","While speaking, Mo Jiuye carefully examined Shadow's appearance - his dark complexion, bushy brows, and scruff on his cheeks and chin.","These would be easy enough for him to emulate. Just as he was about to disguise himself, Fei Nanyu had already opened a cabinet in the study.","He took out several bottles and jars along with something furry resembling the fake beard and moustache his wife had given him.","\"Young Master Mo, allow me to assist you.\"","Mo Jiuye was surprised that Fei Nanyu possessed such skills.","Since the other had taken the initiative, he decided to continue playing the fool.","Although Fei Nanyu's tools were not as good as his wife's, Mo Jiuye was indistinguishable from Shadow after the makeover, at least without close scrutiny.","Now dressed identically in dark clothing, obscuring his forehead would make the resemblance even more uncanny.","Satisfied with his handiwork, Fei Nanyu carefully inspected Mo Jiuye. Confirming his likeness to the figure on the floor, he tossed all the cosmetic items into a copper basin and set them alight.","As he did so, he explained,","\"I don't like leaving behind anything that can be used against me.\"","Seeing his actions, Mo Jiuye sincerely admired him.","A man of such meticulous cunning surely deserved to become an enlightened ruler one day.","Of course, that had little to do with himself - he was merely impressed.","Having disposed of the tools, Fei Nanyu gazed down at Shadow.","\"He cannot be allowed to live.\"","Mo Jiuye understood that Fei Nanyu lacked the opportunity to deal with the body himself and would require his assistance.","\"What do you intend to do?\"","Fei Nanyu shook his head helplessly.","\"He hasn't made things easy for me working in the shadows. I'll send him on his way today.\"","With that, he pulled a gleaming dagger from the drawer and plunged it into Shadow's chest.","Already unconscious, Shadow did not even grunt before his breath escaped him.","Fei Nanyu glanced at Mo Jiuye.","\"I must trouble Young Master Mo to dispose of the corpse.\"","He pushed open the window at the rear of the study.","\"The guards here have been dismissed for today. It's safe.\"","Naturally, Mo Jiuye would not refuse such a request - both out of gratitude for Fei Nanyu killing Shadow on his behalf and simply to repay the favor.","He nodded almost imperceptibly, picked up Shadow's body and leapt out through the open window.","Here, disposing of a corpse would be trivial for Mo Jiuye. His main concern was not creating future difficulties for Fei Nanyu."]},{"number":349,"title":"Chapter 349: Enter the Nine Kingdoms","paragraphs":["There was still a long time before dawn, so he simply took Shadow's corpse out of the Fei Residence with him.","In order not to cause trouble in the future, Mo Jiuye directly used his lightness martial arts skill to take Shadow's corpse to the nearest mountain from the Fei Residence at the fastest speed, and then dug a pit and buried it.","Returning to Fei Nanyu again, it was almost dawn.","Fei Nanyu must have been sleepless all night, still sitting at the desk.","Seeing that Mo Jiuye had been out for so long, he knew that Mo Jiuye must have taken the corpse far away in consideration of not giving Nan Qi a handle before disposing of it.","At the same time, his reliance on Mo Jiuye became even stronger.","His cheap father emperor really had old and blurry eyes, pushing such a capable minister and fierce general thousands of miles away, and even using such indecent means to persecute him.","If it were up to him, someone like this would not be held in high enough esteem.","Mo Jiuye did not know what Fei Nanyu was thinking.","\"Fortunately I have not failed you. Master Fei does not need to worry about future troubles.\"","Fei Nanyu nodded gratefully, then handed Mo Jiuye a package.","\"These are the clothes my entourage usually wears, I'll have to trouble Ninth Gentleman.\"","Mo Jiuye took the clothes and quickly changed into them.","It dawned soon.","Fei Nanyu exhorted: \"Shadow has always kept his head low in front of Nan Qi. Just do as I said, if Nan Qi asks about me, just shake your head to indicate that I haven't done anything these days.\"","\"Okay, I took note of it.\" Mo Jiuye replied.","Nan Qi and Fei Nanyu had agreed to go to the Ninth Prince's Mansion after the morning court, that is, before the Chen time.","Fei Nanyu ordered the outside that he was hungry and asked the kitchen to prepare more breakfast and send it in, but no one doubted it.","It was only after eating breakfast that the two left the study.","As soon as they walked out the study door, Mo Jiuye signaled Little White with a wave of his hand when Fei Nanyu was not paying attention, indicating it to stick close to him.","Little White was very obedient. Seeing its owner gesture to it, it immediately spread its wings and flew up, hovering not far from him.","After all, Fei Nanyu was still Nan Qi’s subordinate. It would be better for it to arrive a little earlier when following him on errands too.","Therefore, after eating breakfast with Mo Jiuye and seeing that it was almost time, Fei Nanyu set off from the Fei Residence.","Fei Nanyu only brought Mo Jiuye with him this time, and all the other guards stayed at the residence, so Mo Jiuye did not have to worry that his actions would give him away on the way.","When they arrived at the Ninth Prince’s Mansion, there were already guests entering the mansion one after another, and the steward at the door was enthusiastically welcoming them.","In order to wait for Nan Qi, Fei Nanyu did not enter immediately, but stood with Mo Jiuye not far from the main entrance of the Ninth Prince’s Mansion.","After waiting for about half a hour, Nan Qi finally arrived.","Seeing him from a distance, Mo Jiuye almost didn’t recognize him.","Nan Qi was obviously much fatter, and the number of followers and guards around him had also increased significantly, indicating that he was really thriving now.","Seeing him arrive, Fei Nanyu hurriedly came forward to salute with clasped fists.","\"Prince Nan.\"","With his hands behind his back, Nan Qi looked high and mighty.","\"Well, exempt courtesy!\"","With this attitude, he must be completely different from the person Mo Jiuye had known before.","It was understandable too. Once a person felt that he had reached the pinnacle of life, it was inevitable that he would become arrogant.","Presumably Nan Qi was no exception. Now he was flattered by the civil and military officials of the whole court and had completely lost himself.","Similarly, Mo Jiuye also saluted Nan Qi with Fei Nanyu.","As expected, Nan Qi still did not trust Fei Nanyu. As they straightened up, his gaze involuntarily fell on Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye kept his head low all the time, but he could still see Nan Qi’s actions out of the corner of his eye.","So he shook his head slightly as Fei Nanyu had prompted him to.","Sure enough, after Nan Qi saw his hint, he shifted his gaze.","\"Master Fei must have waited for a long time. Come with Zhen to enter the mansion now.\"","Fei Nanyu respectfully nodded and led Mo Jiuye to follow behind Nan Qi.","Nan Qi was after all a prince of Da Shun, and was universally recognized as the future emperor. It was not unreasonable for him to bring more people with him when paying a birthday visit to the Ninth Prince’s Mansion.","Therefore, he took a group of people into the Ninth Prince’s Mansion, and no one really dared to stop him.","However, according to the rules over the centuries, the master could enter the main hall of the main courtyard, while the entourage brought along had to be arranged in separate places prepared.","Once the master needed something, there would be someone to inform them specially.","Although Nan Qi was arrogant now, he would not break the rules that had been passed down for hundreds of years.","He only took Fei Nanyu with him into the main hall of the main courtyard.","Mo Jiuye was led with those people brought by Nan Qi to a small courtyard on the west side.","This place was relatively close to the back courtyard. Mo Jiuye was afraid that Little White would appear rashly and startle them, so before he left with the prince’s men, he signaled Little White to fly a little higher and just keep an eye on his location.","When he arrived at the small courtyard, many followers of nobles had already gathered there, and those who were acquainted had started chatting together.","Mo Jiuye found a corner and sat on a rockery.","He looked around habitually and found that there were more than a dozen hidden guards lurking in the tall trees.","In principle, even if guests had brought hidden guards with them, the guards would also hide around their masters to protect them instead of being arranged here to watch these attendants.","From this it could be inferred that these people were not brought by the guests, but arranged by the Ninth Prince’s Mansion.","Mo Jiuye found this very suspicious.","Even if the Ninth Prince held a birthday banquet and arranged hidden guards in the mansion for protection, he would not arrange them here.","That is to say, it was very likely that these people were secretly protecting Si Meng.","The more Mo Jiuye thought about it, the more he felt he had grasped the truth. He carefully observed where those hidden guards were hiding, planning how to take them down all at once, so that he could also take the opportunity to go out and search around.","The anesthetic gun that his wife gave him worked best, it’s just that the thing made a lot of noise when used, and would startle them as soon as it was used, so it was not the best choice.","Mo Jiuye looked at the mini sleeve arrows tied under his sleeves. These sleeve arrows could continuously shoot ten arrows.","Even if his shooting was accurate, he could only take out ten hidden guards at most.","There were still two people left. If they could not be solved at the same time, they would definitely be startled. Not only would his plan fail, more importantly, with Si Meng’s vigilance, he was afraid that Si Meng would flee before he could find him.","Since this was the case, he had no choice but to use the anesthetic his wife gave him.","Mo Jiuye observed that the distance between six hidden guards was relatively close, and it was also the place closest to this small courtyard.","He decided to start with those six people first.","Having made up his mind, under the excuse of going to the toilet, Mo Jiuye went out through the back door of the small courtyard.","Fortunately, there were many people here, and those hidden guards would not pay attention to just him alone, not to mention that he deliberately avoided their sight too.","After leaving the small courtyard, Mo Jiuye quickly hid behind a big tree, and aimed the semi-automatic crossbow in his sleeve at the six hidden guards he planned to take out first."]},{"number":350,"title":"Chapter 350: This great river will basically be yours.","paragraphs":["It must be said that the power and speed of this crossbow really made things easy for him. In the blink of an eye, the six hidden guards who were targeted had an arrow in their forehead and died.","As their bodies swayed unsteadily and fell from the trees, Mo Jiuye had already quickly aimed the crossbow at the other four hidden guards.","With the same result, those four hidden guards still did not know what had happened before they were dead.","Although Mo Jiuye was fast, killing ten hidden guards in a row would definitely alert the remaining two if they were still worthy of being guards.","The two remaining hidden guards sensed something wrong and immediately jumped down from the trees.","Before they could react, Mo Jiuye's figure flashed swiftly in front of them while scattering a bag of powder.","Likewise, the two collapsed without any perception.","Mo Jiuye did not show any mercy, taking out a dagger to finish them off.","The hiding spot of these guards was remote, and although Mo Jiuye's series of actions did not alert anyone, with so many corpses inside the heavily guarded Ninth Prince's Mansion, any mishandling would inevitably reveal clues.","Just nearby there was an abandoned artificial lake, and no one seemed to walk around it. Mo Jiuye unceremoniously threw all the corpses into the river.","As long as he could successfully catch Mr. Si Meng and leave the Ninth Prince's Mansion, even if the corpses floated to the surface and were discovered, they would have nothing to do with him.","After dealing with this, Mo Jiuye carefully observed again before heading towards the place where he had heard the sound of the zither that day.","Although Mo Jiuye had been in the capital for many years, this was his first time at the Ninth Prince's Mansion.","He did not expect that there would be such a desolate place in the Ninth Prince's Mansion.","Because in front of him there was already a patch of weeds, many of which grew taller than a person, showing that no one took care of this place.","If it wasn't for his strong sense of direction, he would even suspect that he had walked to the wrong place.","Fortunately, through the weeds Mo Jiuye could see a courtyard not far away, which looked very dilapidated from a distance.","He guessed that it should be where Mr. Si Meng was, very hidden. If it wasn't for discovering something wrong that day, it would be hard to imagine someone hiding here.","Mo Jiuye did not dare to be careless at all, in order to avoid making noise by walking through the weeds, he walked along the edge instead.","After walking out of the weeds, it felt suddenly spacious.","Although the courtyard looked a little shabby, it was swept clean.","And through observation, there were no hidden guards around.","Mo Jiuye guessed that the dozen or so guards he had just dealt with should be responsible for protecting Mr. Si Meng. Perhaps for some reason, they could not get too close here, so they stayed on the necessary path to defend.","Mo Jiuye analyzed in his mind while carefully approaching the courtyard.","Suddenly, the door in front of him was pushed open, and two people walked out from inside.","One of them was the Ninth Prince of the Da Shun Dynasty, and the other, compared to the glimpse he caught last time, there was not much difference.","Wearing a white robe, a thin figure, with white hair trailing behind his head, and wearing a hat similar to one a lady would wear when going out.","\"Don't worry, Sir, this king will make sure all these venomous bugs have their use today.\"","The Ninth Prince's tone was filled with excitement, while he tucked several small porcelain bottles into his bosom.","Mr. Si Meng wore a hat, so Mo Jiuye could not see his expression clearly, but his tone was filled with indifference and aloofness.","\"Hmm, after this is done, the Da Shun dynasty will basically be yours.\"","\"Thank you for your help, Sir. When this king ascends to that position, you will be the most honorable Imperial Tutor of Da Shun.\" The Ninth Prince continued to flatter.","\"Alright, I'll be waiting for the day the Ninth Prince succeeds,\" Mr. Si Meng still spoke coldly, without a trace of warmth.","However, Mo Jiuye could feel the perfunctory meaning in his words.","The Ninth Prince respectfully saluted Mr. Si Meng with clasped fists.","\"Don't worry, Sir. This king has been accumulating strength for this day for many years and absolutely cannot make any mistakes.\"","Mr. Si Meng nodded, did not respond, but stood in place watching the Ninth Prince's back as he gradually walked away, lost in thought.","Even when the Ninth Prince's figure disappeared from sight, Mr. Si Meng still stood in place.","In order to confirm that he had not found the wrong person, Mo Jiuye commanded Little White in the sky to attack.","Little White immediately flew over from afar with Mr. Si Meng as the target.","Just as Mr. Si Meng was about to turn back into the room, he suddenly stopped and looked up at the sky.","\"Darling, you're back.\"","At this moment, compared with the coldness he had shown to the Ninth Prince earlier, his tone could be described as doting.","Next, Mo Jiuye saw him stretch out an arm, beckoning Little White to land on it.","Having received Mo Jiuye's cue, Little White naturally cooperated fully.","Accompanied by a not too loud cry cutting through the air, a snow-white figure steadily landed on that outstretched arm.","Mr. Si Meng lovingly reached out to pet its snow-white feathers, but Little White fluffed up its feathers at this moment.","To Little White now, Mr. Si Meng was a frightening stranger.","Mr. Si Meng thought Little White had been startled by something during their time apart and did not suspect it had a new owner.","He stretched out a hand, very patiently helping smooth its feathers.","Just then, a crackling sound of firecrackers came from the front yard.","Mo Jiuye suddenly had a flash of inspiration, he knew this was his chance.","In dealing with such an insidious person, he couldn’t make the same mistake as last time and give him a chance to escape when caught off guard.","Mo Jiuye took out a tranquilizer gun from his bosom, aiming at Mr. Si Meng.","Against the noisy backdrop of the firecrackers, Mo Jiuye pulled the trigger.","The tranquilizer dart accurately hit Mr. Si Meng's left shoulder. At this moment Little White also spread its wings to fly back to its owner.","It had to be said, this Mr. Si Meng really was extraordinary.","Others would immediately collapse after being hit by a tranquilizer dart, but he still had the energy to glance in Mo Jiuye's direction before falling down.","Mo Jiuye did not doubt the power of the tranquilizer gun at all. After seeing his task accomplished, he commanded Little White to fly a safe distance away while he rushed up to Mr. Si Meng at top speed.","He was in no hurry to take the person away, but first entered his room to take a look.","The room was very tidy. Apart from some daily furnishings, there was nothing else,","Not even the sort of poisonous bugs and potions that those who use them to protect their lives would have on hand.","The more it was like this, the more Mo Jiuye felt something was off. How could someone who uses these things to protect themselves not have them around?","He did not want to give up just like this. Relying on experience, he knocked on the surrounding walls and cabinets, but still gained nothing."]},{"number":351,"title":"Chapter 351: Escape Route","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye was also not worried that Mr. Si Meng would wake up immediately. He knew the power of this anesthetic gun that his wife used better than anyone else. It could make people fall into a deep coma for at least a few hours.","Since he did not find anything unusual about the surrounding furniture and walls, the only thing left was the wooden bed in the room.","He lifted all the bedding on the bed, and as expected, something was revealed.","He stepped to the head of the bed. The wood planks there showed obvious signs of being loose.","Mo Jiuye lifted the planks, revealing a black hole that could allow a person to come in and out.","Based on past experience, such places were likely to be passages connecting to the outside world.","The passage was next to the other bedside plank, with a small dark box. At this moment, the light was just right, and Mo Jiuye saw at a glance that there were several small porcelain bottles placed in the dark box.","Without thinking, these small porcelain bottles must contain various poisons. As for Gu worms, they would definitely not be placed here.","Because Gu raisers regarded Gu worms as treasures, no matter how many they raised, they would carry them with them.","There were more than a dozen large and small porcelain bottles. Mo Jiuye casually tore off a sheet and wrapped these small porcelain bottles in it.","After tidying these up, Mo Jiuye did not rashly enter to investigate. Although Mr. Si Meng was in a coma, he was still lying outside clearly. If someone found him, Mo Jiuye's previous efforts would be in vain.","Therefore, he had to take Mr. Si Meng with him when entering the secret passage. No matter where the exit of the secret passage was, he could not give the other party any chance to escape.","There were many uncertain factors when entering the secret passage, and Mo Jiuye did not dare to take it lightly.","Most importantly, Fifth Elder Brother and Sixth Elder Brother were still waiting for him outside the Ninth Prince's Mansion. If he did not meet with his two elder brothers in time, they would definitely think something had happened to him, so doing something impulsive would be a great loss.","Thinking of this, Mo Jiuye took out paper and pen from the table and started writing:","[Fifth Elder Brother and Sixth Elder Brother, everything is going well. I discovered a secret passage and will enter to investigate first. Later I will let Little White send you the latest location.]","After finishing the note, he rolled it into a small paper roll and went out to call Little White.","He tied the note to Little White's leg and gently stroked its snow-white feathers.","\"Little White, take this note to Fifth Elder Brother and Sixth Elder Brother, then come find me, okay?\"","It was the first time Mo Jiuye had let Little White deliver a letter. To be honest, with just these simple words, he was not sure if Little White could understand.","However, he did not need to worry about Little White's whereabouts. His wife had said that once it recognized its master, no matter where its master was, it could find him, unless it was trapped by some accident and unable to escape.","Watching Little White fly farther and farther away, Mo Jiuye then went to Mr. Si Meng.","He tore off the hat on his head, and what appeared in front of him was a face similar in age to himself.","Although this face could not be called very handsome, it was still quite eye-catching among the crowd.","With that head of white hair, it completely matched Nan Qi's description of his master having a crane's youthful looks.","Facing the perpetrator who had persecuted his father and brothers, Mo Jiuye wished he could hack him into thousands of pieces. However, reason told him that now was not the time.","He forcibly suppressed the surging anger in his heart, and first searched Mr. Si Meng's body.","Sure enough, his precious Gu worms were tucked into his arms, a total of six.","Mo Jiuye did not dare to be careless at all towards these creatures. In case the mother Gu that controlled his father, eldest brother and second brother was among them, any problem would have unimaginable consequences.","So he also learned from those Gu raisers, tore off another sheet and carefully wrapped the porcelain bottles before tucking them into his arms.","Returning to Mr. Si Meng, Mo Jiuye roughly picked him up and threw him towards the hole.","The hole led straight down for about two meters.","With a muffled thud, Mr. Si Meng was violently thrown to the ground, and Mo Jiuye immediately jumped down after him.","It was relatively dark inside the secret passage. He held Mr. Si Meng in one hand and used a flashlight to illuminate with the other.","After walking like this for about half an hour, light faintly appeared ahead.","Mo Jiuye knew the end of the secret passage was not far away.","He continued forward, and soon a wooden door appeared before his eyes.","It could not really be called a wooden door, as there was no handle on it at all. Mo Jiuye guessed that this should be something like a closet that needed to be pulled back and forth to open.","Sure enough, as he had expected, after he pulled left and right twice, the wooden door showed signs of loosening.","He exerted a little force to the left, and the door opened.","Dazzling light instantly shone in, causing Mo Jiuye to be momentarily blinded.","But soon, he adjusted his vision.","What appeared before him was a spacious and bright room. Apart from the closet that served as the secret passage entrance, there was no other furniture in the room.","Mo Jiuye did not care too much. He threw Mr. Si Meng on the ground, while he carefully walked towards the door.","Gently pushing open the door, a courtyard appeared before his eyes.","In contrast to the cleanliness of the room, weeds could be seen everywhere in the yard. It was obvious that this place had been abandoned.","However, the indistinct traces extending from the front gate towards the houses caught Mo Jiuye's attention.","This was not really abandoned, but someone would occasionally walk around.","Because he could clearly see that some weeds had been broken off.","Obviously, these were traces left by someone stepping on them.","But it made sense to think about it. Since Mr. Si Meng could live in a courtyard with an underground passage, it was understandable that he could leave from here when necessary.","Mo Jiuye first sensed the surrounding movement. After making sure there was no danger, he walked out of the yard.","After all, it was an unfamiliar place. Even with Mo Jiuye's strong sense of direction, he could not accurately determine his location.","In any case, he had to take Mr. Si Meng with him to leave. He had to figure out the route clearly so as not to make any mistakes.","Mo Jiuye was in no hurry to leave. Instead, he used his lightness skill to leap up high and look around.","The scene that met his eyes was one he was most familiar with. When he was little, he and Nan Qi often secretly came here to play.","As it turned out, this was the Qing River less than one mile from the capital.","Apart from the conversation he just overheard between the Ninth Prince and Mr. Si Meng, just based on the exit of this secret passage, he could determine the Ninth Prince's intentions.","It was obvious that this was an escape route arranged by the Ninth Prince for himself after hiding his abilities for many years.","This showed how deep his thoughts were.","While he was lost in thought, Little White flew back and landed steadily on his shoulder.","Mo Jiuye subconsciously glanced at Little White's leg, and the note was gone.","He knew that Little White had successfully completed its first task. He was about to praise it when two figures approached swiftly from afar.","The arrivals were none other than Fifth Elder Brother and Sixth Elder Brother.","After catching his breath for a moment, Sixth Elder Brother said, \"I have to say, Fifth Elder Brother was right that following this little guy would lead us to Ninth Younger Brother. He really got it right.","\"Only, this fellow flies so fast that we two elder brothers almost got thrown off by it.\""]},{"number":352,"title":"Chapter 352: This is Mr. Simeng","paragraphs":["For Little White's flying speed, its master Mo Jiuye still had some understanding.","If it were not for the fact that all the Mo's men were masters of qinggong, they might really not be able to keep up.","He stroked Little White's feathers indulgently.","\"Little White, you know they are following you, why don't you slow down a little?\"","Little White looked up to the sky and cried out.","It seemed to be complaining that Fifth Elder Brother and Sixth Elder Brother were too slow.","At this moment, Mo Jiuye didn't have more energy to appease Little White, but said to the two elder brothers: \"Fifth Elder Brother, Sixth Elder Brother, the man has been successfully captured, in that room over there.\"","He pointed to the room behind him and took the first step forward.","Fifth Elder Brother and Sixth Elder Brother were very curious about how their Ninth Younger Brother had captured Mr. Si Meng and arrived here so quickly.","The two followed closely behind Mo Jiuye, eager to see the arch-criminal who had brought the Mo family to this point.","The three brothers entered the room, Mo Jiuye pointed to Mr. Si Meng, who was like a dead dog, and said:","\"This is Mr. Si Meng.\"","Sixth Elder Brother angrily walked up and kicked Mr. Si Meng.","\"Humph! If you weren't still of some use, I would have skinned you alive.\"","Mo Jiuye didn't stop Sixth Elder Brother's actions, because he was filled with the same feeling at the moment.","Fifth Elder Brother was much calmer. Although he was angry in his heart, he didn't forget to ask first.","\"Ninth Younger Brother, how did you capture him?\"","\"I went looking for the man based on the location I observed that day...\" With enough time, Mo Jiuye told them everything that happened after entering the residence of the Ninth Prince.","Like Fifth Elder Brother and Sixth Elder Brother, they didn't care about the actions of the Ninth Prince, what they cared most about now was finding out the whereabouts of their father and elder brothers from Mr. Si Meng.","Mo Jiuye looked at the sky. It had been an hour since Mr. Si Meng was shot with the tranquilizer gun.","This tranquilizer was different from some drugs that could be awakened prematurely by special means. If they wanted to interrogate him, they could only wait for him to wake up naturally.","Just now when he was at the residence of the Ninth Prince, he saw that his father-in-law had also gone to congratulate.","Mr. Si Meng had given the Ninth Prince so many Gu worms, and his father-in-law was also an important minister. It was inevitable that he would be poisoned.","Therefore, he decided to double back to the residence of the Ninth Prince to save his father-in-law, and also to see if there was a good way to break off the engagement between Princess Yu and his uncle.","Also, Fei Nanyu had done him a big favor today, discovering the secret of the Ninth Prince. Mo Jiuye felt it necessary to give him a reminder, which was also repaying Fei Nanyu.","As for what Fei Nanyu would do, it was not his concern.","With this in mind, Mo Jiuye said, \"Fifth Elder Brother, Sixth Elder Brother, I still have some things to do at the residence of the Ninth Prince.\"","What Mo Jiuye could think of, Fifth Elder Brother and Sixth Elder Brother could naturally think of too. Even if Mo Jiuye didn't take the initiative to suggest going back to the residence of the Ninth Prince, one of the two brothers would do so.","\"Well, Ninth Younger Brother, don't worry, we will definitely keep an eye on the man. You have to pay attention to your own safety. If you encounter any danger, saving your life is the most important thing.\" Fifth Elder Brother thoughtfully reminded him.","Mo Jiuye had just stood high to survey the surroundings. The location here was relatively remote. There were many guests at the residence of the Ninth Prince. He believed the Ninth Prince would not go to the neglected backyard to look for Mr. Si Meng.","Therefore, it was relatively safe here compared to other places.","\"Okay, Fifth Elder Brother and Sixth Elder Brother, just wait for me here until I get back.\"","After bidding farewell to the two elder brothers, Mo Jiuye returned to the capital again, directly scaled the wall and entered the residence of the Ninth Prince.","This time, he didn't go to the small courtyard where the attendants rested, but found the guards he had just killed, changed into their clothes, and then quietly walked towards where the Ninth Prince was holding the banquet.","It had to be said that the Ninth Prince had really gone all out for today's event, even hiring a troupe to perform. A stage was set up in the largest open space in the back garden.","At this moment, the opera had already begun, and the guests who came to congratulate were all sitting under the stage watching the performance. There were still occasional bursts of cheers from the audience.","The Ninth Prince, as the host of the birthday banquet, sat at the main table, right in front of the stage.","Beside him were Concubine of the Ninth Prince and Princess Yu.","Princess Yu's attention, however, was not on the stage, but she kept glancing at Nan Qi's table.","Mo Jiuye observed carefully and could confirm that Princess Yu was looking at Fei Nanyu.","It was understandable. Fei Nanyu had the royal bloodline and had an extraordinary temperament and good looks.","Princess Yu, who had always liked handsome men, would naturally not miss this opportunity to ogle.","But this kind of behavior made people feel disgusted.","Fei Nanyu also seemed to sense that someone was staring at him. He nodded slightly and had already figured out the source of the gaze.","He was very annoyed by this. He said something to Nan Qi, then walked towards the crowd.","Seeing Fei Nanyu get up, Princess Yu hurriedly followed. But there were many people here, and she didn't immediately get close to him.","Fei Nanyu had left to avoid that disgusting gaze, and had no particular destination in mind. So he just strolled around the garden.","Unexpectedly, just after he turned a corner, he heard someone calling him from behind.","\"Young master, please wait.\"","This voice was artificially tender, and Fei Nanyu really hoped that the \"young master\" was not calling him. Unfortunately, it was quiet here, and there was no one else around.","Now his identity was only an aide to Prince Qi. Anyone could call him \"Sir\" to his face.","Princess Yu was no exception. He had no choice but to reluctantly turn around.","\"Are you calling me, Princess?\"","Seeing Fei Nanyu's appearance up close, Princess Yu's eyes widened.","She pretended to be shy as she took out a handkerchief to cover the lower half of her face, then slowly took a few steps forward.","\"May I ask which family's young master you are? I’ve never seen you before.\"","Fei Nanyu was disgusted by her words.","He was adept at dealing with schemes, power struggles and the like. But when it came to women deliberately trying to curry favor with him, he was at a loss.","Especially since he knew clearly that this woman was his cousin.","Just as Fei Nanyu was trying to figure out how to slip away, Princess Yu's body stiffened and she suddenly fell back.","Then a tall figure appeared before his eyes.","When Fei Nanyu looked closely, it turned out to be Mo Jiuye, whom he had dressed up with his own hands.","Seeing that Mo Jiuye was still at the residence of the Ninth Prince, he subconsciously thought that the thing he was trying to do had not yet succeeded.","So Fei Nanyu asked, \"Ninth Young Master, do you need my help?\"","Mo Jiuye was cautious. Before speaking, he scanned the surroundings again. Seeing that there was no suspicious person, he pulled Fei Nanyu to a more secluded corner.","\"I have finished my business. I doubled back to tell Mr. Fei a message.\"","Fei Nanyu's expression was very solemn: \"What message?\"","\"The Ninth Prince has a lot of Gu worms in his hands. He plans to give them to the important ministers who attend his birthday banquet today. Once these people are poisoned by the Gu worms, they will become his puppets.\""]},{"number":353,"title":"Chapter 353: I'll see you soon.","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye spoke to Fei Nanyu in simple and clear terms. He felt there was no need to go into too many details, just let Fei Nanyu know about this matter so he could respond in a timely manner.","He knew that by doing this, he was indirectly helping Nan Qi. If they let the Ninth Prince, who was colluding with the people of Nanjiang and using despicable means to seize power, become the Emperor, the common people of Da Shun would surely suffer.","This was definitely a big deal for Fei Nanyu.","Now he was using Nan Qi to pave the way for his own future. If the throne was seized by the Ninth Prince, it would become much more difficult for him to accomplish anything.","Moreover, he thought the same as Mo Jiuye - no matter whether he could sit in that position in the future, if Da Shun fell into the hands of someone who relied on such despicable means to gain power, the common people would never have a day of peace.","\"Thank you, Ninth Young Master, for letting me know. I will go and think of a way to deal with this,\" Fei Nanyu said.","Mo Jiuye knew Fei Nanyu was anxious to resolve this matter, and he did not intend to stay here long either. The message had been delivered and his mission was successfully completed.","\"Master Fei, go ahead and get busy. I'm planning to return to the northwest today. We'll meet again in the future.\"","\"Is Ninth Young Master leaving the capital city?\"","Mo Jiuye nodded, \"If not for some important business, I probably wouldn't have set foot in the capital city in my whole life. Now that it's done, I naturally have to leave.\"","Fei Nanyu took a deep look at him, feeling complicated inside.","What he admired most was the loyalty and bravery of the Mo Family men. Someone as capable as him would undoubtedly be heavily relied on once he took over that position.","\"Since that's the case, we'll meet again in the future. If Ninth Young Master needs my help with anything, please ask Lord Meng to send me a message. As long as it's within my power, I will definitely do my best.\"","Fei Nanyu was sincerely trying to get on Mo Jiuye's good side, hoping that one day, he would see his sincerity and make use of him.","\"Alright, I'll remember Master Fei's words,\" Mo Jiuye politely responded, then decided not to delay Fei Nanyu's time to strategize.","He did not immediately leave the Ninth Prince's mansion, but walked towards the Jade Princess instead.","Having just seen this woman trying to seduce Fei Nanyu, it was clear she was a flirtatious person.","Yet his uncle He Ziming was an outstanding young talent. How could he let such a woman taint him after marriage?","Although he had just informed Fei Nanyu about the Ninth Prince's misconduct, once Fei Nanyu succeeded, the Ninth Prince and his whole family would be implicated.","However, it was still hard to guarantee nothing would go wrong. If the Ninth Prince escaped punishment, the Jade Princess would still have to marry He Ziming.","In order not to make his father-in-law's family suffer in the future, Mo Jiuye decided to root out the problem once and for all.","How to solve it? Although it was an imperial decree of marriage, they surely wouldn't make a dead person marry over, right?","Mo Jiuye raised his blade and took the Jade Princess's life directly.","This was the most straightforward way to help his in-laws. From now on, they would never have to worry about not having peaceful days after she became their daughter-in-law.","He dragged the Jade Princess's corpse behind an artificial hill and did not hurry to leave.","Because Mo Jiuye was still worried. If Fei Nanyu informed Empress Qi but failed to resolve the crisis, his father-in-law would be in danger.","His father-in-law had shown great righteousness in going through with the marriage and marrying his good daughter to him despite the Mo family's widowed doors. Just the day after their wedding, the entire Mo family was exiled, separating him from his daughter for nearly a year.","Since he had come to the capital city and discovered that his father-in-law was in danger, he could not just stand by and watch.","So, Mo Jiuye walked around the cloister in the garden.","At this moment, a servant boy happened to pass by.","Mo Jiuye went up and knocked out the servant boy, quickly changed into his clothes, then picked up the tray on the ground and walked towards the crowd.","Right now, neither Empress Qi nor Fei Nanyu who were sitting in the front row were present, presumably having left to strategize.","The other officials and their families were all smiling as they watched the performance on stage, completely unaware of the impending danger.","Because of his higher official position, although He Yuanming could not sit in the front row with those nobles, his seat was still very noticeable right in front.","Mo Jiuye spotted his distinct father-in-law among the others enjoying the show at a glance.","He Yuanming had a grave expression, clearly unable to conceal the distress on his face. It was evident how much turmoil Emperor Shunwu's decree of marriage had brought him.","Mo Jiuye pretended to carry the tray to serve tea to the guests and approached He Yuanming. He deliberately spilled water all over him.","\"I'm so sorry, please forgive me, Sir He.\"","Although He Yuanming was quite displeased at being drenched, he did not have the habit of bullying servants either.","He took a look at the apologetic person in front of him and waved his hand. \"It's fine, just be more careful next time.\"","Unexpectedly, instead of leaving immediately, this servant took out a handkerchief and came over to help wipe him.","Taking the opportunity while wiping his father-in-law's wet clothes, Mo Jiuye whispered, \"Father-in-law, please come with me. I'm Mo Jiuye.\"","Hearing these words, He Yuanming's body instinctively stiffened as he scrutinized the person in front of him.","At this moment, Mo Jiuye still had the appearance changed by Fei Nanyu, so He Yuanming did not see a trace of his son-in-law's features on his face at all.","Not knowing the other's intentions, He Yuanming did not make a scene since he mentioned his son-in-law. He replied in a low voice, \"Nonsense. Do you think I'm so blind that I can't even recognize my own son-in-law's appearance? Who exactly are you? This is the Ninth Prince's mansion. I just need to yell and you won't even be able to escape.\"","Mo Jiuye knew his appearance had made his father-in-law misunderstand.","\"Father-in-law, I really am Mo Jiuye. I came to the capital this time to take care of some personal matters and changed my appearance to facilitate my actions. Please come aside to talk, everything will become clear.\"","To make his father-in-law believe him, Mo Jiuye added, \"Ran Ran has a plum blossom-shaped birthmark the size of a fingernail on her left shoulder.\"","At this point, He Yuanming was somewhat convinced.","He looked Mo Jiuye up and down again. Although this appearance bore no resemblance to his son-in-law, the build was quite similar.","\"Are you really Mo Jiuye, my son-in-law?\"","Mo Jiuye nodded slightly. \"Father-in-law, please come aside. I have very important information to tell you.\"","He had been wiping his father-in-law's wet clothes for too long. If this continued, it would inevitably arouse suspicion.","\"Sir, your clothes are wet. Let this subordinate take you to change into a new set,\" Mo Jiuye said.","He Yuanming took the chance to stand up. \"Then what are you waiting for, hurry up!\"","\"Yes yes, please follow me, Sir.\" Mo Jiuye made a humble gesture and led the way.","There should be guest rooms inside the prince's mansion for guests to rest temporarily, but Mo Jiuye did not know their exact location.","However, based on experience, such rooms were usually not far from the banquet venue.","Therefore, he walked towards the row of buildings closest to the garden."]},{"number":354,"title":"Chapter 354: Met the Father-in-law","paragraphs":["Someone saw them coming and recognized at a glance that it was Lord He Yuanming.","He hurried up and said, \"My lord, are you here to change clothes?\"","He Yuanming said unpleasantly, \"Humph, the servants in your household are too undisciplined, getting my clothes wet.\"","The man seemed to be the steward of the household. He hurriedly fawned up and pointed to a room in front saying,","\"I'm really sorry, my lord. Please go there and wait for a moment, I will fetch clothes for you right away.\"","After speaking, he glared fiercely at Mo Jiuye, as if to remind him that there would be consequences for this after the guest left.","Mo Jiuye pretended to shrink back in fear, quickly lowering his head.","This action not only did not attract the steward's attention, but made him seem very frightened by the matter.","He Yuanming and Mo Jiuye went one after the other to the room the steward had pointed out.","Mo Jiuye quickly closed the door, then solemnly knelt in front of He Yuanming and knocked his head three times on the ground.","\"Greetings, father-in-law.\"","He Yuanming quickly helped him up.","But facing this somewhat unfamiliar face, he was still doubtful.","Before he could ask, Mo Jiuye took out the handkerchief that He Yuanming had used to wipe his clothes. He quickly wiped his face a few times, basically restoring his original appearance.","His son-in-law had been away on campaigns for years, but He Yuanming had still seen him a few times.","Now, the brows and eyes of the man before him, who could it be if not his son-in-law?","\"Son-in-law, it really is you. Is Ran Ran alright?\"","Speaking of his daughter, He Yuanming couldn't help but let his tears flow.","Mo Jiuye didn't know why, but seeing his father-in-law care so much about his wife made his affection for him grow once more.","He supported He Yuanming to sit in a chair.","\"Father-in-law, Ran Ran suffered a lot following me, but now that we've settled in the northwest, life has been better every day. Now she is already pregnant and will give birth in a few months.\"","As for He Zhiran being pregnant with twins, Mo Jiuye planned to conceal it for now.","After all, everyone thought twins were more likely to be difficult births, and he didn't want the in-laws to worry unnecessarily.","Hearing that his daughter was pregnant, He Yuanming's tears flowed uncontrolled again.","\"Ran Ran was spoiled by me and her mother since she was little. It doesn't matter if she suffers, as long as she's alright.\"","Mo Jiuye's main purpose in meeting with his father-in-law was to remind him to pay attention to the actions of the Ninth Prince. He knew the steward would bring the clothes soon, so he couldn't afford any delay.","\"Father-in-law, I just discovered that the Ninth Prince is colluding with a sorcerer from the Southern Borderlands who gave him many poisonous bugs.","Today the Ninth Prince will take advantage of the birthday banquet to put the bugs on important ministers at court in order to control the situation.\"","Hearing Mo Jiuye's words, He Yuanming instantly put away his tears. He asked back in disbelief,","\"What? You said the Ninth Prince is colluding with a sorcerer from the Southern Borderlands?\"","Mo Jiuye nodded solemnly.","\"Yes, I saw it with my own eyes, it's absolutely true.","I took the risk to come tell father-in-law, don't fall for the Ninth Prince's tricks.","Also, for big brother's wedding, please keep an open mind, father-in-law. That Jade Princess is already dead, so she can't marry into the He family anyway, even if the Ninth Prince's household doesn't get exposed today for this matter.\"","Hearing so much news, it was impossible for He Yuanming not to be shocked.","He didn't expect that his son-in-law's trip to the capital would help resolve two crises for him.","But he still had doubts to ask.","\"Son-in-law, the Ninth Prince has treasonous intentions. That Southern Borderlands sorcerer would be the best witness to present in court. May I ask where this person is now?","Also, is the Jade Princess's death related to you?\"","Thinking that the Ninth Prince's beloved daughter had died, if it was discovered it would surely cause huge waves. If this matter was really done by his son-in-law, he must find a way to help him escape.","\"Father-in-law, I did indeed kill the Jade Princess. A fickle woman like that is completely unworthy of big brother.","Also, my purpose coming to the capital this time was to capture that Southern Borderlands sorcerer. Now I've succeeded, and my brothers have already escorted him out of the capital.\"","Mo Jiuye still had a certain understanding of He Yuanming's character, otherwise he wouldn't have agreed to marry He Zhiran.","For his Mo family sons taking wives, the requirements for status weren't high. They mainly valued the wife's parents' character.","He Yuanming had been an official at court for many years. Like his Mo family, he always maintained neutrality, not joining anyone's faction. And father-in-law was known for being an upright official, making no small contribution to Great Shun.","The fact that he hadn't been implicated by his Mo family despite everything showed this.","Moreover, he also believed father-in-law truly cared for Ran Ran. Even for Ran Ran's sake, he wouldn't speak of things that shouldn't be told.","Sure enough, when He Yuanming heard Mo Jiuye mention brothers, he seemed even more shocked.","\"Son-in-law, you just said your brothers?\" Could it be the Mo family sons are not dead?","Mo Jiuye was brief.","\"On the way heading northwest, I fortunately discovered eldest brother was still alive. With Ran Ran's help, I've now found six elder brothers, and learned of the whereabouts of other elders and uncles.","This Southern Borderlands man who gave the Ninth Prince poisonous bugs is the chief culprit in persecuting my Mo family sons. So I cannot leave him to father-in-law as evidence against the Ninth Prince. \"","Hearing Mo Jiuye's words, He Yuanming carefully absorbed it all. He sincerely felt happy for the Mo family.","As for his son-in-law mentioning Ran Ran helping, he only thought his son-in-law was being polite, and didn't think much of it.","As her father, he was clearer than anyone on his daughter's abilities.","Unlike other young ladies, He Zhiran never spent her days doing feminine hobbies like embroidery. She only liked reading those medical books.","Were medical books so simple to learn from just reading some books without a teacher?","There was no helping it. He and his wife doted on their daughter, so whether she could understand or not, they indulged her.","If it wasn't for his daughter making a fuss when marrying Mo Jiuye, leaving that box of medical books at home, the books would have been part of her dowry.","Thinking of this, He Yuanming felt more longing for his daughter.","But he was clear that now was not the time for him to be sentimental.","\"Since that's the case, I will find other ways to uncover evidence of the Ninth Prince's treason. We cannot allow such a villain to cause chaos.\"","Mo Jiuye knew with father-in-law's personality, he would strongly oppose the Ninth Prince.","To give him a full picture, he softly added:","\"There is one more thing I hope father-in-law knows, so you are prepared.\"","\"What is it?\" He Yuanming's heart was filled with complicated emotions. His son-in-law's appearance had brought him so much shocking news.","How could he know the matter Mo Jiuye was about to tell him would be even more shocking than everything before.","After all, they had been in the room for some time already, so Mo Jiuye did not dare to directly speak out.","He first went to the door to look out and make sure there were no suspicious people around before returning."]},{"number":355,"title":"Chapter 355: I'll be leaving now.","paragraphs":["\"Father-in-law, what I'm about to say may seem rather far-fetched, so please prepare yourself mentally,\" said Mo Jiuye solemnly.","Seeing his son-in-law's grave demeanor, He Yuanming also became serious. \"What is this about?\"","\"Nan Qi is not the biological child of the Emperor and Concubine Yuan. The true prince is someone else...\"","Mo Jiuye quickly explained to his father-in-law how Nan Qi and Fei Nanyu had been switched at birth, hoping he could figure out how to respond to this in the future.","As expected, this was earth-shattering news for He Yuanming.","\"It seems the future of Da Shun is beset with twists and turns, when even any tomcat or stray dog can become a prince.\"","Knowing his father-in-law was loyal to Da Shun, Mo Jiuye simply told him everything he knew.","\"There's more. Nan Heng has colluded with the Queen of the Southern Tribes. He is already dead. Prince Rui has fled the capital with Consort De, and they are living in hiding under assumed names elsewhere. So father-in-law, please be mentally prepared for who will eventually gain control of Da Shun.\"","For He Yuanming, each revelation from his son-in-law was more shocking than the last.","Seeing his dazed expression, Mo Jiuye could not afford to explain in detail, because right then, someone knocked on the door.","\"Master He, I've prepared the clothes.\"","He Yuanming quickly composed himself to look as if nothing had happened, and opened the door with his own hand.","Just as he was about to take the clothes from the steward, he saw the previously hale and hearty steward collapse on the ground, still clasping the porcelain bottle he had failed to conceal.","At the same time, Mo Jiuye yanked his father-in-law forcefully backwards.","\"Be careful,\" Mo Jiuye said softly.","Before He Yuanming even realized what was happening, Mo Jiuye had already caught a bug with his bare hands.","Because this was so sudden, Mo Jiuye did not have a small bottle on him. The gu worm struggled violently in his grip.","If he had not wanted to leave some evidence for his father-in-law to implicate the Ninth Prince, he might have crushed the gu worm dead already.","Although He Yuanming had never seen a gu worm with his own eyes, seeing his son-in-law's alarm, he guessed that the steward who had just arrived must have been sent by the Ninth Prince to infect him with gu.","Seeing his son-in-law still holding the disgusting worm, He Yuanming quickly fetched a teacup from the table and gave it to Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye accepted the teacup and put the worm inside, promptly covering it with the lid.","\"I didn't expect the Ninth Prince to act so quickly.\"","Mo Jiuye suspected that he had only just informed Fei Nanyu, and even if he and Nan Qi worked together to resist this, they would still need some time.","It was possible some ministers had already fallen into the trap.","Fortunately, he had brought his father-in-law here, and the man had not left yet. Otherwise, with He Yuanming's complete lack of martial prowess, there would have been no chance of escaping this unscathed.","Thinking of this, Mo Jiuye felt extremely anxious in retrospect. If his father-in-law had been infected with gu while he was aware of the plot, he wouldn't know how to explain to his wife when he returned to the Northwest.","\"Keep this gu worm safe, father-in-law, it may come in useful one day,\" said Mo Jiuye.","He Yuanming knew gu worms were extremely dangerous things. Worried that a mere teacup could not contain it, he took out his handkerchief and wrapped the teacup tightly.","\"It's fortunate you were here. Otherwise I could not have escaped this catastrophe unharmed.\"","Right now, Mo Jiuye had no time for further discussion. He dragged the steward into the room.","\"Father-in-law, the Ninth Prince's estate will soon be in great turmoil. It would be best if you leave this nest of right and wrong as soon as possible.\" Mo Jiuye sincerely advised.","He Yuanming nodded. \"I'll go to the palace now and report this matter to His Majesty.\"","Mo Jiuye knew his father-in-law was a man of good judgement. When he went to the palace, he would only mention the happenings at the Ninth Prince's estate, without bringing up Fei Nanyu and Nan Qi's identities.","As for what he would choose to do afterwards, Mo Jiuye was certain his father-in-law would find a better opportunity based on his experience.","With his father-in-law's crisis resolved, Mo Jiuye saw no need to linger.","\"I cannot stay here long, father-in-law. I must take my leave now.\"","Seeing his son-in-law about to depart, He Yuanming was still reluctant. \"Son-in-law, it was not easy for you to come to the capital. Why don't you visit the Minister's residence and let your mother-in-law see you too?\"","Mo Jiuye declined. \"I still have important matters to attend to. In the future, when there is a chance, I will definitely bring Ran Ran and our child to visit you and mother-in-law.\"","\"Since that's the case, I won't keep you. But you must be very careful in your dealings. Ran Ran is still waiting for your return in the Northwest,\" said He Yuanming.","In fact, He Yuanming's main purpose in inviting Mo Jiuye to his home was because he wanted to give his son-in-law some silver for the return trip. Their sudden departure from the capital meant he had only prepared money for his daughter on short notice, which was far from enough.","Now that his son-in-law had come to the capital, he intended to give him more silver. Unfortunately, He Yuanming had a habit of rarely carrying cash and promissory notes when going out.","As a result of today's events, He Yuanming found himself in an awkward spot, as he did not have any valuables on his person that he could give to his son-in-law.","Still, He Yuanming did not give up.","\"May I have your address in the Northwest, son-in-law?\"","Mo Jiuye did not think much of this request. It was only natural for the man to be concerned about his daughter's whereabouts. Initially, he had suggested He Ranran write home to reassure her family, but He Ranran was worried her current identity would negatively impact her family, so she had endured the separation without sending any letters.","Now that he had met with his father-in-law, there was no harm in telling him their address verbally. No one could use that against them.","\"We currently reside in Xiling Village, just west of Yuncheng in the Northwest,\" Mo Jiuye replied.","He Yuanming repeated the address several times in his mind to memorize it, before parting ways with Mo Jiuye.","As a guest, He Yuanming could leave the Prince's estate openly. But Mo Jiuye had to use his lightness skill to leap over the wall and slip away unseen.","Having resumed his original appearance, he went straight to the nearest market to buy a straw hat to hide his face, in case he was recognized by any acquaintances.","Departing the city went smoothly without incident. The city gate guards would not casually interrogate travelers.","Mo Jiuye reunited with his two brothers at top speed.","At this time, Si Meng still showed no signs of regaining consciousness, so traveling with him would be inconvenient. With Mo Jiuye present, Fifth Brother could relax and head out to buy ingredients for their evening meal.","But contrary to expectations, either due to Si Meng's unusual weight or some other reason, he actually woke up over an hour early.","Mo Jiuye was currently worried for his father-in-law, uncertain if Emperor Shunwu would believe him after he brought in the gu worm.","Just then, Sixth Brother's voice sounded in his mind.","\"Ninth brother, come quickly!\"","Hearing Sixth Brother's call, Mo Jiuye immediately pulled back his thoughts and hurried back to Si Meng's room.","Si Meng stared wide-eyed at Sixth Brother.","\"You're...Mo Jinnian?\"","Sixth Brother gave a cold humph. \"Humph! Bet you didn't expect we'd meet like this.\""]},{"number":356,"title":"Chapter 356: Where did you hide my father and brother","paragraphs":["During the time when [Sixth elder brother] was under the influence of the puppet worm, although he didn't know what had happened over the past few years. Without even needing to think, he knew that the puppet worm in his body must have been planted by the person in front of him, indicating that there must have been multiple contacts between them.","At this moment, [Mr. Si Meng] had already realized that the environment he was in was extremely unfavorable, especially after seeing [Mo Jiuye] come close to him, he was completely clear that he had fallen into the hands of the Mo brothers.","Thinking of these things, he couldn't help but resent them, blaming himself for being careless back then and giving [Mo Jinnian] a chance to be rescued. At the same time, he could also determine that the person who rescued [Mo Jinnian] from the south was [Mo Jiuye].","Although [Mr. Si Meng] had guessed most of what had happened, he still couldn't figure out no matter what, who was the expert who had relieved the puppet worm he had planted in the person.","With his status in the world of worm breeding, he dared to say that no second person would come out claiming to be number one. It was impossible for anyone to solve the gu worms he had planted in others.","Could it be that without him noticing, an even more powerful gu worm breeding expert had appeared?","Just as [Mr. Si Meng] was still lost in his own thoughts, [Mo Jiuye] had already angrily walked up to him and kicked him hard.","At the same time, the little white who had just flown back with its owner also flew into the room. Seeing its owner make a move, it excitedly circled around his head, even making a cry of joy.","[Mo Jiuye] didn't show any mercy with this kick, it was a real solid kick to [Mr. Si Meng]'s body. Even with his martial arts, [Mr. Si Meng] still couldn't bear it.","But his hands and feet were tied up with ropes and he couldn't move at all. Just when he was about to lose his temper at [Mo Jiuye], he saw his beloved pet.","\"Baby, go bite him.\"","He was very clear about the power of the pet he had carefully raised for over ten years. Once the little guy bared his claws, the aggressiveness would still be quite strong.","Today, having fallen into the hands of the Mo brothers, he probably had no hope of survival.","Since this was the case, he might as well go down with his beloved pet, at least he wouldn't feel lonely on the way.","To his surprise, the little white didn't listen to his command at all, but kept catering to [Mo Jiuye].","[Mr. Si Meng] still didn't give up, no matter what, he couldn't believe that his baby wouldn't listen to him. It was possible that the little guy was just too excited after not seeing him for so long.","After thinking it over in his heart, he tried to call Little White to harm the Mo brothers again.","Unexpectedly, this time Little White actually manifested an eagle's beak on its own and pecked at his eyes.","Seeing this, [Mr. Si Meng] was stunned for a moment, otherwise, with his martial arts skills, even with his hands and feet tied, he wouldn't be completely without the ability to dodge.","Although Little White didn't accurately peck his eyes, it viciously pecked off a piece of flesh under his eye.","The blood flowed down [Mr. Si Meng]'s cheek, coupled with his painful and shocked look, made him look extremely hideous.","[Mo Jiuye] stretched out an arm, and Little White landed steadily on it, right in front of [Mr. Si Meng].","He deliberately praised Little White in front of [Mr. Si Meng].","\"Little White, well done.\"","\"That's not possible. This is the pet I have carefully raised for over ten years. It can't be wrong.\" At this moment, [Mr. Si Meng] only thought that he had mistaken the pet. It was impossible for his precious pet to recognize someone else as its master.","[Mo Jiuye] didn't care about his thoughts. With the arch enemy of the Mo family right in front of him now, he was in no mood to circle around too much with him.","[Sixth elder brother] went straight to the point as well.","\"Speak, where are my father and brother hidden?\"","Hearing [Sixth elder brother] ask like this, [Mr. Si Meng]'s eyes shrank for a moment, and at the same time he also realized that many things were worse than he imagined.","To the Mo brothers, [Mr. Si Meng] was the biggest enemy.","Similarly, in [Mr. Si Meng]'s mind, the Mo family should be tortured and then go down to accompany his sweetheart after the appointed time.","Unexpectedly, the matter would be completed so soon, in less than a year, things kept happening.","At this moment, he could only stabilize the person in front of him, and then think of a way to escape.","With this thought, [Mr. Si Meng] immediately calmed down.","\"I don't know what you guys are talking about. We are strangers to each other. Why would you catch me?\"","[Mo Jiuye] sneered coldly, \"Hehe... old fox, just now you could still call out my [Sixth elder brother]'s name. What's wrong? Have we become strangers so quickly?\"","[Mr. Si Meng] continued to pretend to be confused.","\"It's not strange at all that I can recognize the famous Mighty God General of the Mo family. People used to have his portraits worshipped in their homes. Some people recognize him a little, it's not strange, is it?\"","Indeed this was the case.","[Sixth elder brother] Mo was born with divine strength. Commoners even circulated that a hammer in his hand weighed at least 100 catties.","Back then, when [Mo Jinnian] led the army on the border, he defeated the armies of the southern border so badly that they couldn't reorganize themselves. At that time, this matter was almost universally known.","It would just be a ghost if the Mo brothers believed his words.","The two brothers didn't want to waste too much words with this kind of person. But they both understood clearly in their hearts that this person couldn't die before finding their father and elder brother.","Therefore, there were great restrictions on interrogating him.","They didn't dare go too aggressively, in case the old guy tried something desperate, getting their father and elder brother killed too.","\"We brothers just want to know our father and elder brother's whereabouts. If you tell the truth, I can consider letting you get away.\"","This is how [Mo Jiuye] said to barely restrain his anger, a strategy of postponing aggression. He was afraid [Mr. Si Meng] would think of doing something extreme.","\"Didn't your father and elder brother die on the battlefield long ago? How could I possibly know their whereabouts?\"","The old fox [Mr. Si Meng] was also formidable. Since you want to play tricks on me, I can pretend to be confused as well.","[Mo Jiuye] didn't have much patience to begin with. Seeing him like this made him even less able to control the anger in his heart.","He also saw that it would be useless to keep beating around the bush with the old guy here, and probably wouldn't get anything out of him.","So he took out a small porcelain bottle from his arms.","It contained a bottle of itching powder that his wife had specially prepared for him.","This was something [He Zhiran] had thought of in advance. Successfully capturing [Mr. Si Meng] in the capital, it wouldn't be easy to get him to speak out without killing him.","So she specifically looked up recipes and made the itching powder.","[Mo Jiuye] just opened the bottle cap, then sprinkled the powder towards [Mr. Si Meng].","Seeing [Mo Jiuye]'s actions, [Mr. Si Meng] reflexively held his breath.","In his understanding, this was poisoning him.","He just didn't know what kind of poison it was. As long as it wasn't inhaled through his nose and mouth, he would still have a chance to escape.","But his knowledge was still too shallow. How could poisoning only be through nose and mouth inhalation?","[Mr. Si Meng]'s breath holding skill was indeed formidable. In his self perception, he didn't inhale any of the poison powder.","Just when he was feeling smug, he suddenly felt an unbearably itchy sensation all over his body.","He kept twisting his body, trying to dispel this awful feeling.","But the more he struggled and moved, the stronger the feeling became.","At the same time, he also realized that the poison [Mo Jiuye] had used on him wasn't the nose and mouth inhalation kind at all, but a poison to make his whole body feel terribly itchy."]},{"number":357,"title":"Chapter 357: Kill Me","paragraphs":["Mr. Si Meng had never seen such a poison before.","He had no choice but to believe that the Mo Family had high-level help behind them.","To be able to take out a poison that even he had never seen before and to remove the puppet poison from Mo Jinnian's body, there was no way they didn't have expert help, even if they beat him to death he wouldn't believe otherwise.","As the itchy feeling on his body became stronger and stronger, Mr. Si Meng could no longer bother to think carefully.","His body was like a worm, constantly twisting, and he even had an urge to just die.","\"Kill me... kill me... ahhhh... so itchy...\"","Mo Jiuye and Mo Jinnian, the two brothers, stood with their arms crossed, coldly watching Mr. Si Meng painfully rolling on the ground. They didn't have any sympathy at all. Compared to what he had done to the Mo Family, this torture was far from enough.","Seeing sweat appearing on Mr. Si Meng's forehead, and his painful moans gradually becoming weaker.","Mo Jiuye knew that at this moment, his consciousness was much weaker than before. So he took the opportunity to ask:","\"Speak, where are my uncles and brothers now?\"","At this moment, Mr. Si Meng also realized that his situation was much more difficult than he had imagined.","Especially the unbearable itchiness he felt in his body made him increasingly realize a fact.","That was, he only had two options today.","First, he could say the whereabouts of the Mo Family sons, and the other side might give him a quick death.","Second, he would die together with Mo Jiuye, Mo Jinnian and Mo Qing.","No matter what he did, it was impossible to successfully complete his revenge plan for his lover.","But it was impossible for him to frankly say the whereabouts of the Mo Family father and son. He would rather choose to die together with the Mo Family brothers, so that when he meets his lover underground, he can give an explanation.","Moreover, he still couldn't be completely sure exactly how many of the controlled Mo Family men had been rescued.","Although he couldn't take the Mo Family men to his lover's grave to worship, taking Mo Qing and his two sons should still count as half a success.","Although Mr. Si Meng had made up his mind, who doesn't want to live longer?","He decided to fight for himself one last time, and if that didn't work, he would die together with Mo Qing.","In order to avenge his lover, Mr. Si Meng was able to plan for many years. His temperament and wisdom were by no means comparable to ordinary people.","Although his hands and feet were tied up, he clearly knew that the treasures hidden in his clothes had long been searched away by the two brothers.","That is to say, not only were there no poisons on him at this moment, there were no Gu worms either.","Fortunately, he had refined his life Gu worm, and this Gu worm was inside his body.","No matter how wise the Mo Jiuye brothers were, they probably couldn't have thought of this point.","So he endured the terrible itchiness on his body and concentrated his mental power to summon his life Gu worm.","\"Mo Jinnian, Mo Jiuye, I'll ask you one last time, will you let me go, or let me take you and your father down with me?\"","Although Mo Jiuye had been watching Mr. Si Meng's miserable state coldly all along, he had never relaxed his vigilance for a moment.","When Mr. Si Meng concentrated his mind to summon his life Gu worm, he noticed something wrong immediately.","Although this was the first time he had seen such a situation, he didn't feel unfamiliar with it at all.","When he read that book \"Encyclopedia of Gu Techniques\" with his wife, he knew that Mr. Si Meng's current reaction was very likely that he was summoning his life Gu worm.","He just didn't know that Mr. Si Meng had left himself such a backup plan that after the death of the life Gu worm, it could still cause his body to explode and release the poison in his heart's blood.","What he was worried about was exactly Mr. Si Meng's next move.","If he really activated the life Gu worm, then the ones who would die with him were very likely to be his uncles.","No, not likely, definitely...","At this moment, Mo Jiuye could only use expedient means to stabilize the other party first.","\"I can let you go, but you have to exchange information about my uncles for it. This condition is not too much, right?\"","Mr. Si Meng didn't want to die either. Just now, if he hadn't wanted to fight for himself once, he wouldn't have acted so extremely either.","Seeing Mo Jiuye's attitude ease up, he felt even more that he really had a chance to escape. He simply started negotiating conditions.","\"I can tell you what you want to know, but first you need to detoxify me.\"","On this point, Mo Jiuye was really powerless. His wife had only given him itching powder, and no antidote.","He spread his hands helplessly at Mr. Si Meng, making a helpless expression.","\"There is no antidote.\"","When Mr. Si Meng heard there was no antidote, big drops of sweat kept rolling down his forehead.","If it wasn't for him not wanting to appear too powerless in front of the Mo brothers, he wouldn't have endured so hard and gritted his teeth.","He didn't expect that after he had threatened them, they didn't even have an antidote...","Now he also understood that the Mo brothers probably wouldn't let him off easily. This time it was medicine that made his body terribly itchy, who knows what methods they would use to torture a confession out of him next time.","Rather than wasting time with them like this and suffer, he might as well just directly take his second option. That way, at least he could leave with some dignity.","Seeing Mr. Si Meng showing signs of activating his life Gu worm again, Mo Jiuye hurriedly took out a tranquilizer gun.","With a crisp \"bang\", before Mr. Si Meng could react, he passed out.","Mo Jinnian had also noticed something wrong just now. He knew that what his little brother did was a forced move.","\"Little brother, this old guy is very cunning. I'm afraid it will be very difficult to get useful information from him.\"","On this point, Mo Jiuye could not deny it either.","\"It looks like now we can only keep him alive first while slowly trying to find a way to interrogate him.\"","\"But the longer we go without news, the more our father, eldest brother and second brother will suffer.\" Mo Jinnian was obviously a little anxious. Still, at this moment the two brothers were at a loss.","Mo Jiuye sighed.","\"This person has a life Gu worm in his body. Just now, if I hadn't knocked him unconscious in time, he would have activated the life Gu worm. At that time, it wouldn't have been just him dying. The people controlled by his life Gu worm would also have died with him.\"","Mo Jinnian didn't understand Gu techniques. Hearing Mo Jiuye explain these details scared him out in a cold sweat.","\"But... but we rushed here to the capital from thousands of miles away and captured Mr. Si Meng alive. Could it be that we would still be helpless?\"","Mo Jiuye pondered for a moment and said, \"For now, we can only bring this person with us quickly to meet up with third brother and the others in the Western Region to see if they have found any useful information.\""]},{"number":358,"title":"Chapter 358: If you want to kill, if you want to cut.","paragraphs":["As long as we can find the father and elders first and remove the Gu worms from them, we can mince this man into thousands of pieces to avenge our Mo family brothers. \" Sixth Elder Brother nodded, \"It seems this is the only way.\"","The two brothers had just discussed their strategy when they heard the sound of hoofbeats.","Sixth Elder Brother quickly walked to the door, \"Let me see.\"","He had just pushed open the door to see Fifth Elder Brother driving a carriage, also leading two horses back.","Without waiting for Mo Jinye to ask, Fifth Elder Brother took the initiative to say, \"Sixth younger brother, I went into the city to buy supplies, and brought our horses back at the same time, and also hitched a carriage.\"","Hearing Fifth Elder Brother's words, Mo Jiuye had to admire his thoughtfulness.","He and Sixth Elder Brother had just decided to take Mr. Si Meng with them first to the northwest to see what progress Third Elder Brother and the others had made there before studying countermeasures together.","The brothers needed horses to travel on the road, and Fifth Elder Brother had solved everything in one trip out.","Mo Jiuye's original plan was to rest here for the night, and also interrogate Mr. Si Meng in the meantime. It would be best if he could find out some key things tonight, but even if he couldn't, he could also understand the other's strengths and weaknesses.","Unexpectedly, Mr. Si Meng acted so radically for the sake of his father and elders that Mo Jiuye was at a loss for a while, unable to let him die immediately.","Just as Fifth Elder Brother brought back the carriage, he had also experienced Mr. Si Meng's strengths and weaknesses, and had no intention of staying here for long. They could slowly come up with countermeasures on the road.","\"Fifth Elder Brother, let's set out now and whip the horses to gallop to the western border to see what progress Third Elder Brother and the others have made over there before studying countermeasures together.\"","Seeing Mo Jiuye's expression, Fifth Elder Brother knew it was urgent.","\"Okay, let's set out now. I just bought some dry rations. We can last for several days on the road.\"","The three brothers threw Mr. Si Meng into the carriage. Even in his unconscious state, none of them dared to take him lightly.","For such an old fox, they absolutely could not give him the slightest chance to escape.","So Sixth Elder Brother was responsible for driving the carriage, Fifth Elder Brother rode one horse and led another, and Mo Jiuye was responsible for guarding Mr. Si Meng in the carriage. Once he woke up, he would continue to parley with him.","Perhaps Mr. Si Meng's subconscious did not want to wake up and suffer from that terrible itch. It was not until the carriage had traveled a hundred miles and it was deep night that he showed signs of waking up.","All the way, Mo Jiuye had remained awake to clearly see Mr. Si Meng's movements. The oil lamp had also been kept on.","Therefore, when Mr. Si Meng showed a little reaction, Mo Jiuye noticed it.","After all, Mr. Si Meng had been shot twice with anesthetic darts in one day. At the moment his head was still a little dizzy.","His first feeling was that his whole body was tense and unable to move freely.","But soon, he realized the danger of his situation.","In the light of the oil lamp, he also saw the face of the person in front of him clearly.","\"Mo Jiuye, what do you want to do?\"","Although Mo Jiuye had no plan for him at the moment, he could not lose momentum.","\"Naturally, I want to learn from you what I want to know.\"","The voices of the two men's conversation were not small, and they did not intend to hide anything from anyone.","Sixth Elder Brother driving the carriage outside could also hear them clearly.","At the moment they were shuttling through the wilds, so there was no scruples about talking.","\"Old fox, if you don't know what's good for you, do you believe I will smash your head with a hammer?\"","Sixth Elder Brother had the same idea as Mo Jiuye, mainly wanting to frighten Mr. Si Meng. As long as Mr. Si Meng had the slightest desire to live, he did not believe he could not get something useful out of him.","Unfortunately, his and Mo Jiuye's methods were of no use to Mr. Si Meng at all.","The two brothers did not know that the effects of the itchy powder on Mr. Si Meng had passed and he no longer felt so uncomfortable. On the contrary, it ignited a glimmer of hope for life in him.","However, he did not want to show it in front of the Mo brothers.","\"Humph! A real man should kill or chop as you please. There is no need to frighten people here.\"","Mo Jiuye saw that this old fox really would not shed tears until he saw the coffin, and quickly raised his hand to hit his head.","This was already a deep blood feud for the Mo family, and Mo Jiuye could no longer endure it at this moment.","Although Mr. Si Meng had martial arts skills, compared to the Mo brothers, it was not enough. Plus his hands and feet were tied up tightly, and the carriage space was small, he had nowhere to dodge. He could only take Mo Jiuye's vicious beating head-on.","This time Mo Jiuye was really angry, and more importantly, it also contained a large part of venting.","After several hits, Mr. Si Meng's face was severely deformed and he could not see his original appearance at all.","\"Mo Jiuye, do you want your father to perish together with me?\"","Mr. Si Meng realized something was wrong as soon as he said this sentence.","The Mo brothers also reacted very quickly, hearing the key point from his words.","Sixth Elder Brother had already stopped the carriage and opened the carriage door to glare at Mr. Si Meng.","\"Speak quickly, what have you done to my father?\"","Fifth Elder Brother also rushed up quickly. The two tall brothers blocked the carriage door together, their eyes fixed closely on Mr. Si Meng.","Mo Jiuye also stopped the fist that was raised high above his head and did not let it fall immediately. He just wanted to wait for his answer.","Seeing the nervousness of the brothers, Mr. Si Meng regretted saying the wrong thing, but also breathed a sigh of relief.","Since he had already said it, he knew that no matter how cunningly he denied it, it would be useless. Perhaps he could also negotiate terms with Mo Qing and the Mo brothers.","\"That's right, Mo Qing has indeed been poisoned by my Gu worm, but so what? If I don't say where he is, no matter how you search you won't be able to find him.","Hahahahahaha...\"","Mr. Si Meng decided to gloat inexplicably and burst into a string of triumphant laughter.","Looking at the Mo brothers, it was incredibly annoying. It was nothing more than taking advantage of the fact that they did not dare kill him for their father's life.","In addition, the threatening meaning goes without saying. In short, Mr. Si Meng's actions greatly displeased the Mo brothers.","The only consequence of displeasure was, on the premise of preserving his life, to beat him violently.","Mo Jiuye had hit him earlier, and this time it was Sixth Elder Brother's turn.","He saw Sixth Elder Brother leap onto the carriage board, then picked up Mr. Si Meng's whole person and threw him to the ground.","Seeing this, Fifth Elder Brother could no longer restrain himself and kicked Mr. Si Meng hard in the body.","The Mo brothers were all veterans. They knew best where it would hurt the most but not be fatal when beating someone.","\"Ah... Ah... Ahhhhhh.... You will pay the price for what you are doing now...\"","Seeing the two elder brothers beating Mr. Si Meng violently, Mo Jiuye made no attempt to stop it."]},{"number":359,"title":"Chapter 359: Get to the West as Early as You Can","paragraphs":["He was well aware that his two elder brothers knew their limits, which was one thing. More importantly, he knew that Mr. Si Meng wanted to activate the destined witch insect and needed to calm his mind to do so.","At the moment, he was being violently beaten and simply could not calm his mind, making it impossible to activate the destined witch insect.","The Fifth and Sixth Elders did in fact know their limits, only stopping when they felt the moment was right.","By this point, Mr. Si Meng's body had gone limp on the ground like a pile of mud.","Not only was he tied up and unable to move, even if he had been able to act freely, trying to get up after being beaten like this would have been difficult.","Mo Jiuye was also not letting up, constantly observing his every move while keeping the tranquilizer gun ready in his hand. If Mr. Si Meng showed any abnormal reactions, he would immediately open fire.","Mr. Si Meng lay limply on the ground, breathing heavily.","But the perpetually proud man was not about to bow his head so easily.","\"You will all regret everything you have done to me today.\"","As he finished speaking, he tried his best to steady his emotions and focus all his willpower, preparing to activate the mother destined witch insect.","Mo Jiuye immediately recognized his intention and was about to fire when he suddenly felt a slight vibration against his chest.","He knew that summoning the destined witch insect for suicide required at least half an incense stick's worth of time. So rather than immediately pulling the trigger, he reached into his robe and pulled out a small cloth bag.","The bag contained the witch insects they had seized from Mr. Si Meng.","In the moonlight, he could see that one of the larger porcelain bottles was shaking nonstop in his palm.","In other words, the vibration he had just felt originated from this bottle.","At the same time, Mr. Si Meng also saw what Mo Jiuye was holding in his hand.","If the light had been better, the brothers would surely have seen the bloodthirsty glint in his eyes.","Though they couldn't make out the color of Mr. Si Meng's eyes, the brothers knew the old fox was staring at the bottles in Mo Jiuye's hand.","Facing his enemy, Mo Jiuye had no intention of passing up a chance to drive him mad.","He waved the porcelain bottles in front of Mr. Si Meng.","\"What's wrong? Anxious to see your treasures? Too bad they're all in my hands now, completely out of your reach.\"","He taunted Mr. Si Meng like this not simply to mock him.","Mo Jiuye was indirectly buying time, because he could feel the shaking of the larger bottle growing more intense.","Without understanding the situation, he didn't want to take any risks.","To be safe, Mo Jiuye finally pulled the tranquilizer gun's trigger, and Mr. Si Meng once again lost consciousness after a crisp bang.","The Fifth and Sixth Elders were not at all surprised by Mo Jiuye's actions, because they too were holding such weapons.","They had just been a little unclear about the situation and hadn't thought to resolve it this way.","At the moment, the two brothers had no time to envy their Ninth Younger Brother's use of advanced weaponry. Their eyes fixed on Mr. Si Meng as they asked:","\"Ninth Brother, what should we do next? Continue on our way?\"","Mo Jiuye nodded. \"Continue on our way, and try to reach the western border as soon as possible.\"","He was now worried that Mr. Si Meng had already shown suicidal intentions twice. Any more delays, and Mo Jiuye feared he would die on the road.","Even with the brothers watching him closely, if Mr. Si Meng stubbornly refused to eat, he could still starve himself to death along the way.","Mo Jiuye found this quite vexing.","The brothers had travelled thousands of miles to the capital and captured their target, but the crafty Mr. Si Meng had yet to reveal any useful information.","Not only had they learned nothing useful, just now the sly old fox had let slip that their father was being controlled by his destined witch insect.","At the same time, they now knew for certain that their father was still alive, but the most crucial detail - his exact location - remained a mystery to them.","The carriage rumbled into motion again amidst Mo Jiuye's swirling thoughts.","Knowing Mr. Si Meng would not wake for a while, Mo Jiuye leaned back in the carriage to ponder.","He recalled the passage on destined witch insects from the Compendium of Witch Insect Techniques.","As he turned it over in his mind, Mo Jiuye suddenly had an inspiration.","The passage mentioned that most witch insect masters kept their destined witch insect inside their bodies, with only extremely rare exceptions.","These exceptional few were those who cultivated both witch insects and poisons. To refine ever more potent toxins, they often tested the effects themselves.","To avoid self-poisoning, they used a special technique to force all toxins in their bodies into the heart corner, using the heart's blood to encircle the toxins and prevent them from spreading through the rest of the body, thus protecting themselves.","Just now, Mr. Si Meng had clearly been trying to activate his destined witch insect to commit suicide, yet the porcelain bottle in his hand had shaken nonstop. This indicated a strong possibility that Mr. Si Meng was one of those rare exceptions mentioned in the book.","The book also stated that for witch insect masters who kept their destined witch insect separate from their body, their heart blood was highly toxic. Once they activated the destined witch insect for suicide, their own bodies would also explode.","Their greatest weapon would be their toxic heart blood. Even the slightest splash on the skin would leave no hope of survival.","Mo Jiuye suddenly felt greatly enlightened.","So Mr. Si Meng's destined witch insect was literally in his own hands.","And he had intended to use the mother's suicide to detonate his body, not only killing the father under the control of his destined witch insect, but taking the three brothers with him.","Looking at Mr. Si Meng's battered face, Mo Jiuye was filled with the urge to end his loathsome life on the spot.","But he could not do that yet.","Because he had thought of a way to prevent Mr. Si Meng from activating the destined witch insect for suicide.","That was, to take Mr. Si Meng's heart blood to nourish his destined witch insect. The destined witch insect would not reject the toxins in its master's heart blood; on the contrary, it would become even livelier.","No matter how the master tried to control it, it would not choose suicide.","Still, Mo Jiuye did not dare be careless about obtaining Mr. Si Meng's heart blood.","Just now, amidst his desperate ramblings, Mr. Si Meng had only revealed that the destined witch insect controlled their father. The situations of their Eldest and Second Brothers remained unclear, and most importantly, he still hoped to ask about his elders' whereabouts.","If it were anyone else, Mo Jiuye could simply plunge a blade in and take the heart blood without such elaborate planning.","Fortunately, he knew the precise location of the heart blood. Before leaving, his wife had equipped him with many surgical tools to help free his family from the witch insects' control.","As for sterile conditions, as long as Mr. Si Meng didn't die, someone as reprehensibly evil as him did not deserve them anyway.","Mo Jiuye carefully planned it over and over in his mind until he was certain nothing could go wrong. Only then did he open the carriage door.","\"Sixth Brother, find a quiet place for us to stop.\"","Sixth Elder reflexively glanced back at Mr. Si Meng, thinking something might be wrong with him."]},{"number":360,"title":"Chapter 360: Blood in My Heart","paragraphs":["As a result, what Sixth Elder Brother saw was that Mr. Si Meng was still in a state of unconsciousness.","He asked in puzzlement: \"Ninth Younger Brother, what happened to the old fox?\"","Although he had restrained his strength when dealing with Fifth Elder Brother just now, he was still a little worried that he had hit the old ghost too hard and sent him to the Western Paradise.","\"Sixth Brother, don't worry. I thought of a way to deal with this old fox.\" Mo Jiuye explained.","Hearing this, the depression in Sixth Elder Brother's heart seemed to dissipate in an instant.","Although he and Ninth Younger Brother had not seen each other for many years, through the contact during this period of time, he discovered that Ninth Younger Brother was no longer the youngster he used to be.","Perhaps it was because of the changes in the family over the years, Ninth Younger Brother had not only become steadier, even his wisdom was not comparable to that of his other brothers.","Therefore, as long as it was something Ninth Younger Brother said, he would believe it unconditionally.","\"Okay, I'll find a quiet place now.\"","The conversation between the two brothers did not escape Fifth Elder Brother's ears.","Although he did not interject, he had the same feeling in his heart as Sixth Brother, which was that if Ninth Younger Brother said he had thought of a way, it must be foolproof.","The three brothers drove the carriage to a secluded and flat grove, and Sixth Brother pulled on the reins.","\"Ninth Brother, I think here is good.\"","In fact, Mo Jiuye was not too worried. He just considered that the identities of the three brothers were rather special, and they were also with Mr. Si Meng, so he wanted to avoid any possible trouble as much as possible.","He opened the carriage door to take a look.","\"Sixth Brother, this location is not bad, let's do it here.\"","There was no time to delay. He planned to take out Mr. Si Meng's heart blood before he woke up.","\"Sixth Brother, stand guard outside and respond immediately if there is any danger. Fifth Brother, come help me in the carriage.\"","Fifth Brother and Sixth Brother nodded solemnly, each attending to their own duties.","Fifth Brother entered the carriage and eagerly asked, \"Ninth Brother, what can Fifth Brother do to help?\"","Mo Jiuye did not explain immediately, but took out two surgical knives given to him by his wife.","\"Fifth Brother, take this old man's shirt off.\"","Fifth Brother did not know what Ninth Younger Brother was going to do, but after just a moment of stunned hesitation, he started to act.","Although sterilization steps were omitted, the lighting requirements for surgery were still extremely high, after all Mr. Si Meng's life could not be harmed yet.","Mo Jiuye thought for a moment, helplessly took out a small but powerful flashlight and a small white porcelain bottle from his package.","Additionally, considering that Mr. Si Meng's heartblood was highly toxic, he could not risk his and his brothers' lives with it.","Mo Jiuye also gave himself and Fifth Brother each a pair of medical rubber gloves.","Seeing him take out so many strange things, Fifth Brother's eyes were not enough.","\"Ninth Brother, what are these?\"","Mo Jiuye had already anticipated that taking these things out in front of his two elder brothers would surely lead to questioning.","He calmly said, \"These were all given to me by the foreigners. I originally thought these things were useless, but your sister-in-law was thoughtful and worried that we might need them on the road, so she insisted on stuffing them into my package.\"","Speaking of foreigners, Fifth Brother was truly convinced.","Not to mention anything else, just the glass used to build the house, he had heard from Eighth Brother that it was purchased by Ninth Brother and his wife from the foreigners.","So if the foreigners could take out such special glass, not to mention these little things!","Mo Jiuye did not know what Fifth Brother was thinking. He also knew that his explanation was too vague. Anyway, having an excuse was better than not having one.","At this moment, he had already entered a state of full concentration.","His cutting skills were not as professional as He Zhiran's, especially since he could not harm Mr. Si Meng's life. So at this moment, his mood was extremely nervous.","He tried hard to recall what his wife looked like when she helped others with surgery, quickly locating the right position. The sharp surgical knife soon cut through Mr. Si Meng's skin and flesh.","Seeing Ninth Brother's actions, Fifth Brother was also sweating for him.","Although Mo Jiuye understood some principles, after all, it was his first time doing it, so his movements were naturally a little clumsy.","Fortunately, everything was going according to his plan, with no deviations.","Fifth Brother, who was staring closely at Mo Jiuye's actions, suddenly heard him say urgently, \"Fifth Brother, get ready to collect the blood.\"","Mo Jiuye had quickly identified the aorta at the center of Mr. Si Meng's heart, which was where the heartblood was located.","Fifth Brother hurriedly brought the porcelain bottle to the right position and removed the stopper.","In order to prevent the toxic heartblood from splashing, Mo Jiuye's actions suddenly became extremely gentle.","He gently fixed the blood vessel with forceps, then pulled up a section and aligned it with the bottle opening.","With another raise of his hand holding the knife, Mr. Si Meng's heartblood smoothly flowed into the porcelain bottle.","Mo Jiuye operated skillfully, and the toxic blood did not splash at all, which relieved him.","The heartblood that slowly flowed out was pitch black in color. Fifth Brother collected about half a bottle before the color gradually became normal.","Mo Jiuye was not too shocked by this situation as he understood it from reading books.","However, it was different for Fifth Brother. This half bottle of pitch-black heartblood completely exceeded his knowledge.","\"Ninth Brother, what is this?\"","Sixth Brother, who was standing guard outside the carriage, was also very curious about what was happening inside when he heard the conversation between the two brothers. If he didn't have to keep a lookout at his post, he would have gone in to ask about it long ago.","Since taking Mr. Si Meng's heartblood was to resolve the current crisis, Mo Jiuye certainly had to explain it clearly to his two elder brothers.","So while he was stitching up Mr. Si Meng's wound, he told them what he knew.","After listening to Ninth Brother's account, the two brothers let out a sigh of relief, but also felt somewhat terrified in retrospect.","If it wasn't for Ninth Brother's quick reaction just now, Mr. Si Meng really would have activated his life-worm to commit suicide, then detonated the toxic blood in his heart, and at that time not only would they be unable to save their father and elder brothers, even the three of them could have possibly died along with him.","They didn't expect Ninth Brother to be so knowledgeable and understand these things.","Especially Fifth Brother, who witnessed Ninth Brother successfully extract Mr. Si Meng's heartblood with his own eyes. His admiration for Ninth Brother was now indescribable in words.","While Mo Jiuye explained things clearly, he had also finished treating Mr. Si Meng's wound.","Fifth Brother carefully covered the porcelain bottle and put it away safely before helping to dress Mr. Si Meng again.","Only then did Mo Jiuye take the porcelain bottle containing the toxic heartblood and carefully pour some into the bottle containing Mr. Si Meng's life-worm.","In the lamplight they could see that the life-worm in the bottle became especially excited when it encountered its master's toxic heartblood, and showed no intention of escaping from the bottle at all.","This indicated that Mo Jiuye's approach was correct. As long as this life-worm could continually come into contact with its master's heartblood, it would stay alive. Even if its master tried to control it to commit suicide, it would not obey."]},{"number":361,"title":"Chapter 361: The Invasion","paragraphs":["After getting all this done, the sky outside had already started to brighten.","The Mo Jiuye brothers had travelled overnight, and after getting Mr. Si Meng's essence and blood, they were quite tired at the moment.","The three decided to take turns resting for a while, and after it got brighter they would check on the situation with the old fox waking up before continuing on their journey.","The Mo Jiuye brothers had just gotten through a difficult spot, and Xi Ling Village was also facing a test at this moment.","The houses the Mo Family had recently built were basically completed, and Hu Cong had also invited many carpenters to come and build furniture together.","There were also chicken and livestock pens and grounds that hadn't been completed when Mo Jiuye was home, and Nan Rui had also noticed something amiss that around where he was living, the Mo Family had not started any construction.","He belatedly realized that it was because he and his mother were here that the construction schedule had been delayed.","Since he had already bought a house site in the village anyway, and would move away sooner or later, he rented a small courtyard to live in temporarily from the villagers.","People arranged by Hu Cong were already building his new courtyard.","As soon as Nan Rui moved out, He Zhiran started organizing people to help build chicken and livestock farms.","Thanks to the special properties of the seeds, the crops in the fields were still thriving even with little rain.","If they hadn't all been worried about the brothers' safety, the atmosphere in the Mo Family recently would have been one of celebration and peace.","Even so, no one was neglecting the tasks at hand, and everyone was working hard at their own jobs.","He Zhiran would go rest inside her dimensional space at night, and leave before dawn.","She had just left her space when she heard the dogs barking chaotically outside.","At the same time, hurried footsteps could be heard coming to the door.","There was a knock.","\"Sister-in-law, Mother told me to take you away from the village to hide first.\"","It was eighth sister-in-law's voice.","He Zhiran hurriedly opened the door.","\"Sister-in-law, what happened?\"","Eighth sister-in-law said urgently: \"There are Barbarians coming down from the mountain to raid us. Seventh brother and eighth brother have already taken weapons and gone over. Mother is worried about your pregnancy and told me to take you away from the village first.\"","He Zhiran was not scared by the Barbarians' raid.","The first thing she needed to do was to clearly understand the specifics of the situation.","\"Sister-in-law, don't panic first. Tell me the details of what happened.\"","In fact, eighth sister-in-law did not know the specifics either.","\"I was still asleep when I heard the dogs barking louder and louder outside.","Then eighth brother hurried out to check what was going on, and ran back to inform everyone that it was Barbarians invading.\"","When she got to this point, eighth sister-in-law also thought it was what the villagers often talked about, with Barbarians coming over the mountain from time to time to raid here.","However, what Mo Chuhan said was Barbarians invading, which had a completely different implication from raiding.","The observant He Zhiran heard something amiss from eighth sister-in-law's words.","\"Sister-in-law, eighth brother told you it was Barbarians invading instead of raiding, right?\"","Eighth sister-in-law froze for a moment, seemingly trying to remember, then nodded forcefully, \"Yes, yes, yes, he said it was invading.\"","When He Zhiran heard eighth sister-in-law's confirmation, she felt that things were not simple.","Just as she was pondering, Old Lady Mo also came over with the women.","He Zhiran took the initiative to greet them: \"Mother, this is not simple. Please take the sisters-in-law and Hanyue to safety.\"","The reason Old Lady Mo brought the women over was because she didn't see He Zhiran come out when she was waiting at the door, so she came to urge them.","Unexpectedly, the ninth daughter-in-law actually told her to take the women away.","Eighth sister-in-law did not discern the severity of the matter, but she would not make the same mistake.","\"No, the number of Barbarians is too large, just relying on your two brothers is simply not enough to hold them back.\"","As she spoke, Old Lady Mo took out the tranquilizer guns that He Zhiran had given them during their exile.","\"As women of the Mo Family, even without men, we still have to defend our home.\"","She looked at He Zhiran's already very swollen belly.","\"You're carrying the Mo Family's only grandchild now. You must not take any risks. Listen to Mother and go into the city with your sister-in-law to notify Lord Meng to think of a way. We can still hold out here for a while.\"","From Old Lady Mo's account and her anxious expression, He Zhiran clearly realized the severity of the situation.","In such a critical moment, how could she as a former soldier abandon her family and leave alone?","Moreover, with her dimensional space she had even more advanced weapons that could suppress the enemies. If they encountered a crisis that they couldn't defuse, she'd rather reveal some secrets than sacrifice her family's lives.","She was not worried about her own safety either, with her space it would be easy peasy to preserve her own life.","\"Mother, I can't leave. You know a little about my skills. My pregnancy makes my body unwieldy, so I might as well stay home and take care of fourth brother.\"","Her thought was that even if she couldn't openly fight alongside the Mo Family's women, staying in Xi Ling Village would enable her to more easily step in to help if any emergency occurred.","It seemed Old Lady Mo saw through her thoughts. She answered without even thinking:","\"Your fourth brother is a Mo Family man. How could he have the cowardly notion of fearing death over valuing life?","I've already left my weapon with him over there. If any Barbarians come to kill him, even if he dies, he'll drag a few under him as padding.\"","He Zhiran understood clearly that Mo Family men indeed had no possibility of playing deserter. Even fourth brother who was still recovering from injury was no exception.","He would rather die a heroic death than cower behind his family members as a shrinking turtle.","Since this method wouldn't work either, He Zhiran could only give up resisting and think of another way.","\"If that's the case, then I'll listen to Mother and go with sister-in-law into the city to notify Lord Meng.\"","\"Good. There's no time to lose, you two sisters-in-law go quickly.\"","After speaking, Old Lady Mo beckoned for the women to make way at the door and let He Zhiran and eighth sister-in-law leave swiftly.","After seeing them off some ways, Old Lady Mo solemnly said to the women who stayed behind, \"Although we're just powerless women, we still can't let outsiders bully us.","The home we finally built up is now suffering a Barbarian attack. We absolutely cannot let them succeed.\"","Hearing the indignant words from mother-in-law, second sister-in-law first took out a tranquilizer gun.","\"Mother is right. As Mo Family people we definitely can't let others bully us.\"","Seeing her actions, the other sisters-in-law also echoed in succession."]},{"number":362,"title":"Chapter 362: I will Take Care of Myself","paragraphs":["A group of women, all nervously holding anesthetic guns, getting ready to join the battle to protect their homeland.","He Zhiran was helplessly led out of the front door by Eighth Sister-in-law.","What first met their eyes were all the villagers running towards the foot of the mountain with hoes and other tools in their hands.","From this it could be deduced that the two elder brothers and the dogs were standing guard there, and those invading Barbarians had not yet been able to break into the village.","At the same time, she could also feel that the dogs' barking was decreasing more and more, but the war cries were endless.","Seeing He Zhiran stop in her tracks, Eighth Sister-in-law urged, \"Ninth younger sister, let's go quickly. I'll safely send you to the city, then I'll also come back to fight alongside everyone.\"","\"Eighth Sister-in-law, have you ever thought that if we just hide in the city like this, by the time we rush back, we might not be able to participate in the battle?\"","He Zhiran knew that Eighth Sister-in-law didn't usually have so many intricate thoughts, so she planned to patiently persuade her.","Sure enough, after hearing her words for a bit, Eighth Sister-in-law became even more unwilling to leave.","But she had to listen to her mother-in-law's words.","\"I'll safely send you to the city, then I can run back.\"","\"I'm heavy and walk slowly. We don't even know how to drive a carriage. Eighth Sister-in-law, with your coming and going, I'm afraid a whole day would pass.\"","He Zhiran knew how to drive a carriage. She guessed Eighth Sister-in-law probably didn't know, and wanted to use this to put her in a difficult position.","\"What should we do then?\" Eighth Sister-in-law was indeed somewhat troubled. She absolutely could not let this pregnant Ninth Younger Sister leave alone.","Seeing that Eighth Sister-in-law had already taken the bait, He Zhiran spoke solemnly, \"I know Eighth Sister-in-law is also worried about Eighth elder brother. You see my belly is quite big, but I can move very nimbly. Going to the city alone is no problem.\"","Eighth Sister-in-law hesitated.","She really wanted to stay and resist the Barbarians together with her husband, regardless of life or death. In this life, she never wanted to be separated from her husband again. Even if they died, at least the couple could keep each other company on the road.","Eighth Sister-in-law unconsciously touched the anesthetic gun in her arms which had already gained some warmth. Although she didn't say anything, her thoughts had all been seen through by He Zhiran's eyes.","\"Eighth Sister-in-law, listen to me. The situation is so urgent now. One more person means one more bit of strength. Not to mention you have such a powerful weapon in your hands. It would be a pity if it couldn't be put to use.\"","Eighth Sister-in-law was thoroughly shaken, but she hadn't completely lost her reason.","She took out the anesthetic gun from her arms and handed it to He Zhiran.","\"Ninth younger sister, take this. It can be used for self-defense on the road. I and those villagers can also make do with hoes.\"","Eighth Sister-in-law didn't know if He Zhiran had this kind of weapon on hand. When she had called her out earlier, Ninth younger sister had just woken up. She believed Ninth younger sister didn't even have time to take out her weapon.","Letting her go to the city alone already went against Old Lady Mo's orders. If she let a pregnant woman leave alone without even a life-saving object in her hands, her conscience would feel even more uneasy.","How many anesthetic guns were there in He Zhiran's space?","Her original intention was to politely refuse, but she worried that if she refused, Eighth Sister-in-law would change her mind again, which would be too regrettable.","So she reached out and took the anesthetic gun.","\"Eighth Sister-in-law, don't worry. I will definitely take good care of myself.\"","Seeing that she had accepted the weapon, Eighth Sister-in-law also felt relieved.","\"Ninth younger sister, I can hear the shouting getting closer and closer. There's no time to delay. Leave quickly and go find Master Meng.\"","\"Alright. Eighth Sister-in-law, be careful.\"","He Zhiran turned around, pretending to continue towards the city.","Looking back again, she saw Eighth Sister-in-law had already run off without a trace. Those villagers who were going to battle had also run over to the foot of the mountain.","He Zhiran decisively turned back.","However, she hid as she moved, in case she was discovered by her family and caused more trouble.","Although He Zhiran was pregnant, relying on her own lack of delicacy, when Mo Jiuye couldn't see her, she often exercised. As a result, even with such a huge belly now, her movements were not clumsy at all.","She deliberately avoided taking the main village road, but moved along the fields where there were very few people.","The shouts and screams grew closer and closer, as well as the sound of metal weapons clashing.","He Zhiran knew the battle scene was not far now.","She didn't rashly approach, but carefully listened to the sounds to judge the battle situation.","Mo Jiuye had said the Barbarians spoke similarly to the dialects of the people in the northwest, but there was an obvious difference.","That was the Barbarians would say \"I\" as \"we\".","Therefore, He Zhiran could determine which side was speaking by listening for this word.","She continued probing and hiding as she moved forward. The sounds entering her ears grew closer and closer.","\"Get them for us. Kill all these moths to the flame. Then everything in this village will be ours.\"","\"You wish.\" This was Eighth Brother's voice.","He Zhiran could hear that when Eighth Brother spoke, his voice was somewhat hoarse. It seemed he was not as calm as he appeared.","Also from the shouting, He Zhiran could determine there were at least over five hundred people.","The able-bodied men of Xi Ling Village together also exceeded one hundred people. It seemed the Barbarians were really serious this time.","But right now she still couldn't see what the Barbarians looked like, and didn't know if they were ordinary commoners gathered together or a formal army.","Immediately after, she also heard Second Sister-in-law's voice.","\"Mother, our weapons are so powerful. Why don't we just take them out and use them?\"","Second Sister-in-law's voice was loud. He Zhiran could hear her clearly. Old Lady Mo always spoke calmly and steadily. He Zhiran couldn't hear how she responded.","But since the anesthetic guns had yet to make a sound, she could infer that the old lady had stopped Second Sister-in-law's behavior.","From this it could be seen that the battle situation was not as severe as imagined. Otherwise the old lady wouldn't have stopped everyone from using the anesthetic guns.","The old lady's considerations were also thoughtful. After all, weapons like the anesthetic guns were too against heaven. If they didn't face mortal danger, she didn't want to bring trouble to the family.","Since the battle was not as tense as imagined, He Zhiran simply moved even closer. She planned to secretly observe. As long as she wasn't discovered by her family, everything would be fine.","She moved forward again a stretch and hid behind a large tree.","The view here was extremely good, and she could clearly see the battle ahead.","Eighth Brother was the most valiant, wielding the large knife used for hunting. It could be said to fell one with each stroke.","Seventh elder brother was also unambiguous. He had already seen his womenfolk run over. In order to prevent them from being tainted by this bloodiness, he desperately resisted, his stance not one bit inferior to Mo Jiuye's.","Although the Mo family's women had not rushed forward to grapple with the enemy like the two men, each one was already standing guard in formation under Old Lady Mo's leadership, with anesthetic guns concealed in their sleeves, ready to attack at any time.","Before seeing the battle scene, He Zhiran had already estimated the Barbarians' numbers.","In her opinion, a force of this size could not be ordinary commoners.","However, what she saw with her own eyes was another scene.","These Barbarians had no unified clothing. They looked no different from ordinary commoners."]},{"number":363,"title":"Chapter 363: Capture the First to Capture the King","paragraphs":["Only, she felt that these people's offensive postures were not as simple as ordinary common people, but looked very organized.","In addition, her one hundred German Shepherd dogs had all come to assist. Without the summons of the two elder brothers, they would take the initiative to attack the invaders.","Although those barbarians did not take much advantage under the brave attack of the dogs, what they held in their hands must have been shiny machetes.","The dogs desperately protected their homes. It was inevitable that when they failed to dodge in time, their bodies would be cut by the other party.","Even so, they still tried their best to bite the enemy's body firmly and refused to let them leave.","The villagers who had rushed over were probably encountering such a battle formation of barbarians for the first time. If Zhao Li had not been a little sensible, shouting for everyone to go up together, I'm afraid they would all be scared silly.","However, when they thought that their homes might be ravaged by these barbarians, their morale was refreshed at once, and they rushed forward holding hoes and other items.","The shouts of killing became louder and louder, and the Mo brothers and dogs were unstoppable.","However, the villagers were much weaker. They were injured one after another.","Second Sister-in-law saw her own father and brothers among the villagers.","They were powerless scholars who had picked up hoes to join the battle today to protect their own homes.","When she saw villagers fall down, she would worry that the next one to fall would be her own father and brother.","\"Mother, why don't we go up too?\" As she spoke, she had already revealed the anesthetic gun in her hand and aimed at the enemy according to the method she had learned at the time.","It was just that Second Sister-in-law used the anesthetic gun for the first time. Although she knew the principle clearly, she lacked practice.","She held up the gun and gestured for a long time, but did not hear Mother-in-Law speak, so she did not pull the trigger after all.","At the same time, He Zhiran observed and found out the clues after a while.","The reason why these people were so calm was entirely because someone was commanding behind them.","Her position was not very high, but she could see behind the barbarians. A flag kept shaking from time to time.","These barbarians would change their formations or attack targets according to the shaking frequency of the chess piece.","That is to say, the person holding the chess piece was the overall commander of these people.","It was very simple to solve this kind of situation. That was to capture the king first.","In the past, He Zhiran might have chosen to use mini sleeve arrows to solve this.","She had just estimated the distance to that flag, and it seemed to exceed the range of the mini sleeve arrow.","In this case, she had to switch to a longer range weapon.","With this thought, He Zhiran's consciousness quickly entered the space and bought a heavier crossbow with longer range from Taobao.","This kind of crossbow was not as convenient to carry as the mini sleeve arrow, but it had longer range and stronger gravity.","He Zhiran could be sure that as long as she could accurately find the position of the commanding person, she would kill him with one blow.","She looked around and found a big rock not far away.","He Zhiran climbed up carefully and stood on it. This position was just right. She could fully see the top of the head of the leading person.","For her, this was enough.","He Zhiran raised the heavy crossbow and aimed at the middle of the man's eyebrows.","With a \"swish\" sound, the arrow flew like a meteor, disappearing into the middle of the man's eyebrows in the blink of an eye.","The small flag that was constantly shaking just now disappeared from her sight instantly.","Sure enough, after the small flag disappeared, these barbarians quickly fell into disarray.","Even so, they did not show any intention of retreating, and still attacked Mo brothers and others.","The Mo brothers also noticed something different about the barbarians. Their frequency of attack became very chaotic.","They didn’t have time to think much about it. They just hoped that with their two people's power, they could completely eliminate these barbarians.","After all, the enemy was strong and we were weak. Even if the Mo brothers were brave, it would take a long time to kill them one by one.","Moreover, they could not take care of others.","Although the villagers' attack was also effective, their injuries became more and more serious.","He Zhiran had thought that after losing their commander, the barbarians would flee automatically.","Unexpectedly, they did not show any intention of leaving at all.","Moreover, when she stood on the rock just now to observe those barbarians, she found that they were all skin and bones, and must have been very hungry.","He Zhiran used this to guess their mentality.","They must have thought that they would starve to death when they went back anyway, so they might as well fight for it here.","That is to say, the reason why they came over the mountains in such a large scale was nothing more than to get something to eat.","It's a pity they used the wrong method.","There are countless poor people in the world. Using such a violent way to make a living is not worth any sympathy at all.","He Zhiran was not some selfless saint either. At the moment, she only hoped that her family would not be harmed.","Especially the place where the fight was taking place was Mo Family’s territory now. She would never allow outsiders to trample on it.","It seemed that she had no choice but to show up.","Just when she was idle recently, she used the toxins in the seven-colored frogs to make a lot of anesthetic powder.","Compared with the anesthetic powder made from the silver ring snake, the efficacy of this anesthetic powder was lighter, but it was enough to deal with these people.","At this time, she could no longer hide.","He Zhiran came down from the big rock and walked quickly to the fighting scene.","Seventh Elder Brother was fighting the barbarians relatively closer, so He Zhiran shouted while walking.","\"Seventh Elder Brother... Seventh Elder Brother...\"","Hearing Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law's voice, Seventh Elder Brother gestured a few tricks and then withdrew.","At the same time, the Mo Family’s women also noticed her arrival.","\"Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law, don't come over, it's dangerous here.\" Third Sister-in-Law shouted. She didn't know what was going on. The one who should have entered the city appeared here.","However, the first thing Third Sister-in-Law thought of was that Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law must not be in any danger.","Old Lady Mo also saw her disobedient ninth daughter-in-law.","She knew better than anyone in her heart that Ninth Daughter-in-Law had her own ideas. Since she could appear here now, she was afraid no one's words would get through.","So she held back the scolding words again.","He Zhiran didn't have time to explain too much to the women. When she got close to Seventh Elder Brother, she quickly stuffed several packets of anesthetic powder into his hands.","\"Seventh Elder Brother, listen to my command.\"","Seventh Elder Brother squeezed the stuff in his hand and instantly knew what it was.","When Fifth Elder Brother, Sixth Elder Brother and Ninth Younger Brother went to the capital, Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law had prepared these small paper packets for them. It was said that they contained a kind of anesthetic powder for emergency use.","Seventh Elder Brother nodded solemnly at He Zhiran, and deliberately released several big moves to drive back the barbarians attracted by himself in order not to hurt her.","He Zhiran turned back to the big rock again and took Rice Ball, who was sleeping in the space, out.","\"Baby, it's time for you to work hard.\" The situation was urgent. She didn't have as much patience as before and went straight to the point."]},{"number":364,"title":"Chapter 364: Stop now If You don't want to Die.","paragraphs":["Rice Ball seemed to sense the seriousness of the situation and didn't immediately act cute or playful when it saw its owner. Instead, it carefully surveyed the surroundings.","At the same time, the little one responded with an \"mm-hmm.\"","He Zhiran pointed ahead and said, \"Darling, call those dogs back.\"","She did this because she didn't want the drugs to harm them. The little ones had already suffered enough injuries in order to protect their home, and she couldn't bear to see them being drugged and losing consciousness.","Rice Ball was obedient and made a strange sound towards the dogs. Soon, the dogs rushed towards her like they were fleeing from a flood or a ferocious beast.","Meanwhile, Seventh Elder Brother, also known as Qi Ge, shouted, \"Qi Ge, it's enough.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, Qi Ge covered his mouth and nose and released a white powder towards the barbarians in front of him.","In the blink of an eye, all the barbarians who were approaching him fell to the ground.","Fortunately, Eighth Brother, also known as Ba Ge, was far enough away and wasn't affected.","Qi Ge had suffered from drugged attacks on the battlefield and became a puppet of Mr. Si Meng. Now, when he saw this similar white powder, he reflexively wanted to avoid it. Even though he pinched his nose, he could still faintly smell the scent of drugs, and he felt a little dizzy.","It was evident that the drugs given by Ninth Sister were even stronger than those from Mr. Si Meng.","Without thinking too much, Mo Chuhan was still entangled with the barbarians.","Qi Ge tightly held the drugs and ran towards him.","Mo Chuhan noticed Qi Ge's actions out of the corner of his eye while fighting the barbarians.","He didn't know what method Qi Ge used to make those barbarians fall, but since Qi Ge had come to help him, he instantly felt a surge of morale.","Qi Ge arrived by his side and whispered, \"Little Eighth, cover your mouth and nose.\"","Although Mo Chuhan was usually absent-minded, he had quick reactions.","Upon hearing Qi Ge's reminder, he immediately made a few fake moves and jumped out of the circle, covering his mouth and nose.","Qi Ge used the same method to release the drugs, and the barbarians who had just planned to pursue Mo Chuhan instantly fell to the ground.","With these two batches of poison powder, most of the barbarians were now lying down. Together with the ones they had just defeated, there were only a few dozen people left standing.","These few dozen people, seeing a large number of their own comrades falling, instantly lost their combat power. Some of them even started to retreat.","The villagers had already prepared themselves to fight to the death, but they never expected that these seemingly invincible barbarians would fall so quickly.","While the villagers were still in shock, the Mo brothers had already approached with their weapons.","Eighth Brother, Ba Ge, even shouted angrily, \"Bastards, did you think this place was somewhere you could come and go as you please?\"","Seventh Elder Brother, Qi Ge, also had no intention of letting these barbarians go easily.","\"If you don't want to die, stop right there.\"","As the voice fell, the slower barbarians were already taken down by the brothers.","The person at the front of the group saw this scene and his legs went weak with fear.","Even without the Mo Family brothers taking action, those with weaker courage would have collapsed on their own.","A few barbarians exchanged quick glances and then someone shouted to the brothers, \"Merciful heroes, we had no choice but to do this...\"","Seeing their teammate begging for mercy, the barbarians lost all other thoughts and immediately turned to kneel before the Mo Family brothers.","Seventh Elder Brother and Eighth Brother stopped simultaneously, looking down at these people.","The inherent heroic aura of the Mo Family men made the barbarians shiver uncontrollably.","Seventh Elder Brother saw that these people had been intimidated by them and asked, \"Tell me, who exactly are you?\"","In response to his question, one of the barbarians trembled in fear and answered, \"We... we are just common folk of the barbarian tribes. From the start of spring until now, we haven't had a drop of rain where we come from. The grass and tree bark on the mountains have been eaten clean. Helpless, we had no choice but to come to Da Shun to find a way to survive.\"","Others followed suit, echoing, \"Yes, we truly have no way to survive. That's why we offended you.\"","Seventh Elder Brother didn't completely believe their words.","During the fight just now, he could sense that these people had no martial arts skills to speak of and were merely relying on brute force to engage in combat.","Furthermore, the weapons they used were only held by a few individuals and were clearly rusty from disuse.","Based on these observations, it was highly unlikely that they belonged to a regular army.","The rest were even more exaggerated, wielding the same hoes as the villagers of Xi Ling Village, and some even had whips.","This was enough to prove that these barbarians were not part of a formal army but rather most likely ordinary civilians.","However, he clearly saw that someone in the rear was holding up a flag and commanding them, which was why the barbarians hadn't scattered in confusion.","He just didn't know why that person holding the flag suddenly fell down.","He asked again, \"I want to know who organized you to come to Da Shun and commit robbery.\"","Faced with the question, dozens of barbarians looked at each other, seemingly unsure how to answer.","Mo Chuhan, upon seeing their hesitance, narrowed his eyes and said coldly, \"Since you don't know, there's no point in keeping you alive.\"","With that, he looked at Seventh Elder Brother by his side.","\"Seventh Elder Brother, shall we take action?\"","Seventh Elder Brother nodded indifferently and said, \"Yes, let's.\"","The barbarians saw the brothers raising their weapons once again and pointed towards the direction behind them, shouting, \"It's the person holding the flag. He said that as long as we follow his commands, we'll be able to take food from the people of Da Shun.\"","In fact, Seventh Elder Brother's earlier question was meant to find out the identity of the person holding the flag.","\"Who is that person?\"","The barbarians vigorously shook their heads.","\"We don't know who he is. All we know is that he's very capable. He spent ten days teaching us to follow his commands, claiming that this would ensure we could return from Da Shun with food.\"","Upon hearing their words, both Mo Family brothers fell into contemplation.","The barbarians noticed their silence and one of them stepped forward to say:","\"That day, I overheard the commander talking to someone.\"","\"What did they talk about?\" Seventh Elder Brother asked eagerly.","\"Commander told that person that he should take advantage of the opportunity when we, the common people, are brought to Da Shun for plundering, to investigate the truth about the Mo Family.\"","\"What happened afterwards?\" Mo Chuhan asked again.","The barbarian continued to answer, \"Their words were not very clear. Later on, they seemed to have mentioned that the place where the Mo Family resides is too close to the western border. As long as they don't get involved, there is still a chance of winning.\"","He glanced at the two brothers of the Mo Family, his expression still unpleasant, and quickly added, \"I only know these things, and I have told you all.\"","Though the account given by the barbarian was not very complete, the Mo Family brothers, being military commanders, were still able to analyze it to some extent.","The barbarians often harass the western border of Da Shun, and the western border is not very far from Yun City."]},{"number":365,"title":"Chapter 365: Poor Dog","paragraphs":["In the past, the thing Barbarians feared most was the Mo Family men. Even if they wanted to invade Da Shun, they would choose to attack when the Mo Family was guarding the southern border.","It would take at least half a month for the Mo Family to rush from the southern border to the western border across the entire Da Shun territory. The Barbarian invaders would take advantage of this half-month window to catch Da Shun off guard.","The two brothers guessed that the Barbarians must have heard that the Mo Family was exiled to the northwest.","Putting aside whether their other brothers survived, just Ninth Brother alone was enough to deter the entire forces of Barbarians.","The Barbarians were worried that the patriotic men of the Mo Family, even though exiled here, would not want to see Barbarians invade the Da Shun territory.","That was why they took the opportunity of inciting the Barbarians to raid Xi Ling Village, to probe the situation of the Mo Family.","Other than that, they could not think of any other reasons.","The current Mo Family had completely lost hope in the Da Shun court. Just barely staying alive was difficult for them, how could they possibly handle other matters?","However, only the Mo Family knew this clearly. In the eyes of outsiders, these men of the Mo Family were loyal patriots who would surely not sit idle when the nation was in peril.","It was not surprising that the Barbarians would have such worries.","This showed that the goal of the Barbarians in raiding this time was merely to plunder the common folk, while the masterminds behind it wanted to take the chance to scout for information on the Mo Family.","After the two brothers figured this out, they did not plan to explain it to anyone. With so many Barbarians left unchecked, whether they lived or died had to be settled first.","First, Seventh Elder Brother looked over the villagers of Xi Ling Village. The injured were being carried into the village under Zhao Li Zheng’s command.","There were still many severely injured, after all most clashes involved iron weapons. Although the Mo brothers shielded them at the forefront, those villagers could not emerge completely unscathed.","...","He Zhiran was also not idle on her side. The dogs called back by Rice Ball were variously injured, with a few unable to make it back.","These dogs were personally bought by her from the space. She had witnessed their growth and saw their loyal guardianship of their home everyday. When free, they would even wag their tails ingratiatingly at her.","Thinking of this, He Zhiran’s eyes reddened slightly, but now was not the time for her to be overly sentimental.","The priority was treating the injuries of these dogs that still survived.","Moreover, she saw that many villagers were also injured.","She sent Rice Ball into the space, while her consciousness swiftly gathered a large amount of medicine for external injuries, bandages and other items, packing them into a large package to take out from the space.","Fortunately she was well prepared, having swapped the medicines into porcelain bottles and the bandages into white linen of this era, sterilized at high temperatures, making them usable like modern gauze bandages.","Whether people or dogs, the number needing treatment was not small. With just herself alone, the treatment would likely be delayed.","Seeing that Seventh Elder Brother and Eighth Brother had dealt with those Barbarians, He Zhiran shouted loudly at the Mo Family women: “Mother, sisters-in-law, come quickly to help!”","The women were currently still in shock. They had just seen Ninth Sister-in-Law come over to say a few words to Mo Yuance, after which those Barbarians immediately collapsed in swathes...","After all, they had never experienced such scenes before, and were unclear on things like white powder either, only assuming that it was dust stirred in the fight.","All of this was too inconceivable, which they still could not digest quickly.","Hearing He Zhiran’s shout, other than Old Lady Mo, the rest felt like suddenly awakening from a dream.","Old Lady Mo knew that her ninth daughter-in-law would not call them groundlessly. She reminded:","“Go quickly, see what matter your Ninth Sister-in-Law has.”","Hearing their mother-in-law’s prompt, the women successively collected their thoughts and hurried with large strides towards He Zhiran.","On seeing her family come over, He Zhiran immediately placed the large package before everyone.","“Mother, sisters-in-law, our dogs are injured. I cannot handle it alone and need your help.”","The Mo women now saw the bloodied dogs before them, feeling equally awful, with the more tender-hearted already tearing up.","Second Sister-in-Law said sorrowfully: “Poor dogs, to have sustained such tragic injuries guarding us.”","Old Lady Mo had the calmest disposition. Seeing her daughters-in-law still lamenting over there, she hurried urged:","“If you feel sorry for these dogs, then follow your Ninth Sister-in-Law’s arrangements to immediately help treat the wounds.”","In her youth she had followed the old Lord to border passes before, and saw such battle scenes a few times.","Only difference was, what she saw injured then were people, while what she saw now were injured dogs.","The feeling was the same – it made one’s heart ache to watch.","Even without the mother-in-law speaking, the sisters-in-law would have gone all out to help save them. Just that they did not know medicine, and could only look to He Zhiran for instructions.","He Zhiran opened the package.","“See here everyone, first wipe the wounds with this – it prevents rotting, and this stops bleeding – apply it then tie a firm bandage...”","Inside were not just medicines, but He Zhiran had also prepared a few razors.","These were not unfamiliar to them as ancient women – they used it to groom their husband’s beards.","“And these, to shave away the hair around the dogs’ wound area for ease of treatment.”","As time did not wait for man, while handing out the razors to them He Zhiran went on: “Also, bring severely injured dogs to me. Just treat surface wounds on your side.”","Including Old Lady Mo and Mo Hanyue, the women earnestly nodded, immediately checking the dogs’ injuries.","Truthfully, they feared dealing with such bloody wounds in their hearts.","But thinking that it would be useless culpability if they delayed rescue over fear, they steeled themselves to overcome the fear, boldly trying to treat the dogs’ injuries.","He Zhiran observed that Mo Hanyue performed the best, her techniques also seemingly more skilled than the rest.","In fact, He Zhiran did not know that the lass often had to bandage her own injured rabbits from their fights. Treating these bigger dogs was no different for Mo Hanyue from treating her rabbits.","Seeing her motions, He Zhiran was very pleased. She instructed the women to direct any doubts to Mo Hanyue.","Mo Hanyue could handle the dogs, freeing up her hands to check on the villagers.","Xi Ling Village had no doctors. Getting one had to be from the city, which would delay rescue by much.","If there were severely injured, lives could be easily lost from it."]},{"number":366,"title":"Chapter 366: Whatever you need to do, just ask.","paragraphs":["At this time, the women in the village heard that the fighting here had stopped and came over one after another. Seeing their own people injured, their crying became louder and louder.","When He Zhiran arrived, this was the scene.","She pushed through the crowd in front.","\"Everyone make way, let me see their injuries.\"","The villagers were not unfamiliar with He Zhiran, and some people also knew that she understood medicine.","\"Hurry, hurry, the ninth house is here, please ask her to help.\"","Soon, the crowd automatically gave way to a path, and even some women thoughtfully helped her up seeing that she was heavy with child.","He Zhiran stood in the center of the crowd, with a clear view of all the participating soldiers.","Nan Rui, covered in blood, stood not far away, holding a shiny sword in his hand, looking worriedly at the injured villagers.","He Zhiran had heard from Mo Jiuye that Nan Rui did not know any martial arts and now lived in Xiling Village after having dismissed his guards.","It was not easy for an incapable young master from a prestigious family to stand with the common people to resist foreign enemies at a critical moment. For this, He Zhiran rather admired him a lot.","Fortunately, although Nan Rui looked miserable, he was not injured.","At the moment she could not bother to greet Nan Rui. She quickly checked the number of injured villagers, about two dozen or so.","Fortunately, they had only superficial wounds, but the wounds were very deep, and some could even see the bones, oozing blood continuously.","Such injuries were not difficult for He Zhiran to deal with, the only headache was that there were too many injured people.","If Mo Jiuye were here in this situation, it would be great. His treatment of external injuries had reached perfection, and even suturing was skillfully done.","Thinking of Mo Jiuye, he had been away from home for more than half a month, and she wondered if things were going well for him in the capital.","For the first time, He Zhiran felt the feeling of missing someone immensely.","Although she missed him in her heart, she did not forget that there were still more important things to do at the moment.","At this moment, Zhao Li came up to her with a worried look on his face, \"Auntie Nine, can their injuries be cured?\"","\"Uncle Zhao, I can cure their injuries, it's just that there are too many people and I'm afraid I can't handle it alone.\"","As she spoke, she looked at the uninjured villagers.","\"Is anyone willing to help?\"","Under the current circumstances, He Zhiran could only seek help from these villagers. No technique was required, just be more careful.","Zhao Zechuan was the first to stand up. Although he was not injured, the azure long gown he wore was already stained with some blood and looked somewhat disheveled.","\"Sister-in-law Nine, I can help. Just tell me what to do.\"","Fang Chuanzhou and Xie Tianhai also came forward with their families.","\"Auntie Nine, we can help too.\"","Nan Rui also came over, \"I can help too.\"","And of course Hu Cong would not refuse.","He Zhiran first looked at everyone. Although they should have suffered some superficial wounds, they did not seem to be a big problem.","\"Well, thank you all for your hard work.\"","\"It's no hardship at all, this is what we should do.\"","When everyone answered, they all felt a little ashamed. A pregnant woman could volunteer without hesitation to do these things, how could they be afraid of hardships?","Saving people was like putting out a fire. He Zhiran had no time to explain more and immediately instructed, \"Wash your hands thoroughly first, then come over here to get medicine from me.\"","Upon hearing this, people rushed to the nearby stream to wash their hands and then rushed back to He Zhiran.","At this moment, He Zhiran had already started to treat the wounds of the most seriously injured.","She skillfully treated the man's wounds while pointing to the medicines she had brought to teach them how to treat wounds.","Soon everyone tried to follow He Zhiran's method.","By this time, it was broad daylight, and the outsiders who had come to help build the Mo family house had arrived one after another.","They were first stunned by the scene in front of them.","At the foot of the mountain was the location of the new Mo house. All those barbarians who had been drugged unconscious by Qi Ge lay scattered around, and with the blood stains around, it suddenly gave a feeling of dead bodies covering the fields.","The bolder ones saw that the two Mo brothers were tying up those people over there and carefully approached.","\"Master Seven, Master Eight, what is this?\"","Qi Ge turned his head. Although he could not call out the man's name, he knew he was the worker they had hired.","\"Hurry up and call everyone to come and help tie these people up.\" Qi Ge said, pointing to the barbarians lying on the ground.","The worker was startled by his words.","\"Se...Seven Master, do we need to tie up the dead as well?\"","Seeing the man's expression, Qi Ge also realized the misunderstanding.","\"They're not dead, just unconscious.\"","\"Re...really not dead?\" The worker still could not quite believe it.","\"Most of them are alive. Just tie up the living ones.\" Qi Ge was obviously a little anxious. With so many barbarians, without anyone to help, how long would it take for him and his younger brother to finish tying them up?","Seeing this, the dull worker nodded slowly and then went back to call people to come and help.","With more people participating, soon all the invading barbarians were tied up with their own waist belts.","Subsequently, without the Mo brothers instructing, the workers simply cleaned up the battle scene.","When Qi Ge and Ba Ge started fighting the enemies, they did not intend to let these people off easily. As a result, at least a hundred barbarians died before falling unconscious from the drugs.","Those who were alive were more or less slightly injured.","In this situation, even without treatment, no one would die.","Now the Mo family was just an ordinary commoner, or even less than an ordinary commoner, after all they were people whose homes were confiscated by the imperial edict and exiled.","Mo Chuhan wiped the sweat from his forehead.","\"Brother Seven, such a big incident has occurred, I think it is necessary to go to the yamen to notify Master Meng, and also to listen to his opinion on how to deal with these people.\"","\"Well, I'll trouble my younger brother to rush to the county yamen.\" Qi Ge also agreed with this very much.","\"Alright, I'll go now. Brother Seven will be in charge here.\"","After speaking, Mo Chuhan turned and left.","Under Mo Hanyue's guidance, the women were becoming more and more adept at treating the injured dogs, without wasting half a minute.","They truly felt distressed for these dogs, thinking that if they acted faster, the dogs would suffer less.","It was the same here with He Zhiran. She was responsible for treating the seriously injured villagers while the others were handed over to Fang Chuanzhou and the others.","With everyone's concerted efforts, finally after an hour, the injuries of all the villagers and dogs were treated.","The villagers were carried home by their families, while the workers carefully carried the dogs back to their resting shed to recuperate. Mo Hanyue volunteered to go and take care of them.","With such a big incident happening today, the Mo family house construction could only be suspended for a day."]},{"number":367,"title":"Chapter 367: What impression Do you have","paragraphs":["Although this was the case, the workers did not leave. Under the leadership of Seventh Elder Brother, together with the villagers, they piled all the corpses of the dead barbarians to one side.","For the one shot dead by He Zhiran's crossbow arrow, Mo Chuhan was very concerned. After all, his identity was suspicious. It would be great if they could find some clues from him.","Seventh Elder Brother was no stranger to searching matters. In the past when fighting wars, after capturing the enemy general, there would also be such an operation. First he searched the body of the barbarian commander.","Apart from a token that looked rather special, there was also a small porcelain bottle that seemed to contain gu worms.","Seventh Elder Brother did not dare mess with the small porcelain bottle. He was afraid that something bad would happen if he was not careful, so he would wait for Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law to come and decide.","He kept the small porcelain bottle and then took the token to observe it carefully.","He always felt that he had seen this token somewhere before, but could not remember where for the moment.","Just when he was annoyed, two people suddenly appeared before him out of thin air.","The arrivals were precisely Mo Chuhan and Meng Huaining.","Mo Chuhan knew the urgency of the matter. He did not ride a horse into the city at all, but raised his qinggong skill to the fastest speed.","On his return as well, Meng Huaining also understood martial arts. They were both clear that their qinggong was much faster than riding a horse, so they both displayed qinggong to rush back.","As for those yamen runners, they had already been left far behind by them.","When Seventh Elder Brother saw the two of them, he hurriedly displayed the token that had troubled him for so long.","\"It's good that you're here. Take a quick look at this token and see if you have any impression of it?\"","When Mo Chuhan saw the token, he also frowned slightly.","\"Seventh Elder Brother, what is this?\"","Seventh Elder Brother pointed his lips at the corpse of the commander on the ground: \"It was searched from him.\"","Mo Chuhan took the token and flipped it around before returning it to Seventh Elder Brother.","\"I've never seen this thing before.\"","Meng Huaining also took a peek and did not recognize it either.","Although they did not recognize it, he was more observant than the Mo brothers.","\"Seventh Elder Brother, Eighth Elder Brother, look, the veins on this token look a bit strange, it looks a bit like a mandala leaf.\"","After Meng Huaining's reminder, the two brothers also discovered it.","\"It's true, these veins do look similar to the leaves of a mandala,\" Seventh Elder Brother said.","Then the three of them looked at each other, as if they had all guessed something.","\"Mandala is the national flower of Nanjiang. Could this incident be related to Nanjiang?\" Seventh Elder Brother couldn't help asking.","This was also Meng Huaining and Eighth Brother's guess in their hearts.","\"It's highly likely that someone from Nanjiang is making trouble,\" Mo Chuhan said in a somewhat displeased tone.","Meng Huaining was not so arbitrary. He looked at those barbarians who were not confused and walked over.","\"Sir, I ask you, did that commander speak in the local accent of you barbarians?\"","Meng Huaining was wearing an official uniform when he rushed over. Since ancient times, commoners have been afraid of officials, and these barbarians were no exception. Especially since they had committed the misdeed of robbing Da Shun commoners, they were even more terrified.","Therefore, when Meng Huaining asked, they were scrambling to answer, hoping to have a chance to redeem their crimes and establish merit.","\"Sir, I know.\"","\"Sir, that man spoke differently from us, he was definitely not a barbarian.\"","\"Sir, he spoke a little like the southern accent. I went south a few years ago and would definitely not mistake it.\"","\"Sir...\"","Now, what more was there for the Mo brothers and Meng Huaining to not understand? From what these barbarians said and that token, it could be analyzed that the commander was sent from Nanjiang.","\"Could it be that Nanjiang colluded with the barbarians and planned to jointly attack Da Shun?\" Mo Chuhan spoke out his guess in his heart.","Seventh Elder Brother stroked his chin and frowned, \"It's not impossible.\"","Although the Mo family was exiled and hated Emperor Shunwu and the court, their deep-rooted patriotism could not just disappear. When they heard that there were foreign enemies attacking Da Shun, they instinctively felt like resisting.","However, they soon realized their current status.","Seventh Elder Brother sighed and lightly patted Meng Huaining on the shoulder: \"How this matter will eventually turn out can only be worried by Brother Meng. My Mo family now only wants to live in peace.\"","Meng Huaining could completely understand the feelings of the Mo brothers. After all, his own family had also been suppressed by Emperor Shunwu before.","It was just that the Meng family was slightly better off than the Mo family, and had not reached the point of exile. His family members had placed all their hopes of turning over a new leaf on him.","Therefore, even though Meng Huaining was indifferent to the court, he could not just sit idly by in the face of such a big matter.","\"Well, I will sort it out later and write a memorial to report to the capital.\"","What he meant by writing a memorial was that he would write a letter to Fei Nanyu.","Although he did not have much contact with Fei Nanyu, he could feel that they belonged in the same circle.","Especially since Fei Nanyu had helped him a lot with the plague incident. He was able to come to Yucheng to take office instead of being stripped of his official position. These were all Fei Nanyu's contributions.","No matter from which point of consideration, he would choose to notify Fei Nanyu of the news.","Of course, the Mo brothers would not care who Meng Huaining would report this matter to. What they needed to resolve now was the issue of what to do with these barbarians, as well as to put the defense of their Xiling Village homes on the agenda.","Whether it was the barbarians or Nanjiang people, what they feared was his Mo family.","Even though they did not intend to work for the court anymore, those outsiders were not clear about their thoughts.","Therefore, it was very necessary for the Mo family to be more vigilant from now on. The top priority was to protect themselves.","Seventh Elder Brother looked at those barbarians with pitiful looks on their faces and asked Meng Huaining.","\"Brother Meng, how do you plan to deal with these people?\"","On the way here, Mo Chuhan had already told Meng Huaining about the general situation of what had happened here.","He knew clearly that the barbarians captured by the Mo brothers were all commoners.","At the same time, he also knew that the barbarians did have hard lives. It could be determined from their emaciated appearances that they must have been starving badly.","The pitiful had something to be hated for. Meng Huaining did not sympathize with them, but felt that if things continued like this, it would be difficult to guarantee the safety of Yucheng's commoners.","Just as he was thinking about how to handle it, the treatment of the wounded on He Zhiran's side was nearing completion. She was being supported by a somewhat uneasy Eighth Sister-in-law as she walked over here.","\"Brother Meng, Seventh Elder Brother, Eighth Elder Brother, how has the situation been handled?\" He Zhiran asked.","A style had been formed in the Mo family now, which was to look upon Mo Jiuye and his wife as leaders.","When Mo Jiuye was at home, whether for big or small matters, they would go to discuss it with them.","Therefore, when they saw He Zhiran ask, they recounted what they had learned about the situation in every detail.","When He Zhiran heard that she had killed the most critical figure, she felt somewhat regretful in her heart.","In her anxiousness just now, there was nothing she could do.","Seeing that she did not respond for a long time, Seventh Elder Brother hurriedly took out the small porcelain bottle.","\"Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law, take a look. This is what was found on that man. I suspect there are gu worms inside. I didn't dare open it rashly.\""]},{"number":368,"title":"Chapter 368: You're just in time to be back.","paragraphs":["Seventh Elder Brother knew that Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law could resolve Gu poison and should have more understanding of Gu worms. Handling this kind of thing to her was the most reassuring approach.","He Zhiran took over the porcelain bottle and gently shook it next to her ear a few times.","If there really were Gu worms inside, and they were raised by that commander, apart from puppet Gu, it would be impossible for the Gu worms to continue living once their master died.","She did this to further confirm whether the Gu worms were dead. If the Gu worms were dead, she could hear slight collisions inside the bottle by shaking it. On the other hand, if the Gu worms were still alive, they would avoid the collisions themselves.","The result of the experiment proved that what she heard was the sound of Gu worms colliding with the bottle walls, so she could determine that the Gu worms were already dead.","He Zhiran gently opened the bottle stopper and poured the Gu worms from inside into her palm.","The Gu worms were yellowish brown in color. Based on their appearance, it could be determined that these were Gu worms that had not been fully domesticated yet, because immature Gu worms meant that He Zhiran could not determine what kind they were for the time being.","Since the Gu worms were not adult, they could not breed offspring to harm people yet. That is to say, that commander was a novice at raising Gu.","However, this further confirmed his identity as a Southerner.","\"Seventh Elder Brother, Eighth Elder Brother, we really have to be more vigilant from now on to prevent more ill-intentioned people from infiltrating Xi Ling Village.\"","Her thinking was almost identical to that of her two elder brothers. Whether they were Southerners or Barbarians, what they feared were the Mo Family.","Moreover, the fact that the Mo Family had been exiled here was no longer a secret. If someone wanted to find out about them, they would naturally think of ways to mix in here.","But why would the Southerners go through so much trouble?","If they wanted to inquire about the Mo Family, they could simply send people disguised as Da Shun people to come over.","This point inevitably caused He Zhiran to think deeply.","Seeing that her two elder brothers did not refute her opinion, she continued:","\"I suspect that the Southerners wanted to inquire about the Mo Family on one hand, but more importantly, they wanted to eradicate the Mo Family with the Barbarians' power.\"","Seventh Elder Brother listened and kept nodding.","\"Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law's analysis is right. It seems we really have to make preparations as soon as possible.\"","Just as He Zhiran was about to say something more, they suddenly heard hurried footsteps coming from the direction of the village.","Everyone looked in the direction of the sound.","They saw Tao Ran leading a group of men, women, young and old running towards them.","Tao Ran was an old subordinate of the Mo Family. He was made into a medicine slave by Master Simeng's means to work for him. Fortunately, He Zhiran helped him detoxify.","After recovering for a period of time, he left.","This time, the old subordinates of the Mo Family who were also made into medicine slaves by Master Simeng returned to Xi Ling Village with him.","From the whole group, it was clear that they had brought their families to take refuge this time.","Seeing them, Seventh Elder Brother and Eighth Elder Brother were obviously very happy. The two welcomed them one after the other.","\"Tao Ran, it's good that all of you are back.\" Eighth Elder Brother was straightforward. He was just thinking that it would be great if Tao Ran and the others had come back earlier. With them here, there would be an extra line of defense against external enemies.","It had to be known that these people were truly battle-hardened warriors. It would not be an exaggeration to say that one of them could match a hundred enemies.","As a result, he really got what he wished for. As he was thinking about Tao Ran and the others in his mind, they came.","Tao Ran discovered something was wrong as soon as he entered the village. He brought people all the way here.","\"Seventh Master, Eighth Master, what on earth happened?\"","The scene before Tao Ran and the others was too familiar. Wasn't this exactly what a battlefield looked like after fierce fighting?","While speaking, Tao Ran did not forget to carefully examine Mo Yuance and Mo Chuhan to see that they were unharmed before he felt much more relieved.","Encountering something like this, Mo Chuhan could not ask Tao Ran too many questions either. He told everyone what happened this morning and their analysis.","After listening, Tao Ran was filled with righteous indignation. \"These people are really... Eighth Master, please rest assured. We have brought our families to settle here long-term this time. Our skills are nothing special, but we are still capable of killing external enemies.\"","Seeing this, the other old subordinates also came forward one by one to express their willingness to guard this place.","Their second lives were given by the Mo Family. Before leaving here, they had already decided to devote their lives to the Mo Family.","Mo Chuhan patted several people's shoulders excitedly.","\"Good. With you all here, I believe our home will definitely be very safe.\"","Since dealing with those Barbarians was handed over to Meng Huaining, the Mo brothers stopped bothering about it and urged Tao Ran and the others to go back and rest.","Fortunately, He Zhiran had moved quickly to buy the Cui family's manor and farmland.","Under the Mo brothers' arrangement, Tao Ran's group were all allocated courtyards to settle their families.","Although He Zhiran was not unfamiliar with arrangements for battles, she was clearer that her two elder brothers were veterans. They were undoubtedly proficient in guarding and making arrangements, possibly even more brilliant than her.","Therefore, regarding the arrangements for Tao Ran and the others, she did not plan to participate too much, leaving everything to her two elder brothers.","After busy for so long, it was really too tiring for her as a pregnant woman.","Seeing that she had done what she should, she dragged her weary body to go back and rest.","Seeing her slightly stumbling steps, Old Lady Mo took the initiative to support her.","The old lady knew that her ninth daughter-in-law had worked hard with great achievements today. If she had really gone to the city as she arranged, her two sons would have had a hard time dealing with so many Barbarians.","\"Mother thanks you on behalf of everyone.\"","Old Lady Mo sincerely thanked her daughter-in-law. At the same time, she felt great distress for He Zhiran. With such a big belly and pregnant with twins, she did not care for herself at all for everyone's sake.","He Zhiran smiled lightly and patted the old lady's hand.","\"Mother, I know my limits. Don't worry.\"","Seeing this, Old Lady Mo reproached, \"You're still saying you know your limits. You're even stumbling when walking.\"","\"Hehe... Mother, I'm just a little tired. I'll be fine after resting for a while.\" He Zhiran pretended to say lightly.","Being supported by her mother-in-law personally back home, He Zhiran immediately went into the space.","At this moment, she was already starving and just wanted to replenish her strength as soon as possible.","The space had everything she could possibly want. At worst, she could still buy things from Taobao Treasures.","Not only that, after Little Collector heard she was pregnant, he specially helped her buy takeaway packages from modern high-end restaurants at low prices several times for her to enjoy the long-awaited delicious food.","She leisurely enjoyed the delicious food in the space while Meng Huaining had a headache outside.","Facing so many Barbarian commoners, it was easy to deal with the dead ones. Who told them to come and plunder Da Shun?","That was the price to pay for doing bad things. Dying was also reasonable.","However, the remaining living ones were problematic no matter if they were beaten or punished.","If they were beaten and injured, they would not be able to leave this place. If they were punished, these people were also penniless.","But letting them leave just like this was also not appropriate.","Just when he was in dire straits, Hu Cong came before him."]},{"number":369,"title":"Chapter 369: Medicine for Health Preservation","paragraphs":["\"Is Meng Huaining troubled because of how to deal with these people?\"","Meng Huaining gave a wry laugh and nodded, \"They are, after all, commoners, and can't negotiate with the Barbarian Emperor for exchanging money for people like soldiers could. Given the current situation of the Barbarians, the Barbarian Emperor would be happy to see more commoners die, so that he could save some food.\"","This point was undeniable to Hu Cong as well.","He came here wanting to think of a way to help Meng Huaining share the burden.","\"I do have a rough idea. May I ask Meng Huaining for his decision after I lay it out?\"","Meng Huaining was racking his brains over this matter. Seeing Hu Cong had a solution, he hurriedly asked, \"What good solution does Brother Hu have?\"","Hu Cong said somewhat embarrassedly, \"Meng Huaining must have heard that when I was in the capital, I had my own engineering team.\"","Hearing this, Meng Huaining seemed to have thought of something.","\"Does Brother Hu mean to recruit these people as workers for your engineering team?\"","Hu Cong nodded, \"I do have this idea. I see these people are skin and bones, their days under the Barbarians must have been hard.","In another month, the construction here will be basically completed. I plan to make a living from construction in the future, so having a team is very necessary.\"","Meng Huaining knew Hu Cong's background well and was clear about many of his situations.","He just couldn't figure out why Hu Cong would choose those Barbarians of unknown origin and background instead of the many commoners of Da Shun when recruiting.","\"Brother Hu, isn't it better to recruit the commoners of our Da Shun for your engineering team?\"","Hu Cong smiled and continued explaining, \"I will also recruit Da Shun commoners. Among those who are currently helping the Mo Family build houses, some have already caught my eye.","I am quite harsh, those who can't meet my standards definitely won't make it onto my engineering team.","Also, the design of these houses I'm building now is from Madam He Zhiran of the Mo Family. That she is willing to trust me with such a good design, I must also ensure it doesn't spread from my hands.","Recruiting these Barbarians does carry the risk of leakage, but Meng Huaining might not know, I have already discussed with Madam He earlier to help me formulate a kind of medicated pellet.\"","This pellet is not very toxic, but the antidote must be taken on time, so that I can control these people to be loyal to me.\"","As for the details of the medicated pellets, Hu Cong did not mention them to Meng Huaining.","He did go to He Zhiran earlier, hoping to cooperate with her to earn money through the construction of the courtyard houses.","After several discussions, the two had reached an agreement to split the profits fifty-fifty.","With money to earn, He Zhiran would not object. Besides, she never intended to hide the construction of the courtyard houses.","Since Hu Cong was willing, she was happy to help while earning profits herself.","Of course, she and Hu Cong also discussed the issue of the engineering team.","In the end, it was He Zhiran who came up with this slippery idea.","She could indeed formulate the kind of poison Hu Cong mentioned that requires taking antidotes periodically.","However, as a modern soul, she did not want to control ordinary people in this way.","Therefore, she developed a long-acting laxative.","This medicine is harmless to the human body. As the name suggests, the duration of \"long-acting\" is one hundred days.","Once someone takes this pellet, if they don't take a second pellet after one hundred days, they will feel slight abdominal discomfort in the first two days, and diarrhea symptoms will appear on the third day.","After a few bouts of diarrhea, all toxins in the body will be completely expelled.","Not only that, He Zhiran also added some detox ingredients in the pellets. It not only doesn't affect the taker’s body, but can even expel toxins accumulated in their body.","It can be said that this is not a poison at all, but a rare health elixir.","However, the taker would not be able to discover the properties of this medicine and would definitely think the poison broke out because they didn't get to take the next pellet.","With these pellets, Hu Cong was fully confident that he could make these workers absolutely loyal.","Meng Huaining was already having headaches over the issue of these Barbarians. Although Hu Cong’s solution was not perfect, it was still better than no solution.","\"Brother Hu, whether they are Da Shun’s or the Barbarians’ commoners, it is good for them to stay and work for you, but I do hope you don't harm their health.\"","As a local parent official, he valued the lives of commoners more.","He could not assist a tyrant for his own benefit.","Hu Cong knew Meng Huaining cared about the commoners and quickly explained, \"Meng Huaining can rest assured. Madam He is still quite confident in making medicine.\"","Meng Huaining believed He Zhiran wholeheartedly. Hearing Hu Cong mention again that the medicine came from her hands, he strangely felt much more assured.","\"Since this is the case, Brother Hu can arrange it after these people wake up!\"","Seeing Meng Huaining had no objection, Hu Cong lightly coughed with a fist against his lips.","\"Cough cough... Meng Huaining, I need fifty people at most.\"","Meng Huaining was dumbfounded. There were at least three to four hundred living Barbarians in front of him. Hu Cong could only keep fifty people. How was that any different from not coming up with a solution?","Seeing Meng Huaining's expression, Hu Cong roughly guessed what he was thinking.","\"Meng Huaining can rest assured that even if I can't accommodate more people here, I have a way to resolve it.\"","Meng Huaining raised his brows, \"What good solution does Brother Hu have?\"","\"I understand Meng Huaining’s intention. You feel somewhat unresigned to let these people easily go back, yet they are commoners that can’t simply be killed.\"","Meng Huaining nodded repeatedly, \"That's indeed the case.\"","Hu Cong went on to share his idea, \"I see these Barbarians are not all lawless villains either. If they have food to eat their fill, who would be willing to come out and rob?","Later when they wake up, if Meng Huaining trusts me, please leave it to me.\"","Meng Huaining didn't know what good solution Hu Cong had.","As long as these people could be sent away smoothly and would no longer offend again in the future, he would be at ease.","\"Alright, I’ll leave it to Brother Hu to handle.\"","Meng Huaining didn’t doubt Hu Cong’s capability at all. After all, someone who has been an official in court for many years must have the ability to handle affairs.","The effects of He Zhiran’s anesthetics didn’t last very long. The unconscious Barbarians began to wake up one after another after about an hour.","The Barbarians who just woke up were all completely blank-faced, completely unaware of what had happened, and were all tied up by their own waist belts.","Here, Meng Huaining had handed full authority to Hu Cong to handle things, so he did not react at all.","Those officials who had just rushed over also stood by Meng Huaining’s side at all times. They would not make any moves if their superior did not speak.","Hu Cong understood Meng Huaining’s intention and strode to the front of those people.","He pointed at those who were not knocked unconscious and said, \"You explain to them what exactly happened.\"","It would be clearer if their own people did the explaining."]},{"number":370,"title":"Chapter 370: How to Guarantee","paragraphs":["Those barbarians who were not stunned at this moment only wanted to live. Naturally, they would spare no effort to explain the reason to their companions.","After everyone understood the situation, they kept begging for mercy like those companions who were not stunned.","Such a scene did not move Hu Cong at all.","He and Meng Huaining felt the same, not much sympathy for these people.","\"Don't make any noise. Those who want to live, listen to me.\"","As Hu Cong's voice fell, the barbarians instantly calmed down and looked at him timidly.","Hu Cong saw him beckoning not far away, and a worker brought over a large basin of steaming hot steamed buns.","Hu Cong took the basin in person and moved closer to those barbarians.","This was what he had specially ordered after seeking Meng Huaining's consent.","The steamed buns had just been taken out of the steamer, emitting a sweet scent that made people drool.","These barbarians probably hadn't had a full meal for several months, let alone these hot, steaming white flour buns.","As Hu Cong expected, when these barbarians saw the steamed buns, they couldn't help but swallow, and the desire in their eyes was unstoppable.","What's more, Hu Cong deliberately brought the buns closer to them.","If these barbarians' hands and feet were not tied up, they would probably have jumped up to grab them.","Seeing that he had achieved the effect he wanted, Hu Cong took a few steps back.","\"Do you want to eat?\"","The barbarians swallowed again, stared at the buns, nodded woodenly.","Although Hu Cong asked this, he did not immediately give them the buns to eat.","\"If you want to eat your fill and dress warmly, you have to work for it. Trying to get these things through looting will never work. It may even cost you your life.\"","He nodded at the barbarian corpses, \"See that? These people are the best examples.\"","There were not a few relatives or friends of the dead barbarians among the survivors. Hu Cong carefully observed their expressions.","Anyone who was sad or crying, even if they had the ability, he would not consider keeping them.","There were about thirty or so such people. Hu Cong directly asked the officers to take them aside.","Then, Hu Cong continued, \"I can now give you a chance to eat your fill. Who's willing?\"","As expected, upon hearing that they could eat their fill, the remaining barbarians expressed their willingness.","Although they didn't know what they would do after being selected, or whether they could survive.","But looking at the large basin of steamed buns, these barbarians felt that they had rushed here to rob in order to eat their fill, right?","Now there was a chance to eat their fill. Even if it meant death, they wanted to die with a full stomach.","So after his words fell, someone answered quickly.","\"I can herd sheep. I have herded sheep for the rich since I was young.\"","\"I'm strong. I can do anything.\"","\"I can build houses.\"","\"I can do carpentry.\"","\"I don't have any special skills, but I can work hard.\"","\"...\"","Hu Cong just stood there listening quietly as these people volunteered their strengths.","After a while, when the voices died down a bit, he waved at the crowd.","\"Alright, don't make any noise. Those who can build and do carpentry, stand up.\"","These barbarians were tied up and leaning halfway. Although they couldn't walk, standing up was no problem.","Soon, more than sixty people stood up.","This number was a little beyond Hu Cong's expectations.","In his impression, the barbarian lands were barren, people were underfed and poorly clothed, and wealthy people were few, let alone people who built houses and made furniture.","He had planned to select fifty people from these, and thought that even if they didn't have these skills but were willing to work hard, he could teach them slowly.","Now, more than sixty people had volunteered.","It seemed there was still room for selection.","Just as Hu Cong was thinking about how to test these people, some of the sixty-odd barbarians who stood up couldn't help but gingerly ask.","\"May I ask, do you want us to stay and work? I can forego wages, I just hope to bring some food back for my family. I'm willing to stay here and be your ox and horse for life.\"","After he finished speaking, many others echoed that they were willing to do the same as their companion.","This was also Hu Cong's plan for the next step. Since someone had said it for him, it saved him some trouble.","\"If you work for me, I guarantee you'll eat your fill, but how can you guarantee your loyalty to me?\"","When it came to loyalty, the barbarians looked at each other, then someone shouted, \"I guarantee loyalty and good work.\"","Hu Cong smiled, \"Your casual words, how can they guarantee anything?\"","\"This...\" The barbarians were rendered speechless.","\"I don't need you to be oxen and horses either, just work hard and I guarantee you'll eat your fill.\"","Hu Cong paused, then continued, \"But the premise is that you must demonstrate loyalty to me.","However, this loyalty is not so simple as just saying it, I have a poison here. After taking it, it will take effect after 100 days, and at that time I will give you the next pill to ensure your life is free of worries, and it won't affect your lifespan.","That is to say, as long as you are loyal to me, I will provide the antidote on time.\"","Hearing that the other party wanted to use poison to win their loyalty, a large number of people were intimidated.","But among these people, there were also some bold ones.","These people didn't even hesitate and said, \"I can take the poison and guarantee my loyalty to you.\"","\"I'm also willing. As long as I can eat my fill, let me do anything.\"","Seeing someone take the lead, some hesitant people also spoke up successively.","The remaining few timid ones were still hesitating.","Seeing that the number had reached his expectation, Hu Cong said in a loud voice, \"Alright, those of you come with me.\"","The barbarians who were kept behind were overjoyed.","But there were still concerns in their hearts.","\"Can we send back some of the food we earn to our families?\"","This was also the voice of many people. They had no other concerns now, they just hoped that while they could eat their fill, their families would not starve."]},{"number":371,"title":"Chapter 371: It will Cost you your life.","paragraphs":["Hu Cong discovered that these barbarians were becoming more and more capable, and everything was proceeding according to his train of thought.","\"I can advance you all one month's wages ahead of time to purchase food for your families.\"","Hu Cong did not consider himself to be a philanthropist. It was impossible for him to give food to those people's families for free. However, after they had taken the medicine pellets, he could advance them one month's wages ahead of time.","That way, these people would be able to go and buy the things they needed.","The barbarians who had voluntarily stayed behind had originally only hoped they wouldn't go hungry. Normally they would save up as much food as they could and find ways to send it back home.","They hadn't expected that not only would they have wages, but they could even get one month’s wages in advance. For them this was like a godsend.","Being able to bring some food back for their families, let alone being asked to take some kind of poison, even if they had to die on the spot, it would have been worth it.","\"We are willing to take the poison and be loyal to you forever.\"","\"Yes, we are willing...\"","Seeing that these people were being treated so well, those who had hesitated earlier regretted it.","\"I also want to stay.\"","\"Me too.\"","It must be said, Hu Cong was quite selective in choosing people!","These people had hesitated for a moment instead of immediately stepping forward, so Hu Cong had already eliminated them.","Hearing that there were good conditions now, they stepped forward again. Hu Cong did not want people of such moral character.","He completely ignored those people and carefully counted the number of people staying behind - forty-five in total.","Although it was five fewer people than he had expected, it didn't matter.","The people he needed had to be of guaranteed character.","Hu Cong called the forty-five people who were staying behind to one side, then went to He Zhiran to get the medicine pellets.","When He Zhiran heard that Hu Cong was using this method to keep a group of barbarians behind, he approved of his approach.","No matter which country, there were good and bad people. As long as Hu Cong could discern clearly, it was fine.","Hu Cong took the medicine pellets and hurried back to the foot of the mountain.","There, the officials were keeping a close eye on the barbarians carefully cleaning up the battlefield.","This was the land belonging to the Mohists, Meng Huaining’s future in-laws. He wanted to demonstrate his capabilities while his two elder brothers-in-law were away and restore this place to its original state.","The barbarians had completely lost their fighting spirit. All of them were listening to directions from the officials on what to do.","The ones selected by Hu Cong were still standing in their original places. Hu Cong distributed the medicine pellets and made sure they swallowed them before giving each person fifty coins in wages.","What made these people even more delighted was that the large basin of white steamed buns had also become their breakfast.","Hu Cong didn’t actually know the real medicinal effects of the medicine pellets made by He Zhiran. He thought they really were the kind of poison that needed to be taken regularly. Therefore, he was very at ease about these people.","Letting the barbarians stay here and eat white steamed buns made the ones cleaning up the battlefield extremely envious. It was a pity they didn’t know that if they stayed they could also eat such delicious white steamed buns.","Hu Cong didn’t care about what those barbarians were thinking. Seeing that his own people were full, he gave them another great benefit.","“You can now take the wages and go into the city to buy supplies.”","He pointed at the barbarians cleaning up the battlefield and said, “If there are any trustworthy people among them, they can be entrusted to bring food to your families.”","Upon hearing this, everyone’s eyes lit up. They thought it was worth it to eat this “poison”. They knelt down to Hu Cong to express their gratitude before going into the city together to buy supplies.","By noon, the barbarians had cleaned the desecrated areas of the Mohist residences until they looked new again. Under Meng Huaining’s arrangement they carried the corpses back to the barbarians’ lands along with the food they were instructed to deliver to their family members who had stayed behind.","Meng Huaining did not leave immediately. Currently there were no troops garrisoned at all in Yuncheng. Normally the only people maintaining law and order in the city were the officers under him.","Including the subprefect Mo Chuhan there were only thirty officers in total.","It was because the Mohist brothers had blocked the barbarians today at Xiling Village that they had not been able to take advantage of the opportunity to barge in.","If the Mohists brothers had not been there, the consequences were unimaginable.","Now by letting these barbarians go back, it was equivalent to releasing tigers back into the mountains.","But what could be done without letting them go?","He could not possibly detain all of these barbarians, right?","Even with Meng Huaining’s wisdom, when encountering something like this he still felt utterly bewildered.","At this time, Mo Chuhan had already settled those veterans who had come to join them together with his seventh elder brother. For now they were living in the house that had previously belonged to the Cui family.","The Cui family had been richer than the other two families. Basically all of their houses were brick houses. Although they were still a far cry from the","new courtyards the Mohists had built, at least they could block the wind and rain.","In the future, after the brothers had earned some money, they would consider rebuilding proper houses for their subordinates.","The two Mohist brothers knew Meng Huaining was still at the foot of the mountain dealing with the barbarians. After they finished settling the veterans, they came over here to find him.","Seeing the worried look on Meng Huaining’s face, Mo Chuhan went up and asked,","“Brother Meng, have you encountered some difficult problem?”","Meng Huaining gave a bitter laugh and talked about his concerns and how he had dealt with the barbarians.","Such a situation - Meng Huaining had thought of it, and so had the Mohist brothers.","It wasn’t that they were being overly worried. Originally, from what the villagers had told them, the barbarians coming to raid numbered at most a couple dozen people at a time.","If they discovered it in time, the barbarians wouldn’t even be able to steal anything. Instead, they would be given a beating.","If that really was the case, the Mohists would of course not be worried.","But accidents could always happen in any event, just like today when several hundred barbarians came, and one of them was even such a frightening commander.","If a similar situation happened again, it would still be something very troubling.","It would give anyone a headache to have their homes encroached on like this.","Moreover, Ninth Brother and Ninth Sister had even more plans. The number of domestic poultry and livestock raised at home would grow more and more. If these were not well protected and destroyed by the barbarians, it would be an irreplaceable loss.","Although Mo Chuhan and Mo Yuance had some countermeasures in mind, at most they could only do so to protect their own family, and perhaps they could protect Xiling Village.","As for all of Yuncheng, they were afraid they did not have that kind of capability, and did not want that kind of capability either."]},{"number":372,"title":"Chapter 372: Asking to Die is a Luxury.","paragraphs":["After all, the Mohists had a special identity and had completely lost confidence in the court.","To put it bluntly, the fact that they hadn't rebelled already showed their loyalty.","As the chief catcher, Mo Chuhan knew Yun City's situation very well.","\"Brother Meng, after such a big incident happened, I suggest you still seek help from the prefecture as soon as possible.\"","Meng Huaining nodded: \"For now, this is the only way. Yun City does not have any troops to defend it. Once the barbarians attack again, it would harm those innocent commoners.\"","Although he said that, he was very clear in his heart that the barren northwest was not valued by the court at all. Even if he made a request to the prefecture, the troops would not be comparable to other places.","Even if he brought up this matter with the prefect, he was afraid there would be no troops sent to provide support.","In any case, it was necessary for him to report to his superiors after such a major incident happened. As for whether the military force issue could be resolved, Meng Huaining did not have any hope at all. He was afraid that in the end, he would have to find a way by himself.","In fact, the two Mo brothers were more optimistic than Meng Huaining in facing the threat of the barbarians.","\"If nothing unexpected happens, after failing to raid and suffering so many casualties this time, the barbarians should not take action again in a short period of time.","Commoners are timid. If they weren't really out of food, they would not want to take risks to come and venture.\"","\"The only thing I worry about is that the barbarians have set their minds on attacking Da Shun. If the army invades, it would definitely not enter from Xi Ling Village here.","After all, it is difficult here with high mountains and rugged roads. It would be very inconvenient for them to transport grain and fodder.\"","\"The court should be worried. The most dangerous place now looks to be the western border.\"","Meng Huaining had been a county magistrate since he started his official career. After all, he was a civil official without a high position. He had also focused on governing the locality in recent times, so his insight into military affairs was far from that of the Mo brothers.","Hearing Seventh Elder Brother Mo's words, Meng Huaining felt like he was enlightened.","\"Although Yun City is at some distance from the western border, once a war starts, the commoners there will surely flee in this direction. It looks like I have to make some preparations early too.\"","As the parent official of Yun City, he could not overreach. But he had to ensure the safety of the commoners under his rule.","Thinking of this, Meng Huaining felt it necessary to plan properly.","He cupped his fist towards the two Mo brothers: \"Thank you two elder brothers for the reminder. I will go back now to make arrangements.\"","After such a big incident happened, the Mo brothers knew Meng Huaining still had a lot of things to deal with, so they did not keep him back and sent him all the way to the village entrance before heading back.","The time went back to the early morning.","On the official road three hundred li from the capital.","\"Ninth Younger Brother, the old guy is awake.\" Fifth Elder Brother Mo's voice was a little hoarse. Ever since they had taken out the toxic blood from Mr. Si Meng's heart, he had been keeping watch, afraid of any sudden circumstances happening.","At this time, Mo Jiuye was driving the carriage while Sixth Elder Brother Mo was riding on horseback.","Hearing Fifth Elder Brother's shout, Mo Jiuye hurriedly drove the carriage into the woods by the roadside to stop it, then immediately entered the carriage.","Sixth Elder Brother Mo also wanted to go into the carriage to take a look, but for everyone's safety, he could only stand outside the carriage to keep watch.","It was because Fifth Elder Brother had been keeping an eye on Mr. Si Meng that he would notice the slightest abnormality.","Therefore, when he informed Mo Jiuye, Mr. Si Meng had just moved his eyelids a little.","However, Mr. Si Meng was indeed regaining consciousness.","Probably because of the pain from the wounds, or numbness in his hands and feet from being tied up, his eyes were not fully open yet. First, he let out a painful moan.","\"Since you're awake, don't pretend to be dead anymore.\" Mo Jiuye did not have any patience for his big enemy at all. If not for still having questions to ask, he would have gotten rid of him already.","Hearing this voice, Mr. Si Meng's previously still groggy mind instantly became clear.","He forced his somewhat heavy eyelids open, and what entered his eyes were the angry looks from the two Mo brothers glaring at him.","He did not know that he had lost the toxic blood in his heart. He thought the pain in his body was from being beaten by the Mo brothers.","\"I'll say it again. Don't treat me like this. Surely you're not stupid enough to want to keep me company in death!\"","After speaking, Mr. Si Meng let out a series of cold laughs to demonstrate his advantage.","He had thought that continuing to threaten them this way would have the same effect. He did not expect that the looks in the Mo brothers' eyes would become more and more mocking, and there was even a feeling that they were taking him for a fool.","Mr. Si Meng subconsciously sensed that something was wrong, especially the position of his chest, which felt particularly painful. That kind of pain was somewhat different from that after being beaten.","He suddenly changed his expression, and his eyes also showed some unease.","\"What have you done to me?\"","Mr. Si Meng simply could not believe this was true. While speaking, he had tried to communicate with his life-bound Gu worm but got no response at all.","And seeing that Mo Jinian was alive and well in front of him, he could ascertain that the Mos must have found some expert to control his life-bound Gu worm. Otherwise, he would not be unable to communicate with his life-bound Gu worm now.","At the same time, he also felt a piercing pain coming from the position of his heart where he had hidden the toxic blood.","Could it be that his toxic blood heart Gu had also disappeared?","It had to be said that Mr. Si Meng was quite smart.","Although he did not know how the other party did it, he had realized the severity of the problem.","Seeing the smug look in the Mo brothers' eyes, he felt even more certain of the truth.","\"You're so sinister!\"","\"Sinister? You're the sinister one!\" Fifth Elder Brother gritted his teeth in anger.","Mo Jiuye was much calmer today. He did not get angry and retort Mr. Si Meng due to fury.","He only had one goal, which was to ask about the whereabouts of his father and brothers.","\"The you now, seeking death would even be a luxury.\"","This was his final reminder, hoping that Mr. Si Meng would know the time and situation better and not make them brothers interrogate too hard.","Mr. Si Meng had always thought highly of himself. After being caught by the Mo brothers, he had originally thought that even if he were to die, he would die proudly and drag the brothers down with him, and it would still be worthwhile. He did not expect that his toxic blood heart Gu would inexplicably disappear and he could no longer control the life-bound Gu worm. This made him feel somewhat unprepared while also realizing that his own situation was very dangerous after hearing Mo Jiuye's verbal threat.","However, he no longer had any capital to threaten the other party.","Moreover, judging by the Mo brothers' hatred of him, as Mo Jiuye said, even seeking death would be a luxury for him now.","Realizing this point, Mr. Si Meng was already starting to panic.","What he feared now was not death itself, but being unable to avenge his beloved woman, as well as possibly facing a fate worse than death through torture.","Seeing that Mr. Si Meng was still silent, Mo Jiuye knew that he had recognized his predicament.","\"If you don't want to suffer torture, just honestly tell me about my father and brothers' whereabouts. I'll consider giving you a quick death.\"","Mr. Si Meng still did not respond to Mo Jiuye. At this moment, his thoughts had drifted far away, back to thirty years ago..."]},{"number":373,"title":"Chapter 373: Do what you want.","paragraphs":["At that time, he could be said to be the most outstanding figure among the nobility of Southern Borderlands. Not only was he talented in both civil and military arts, but he also had a prominent family background. Many noble young ladies were infatuated with him.","People at the time spontaneously called him Shao Xin the Jade Faced Gentleman.","However, he only had eyes for one person - Yuan Meng, the princess of Southern Borderlands at that time.","Yuan Meng was not only beautiful, but also smart and good at military affairs.","Shao Xin felt that in the entire Southern Borderlands, only the princess could match him.","Yuan Meng also thought highly of herself. In her eyes, in the whole of Southern Borderlands, only Shao Xin was quite outstanding.","Shao Xin was over the moon to gain the princess' favor. It could be said that he got what he wished for, and devoted all his heart to Yuan Meng.","Until one day, Mo Qing's appearance broke their beautiful dreams.","From then on, Yuan Meng no longer treated him well. She even asked him to help her win Mo Qing's heart.","Facing such a request from the woman he loved, Shao Xin was helpless.","However, in order to fulfill the wish of the woman he loved, he could only go against his conscience to do things, hoping that Yuan Meng would eventually see his blind infatuation and turn back.","Who knew that after several setbacks, Yuan Meng was still obsessed with Mo Qing. She even became an accomplice to his evil deeds.","No matter who was at fault, the woman he loved eventually still died at Mo Qing's hands.","Yuan Meng might not love him, but as long as she was alive, he could see her at any time. But Mo Qing took away his hopes and dreams with one mistake.","Since this was the case, all those surnamed Mo had to accompany his beloved to her grave.","After Yuan Meng's death, Shao Xin was devastated overnight and his hair turned white.","In order to avenge his beloved woman, he reluctantly sold off all his family possessions to find a master to teach him Gu sorcery.","When his family found out that he had secretly sold all their assets, they angrily disowned him.","Not only that, he also paid a heavy price to become a first-rate Gu master.","For example, he was no longer a fully intact man...","Back then, he found the number one Gu master in Southern Borderlands to teach him Gu techniques. He gave all the silver earned from selling his possessions to his master.","As a result, his master told him that his Yang energy was too strong, and it was unlikely that he could become a top Gu master.","In order to avenge Yuan Meng, he self-castrated to make the Yang energy in his body weaker.","It could be said that in order to avenge his beloved woman, he had been plotting for many years and paid a great price.","He once swore that on the anniversary of Yuan Meng's death, he would take all the Mo men to her grave to worship and comfort her spirit in heaven.","Over the years, he had schemed step by step to today. He did not expect that at the most critical moment, he would stumble.","He had thought that after capturing Mo Jiuye and finding the missing Mo Chongyuan, all the Mo men would be gathered.","Unexpectedly, at the most critical moment, everything no longer went according to his plan. Not only did he fail to catch Mo Jiuye, even the Mo men he had in his grasp disappeared one after another.","In the past few days, not counting Mo Jiuye, two more had appeared before his eyes.","From this, it seemed that the other missing Mo men had also been rescued. It was just that they did not show up in front of him this time.","Thinking of this, feelings of despair had already filled his heart.","At this moment, he just wanted to die and let the Mo family never find Mo Qing and his son.","It was just that looking at the current situation, he knew it was impossible for him to die.","Si Meng tried to calm his mind and asked, \"What exactly do you want?\"","Mo Jiuye sneered, \"Do I need to spell out what I want so clearly?\"","Si Meng let out a series of cold laughs, \"Hehe... Anyway I can't live anymore, so go ahead and make your move!\"","He was convinced that he could withstand their torture as long as he stubbornly refused to reveal the whereabouts of Mo Qing and Mo Family Eldest Son. Then he could drag them down to hell together.","Mo Jiuye had already anticipated that Si Meng would not confess so easily. Rather than wasting time here talking nonsense with him, it would be better to be more straightforward.","Thinking of this, he reached into his robe and took out a bag of itching powder. He did not even make a pretense of threatening, and directly sprinkled it on Si Meng's body.","Si Meng was a master of poisons after all. He had already remembered the smell of this itching powder. When Mo Jiuye opened the medicine packet, he wanted to say something. However, Mo Jiuye did not give him the slightest chance to speak.","The unbearable itch instantly spread all over Si Meng's body, causing him to let out a laugh even more unpleasant than crying. His head jerked up violently, as if wanting to hit the carriage roof.","Mo Jiuye and Mo Chongyuan were watching him closely. How could they possibly give him such a chance?","Mo Chongyuan didn't hesitate and immediately went up to cover Si Meng's mouth, not even giving him a chance to vent with his voice.","Si Meng's eyes were full of pain, and he even shed tears.","Both Mo Jiuye and Mo Chongyuan could feel that Si Meng was definitely suffering horribly right now.","However, compared to what he had done to the Mo men and his subordinates, this little bit of suffering was like a drizzle.","Mo Jiuye's eyes turned blood red. He took out another small porcelain bottle.","This was also given to him by He Zhiran. It was medicine that could make wounds fester.","However, He Zhiran had modified it slightly. When poured on the body, the medicine could only accelerate the festering of wounds, even exposing the bones, but would not spread.","Such medicine would not endanger Si Meng's life. It could still make him suffer horribly.","Especially the appearance after the wounds festered was simply too horrifying to look at directly.","Mo Jiuye forcibly grabbed Si Meng's white hair and made him sit up straight.","Then he poured the medicine on the wound on his leg. From this angle, Si Meng could see it very clearly.","His purpose was to make the old fox personally watch as his own flesh festered bit by bit until the bones were exposed.","Si Meng's expression became increasingly frightened. However, he had absolutely no ability to resist. He could only endure the terrible itch and be at their mercy.","Mo Chongyuan also saw Mo Jiuye's intentions. He went forward and tore open Si Meng's pants, exposing the scars they had beaten onto his legs.","Mo Jiuye shook the medicine bottle in front of Si Meng's eyes and said in a low voice, \"Do you know what this is?\"","Although Si Meng did not know exactly what it was, he could be certain it was something to torture him.","Thinking of everything he had suffered these past two days, Si Meng was truly afraid.","He wanted to beg for mercy, to make up some excuses to fool them about Mo Qing and Mo Family Eldest Son's whereabouts. But his mouth was blocked and he simply could not express himself. He could only stare at Mo Jiuye in terror and let out a series of whimpers.","Mo Jiuye could see that the old fox was begging for mercy with these actions. But he had no intention of letting his enemy off."]},{"number":374,"title":"Chapter 374: I'll tell you the whereabouts of Ink Qing","paragraphs":["<Mo Jiuye> quickly opened the bottle cap and slowly poured the liquid medicine onto <Mr. Si Meng>'s leg wound.","In just a few seconds, <Mr. Si Meng>'s wound began to rot before his own eyes.","Gradually, pus began to ooze from the wound that was still attached to the flesh, frightening <Mr. Si Meng> so much that his entire body was drenched in cold sweat. Combined with the strange itchiness all over his body, he now only wanted to bash his head to death.","<Mo Jiuye> let out another cold laugh, holding up the porcelain bottle in his hand, pretending to pour it onto <Mr. Si Meng>'s other wounds.","<Mr. Si Meng> shook his head vigorously at <Mo Jiuye> and made a series of incomprehensible sounds.","<Mo Jiuye> knew that the old fox couldn't handle it anymore.","His purpose in doing this was to get useful information out of <Mr. Si Meng>'s mouth. Since the other party showed signs of wanting to compromise, he would give him a chance to speak.","After all, <Mr. Si Meng> was now completely under his control. There was no rush to torture him to avenge his father and brothers.","So <Mo Jiuye> put away the small bottle and tore off the cloth blocking <Mr. Si Meng>'s mouth.","\"Think carefully before you speak, otherwise you will face more severe torture.\"","<Mr. Si Meng> gasped for air. He was calculating how to muddle through for now.","He did not expect that the other party would give him a direct reminder that if he did not show some sincerity this time, the next storm would be even more violent.","\"Ask what you want!\"","<Mo Jiuye> did not waste any words: \"Where are my father and two brothers now?\"","Although <Mr. Si Meng> was tortured physically, his mind was not lost because of it.","At the same time, he also realized that now that he had fallen into the hands of the Mo brothers, he would not be able to live.","But he was unwilling. He felt ashamed to die and go underground without having succeeded in avenging his beloved.","But if he didn't say anything, he thought death would still be a very extravagant thing for him.","<Mo Jiuye> saw that he hesitated for a long time before speaking, and knew that the old guy was calculating another countermeasure in his heart.","Facing such a person, he couldn't give him a moment's breathing room.","So while <Mr. Si Meng> was still thinking, he opened the stopper again and poured the medicine onto another one of his wounds.","The pain made <Mr. Si Meng>'s consciousness return instantly.","\"Don't... don't torture me anymore, I'll tell you <Mo Qing>'s whereabouts.\"","\"Speak.\"","He's in the Western Territories.\"","\"Where in the Western Territories?\"","While answering <Mo Jiuye>'s questions, <Mr. Si Meng> kept watching his expression.","He could confirm that <Mo Jiuye> was very eager to rescue <Mo Qing> and his two brothers.","\"Only I know <Mo Qing>'s whereabouts in this world. I can fulfill your family reunion, but I have one condition.\"","For those who had persecuted his whole family, <Mo Jiuye> had no intention of indulging him.","He got up slightly and kicked the blood hole in <Mr. Si Meng>'s leg.","\"Even on the verge of death, you still want to negotiate terms with me. You really know how to dream.\"","<Mo Jiuye> didn’t kick lightly. <Mr. Si Meng> yelled out in pain.","\"Don't... don't hit me anymore...\"","Naturally, <Mo Jiuye> needed to grasp the degree. This old fox had been tortured by them so much. Coupled with the bloodletting operation he had just performed, his body was severely injured. If he was too aggressive, it would be easy for <Mr. Si Meng> to lose his life, which would be totally not worth it.","<Mo Jiuye> stopped and glared at him angrily.","\"Tell me, where exactly are my father and two brothers?\"","<Mr. Si Meng> pleaded for mercy verbally, but still wanted to get revenge.","\"As long as you promise me a quick death, I'll tell you.\"","<Mo Jiuye> was too lazy to even pretend to the biggest enemy of his family.","He opened the bottle again and poured the liquid onto another one of <Mr. Si Meng>'s wounds.","\"No need to talk terms with me, you don't have that privilege.\"","<Mr. Si Meng> saw his actions and it was too late to try to stop him verbally.","\"Don't... don't use it again, I'll tell you.\"","<Mo Jiuye> showed no mercy at all and poured the medicine onto <Mr. Si Meng>'s wound again.","The pain and itchiness drove <Mr. Si Meng> to be covered in cold sweat. In addition to the strange itchiness throughout his body, it felt as if he was about to pass out.","Deep down, however, he knew it was impossible for him to lose consciousness. He could only stay lucid and bear it.","\"I won't talk about conditions, I won't!\"","The <Mo Jiuye> and <Mo Chongyuan> brothers stared at him silently.","\"Speak!\"","\"<Mo Qing> is in the hill of the Western Territories.\"","When it comes to Little Hill, the brothers were no strangers.","When they were stationed in the Western Territories, they had both been to Little Hill.","Little Hill was named so because it was near the border and composed of countless small hills.","The small hills were layered and undulating, connected together to form what looked like a towering mountain peak.","There were many wild beasts there, and almost no one dared to go deep inside.","Neither <Mo Jiuye> nor <Mo Chongyuan> stayed there for long, only walking around the outskirts without ever really going inside.","However, the two brothers knew clearly that the area of Little Hill was very large. With <Mr. Si Meng> simply naming a mountain, it would not be easy to find their father and elder brother.","<Mo Jiuye> grabbed his collar and asked coldly, \"Where exactly in Little Hill?\"","<Mr. Si Meng> knew that he simply couldn’t trick them. He looked around and randomly named a location.","\"Go up the mountain from the vicinity of the Western Territories border. It's in a cave halfway up the mountain.\"","Upon hearing <Mr. Si Meng>’s words, the brothers let out a cold laugh simultaneously.","No matter what mountain it was, there were countless caves on the mountains. What he said was clearly perfunctory.","Obviously, the old fox did not want to tell them the true location of their father and elder brother.","This time, <Mo Chongyuan> came forward, grabbed <Mr. Si Meng>’s messy white hair with one hand, and with some strength, lifted him up.","\"Old fox, do you think you can fool us brothers by randomly naming a place?\"","In <Mr. Si Meng>’s impression, the Mo men were all military officers with only a warrior’s courage. He might still be slightly superior to them in a battle of wits.","He did not expect that after making up such a detailed location, he would still be seen through.","But if he changed his story now, even if what he said was real, it was unlikely they would believe him.","Rather than doing so, he might as well stick to what he just said.","\"I didn't lie to you, <Mo Qing> is indeed in the place I said.\"","Seeing that he still spoke like this, the fifth brother loosened his grip and threw the man inside the carriage.","\"You old thing, are you still trying to deceive us brothers?\"","As he spoke, the fifth brother had already taken out a gleaming dagger and placed it against <Mr. Si Meng>’s throat.","Seeing this, <Mo Jiuye> hurriedly went forward to stop him.","He was not worried that the fifth brother would accidentally kill the old fox, but it was obvious that at the moment, <Mr. Si Meng> was actively seeking death. If he suddenly exerted himself and rushed towards the dagger, it would be easy for him to take his own life. Then how could he find out about his father and brothers’ whereabouts?","\"Fifth brother, let me handle this.\""]},{"number":375,"title":"Chapter 375: Where the hell are my father and Brothers","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye said, then opened the food that Fifth Elder Brother had bought in the city the day before yesterday. Among them there was cooking salt that they would need on the road.","He grasped the salt in his palm, then clenched hard. The salt, which was originally like grains of sand, instantly turned into powder.","Mo Jiuye sprinkled the crushed salt on the few blood holes on Mr. Si Meng's body.","In just an instant, a scream came from the carriage: \"Ahhhhhhhh...\"","Fortunately, the location they chose was remote without any people. Otherwise, this scream would surely alarm passersby.","Even so, Little White, who was standing on top of the carriage, was still startled, flapping his wings high up.","Mo Jiuye and Mo Chongyuan looked coldly at Mr. Si Meng's miserable state.","After a long while, when he stopped screaming, Mo Jiuye asked, \"Have you thought about what to say now?\"","\"I've...I've thought about it...\"","Mr. Si Meng sounded weak.","\"Speak. Where exactly are my father and brothers?\"","\"They...they really are at Xiaoqiu Mountain. After the Princess died, her corpse was sent back to the Southern Borderlands. For my heart's desires, I personally built her a mausoleum with shroud and crown at Xiaoqiu Mountain. Your father is there keeping vigil over her.\"","This time, the two brothers believed his words a little more.","At the very least, keeping vigil over Yuan Meng was indeed one of Mr. Si Meng's motives.","\"Where is the mausoleum with shroud and crown?\" Mo Jiuye continued asking.","\"On the sixth hillock.\"","This sixth hillock was not unfamiliar to the brothers, because Xiaoqiu Mountain was made up of countless hillocks, and the local commoners would also use names like \"the sixth hillock\" to refer to them.","Although they still could not completely confirm whether or not Mr. Si Meng was telling the truth, this answer was still more reliable than the previous one.","In order to further confirm, Mo Jiuye grabbed another handful of salt in his palm.","\"From what I know, the sixth hillock is all thorn bushes. How could a mausoleum with shroud and crown be built there?\"","In fact, he had no idea what the situation on the sixth hillock was. He was purely bluffing.","Mr. Si Meng shook his head forcefully: \"That's impossible. Aside from more fierce beasts, the sixth hillock has absolutely no thorns. I chose that place to build the mausoleum with shroud and crown precisely because there are wild beasts there, so no one will go disturb it.\"","Moreover, he had also set up many traps with poisons around it. Other than him, no one who approached would make it out alive.","This was something he would not tell the Mo brothers.","Although he could not accomplish his own goals while still alive, as long as the Mo brothers dared to go save people there, he would definitely let them go and never return. The end result would still be to accompany his beloved in death.","As for Mo Qing, he was being controlled by Si Meng's life-bound Gu worm. Normally he would manipulate the mother Gu worm to control Mo Qing once every ten days or so, to make Mo Qing obediently keep vigil over Yuan Meng there.","Now calculating the time, it had already been four days since the last time he had manipulated the mother Gu to control Mo Qing.","That meant there were six more days until Mo Qing, without his manipulation, would lose all ability to act, and even lose the instinct to eat.","He believed that aside from him, no one would be able to enter the location of the mausoleum with shroud and crown alive. Even if the Mo brothers found it, they would not be able to rescue Mo Qing and his sons.","Especially since it took more than ten days to reach the Western Borderlands from here, even rushing day and night on fast horses. By then, Mo Qing would have long starved to death.","There were also Mo Family Eldest Son and Second Son. They were there as well, just doing things different from Mo Qing.","The two brothers were controlled by other mother Gu worms, with control times slightly longer than Mo Qing, around twenty days.","They were mainly responsible for hunting the wild beasts that approached the mausoleum with shroud and crown there, and at the same time taking care of the food and drink for the three of them.","In summary, Mr. Si Meng's final bargaining chip was that the Mo brothers would simply be unable to smoothly enter the location of the mausoleum with shroud and crown, and it was far more likely they would die in the poison mist traps he had set up.","That meant Mo Qing and his several sons would all die on the sixth hillock.","Thinking of all this, Mr. Si Meng felt that he really had nothing left to worry about.","\"I don't know who told you the sixth hillock was all thorn bushes. There really aren't any thorns there, just more fierce beasts and taller trees. With your father's skills, dealing with some fierce beasts is no trouble at all.\"","He did not take the initiative to mention that Mo Family Eldest Son and Second Son were also there. His goal was to avoid making the other party feel he was being too proactive, which would seem suspicious.","Mo Jiuye had been bluffing him, so hearing him say this, he more or less understood something. He continued asking, \"Where are my eldest and second brothers?\"","\"They're with Mo Qing.\"","After answering this sentence, Mr. Si Meng closed his eyes, putting on the appearance of waiting for death.","How could Mo Jiuye let him die before finding his father and brothers?","Considering it would take some time to take him away from the capital, if the old fart didn't eat, sooner or later he would starve to death.","To keep him alive, Mo Jiuye called towards outside the carriage, \"Sixth Elder Brother, bring some water and food here.\"","Sixth Elder Brother had been listening to the movements outside, and had long wanted to see what was going on inside the carriage. Hearing Ninth Younger Brother calling him, he hurriedly jumped onto the carriage with a waterskin and food.","Mo Jiuye opened the lid of the waterskin and poured water into Mr. Si Meng's mouth.","Mr. Si Meng was caught off guard and choked by the water, coughing loudly.","The Mo brothers wouldn't consider his circumstances. Seeing that he had opened his mouth, Mo Jiuye also stuffed a large piece of hardtack in.","Mr. Si Meng was forced to eat something. Powerless, he closed his eyes.","In fact, the several Mo brothers had not rested well while taking Mr. Si Meng with them on the road, and had not even had time to eat.","At this time, whether it was true or false, they had finally gotten some information out, making the several of them feel somewhat relieved.","Although they were in a hurry on the road, after all, they were not made of iron. The horses were the same. If they hadn't been He Zhiran's dimensional horses that could travel thousands of miles, they probably would have already collapsed from exhaustion travelling such a long distance continuously.","The environment here was not bad, and there were no people to disturb them, so the brothers decided to rest here for a while.","The three of them took turns watching Mr. Si Meng, finally getting a bit of rest.","Now that they knew of their father and brothers' whereabouts, none of them wanted to delay any more time. Their only goal now was to rescue them as soon as possible.","Resting until the afternoon, Mo Jiuye looked at the sky and suggested, \"Fifth and Sixth Brothers, let's continue on the road and reach the Western Borderlands sooner.\""]},{"number":376,"title":"Chapter 376: Arriving in the West","paragraphs":["\"Alright, let's set off now,\" Fifth Elder Brother said while pulling up the reins.","Sixth Elder Brother also got on his horse, while Mo Jiuye was responsible for guarding Mr. Si Meng in the carriage, preventing any accidents from happening.","The carriage had just started when Little White stood on top of it and let out a gurgling cry.","This was when Mo Jiuye remembered that he was so focused on interrogating Mr. Si Meng that he forgot about Little White.","He opened the carriage window to let Little White fly in.","Little White obediently stood on his shoulder and kept showing off arrogantly to Mr. Si Meng, who was like a dead dog.","As Mo Jiuye smiled, he also fed some food to it. Then, while Mr. Si Meng was unconscious, he wrote a letter saying everything was going smoothly, they had successfully captured Mr. Si Meng, and were rushing with him to the western border.","He tied the letter to Little White's leg. The letter was to He Zhiran.","After Little White was full, it flew to Xilin Village with Mo Jiuye’s letter.","The three brothers journeyed very smoothly. In order to reach the western border as soon as possible, they persisted in traveling whenever they had a bit of energy left.","At this pace, they finally arrived at the western border after eleven days.","Since it was a border city, the city gate guards would be stricter and inspect all passersby.","By now, Mr. Si Meng was so weak he was unrecognizable. If they didn’t need him alive, the brothers wouldn’t even want to feed him a bite.","But with such a battered man in the carriage, they definitely wouldn’t pass the inspection at the city gate. It might even cause them a lot of trouble.","Sixth Elder Brother worriedly asked, “Ninth younger brother, what should we do?”","Mo Jiuye looked at the commoners lining up to enter the city ahead of them.","\"Let's get in line first. I'll go up front and pave the way.\"","Everyone knew money could push a ghost to grind. So Mo Jiuye didn’t believe those guards wouldn’t like silver.","While the carriage was queueing, Mo Jiuye quickly went to the guards and looked extremely anxious.","Seeing a man running towards them, the guards thought he wanted to force his way into the city. They immediately blocked him with their weapons.","\"What are you doing? If you want to enter the city, go line up.\"","Mo Jiuye didn’t care about money. As long as they could enter the city smoothly, it was fine.","So as the guards questioned him, he took out a silver ingot and stuffed it into their hand.","Then he pointed to the carriage at the back of the queue and said, \"My family member is critically ill. I’m rushing into the city for medical treatment. Can you make an exception?\"","The moment the guard got the silver, his heart bloomed with joy.","Judging from the size of the ingot, there was at least five taels—his five months’ salary.","The guard immediately changed his attitude. It could be said he did a 180 degree turn.","\"Seeking medical treatment is important. Don't delay it.\"","After saying that, he quickly drove away all the commoners blocking the passage, making way for the carriage.","The carriage smoothly entered the city and headed straight for the small mound Mr. Si Meng mentioned.","Although it was rarely visited by people, there was a Da Shun army camp nearby.","Surely someone in the army would recognize them. They had to be careful not to expose their identities.","Therefore, the brothers decided to find a place farther away from the military camp to climb the mountain.","Of course, someone still needed to stay behind to guard Mr. Si Meng. In case he was wrong about the location, the brothers could continue interrogating him.","Although Mo Jiuye knew some basics about Gu techniques, he didn’t understand the details very clearly. Especially puppet Gu, he had no idea how to manipulate it.","That old fox Mr. Si Meng would never tell the truth.","Logically, when Mo Jiuye and the others entered the western border, they should look for Third Older Brother and the others first to see if they had found any clues.","But considering the manipulation time of the puppet Gu queen, Mo Jiuye didn’t dare to take it lightly.","It had been half a month since they captured Mr. Si Meng and took away all his Gu worms, including extracting his life Gu.","That meant Mr. Si Meng had at least half a month without commanding the puppet Gu larva in their father and brothers. Mo Jiuye worried that without mobility for too long, they might starve to death.","So he decided not to look for Third Older Brother first. Instead, he would go to the location Mr. Si Meng mentioned to look for his father, Eldest Brother and Second Brother.","As long as they successfully found them, he could remove the puppet Gu in them using his wife's method first to save their lives. That was the most important thing.","Finally, after discussing, the brothers decided Fifth Elder Brother, who was more attentive, would stay at the foot of the mountain to guard Mr. Si Meng, while Mo Jiuye and Sixth Elder Brother would climb the sixth mound of Xiaoqiu Mountain together.","Mo Jiuye looked at the sky. It was already the afternoon hour of Shen.","Although Xiaoqiu Mountain was made up of many small mounds, to reach the sixth mound, they had to climb over the previous five.","Looking from afar, the mounds didn’t seem big. But walking on them, there was quite a distance.","Fortunately, Mo Jiuye and Sixth Elder Brother had supreme martial arts. The two brothers leapt using Qinggong and crossed the five mounds in about an hour.","As the sixth mound entered their eyes, it did feel different from the others.","There was some space between the trees on the other mounds. Looking from a distance, it didn’t block the view too much.","However, the sixth mound was very different. At first glance, the entire hilltop was covered in lush greenery. Not only were there no visible roads, even the nearby ground was covered in a thick layer of moss.","Even the birds passing by would choose to detour around it. It showed how dangerous this mound was.","Based on experience, this was the place with the most snakes, insects, rats and ants. Once people walked in, there was no telling what danger they would encounter.","Sixth Elder Brother took out a dagger and held it in his palm.","\"Ninth younger brother, I'll take the lead to clear the way.\" He planned to hack his way through the thorns to open up a path.","Mo Jiuye knew that this was the only way in this situation.","So he also took out a dagger and held it in his palm. However, he didn’t take action immediately. Instead, he took out a package of realgar powder from his clothes and sprinkled it on himself and Sixth Elder Brother.","Only by doing this could they effectively avoid the invasion of snakes, insects and other toxins after entering the woods.","Saving their father and brothers was important, but if they couldn’t even ensure their own safety, how could they save others?","After the two brothers looked at each other firmly, they strode into the woods step by step.","The two cooperated seamlessly. One left, one right, cutting away the thorns blocking their path, while also staying vigilant at all times, noticing any snakes or insects that might appear under their feet.","Fortunately, Mo Jiuye had sprinkled realgar powder on them. Along the way, the poisonous snakes they encountered smelled it and automatically avoided them.","Because of this, the two brothers’ entry into the sixth mound went quite smoothly at first.","Even for the few poisonous snakes that weren’t afraid of the realgar smell, the two brothers killed them swiftly."]},{"number":377,"title":"Chapter 377: This Is Not Right","paragraphs":["The deeper they went, the more ominous the atmosphere around them became.","\"Ninth younger brother, should we stop and observe the situation?\" Sixth elder brother inexplicably felt a moment of panic. Even breathing the air around them gave him a suffocating feeling.","Mo Jiuye had the same feeling. Supposedly the air in this primal forest should be the freshest, but instead, he seemed to smell a stench of decay.","The two brothers exchanged a glance and then adeptly leapt upwards, landing atop the tallest and most robust nearby tree.","Looking down from this vantage point, there was still only lush, verdant forest as far as the eye could see, with even the forest floor obscured from view.","Fortunately, the tree they were standing on was quite tall. Climbing up a bit higher would allow them to see much farther.","Now, both brothers felt their vision open up.","About two li away, the dense undergrowth gave way to a stretch of flat grassland. In the middle of the grassland was a small lake, and the two brothers, with their sharp eyesight, could vaguely make out several people lying next to the lake shore.","Yes, there were definitely several human figures.","\"Ninth younger brother, there seem to be people over there,\" Sixth elder brother said.","Because of the great distance, they couldn’t clearly make out what those people looked like. The two men could only discern the outlines of human shapes.","A sense of foreboding instantly rose within Mo Jiuye.","\"Sixth elder brother, let's go over and take a look,\" he said.","Although anxious, Mo Jiuye had not lost his reason. As they continued forward, he kept the antidote pills his wife had made clasped tightly in his fist. He also gave one to Sixth elder brother.","\"Sixth elder brother, these are antidote pills that can save your life if necessary,\" he said gravely.","Sixth elder brother solemnly nodded, gripping the pill in his hand.","The two brothers were unclear whether there were any poisons or toxins nearby, but if this truly was Mr. Si Meng's territory, their presence was a certainty.","Of course, they also knew one fact clearly - Mr. Si Meng had already shown good faith by revealing the location of the sixth hill. Asking him for more details risked him laying some sort of trap for the two brothers.","Rather than being tricked by him, it was safer for the brothers to search on their own.","As the two brothers cleared away obstacles in their path, Mo Jiuye carefully observed their surroundings. Based on his past experiences at Si Meng Mountain Villa, wherever Mr. Si Meng's domains extended, poisons and toxins were indispensable elements.","Just after Mo Jiuye finished chopping away an obstruction ahead, he felt the ground under his feet become uneven.","He threw out an arm to stop Sixth elder brother from continuing forward.","\"Sixth elder brother, be careful!\"","Sensing something amiss, the two men leapt backward several meters in the span of their words.","Taking a closer look ahead, sure enough, concealed amongst the undergrowth they had just cleared away was a deep trench spanning the width of their path.","The trench was shaped like an irrigation canal, situated just wide enough to block passage forward. Finding such an oddly configured trench naturally occurring in the mountains was quite rare - most were manmade.","\"Ninth younger brother, there's something strange about this trench,\" Sixth elder brother warned.","Mo Jiuye nodded. \"I suspect there may be toxins inside.\"","When it came to poisons, Sixth elder brother had no specialized knowledge. But he had not forgotten about the antidote pill Mo Jiuye had given him earlier.","\"Ninth younger brother, should we take the antidote pills first?\"","\"Hold on. Let me go take a look first, then we'll decide,\" Mo Jiuye replied.","After speaking, he cautiously crept forward again.","\"Be careful,\" Sixth elder brother reminded, maintaining a battle-ready posture. If his younger brother encountered any danger, he would immediately rush forwards to help.","Mo Jiuye slowly parted the still quite dense undergrowth in front of him and gingerly stepped towards the trench.","When he finally peered over the edge, even the widely experienced Mo Jiuye was shocked speechless by the sight.","The trench was filled with countless scorpions, their venomous tails raised menacingly high, sending chills down his spine at the very sight.","Moreover, the scorpions seemed to have already sensed an unfamiliar presence approaching, and were continuously scuttling towards the top of the trench walls.","Seeing Mo Jiuye standing stock still, Sixth elder brother anxiously called out, \"Ninth younger brother, what's going on?\"","Mo Jiuye raised a hand, signaling his brother not to speak. Then he quickly took out another packet of realgar powder and sprinkled it towards the mass of scorpions.","Unexpectedly, while realgar powder was quite effective against venomous snakes, it barely made these venomous scorpions flinch.","They only dodged briefly before resuming their climb upwards as if nothing had happened.","Mo Jiuye gasped. This was his first encounter with such venomous scorpions, and realgar powder had actually failed!","With no time to waste, he hurriedly grabbed a small bottle from his side and sprinkled its liquid contents towards the scorpions.","\"Sixth elder brother, light it on fire!\"","Hearing Mo Jiuye's order, Sixth elder brother rapidly lit a match and flung it into the trench.","Mo Jiuye pivoted and pulled his brother far away with him.","After several muffled booms from within the trench, flames instantly soared more than ten feet high.","Soon after came the sounds and smell of scorpions crackling and charring en masse.","Sixth elder brother watched the scene before him incredulously.","\"Ninth younger brother, is this enough?\"","Mo Jiuye also wasn't certain that all the scorpions had been burned to death. But he believed his wife would never have given him anti-venom supplies that didn't work.","The flames soon subsided, and the air filled with the smell of something burnt.","This time, Sixth elder brother stepped forward of his own initiative. \"Let me take a look.\"","Although Sixth elder brother was checking, Mo Jiuye still didn't dare let his guard down. After all, all the life-saving items were currently in his own hands.","He closely followed his elder brother’s footsteps to assess the aftermath. The trench, just now teeming with scorpions, had been reduced to piles of ash.","Even so, Mo Jiuye’s wariness did not abate. The trench spanned quite a distance - if any areas hadn't been touched by the flames and still harbored surviving scorpions, they could still be lethal.","For now, at least he and Sixth elder brother were safe.","Time was of the essence. \"Sixth elder brother, let's head over now,\" Mo Jiuye urged.","Sixth elder brother nodded, then leapt across the trench alongside Mo Jiuye.","Ahead, more obstructing brambles awaited, but having found their bearings, the two men no longer worried about wandering aimlessly.","After continuing some ways, Mo Jiuye, still walking in front, suddenly felt something soft depress under his foot. Glancing down, he saw that he had trodden directly onto the back of a rainbow frog!","At the same time, countless similar rainbow frogs began hopping towards the two men from all directions.","Even the normally unflappable Mo Jiuye broke out into a cold sweat at this sight. During their ordeal at the bottom of Si Meng Mountain Villa’s well, he and his wife had already encountered these rainbow frogs before. Their skin oozed toxins from every pore.","In other words, even though he had only stepped on one rainbow frog, the possibility that its toxins had already entered his system could not be discounted.","He immediately popped an antidote pill into his mouth, reminding Sixth elder brother to also ready one and take it at once if he made any skin contact with the rainbow frogs.","Concurrently, he scattered realgar powder around them.","Last time at Si Meng Mountain Villa, it had been Rice Ball who tamed these rainbow frogs, so Mo Jiuye was uncertain if the realgar powder would still be effective now."]},{"number":378,"title":"Chapter 378: They're Big Brother and Big Brother.","paragraphs":["The realgar powder was not as effective against the rainbow frogs as it was against the snakes. The rainbow frogs only moved slowly for a moment before returning to their original state. Mo Jiuye and Sixth Elder Brother were unable to dodge in time and had already been touched by several rainbow frogs.","Fortunately, they had taken the antidote pills which allowed them to resist the toxicity of the rainbow frogs.","In Mo Jiuye's mind, such harmful creatures should not exist in this world, so he simply lit another fire to burn all of the rainbow frogs to death.","He and Sixth Elder Brother were in a hurry to check the identity of the person lying by the lake, and had no time to watch the burning scene. The two continued to hack their way through the undergrowth ahead.","They had assumed there would be more poisonous things ahead, but that was not the case.","Ahead was a white fog that completely blocked the two brothers' sight.","\"Ninth younger brother, this smell seems familiar.\" Sixth Elder Brother's mind was racing as he tried to remember where he had smelled this before.","Indeed it did seem familiar. This was the anesthetic that Minister Si Meng had used to confuse the Mo brothers when they were in the South.","Fortunately, the two had taken the antidote pills, otherwise they would have been knocked out by the poison.","Mo Jiuye also found the smell familiar. The first time he had fought with Minister Si Meng in the South, the latter had scattered such an anesthetic before escaping in a panic.","Although his wife's pills could solve hundreds of poisons, one could never be too careful in such matters and he absolutely could not gamble here.","\"Sixth Elder Brother, cover your nose and mouth, let's get through this quickly.\"","\"Alright.\"","The two brothers held their breath and covered their noses and mouths, rushing through the poisonous fog.","The scene that appeared before their eyes could be described as suddenly clear.","However, they currently had no time to look around and quickly raced towards the few people by the lake.","\"Ninth younger brother, it's Third Elder Brother and Liang Hao!\" Seeing his own brothers lying there, Sixth Elder Brother sounded rather anxious.","Mo Jiuye did not respond. He raced towards them.","Before the two brothers could get close, two figures suddenly leapt out from the bushes. Without a word, they raised their weapons and attacked their faces.","As Mo Jiuye and Sixth Elder Brother quickly dodged backwards, they also observed the appearance of the attackers.","The attackers were completely disheveled, and their bangs completely covered their facial features.","The two were very tall, and looked much thinner than normal people.","But from the details of their movements, Mo Jiuye and Sixth Elder Brother discovered something wrong.","\"Sixth Elder Brother, it's Eldest Brother and Second Elder Brother.\"","Before Sixth Elder Brother could respond to Mo Jiuye's words, Eldest Brother and Second Elder Brother waved their weapons again to attack them.","It was a good thing to be able to find the brothers they had been searching for here, but clearly, Eldest Brother and Second Elder Brother had no self-awareness.","This state was entirely because they were being controlled by the Marionette Witch Insect.","Facing their own brothers, no matter what, Mo Jiuye and Sixth Elder Brother could not use ruthless moves like against an enemy. But without ruthless moves, there was no way to stop their offense.","Mo Jiuye suddenly had a clever idea. He took out a package of anesthetic from his arms and sprinkled it towards the two elder brothers.","Soon, the two who were still attacking them staggered for a few moments before showing signs of collapsing.","Mo Jiuye and Sixth Elder Brother quickly went forward, one after the other, to support them before gently placing them on the ground.","At this time, Mo Jiuye was not blinded by the excitement of seeing Eldest Brother and Second Brother. Because Third Elder Brother and Liang Hao were still lying by the lake between life and death.","Considering the poisons they had encountered along the way, it was unlikely Third Elder Brother and the others had good fortune to make it this far.","He could only hope he had not come too late.","Mo Jiuye did not think much more. He raced swiftly towards Third Elder Brother and the others.","First he checked Third Elder Brother's breath, it was very weak, but he had not yet stopped breathing.","From his darkened skin, it could be determined that Third Elder Brother had been poisoned.","In fact, Mo Jiuye and Sixth Elder Brother did not know that the poison barrier Minister Si Meng had set up there was not just a simple anesthetic.","Third Elder Brother was clutching a handkerchief. If the guess was correct, he should have also discovered that poison fog and used this to cover his nose and mouth.","Although Third Elder Brother's method of resisting the poison barrier was not perfect, at least he had taken precautions. Otherwise, what Mo Jiuye would have seen when he arrived here was Third Elder Brother's corpse.","Looking at the condition of Liang Hao and the others, it was about the same as Third Elder Brother’s, all on the verge of death.","In this situation, Mo Jiuye was also at a bit of a loss.","The only thing he could do now was to first give them the antidote pills and hope it was not too late.","Mo Jiuye took out the antidote pills from his arms and handed some to Sixth Elder Brother. The two brought the pills to Third Elder Brother and the other’s mouths.","But unfortunately, they had completely lost consciousness and simply could not swallow them.","This greatly worried Sixth Elder Brother.","\"Ninth younger brother, what should we do? They simply cannot swallow the pills.\"","At this point, Sixth Elder Brother was sweating profusely from anxiety.","At this moment, Mo Jiuye was calmer. He took out another pill again and crushed it in his palm.","\"Sixth Elder Brother, quickly take out the water bag.\"","Sixth Elder Brother swiftly took the water bag from his waist. When Mo Jiuye had poured all the medicine powder into Third Elder Brother’s mouth, he reached out and pinched his throat, pouring water down.","This method of Mo Jiuye’s proved very effective. Third Elder Brother had successfully taken the antidote.","Using the same method, the two brothers also fed the antidote to Liang Hao and the others.","After going through this process, the only thing the two brothers could do was wait.","At the same time, they prayed that the antidote would save Third Elder Brother and the others.","Their goal was to save their elder brothers and father. They did not want any other brothers to have any more mishaps.","The antidote worked very well. In less than an incense stick worth of time, most of the black on Third Elder Brother and Liang Hao’s faces had faded away, and their breathing was much more even than before. It was just that there was still no sign of them waking up.","Despite this, Mo Jiuye and Sixth Elder Brother were much more at ease.","They could confirm that Third Elder Brother and the others were no longer in mortal danger and waking up was just a matter of time.","No longer worried about Third Elder Brother and the others’ safety, Mo Jiuye finally shifted his attention to Eldest Brother and Second Brother.","His wife had given him two types of anesthetics at that time. The difference between the two anesthetics was in the duration of efficacy.","On the way here, in order to prevent Minister Si Meng from making trouble, Mo Jiuye had mainly used the long-acting anesthetic on him.","Right now, Mo Jiuye only had the short-acting anesthetic left on hand. That meant the anesthetic he had just given Eldest Brother and Second Brother could only knock them out for about an hour before they would wake up.","From the previous situation of the two elder brothers, it was clear they had no self-awareness at all and everything was under the control of the Marionette Witch Insect.","In this situation, if they did not promptly remove the insects after the two woke up, the consequence would be as soon as they regained consciousness, their first reaction would be to attack Mo Jiuye and Sixth Elder Brother.","Therefore, Mo Jiuye decided to remove the Marionette Witch Insects from their bodies before Eldest Brother and Second Brother woke up.","Although this was Mo Jiuye’s first time personally removing the insects, he had witnessed his wife do it many times.","The surgery to remove the Marionette Witch Insect was very simple, and the location was not in a vital area of the human body. In addition, Mo Jiuye had the experience of taking out Minister Si Meng's Heart Blood, so this operation was a piece of cake for him."]},{"number":379,"title":"Chapter 379: What have you got to Say","paragraphs":["After all, this was an open place, and wild beasts could show up at any time.","Mo Jiuye scanned around and saw a small cave entrance.","\"Sixth elder brother, let's carry them in.\"","Not only Big Brother and Second Brother, but also the unconscious Third Older Brother and Liang Hao's group needed to be carried in.","Only by ensuring their safety could Mo Jiuye feel at ease to remove the Gu worms from his two elder brothers.","In front of the cave, there was no moss or weeds on the ground, which clearly showed that people came in and out frequently.","Inside the cave, two bluestone slabs the size of single beds had been polished so smooth without any edges or corners.","Moreover, Big Brother and Second Brother had just rushed towards them from this direction. It could be inferred that this was where the two elder brothers had lived for many years.","Needless to say, the simplicity was evident. The bare stone slabs had no beddings. There were no spare clothes inside the cave either.","This could be determined from the tattered clothes on Big Brother and Second Brother.","There were white beast bones scattered all over the ground in the cave, placed very messy, obviously no one had cleaned them up.","From these details, one could see what kind of inhuman life Big Brother and Second Brother had led for so many years.","There was no time to think too much. Mo Jiuye asked Sixth Elder Brother to carry Big Brother and Second Brother onto the two stone slabs separately.","He was in no hurry to remove the Gu worms for his two elder brothers. After all, his wife would use those advanced instruments in her space to test and determine the position before performing surgery to remove the Gu worms.","The biggest advantage of doing this was that it could accurately locate the Gu worms and prevent any deviations during surgery.","But now there were no such conditions.","Although Mo Jiuye could roughly determine the location of the Gu worms, he did not dare to act rashly.","Once the offspring Gu worm encountered danger in the host body, it would escape to other parts of the body. If such a situation occurred, it would be difficult to remove the Gu.","In order to more accurately determine the location of the offspring Gu worms, Mo Jiuye took out the small porcelain bottle containing the mother Gu worm found in Mr. Simeng's place.","He could not determine which Gu worm was the mother Gu controlling the offspring Gu in his elder brothers' bodies, so he could only try shaking them gently one by one.","As long as the mother Gu worm moved slightly in the porcelain bottle, the offspring Gu it controlled would also wiggle in the host body.","Mo Jiuye and Sixth Elder Brother cooperated, with each person staring at one elder brother’s arm.","He tentatively shook a porcelain bottle.","Soon, there was a noticeable bulge on Second Brother's arm.","A bean-sized lump could be seen with the naked eye under his skin.","Mo Jiuye determined the location of the offspring Gu worm and immediately handed a porcelain bottle to Sixth Elder Brother.","\"Sixth elder brother, see the Gu worm at the first moment and put it into the porcelain bottle.\"","After Sixth Elder Brother nodded solemnly, he held the porcelain bottle with his eyes fixed on Ninth Younger Brother’s action.","Mo Jiuye moved the knife and made a not very deep cut on Second Brother's arm.","A black Gu worm appeared before the two brothers.","Without any hesitation, Sixth Elder Brother nimbly put the offspring Gu worm that had just revealed its head into the bottle.","Mo Jiuye skillfully helped Second Brother disinfect the wound and sutured it. Although his suturing technique was not great, the effect was satisfactory.","Using the same method, Mo Jiuye found the mother Gu controlling Big Brother by shaking, accurately located the offspring Gu worm in his body and performed the surgery.","When everything was finished, Mo Jiuye's forehead was sweating.","He did not forget to reassure Sixth Elder Brother.","\"The Gu worms in Big Brother and Second Brother have been removed. As long as the effects of the anesthetics wear off, they will wake up.\"","Estimating the time, it had been more than half an hour since he had given the two elder brothers the anesthetics. If nothing unexpected happened, they would wake up soon.","Judging from the physical condition of Big Brother and Second Brother, their whole bodies were thinner than just skin and bones, and their faces looked much older compared to his impression.","Especially Big Brother, there was a long scar above his forehead.","However, compared with Fourth Elder Brother and Seventh Elder Brother, the situation was much more optimistic. At least their limbs were not seriously injured.","Just as Mo Jiuye was carefully observing the conditions of Big Brother and Second Brother, he suddenly felt a slight movement behind him.","He and Sixth Elder Brother turned around at the same time and saw that Third Older Brother had opened his eyes slightly.","Not knowing whether it was because the toxins in his body had not completely subsided, his eyes looked a little swollen.","\"Third Older Brother, you are awake?\" As Mo Jiuye and Sixth Elder Brother were already squatting in front of him.","Seeing the two brothers, Third Older Brother still couldn't believe this was real.","He rubbed his somewhat uncomfortable eyes vigorously and looked at the two again.","\"Sixth Younger Brother, Ninth Younger Brother, where is this place?\"","\"Third Older Brother, we are now in the foothills of the Western Realm.\"","Hearing that it was the foothills, Third Older Brother's confused consciousness finally began to return slowly.","Seeing him trying hard to sit up, Mo Jiuye and Sixth Elder Brother supported him from left to right.","\"Third Older Brother, don't worry, take your time.\"","Third Older Brother first looked left and right and saw Liang Hao and the others lying not far away, still in a coma.","There were also two people on the stone slabs who looked like beggars and he could not see their appearance clearly.","\"Sixth Younger Brother, Ninth Younger Brother, how are Liang Hao and the others?\"","He did not recognize his two elder brothers. At this moment, his first concern was naturally the good brothers who had risked danger with him.","\"Third Older Brother, don't worry. Liang Hao and the others have taken the antidote. I believe they will wake up after a while.\"","Hearing Ninth Younger Brother say this, Third Older Brother finally felt relieved.","He then asked, \"Why did you two appear here? Were you injured by the poisons on the Sixth Mound?\"","Recalling the poisons they had encountered after entering the Sixth Mound, Third Older Brother was still terrified.","If it hadn't been for their martial arts prowess to dodge onto the trees in time, they would have long become a delicious meal for those scorpions and toads.","Mo Jiuye knew that Third Older Brother and Liang Hao’s group had encountered the same as him and Sixth Elder Brother when they went up the Sixth Mound.","It was just that he and Sixth Elder Brother had the life-saving items prepared by his wife, so they were not injured.","Third Older Brother and the others did not have such adequate preparation. It was extremely fortunate that they still had a breath left when he came to their rescue.","In order not to make Third Older Brother worry, Mo Jiuye briefly recounted how several brothers went to the capital to capture Mr. Simeng, and then came here to look for their father and elder brothers.","After listening, Third Older Brother's gaze fell directly on Big Brother and Second Brother who were still unconscious lying on the stone slabs.","\"Ninth Younger Brother, are they Big Brother and Second Brother?\"","Mo Jiuye nodded solemnly: \"Fortunately our brothers are unharmed. We had just arrived here when Big Brother and Second Brother appeared. However, they were also under the control of Mr. Simeng's puppet Gu worms and had no consciousness at all. I could only temporarily make them pass out and then remove the Gu worms.","Now the Gu worms have been successfully removed from Big Brother and Second Brother. They will wake up after a while.\"","Third Older Brother excitedly grabbed Mo Jiuye's arm while using his support to try to stand up."]},{"number":380,"title":"Chapter 380: Do You Still Know Me","paragraphs":["However, the poison in his body had been eliminated, but there were still residual aftereffects.","The brothers didn't know that the poison barrier contained not just simple anesthetics or lethal poisons.","Mr. Simeng was cunning and deceitful. In order to prevent the Mo brothers from finding this place and rescuing people, he deliberately added cartilage ingredients to it.","Now the third brother's legs were so soft that he couldn't stand up at all.","\"Ninth brother, what's wrong with me? I feel weak all over and my hands and feet don't seem to obey orders?\"","Mo Jiuye knew how to lift curses and treat some external injuries. He had only learned the basics while helping his wife.","At this moment, he really couldn't say clearly what was going on with the third brother.","However, as long as the third brother was alive, it was good. After finding their father and taking everyone back to Xi Ling Village together, Ranran would surely have a way.","\"Third brother, don't worry. Your poison has just been lifted, and there may be some aftereffects. Let's wait and see,\" Mo Jiuye comforted.","At the same time, Liang Hao and others also gradually woke up. They had the same condition as the third brother, feeling weak all over and unable to stand up with soft hands and feet.","Now that the Mo brothers had all been found, their top priority was to find out what had happened to their father.","However, the eldest and second brothers were not fully awake at this time, and the third brother and Liang Hao were having trouble moving.","Mo Jiuye had to stay and wait for the eldest and second brothers to wake up, check the situation, and then go look for their father.","The sixth brother was fine, but he didn't have as many life-saving methods as Mo Jiuye. If he went out and encountered danger, not only would he not be able to successfully find his father, but he would also become a burden to the brothers.","Therefore, no matter how anxious he was in his heart, he did not ask to go out and look for people immediately.","Since nothing could be done now anyway, Mo Jiuye simply asked about the experiences of the third brother and the others after arriving in the Western Territory.","\"Third brother, how did you find this place?\"","\"It was purely by accident that we found this place,\" the third brother replied somewhat helplessly.","After a pause, he continued: \"After arriving in the Western Territory, we looked for clues everywhere.","After nearly three months here, we had turned the entire Western Territory upside down, but found no suspicious traces.","Finally, only the hills were left unchecked, so I pinned my last hopes on it. I thought that if we still couldn't find any clues in the hills, we would hurry back to Yun City immediately and think of other ways as brothers.","When we got to the sixth hill, I felt something was wrong.","Especially the trees and thorns that were different from the other hills, I was determined to take a closer look.","Who knew, shortly after we entered the sixth hill, countless scorpions appeared. Fortunately, Liang Hao, who was walking in front, was alert and reminded everyone to use their lightness skill to climb the trees, so we escaped disaster.","Later, we encountered frogs of various colors. Luckily, I had the realgar powder that you and Ninth Sister had given me. When they were moving slowly, we narrowly avoided danger.","I observed the living environment of those poisons and it was obvious that they were artificially raised. So I became more certain that this place was very likely to be where our father and brothers were imprisoned.","I thought that as long as we found the water source ahead before falling unconscious, we might be able to alleviate the symptoms of poisoning.","We could already see the water source ahead after getting through the poison barrier, but the toxins spread too fast and we passed out before we could get close to the water source.\"","The third brother still didn't know that if the sixth and ninth brothers hadn't arrived in time, they might have already died at the hands of the eldest and second brothers.","Mo Jiuye also felt chills down his spine when he thought of this, but since the danger had been defused, it wasn't the time to go into details about the process, so he didn't mention it immediately.","Just then, the sixth brother, who was closest to the eldest and second brothers, cried out in surprise.","\"Second brother, you're awake?\"","Although the third brother and Liang Hao were having trouble moving right now, their eyes all shifted to the second brother. Mo Jiuye walked over quickly, staring closely at the second brother.","\"Second brother, do you still recognize me?\"","Mo Jiacheng hadn't fully opened his eyes yet. He just moved his fingers slightly, but the sixth brother thought he was awake.","He did regain consciousness. He felt dizzy and disoriented, as if he had just suffered a heavy blow.","Hearing the familiar voice calling beside his ear, he forced his eyes open a tiny slit.","Mo Jiacheng murmured softly, \"Sixth brother?\"","Seeing that the second brother recognized him, Mo Jinnian nodded vigorously in excitement: \"Second brother, it's me, Jinnian. You've suffered.\"","Mo Jiuye also leaned in: \"Second brother, look at me, who am I?\"","The second brother's eyes moved and fell on Mo Jiuye.","\"Are you the ninth brother?\"","When he got into trouble, Mo Jiuye was still a teenager in his teens, but now he had grown into a tall, handsome man. It was understandable that the second brother would doubt when he saw him.","\"Second brother, it's me, Jiuye.\"","The second brother's mind felt a little slow at the moment.","The man in front of him did look exactly like the ninth brother, but he seemed to have much more vicissitudes than the ninth brother in his impression.","\"Are you really the ninth brother?\"","Mo Jiuye was not surprised at all by the skepticism. More than five years had passed since the last time he saw the second brother.","\"Second brother, I'm Jiuye. I'm twenty-two now.\"","\"What did you say?\" The second brother was even more confused.","Just as Mo Jiuye was about to explain briefly, there was also movement on the eldest brother's side.","\"Second brother, let me explain to you later.\"","As he spoke, Mo Jiuye and the sixth brother had already come to the stone bed of the eldest brother.","The sixth brother grabbed the eldest brother's hand and called out softly, \"Eldest brother... Eldest brother... It's me, Jinnian.\"","Mo Jiuye did the same, standing in front of the eldest brother calling out.","Mo Junrui seemed to be in better condition than the second brother. As he was called, he had already sat up with the help of the sixth brother's arm.","\"Sixth brother, ninth brother, what happened to me?\"","He also had a moment of disbelief when he saw Mo Jiuye, but when he was groggy just now, he seemed to hear the ninth brother say that he was twenty-two years old.","And from the eyebrows of the man in front of him, he could confirm that this was the ninth brother without a doubt.","As for the sixth brother, nothing had changed, he had just matured a little."]},{"number":381,"title":"Chapter 381: Let's Split up and Search.","paragraphs":["Having seen this younger brother's identity was not questioned by the eldest brother, Mo Jiuye went ahead and explained.","\"Eldest Brother, Second Brother, years ago you were tricked by the southern border people on the battlefield...\"","Mo Jiuye gave a brief account of what happened.","Upon hearing that the Mohist men had suffered so much misfortune for no reason, and the Mohist family was ordered by Emperor Shunwu to have their family assets seized and be exiled, Second Brother was immediately furious, the veins on his forehead bulging.","He clenched his fist and smashed it heavily onto the stone bed.","A muffled boom rang out inside the cave, and the stone bed instantly cracked and shattered.","Second Brother nimbly leapt up from the broken bed and landed steadily on the ground. Angrily he said,","\"These scoundrels! My Mohist men were utterly loyal to Great Shun, but in the end we were reduced to this!\"","As he spoke, he glanced down at himself again - calling his appearance half-naked would be too generous.","If not for his face being kept filthy from years of captivity here, the blush spreading across it now would surely be visible, red as a baboon's bottom.","Mo Jiuye had witnessed Second Brother's temper flare like this many times already.","By comparison, Eldest Brother was much calmer.","\"Sixth Younger Brother, Ninth Younger Brother, you just said our father suffered the same fate as us brothers, and you still haven't found his whereabouts?\"","\"Mm. We'll go out and search for him right away. If all goes well, Father should be nearby.\"","As Mo Jiuye spoke, he was already striding towards the cave exit.","He had observed that despite being under the puppet worm's control, Eldest and Second Brother were luckily kept fed by Mr. Si Meng, so their bodies seemed fairly healthy.","Especially Second Brother - his inner power was as strong as ever, able to smash through such a thick stone slab in one blow.","Just then, Second Brother also regained his senses. He had indeed lost control of his emotions for a moment there. After venting them out, his rationality instantly returned.","\"Let's search separately,\" he said.","Hearing Ninth Younger Brother's words, he realized that he and Eldest Brother must have been living here for quite some time. Yet he was completely unfamiliar with the surroundings here, having no memories at all.","Of course, that was to be expected - under the puppet worm's control they had no consciousness of their own, so how could they be familiar with the environment?","As they passed by Third Older Brother and the others, Eldest and Second Brother simply nodded in greeting. After all, the most urgent task now was to find their father's whereabouts.","Seeing his brothers all heading out to search, Third Older Brother felt increasingly anxious.","\"Ninth Younger Brother, is there really no way for me to stand up?\"","He had just tried focusing his energy, and his legs didn't feel as limp anymore. But getting to his feet was still difficult.","Mo Jiuye knew Third Older Brother was anxious. He reassured, \"Third Older Brother, you all just rest here. Once we find Father we'll come back here right away.\"","Third Older Brother knew that no matter how impatient he felt, it would be futile. He could only reluctantly nod, \"Alright, we'll wait here.\"","No one knew what they might encounter on this search.","And whether their father really was at the Sixth Mountain Ridge was still uncertain.","Where Third Older Brother and the others had collapsed unconscious by the lake, their scattered packages remained. Mo Jiuye knew those likely contained food and other items, so before leaving he gathered all the packages and brought them back for Third Older Brother, and also filled up a waterskin.","Luckily Third Older Brother and the others' packages contained spare clothes, so now Eldest and Second Brother didn't have to awkwardly expose themselves.","The two quickly changed into fresh outfits and followed Mo Jiuye and Mo Jinnian out of the cave to search for their father.","The Sixth Mountain Ridge was very large in area, and the open space in front of the lake was also sizable.","The clearing was surrounded by mountains and forest, with lush, densely foliated vegetation that obscured the view beyond if one did not push aside obstructing branches and thorns.","With the experience of entering this area before, Mo Jiuye dared not let the elder brothers wander too far apart from himself.","How could this place of Mr. Si Meng's possibly lack toxins?","He worried if the brothers separated and happened to encounter something poisonous, he wouldn't make it in time to rescue them.","That would be a most unworthy trade - saving one only to lose another.","Thus, when the elder brothers proposed splitting up to cover more ground, he firmly refused, clearly explaining his reason was to prevent everyone from getting poisoned.","Just as Mo Jiuye expected, in another direction they discovered the same type of poison barrier they had passed through to enter the Sixth Mountain Ridge's center.","Passing through the barrier, they were met with the same rainbow frogs, followed by scorpions.","This confirmed that the path ahead likely led to the Seventh Mountain Ridge.","Mr. Si Meng had set these obstacles to prevent intruders coming from the direction of the Seventh Mountain Ridge.","Mo Jiuye decisively gave up on that path.","\"Elder brothers, let's head back and search the other directions.\"","While Mo Jiuye's judgment made sense to him, it wasn't so clear to the others.","\"Ninth Younger Brother, this area looks completely different. Why should we search the other directions?\"","Mo Jiuye pointed back the way they had come. \"The obstacles here are the same as when we first entered the Sixth Mountain Ridge center. In all likelihood, just past here is the Seventh Mountain Ridge, not far away. That old fox is a top-class poison master, he must have full confidence in his toxins. In his mind, no one could possibly intrude upon the Sixth Mountain Ridge clearing and leave alive. So he had no need to create two sets of barriers. The ones we just passed must be to prevent entry from this direction.\"","Sixth Elder Brother had the most interaction with Mo Jiuye, so he knew Ninth Younger Brother was far smarter than himself. Hearing Mo Jiuye's explanation, he was the most convinced.","\"What Ninth Younger Brother says makes sense. Eldest Brother, Second Brother, let's listen to Ninth Younger and head back.\"","Eldest and Second Brother's impressions of Mo Jiuye still lingered from when he was 16 or 17. Facing such a clever and wise younger brother now felt somewhat unfamiliar.","However, Ninth Younger Brother's words did seem reasonable.","\"Alright, we'll listen to Ninth Younger and go back for now.\"","Returning to the open space, the sky had gradually darkened.","But the brothers showed no intention of giving up the search.","Eldest and Second Brother found some thick wooden staffs, while Sixth Elder Brother used flint to light them as makeshift torches so they could continue searching the surroundings.","Just as the moon began to rise, a sudden roar of a tiger came from behind the brothers.","They halted in their tracks, with Mo Jiuye and Sixth Elder Brother already grasping their daggers.","In the blink of an eye, a vividly striped fierce tiger bounded towards them.","Accustomed to protecting their younger siblings since their youth, Eldest and Second Brother's instinct was to place themselves between the tiger and Mo Jiuye and Mo Jinnian."]},{"number":382,"title":"Chapter 382: Don't you Think it's Weird","paragraphs":["The two of them had no weapons in hand. When the tiger came in front of them, they could only use their fists to hit it.","Although this could prevent the tiger from hurting people, it was unable to kill it with one blow.","The tiger's body was hit hard several times. Feeling the pain, it dodged back.","The brothers could see the direction the tiger escaped was somewhat strange.","Before the sky had completely darkened, they went to check that direction.","There was a marsh not very big over there. Those without lightness kungfu would not be able to pass through it at all.","With the sensitivity of a beast, even when escaping, it would not go to such a place.","There were two possibilities. First, the Eldest Brother and Second Brother had beaten the tiger silly and it lost its judgment.","Second, the marsh was not as simple as it looked.","Mo Jiuye chased out first, while reminding the elder brothers.","\"Let's follow and take a look.\"","The brothers followed closely behind the tiger.","Mo Jiuye was the fastest. When he had just chased to the front of the marsh, he saw the huge figure of the tiger disappear swiftly.","Moreover, the way it disappeared was very bizarre. It sank into the marsh in a blink of an eye.","This was completely different from what the brothers knew.","Normally, no matter if it was human or animal, they would sink slowly into the marsh. But that tiger disappeared instantly.","The brothers looked at each other.","The Eldest Brother walked forward a few steps and said, \"This marsh is not simple. Let me step on it and try.\"","Seeing that the Eldest Brother had already taken a step forward, Mo Jiuye quickly stopped him, \"Don't.\"","The Eldest Brother was stopped by Mo Jiuye and felt somewhat puzzled, \"Ninth Younger Brother, aren't you feeling strange that the tiger just disappeared like this?\"","Strange?","Of course it was strange.","But Mo Jiuye did not want his brothers to take risks.","Sixth elder brother had gotten used to listening to Ninth Younger Brother's arrangements recently. Seeing that Eldest Brother was a bit disobedient, he quickly came over to help stop him together with Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye did not explain too much. While Sixth elder brother was helping to stop Eldest Brother, he picked up a stone on the ground that was a little bigger than a fist.","He threw the stone into the marsh. Through the light of the torch, they could see the stone disappear quickly without making any sound.","The brothers were shocked again.","\"Ninth Younger Brother, this should not be a marsh.\" Sixth elder brother said.","This was the same judgment of the brothers. Compared to the tiger, the stone was much lighter.","If it could be explained that the heavy tiger sank quickly, how could a stone also disappear so fast?","Mo Jiuye frowned and thought for a long time before speaking, \"I suspect this is just a marsh-shaped barrier. The inside is empty.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, the brothers heard the tiger's roar coming out again.","And they could clearly distinguish that the sound came from under this marsh.","With this, Mo Jiuye became even more certain of his guess.","The tiger had fallen into this marsh and it had been almost half a stick of incense. It should have suffocated and died already.","But listening to its voice, there was no feeling of suffocation or weakness at all.","Mo Jiuye handed the torch to Sixth elder brother, \"I'll go down first to take a look. Don't take any rash actions before you hear from me.\"","He knew that if he did not act unexpectedly, he would definitely be stopped by the elder brothers. Therefore, as soon as he finished speaking, Mo Jiuye had already jumped into the marsh.","At the same time, several anxious voices came from behind his head.","\"Don't.\"","\"Let Eldest Brother go, Ninth Younger Brother.\"","\"Don't be reckless, Ninth Younger Brother.\"","\"Ninth Younger Brother...\"","Speaking was not as fast as taking action. While Mo Jiuye was listening to these calls, his body had already sunk into the marsh and he stood firmly on the hard ground.","The place that should have been pitch black had dim lights.","Mo Jiuye could determine that the lights were from oil lamps, which meant there should be people here.","Without thinking too much, because the startled tiger he saw in front of him was glaring ferociously at him, already posing to attack.","Mo Jiuye knew clearly that in order to find out the situation here, he had to deal with this tiger first.","So he raised his dagger, aimed at the tiger's throat and stabbed down.","If it was an ordinary person, the small dagger would not pose much threat to the tiger even if it stabbed down.","But what kind of person was Mo Jiuye? He was the War God praised by the people of Great Shun. If he made a move, how could the tiger possibly have any hope of surviving?","The dagger stabbed right at the tiger's throat accurately. The tiger only struggled for a bit before dying.","Mo Jiuye pulled out the dagger and wiped the blood clean on the tiger's fur before observing the surroundings.","When he had just jumped into the marsh earlier, he had felt his body descend at least three zhang.","From this it could be determined that his current location was like an underground cellar.","Although there were lights here, it was very dim. Mo Jiuye simply took out his flashlight.","He first shone it upwards.","The top was very different. Through the light of the flashlight, he could clearly see it swaying slightly, and it looked no different from the marsh seen from outside.","He could not discern what this thing was exactly, but he could confirm that it had penetrability. This was how he had entered, and it did not seem to be damaged.","Just now when the tiger entered the cellar and made sounds, it could be transmitted outside. This showed that there was no sound insulation here.","In order not to worry the elder brothers outside, Mo Jiuye shouted loudly, \"Elder brothers, I have entered safely. It is very safe now.\"","He had thought it was just to report his safety, but soon after his words fell, the figures of the elder brothers appeared around him one after another.","Eldest Brother was the first to jump down. Hearing Ninth Younger Brother's voice, he determined that he could enter just by jumping into the marsh.","Right after was Sixth elder brother and Second Brother, appearing almost at the same time in front of him.","\"Ninth Younger Brother, did you find anything?\" Eldest Brother asked first.","Mo Jiuye had just killed the tiger and observed the top of the cellar, then reported his safety to the elder brothers. He had not had the chance to check out more.","\"I haven't had the chance to check yet.\"","Hearing the Ninth Younger Brother say this, the elder brothers very cooperatively separated into the four directions and started examining around respectively.","Mo Jiuye did not stay idle either. With the elder brothers around, he could only put away the flashlight temporarily and check the surroundings relying on the light of the oil lamps.","He estimated that the four sides of the cellar were ordinary stone walls, but none of them would believe there were no other passages here.","The builder would not boredly create such a mysterious square pit.","Although the brothers had not discovered anything yet, they were not discouraged.","They continued groping the walls to check them thoroughly."]},{"number":383,"title":"Chapter 383: The Father","paragraphs":["Just as a few people didn't find anything and were somewhat disappointed, Mo Jiuye suddenly stopped his movements.","\"Eldest Brother, Second Brother, Sixth elder brother, if I'm not wrong, there should be an entrance here.\"","Hearing Mo Jiuye's voice, everyone gathered around.","Mo Jiuye pointed to the place his hand had touched and said, \"It's not as smooth here, and it's a bit more concave compared to the other walls.\"","The elder brothers reached out and touched that spot, and indeed felt the same as Mo Jiuye.","\"Ninth younger brother, let's try pushing it,\" Sixth elder brother suggested.","Mo Jiuye nodded lightly, and his palms began to gently push the different spot.","They had thought it would take some effort, but unexpectedly, with Mo Jiuye's light push, the stone slab moved.","In the silent basement, a sudden loud rumbling sound rang out.","The stone slab in front of the brothers quickly disappeared, revealing a dimly lit passageway.","Mo Jiuye went in first, while also remaining vigilant at all times, wary of things like hidden arrows.","The passageway was very spacious, wide enough for two people to walk side by side.","Sixth elder brother very naturally walked to Mo Jiuye's side, also adopting a defensive stance.","The passageway was about a hundred meters long and completely flat the whole way.","Unexpectedly, as the brothers walked all the way to the end, they did not discover any hidden arrows.","The only difference was that the temperature here became lower and lower.","If the initial temperature felt like spring or autumn, upon arriving here, it felt like the onset of winter.","Although it hadn't reached the point of biting cold winds, one couldn't help but want to rub their hands together to stay warm.","However, the brothers all had some martial arts skills, so with a little internal energy, they could easily dispel this feeling of cold.","Stepping out of the passageway, the view opened up before them.","They hadn't gone above ground, but rather the path ahead was completely illuminated.","The light here didn't come from oil lamps, but from seven luminous night pearls hanging overhead.","These seven night pearls were a bit smaller than the ones Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran had taken from the Dashun Country Treasury, but the light they emitted was comparable to the daylight of incandescent lamps.","Thanks to the good lighting, the scene before them was in full view of the brothers.","A huge painted lacquer coffin sat squarely in the middle of the open space.","Hanging from the four corners of the coffin were two silver bells, but with no wind here, the bells just hung quietly.","Most distinct was the carving of lifelike flying phoenixes and monkeys on the coffin lid.","Although such an extravagant coffin here would easily draw the brothers' attention, at this moment, they couldn't focus on it at all.","Because kneeling in front of the coffin was an emaciated person.","His clothes were about the same as when the brothers first saw Eldest Brother and Second Brother, and could only be described as tattered.","His head of silver hair was matted into clumps on top of his head.","Moreover, at first glance this person looked like a desiccated corpse, giving off no signs of life.","In his hands he still grasped a stack of paper money, while in front of him was a bronze basin, with ashes from burnt paper money inside.","It was very obvious that this person was kneeling here burning paper for the person in the coffin.","The brothers simultaneously felt a strange suffocating sensation, and quickly crowded around.","Mo Jiuye gently brushed aside the silver hair covering the man's cheeks. Upon seeing his true appearance, the brothers' eyes reddened around the rims.","\"Father.\"","\"It really is father.\"","Eldest Brother made a motion as if he was about to reach out and touch Mo Qing, but was stopped by Mo Jiuye.","Being stopped didn't upset Eldest Brother, as he also realized that the ninth younger brother was very wise now, and must have had a reason for stopping him.","After blocking Eldest Brother, Mo Jiuye carefully extended a hand and placed it under Mo Qing's nose to check his breathing.","From his terrible complexion, they could judge that father's condition was not very good.","Second Brother anxiously asked, \"Ninth younger brother, how is father?\"","Mo Jiuye didn't answer immediately. Instead, like He Zhiran had done before, he placed his hand on father's carotid artery.","Then he exhaled heavily.","\"It's alright, he still has breath.\"","Hearing that father still had breath, Sixth elder brother hurriedly moved closer.","\"Let's take father away now.\"","As he spoke, he was about to pick up the unconscious Mo Qing on his back.","Mo Jiuye shook his head. \"Don't move him for now. Father's condition is very worrying, and moving him might endanger his life.\"","Hearing the ninth younger say this, Sixth elder brother's outstretched hand immediately froze in midair.","\"Then what should we do? We don't know medicine, so how do we treat father?\" Sixth elder brother asked anxiously.","This was also the biggest worry for Eldest Brother and Second Brother.","Mo Jiuye was also nervous now, but after following his wife for so long, he had picked up some medical knowledge.","He knew that without figuring out the situation first, moving was unwise, as it could accelerate death.","He was also very clear about another thing - the control interval for the Puppet Worm.","From interrogating Mr. Si Meng, he knew that the Puppet Worm afflicting father was that man's lifework.","They as brothers had already captured Mr. Si Meng for over half a month now, and the control periods for the Puppet Worm were irregular, at minimum 10 days or half a month for manipulation to enable the host worm to move the host like a puppet, which was to maintain basic survival.","This was also why the brothers had rushed day and night to get here.","From father's current state, Mo Jiuye analyzed that he should have lost the mother worm's control, and lost many survival behaviors, leading to his current condition.","In short, the biggest reasons were likely the long period without food, along with the cold indoor temperature, resulting in father's current dire state.","Thinking of this, Mo Jiuye hurriedly took out his water skin.","He poured water into the lid of the waterskin, then gently pried open Mo Qing's mouth, slowly pouring water in bit by bit.","After doing this several times and seeing that Mo Qing didn't reject it, he handed the lid and waterskin to Sixth elder brother for him to continue feeding Mo Qing water.","As for himself, he took out the cardiac stimulant his wife had given him.","With father's situation so critical now, he didn't care if this item was suitable to take out.","At this moment, nothing was more important than father's life.","Of course, if his elder brothers asked later, he would take full responsibility for the item's origins - there was no way he would expose his wife's secrets.","Mo Jiuye quickly injected the cardiac stimulant into Mo Qing's muscle, then continued watching Sixth elder brother feed him water.","After about the time it takes to burn a stick of incense, checking Mo Qing's breathing and pulse again showed improvement.","Although he was still very weak, it was much better than when the brothers first saw him.","Having done what they could for now, the only thing left for the brothers to do was wait for father to regain consciousness.","In his current condition, it wasn't suitable to immediately remove the worm - he was too frail."]},{"number":384,"title":"Chapter 384: That was too much.","paragraphs":["Anyway, Mo Jiuye already had control of the father's gu worms in his hands. As long as the mother gu remained alive, the subsidiary gu inside the father's body would not endanger his life.","Once the father regained some strength, the gu extraction surgery could be performed on him.","However, Mo Jiuye still had a concern.","That is, as long as the puppet gu inside the father's body is not removed, he will not have independent consciousness.","It is estimated that when he wakes up, he will continue to do what he did when he was under control.","Mo Jiuye's thoughts were not understood by the other brothers. Seeing their father's condition improve, they all stood up and went to check the situation inside the entire tomb.","Apart from the coffin and Mo Qing, there were remnants of animals scattered on the ground.","From this, it can be determined that their father has been surviving by eating these things.","And judging by his appearance, he should have been controlled by Mr. Si Meng to keep vigil here.","Therefore, the brothers concluded that these animal remains were their father's food, but none of them were brought back by him from hunting.","So, the purpose of Mo Jiuye and Mo Qing being here is self-evident.","Mr. Si Meng is really good at assigning tasks. He made Mo Qing keep vigil here, while Mo Jiuye and Mo Qing's eldest and second brothers were responsible for hunting and providing him with wild animals to eat, ensuring the survival of their father and the three of them until now.","As for the central coffin, there is no doubt that it belongs to Princess Yuan Meng of the Southern Frontier.","Upon closer observation, there are ten memorial tablets around the coffin, each engraved with the names of all the male members of the Mo family.","Not only that, but the tablets also record a specific date, which is the date of their deaths.","However, this date is somewhat special—it is the beginning of July this year.","It is still the end of May now, which means there is still more than a month until the beginning of July.","While they are still alive, their memorial tablets have already been made, and the date of their deaths has been written.","This is enough to prove that Mr. Si Meng's conspiracy is to capture all the male members of the Mo family and plan to kill them on the day of July 7th this year, in order to avenge Yuan Meng.","The brothers angrily threw all the memorial tablets into the copper basin, and Mo Liu set them on fire with a torch, saying in anger, \"Si Meng, you old devil, you've really gone too far.\"","Although the others didn't say anything, the anger in their hearts was no less than that of Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye looked at the burning memorial tablets in the copper basin, stood up angrily, pried open a corner of the coffin lid with a dagger, and then exerted force to open the coffin.","Inside, there was no Yuan Meng's corpse, only a set of very exquisite palace attire.","On one side of the coffin, there was a large memorial tablet with clear engravings—Spirit Tablet of Beloved Wife Yuan Meng!","Mo Jiuye casually picked up the spirit tablet and crushed it with force, then took out the palace attire from inside and threw it into the copper basin.","The fire in the copper basin had not completely extinguished yet, and when it encountered the flammable palace attire, it burst into flames again.","At this moment, Mo Qing should have been affected by the cardiac stimulant needle in his body, and he was showing slight movements, but it seemed a bit sluggish.","Mo Jiuye saw Mo Qing's hand reaching towards the side, skillfully picking up a stack of paper money, and preparing to throw it into the bronze basin.","Mo Jiuye's eldest brother, with bloodshot eyes, hugged him tightly.","\"Father, this is the archenemy who has caused great harm to our Mo Family. We cannot treat her like this.\"","However, Mo Qing showed no response at all and continued to maintain the motion of burning the paper money.","Mo Jiuye knew clearly that his father was under the influence of a puppetry gu, which caused him to lack autonomous consciousness.","While his brothers were still trying to persuade, Mo Jiuye had already stepped forward and hugged his father from behind.","Mo Qing, who already had weak physical strength, lost his ability to move after being held by Mo Jiuye.","His eyes became vacant, and he stopped his actions, allowing Mo Jiuye to hold him.","Seeing that he had successfully restrained his father, Mo Jiuye planned to carry him away from that spot.","However, to everyone's surprise, while Mo Jiuye had lifted him up, his father remained in a kneeling position, with his legs curled up and unable to stretch out.","It looked as if Mo Jiuye was carrying a corpse.","At this point, the brothers became anxious.","\"Father, what's happening to your legs?\" Six Brother's voice choked up.","Unfortunately, no matter how urgent the brothers appeared, Mo Qing showed no response, still staring ahead with vacant eyes, and if not for Mo Jiuye restraining his hands, he would still be attempting to burn the paper money.","\"Jiuye, what's wrong with father's legs?\" Second Brother had already guessed a possible reason, but deep down, he was unwilling to believe it and asked anyway.","Mo Jiuye had arrived at the same conclusion, that his father's legs were unable to stretch out due to the long-term kneeling posture.","In this situation, he had no way to help and dared not risk trying to stretch them out. He could only bring his father back to Xi Ling Village and let his wife figure out a solution.","\"Let's take father away from here first and then come up with a plan.\" Although Mo Jiuye's tone sounded calm, his mind was in chaos.","Although his father had regained consciousness, when he held him, Mo Jiuye could feel how weak his life force was.","He couldn't guarantee that his father would survive after leaving this place.","He dared not voice such thoughts and didn't want to face such a reality.","Given the current situation, the best choice was to take his father away from this cursed place.","Six Brother approached Mo Jiuye.","\"Jiuye, don't worry, I'll try using lightness skills to see if there are any obstacles up there.\"","Mo Jiuye didn't refute this. They had already thoroughly searched the tomb, and apart from the top of the swamp, there was simply no other entrance or exit.","Therefore, if they wanted to leave, they could only go back the way they came.","\"Alright, be careful, Six Brother.\"","As Mo Jiuye's words fell, Six Brother had already leaped up using his lightness skills.","Because the space here was relatively large and empty, Six Brother could only use the surrounding walls as support.","It could be said that for someone who didn't possess martial skills, entering this place and trying to leave would be as difficult as reaching the heavens.","Fortunately, all the Mo Family members were martial arts experts, so leaving this place was not only not difficult but as easy as turning over their hands.","Sixth Brother's head broke through the softness of the swamp, and he reappeared in the same spot he had just entered.","After looking around, he didn't see anything unusual, so he jumped down again.","This whole process could be described as taking no more than a blink of an eye.","Mojyuye saw him reappear and asked, \"Sixth Brother, how's the situation?\"","\"No problem at all. As long as we use light skills to go up, we'll be back in the same place we were before we came in.\"","Now, the brothers had a clear idea and planned to leave this place immediately with their father.","At the same time, Sixth Brother approached Mo Jiuye.","\"Ninth Brother, give our father to me. I just went up once and gained some experience, so it will be easier for me.\""]},{"number":385,"title":"Chapter 385: Shall I cure my father first","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye did not refuse. Sixth elder brother's lightness skill was no worse than his own, not to mention that he had other things he wanted to deal with.","Seeing that the three elder brothers had used their lightness skills to take father away, Mo Jiuye tore off the hem of his clothes and flew up to collect all the Night Pearl hanging in the tomb.","He had learned this good habit from his wife. When he encountered treasures, especially those of his enemies, he must not leave them behind.","Although Mo Jiuye did not have a space as powerful as his wife's, taking away these few Night Pearls was no problem.","The Night Pearls were wrapped up but still could not completely block their glow.","Although the tomb was much darker, Mo Jiuye's vision was not affected at all.","He scanned the place again, scattering the large amount of paper money stored here around the tomb, and threw down a match as he leapt up with his lightness skill.","The paper money caught fire as soon as it met the match, burning up instantly. Mo Jiuye quickly left this place.","There was no need to ask, this was the place Si Meng old fox cared about the most. He must destroy it to torment Si Meng even after death.","When Mo Jiuye reappeared on the ground, the elder brothers had already settled father down nearby.","Through the glow of the seven wrapped Night Pearls, he could see that father was still kneeling with his right hand continuously taking and burning paper money.","The only way to change this situation was to remove the gu from father.","Given father's current weak state, Mo Jiuye was not fully confident he could successfully remove the gu worm from him.","However, letting father continue like this was not a long-term solution.","Sixth elder brother had witnessed Mo Jiuye removing gu worms from Big Brother and Second Brother before, and believed that Ninth Younger Brother could successfully remove the gu worm from father as well.","\"Ninth younger brother, shall we try removing the gu from father first?\"","Mo Jiuye was hesitating the whole time. After all, he was not fully confident. But he also did not want to see father tormenting himself like this.","Instead of answering Sixth elder brother directly, he said, \"Let's take father back to the cave first, and check on Third elder brother and the others as well. There are many wild beasts here, especially at night. Wolf packs may come out hunting anytime.\"","Third elder brother and the others have limited mobility now. It would be too unfortunate if any danger befalls them.\"","The brothers tacitly nodded and carried father towards the cave swiftly.","When they were about two li away from the cave, the brothers heard wolf howls.","\"Not good, Third elder brother and the others are in danger!\"","As Sixth elder brother spoke, he circulated his qi again, displayed his lightness skill to the maximum, and rushed towards the cave.","The other brothers also realized something was wrong and followed closely behind Mo Jinnian.","What entered their eyes when they arrived at the open ground in front of the cave were more than a dozen hungry wolves howling at the cave entrance.","In the dim night, green lights flickered like fireflies - those were the feral glint in the wolves' eyes.","Mo Jiuye and Sixth elder brother raised their arms at the same time, shooting arrows from their mini crossbows straight at the starving wolves.","In a blink of an eye, some of the wolves in front collapsed. Hearing the lead wolf's cries, the remaining few fled down the valley.","With the danger resolved, the brothers hurried into the cave with Mo Qing.","They saw Third elder brother, Liang Hao and the rest, each holding a torch that was nearly burnt out, waving it around with effort.","From their condition it was apparent that the effects of the softened cartilage had not completely worn off, otherwise they would not have looked so miserable facing these wolves.","Seeing his brothers return, Third elder brother heaved a sigh of relief even as he felt the torch in his hand weigh like a thousand pounds.","If not for fear that losing his grip would drop the torch and cause a fire, he would have let go of it already.","Mo Jiuye noticed their hands had barely any strength left to hold the torches. He quickly went up to take over the one closest to him in Third elder brother Song Chao's hand.","Mo Jinnian similarly took over the torches that Liang Hao and the others were holding.","Mo Jiuye asked with concern, \"Third elder brother, are you alright?\"","Third elder brother smiled wryly and shook his head, \"We're fine, fortunately you all came back in time.\"","As he spoke, he looked towards the cave entrance where Second Brother was hugging someone.","Third elder brother's eyes widened, \"Who's this?\"","\"Third elder brother, this is Father. We finally found him.\"","On hearing that it was Father, Third elder brother instinctively tried to get up to take a look.","However, despite feeling much better than when he first awoke, his legs still lacked the strength to support his whole body.","He failed to stand up and stumbled in front of Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye quickly supported him.","\"Third elder brother, don't panic. Father has not had his gu removed and still lacks self-awareness.\"","By this point, Second Brother had already carried Father in and gently laid him down beside Mo Yunfeng's side.","\"Yunfeng, Father's condition is not very good.\" There was undisguised grief in Second Brother's tone.","Mo Yunfeng was scrutinizing Father closely, finding it hard to believe that this emaciated, aging man would be his father.","In his impression, Father had been tall and valiant, while the old man before him now bore not a trace of Father in his prime.","He reached out a trembling hand, trying to touch Father. But he was startled by Mo Qing's sudden movement.","Mo Qing was still repeating his previous actions of taking paper money by his side and burning it. This time, he happened to grab Mo Yunfeng's arm.","Mo Yunfeng had little strength to begin with. Getting his arm pulled by Mo Qing to make the gesture of offering the paper money into the bronze basin, Second Brother had no choice but to step forward and pry Mo Qing's hand off Mo Yunfeng's arm.","Mo Yunfeng was utterly baffled.","\"Second Brother, what is Father doing?\"","Not just Second Brother, even the other brothers who knew did not wish to answer.","It could be said to be the greatest humiliation in Father's life.","At the same time, Sixth elder brother looked at Mo Jiuye, eyes crimson red.","\"Ninth Younger Brother, shall we try removing Father's gu now?\"","He had participated in the entire process when Mo Jiuye helped Eldest Brother and Second Brother remove their gu previously. He believed that with Ninth Younger Brother's abilities, he would surely succeed in dispelling the gu worm in Father as well.","That way, Father no longer had to continue suffering such humiliation.","Mo Jiuye pondered for a moment before making up his mind.","\"Alright, let me take a look first.\"","As he spoke, Mo Jiuye took out all seven Night Pearls that were bundled in his hem.","The cave was instantly awash in light as bright as day.","Using the same method, in order to ascertain the gu worm's location in Father's body, Mo Jiuye took out Master Si Meng's life gu.","Sixth elder brother stepped forward tacitly to strip off the measly strips of cloth covering Father's upper body, revealing his torso that was as withered as dead wood.","Mo Jiuye gently shook the porcelain bottle while observing Father's arms.","The result puzzled him greatly."]},{"number":386,"title":"Chapter 386: See you at my brother's House.","paragraphs":["According to reason, the puppet gu worms live in the brachial artery of a person's arm.","However, after shaking Father's arms several times, Mo Jiuye didn't find any trace of the child gu worms.","This made Mo Jiuye doubt for a while whether it was because the mother gu worm had died.","But on second thought, that was impossible. If the mother gu worm had died, Father certainly wouldn't have survived either.","Looking at it this way, the child gu worms in Father's body must not be in the arms, otherwise, with his emaciated body, the child gu worms would have been discovered with the slightest movement.","Seeing that Mo Jiuye had no reaction, the brothers held their breath and stared at him.","Under the gaze of his elder brothers, Mo Jiuye continued to shake the mother gu worm in his hand, but his eyes had shifted from Father's arms to other parts of his body.","As he shook the mother gu worm, he observed carefully until finally he noticed something wrong around Father's heart.","To Mo Jiuye, there was nothing unfamiliar about this anomaly.","Because there he saw the traces of the child gu worm's movements.","This location made Mo Jiuye gasp.","Seeing the ninth brother's reaction, the brothers could determine that Father's situation was not optimistic, they just didn't know exactly why.","The second brother couldn't help but ask, \"Ninth Brother, how is Father's condition exactly?\"","Mo Jiuye put away the porcelain bottle containing the mother gu worm and slowly stood up.","\"The location of the child gu worm in Father's body is in the heart.\"","\"What did you say?\" The sixth brother was very shocked by this: \"The child gu worms of Eldest Brother and Second Brother were clearly in their arms, so why is Father's gu worm in his heart?\"","Mo Jiuye was also very puzzled by this.","When he read the book Gu Insects Compendium, there was no such introduction at all.","Uniformly, for any puppet gu, the location of the child gu worm was in the arms. But for Father, why did it change?","Could it be that what was in Father wasn't a puppet gu?","For the time being, Mo Jiuye couldn't think through the reason.","But he could confirm one thing, which was that the location of the child gu worm in Father's body was the same as the location of the poisonous blood in Si Meng's heart.","He couldn't help but associate this location of the gu worm with the innate gu.","Although he had successfully located the gu worm, he didn't dare to rashly operate to remove the gu worm for Father.","When he performed surgery to remove the poisonous blood from Si Meng's heart at the time, he discovered that it was in a location tightly attached to the heart. The slightest deviation during the surgery would cost a life.","Fortunately, he didn't know about this situation at that time, so when removing the poisonous blood from Si Meng's body, he was not nervous and did not make any mistakes.","Now putting it on his own father, Mo Jiuye really couldn't make this cut.","It wasn't that he was timid, but that the location of the gu worm was too close to the heart. He wasn't a professional doctor like his wife, and any mistakes would immediately cost his father's life.","He really didn't dare to gamble with his father's life.","Mo Jiuye first looked at Father, who was still repeating the same action, then looked at the anxious elder brothers.","\"For now, there are only two ways to successfully help Father remove the gu worm.\"","The eldest brother anxiously asked, \"What methods?\"","\"The first method is to find the old fox Si Meng and have him personally manipulate the innate gu to remove the gu worm for Father.","The other method is for us to return to Xi Ling Village at the fastest speed and find a way with Ran Ran.\"","After a pause, Mo Jiuye continued:","\"The old fox Si Meng would be happy to see the Mo Family People accompany him in death. Moreover, with the innate gu in his hands, there's no guarantee that he won't do something unexpected.\"","Mo Jiuye was very clear about the power of the innate gu in its master's hands.","Even separated from its master's body, its power was still formidable and could cause unimaginable consequences.","For example, if Si Meng verbally agreed to remove the gu for Father, but once he obtained the innate gu, he could activate it to directly kill the child gu worm in Father's body. That would be a pyrrhic victory.","Therefore, Mo Jiuye didn't dare place his hopes on Si Meng.","\"Ninth younger brother, do you mean that the best way to remove the gu worm for Father is to return to Xi Ling Village and find Ninth Sister?\" the sixth brother asked to clarify his understanding.","Mo Jiuye nodded solemnly: \"Yes, this is the only way. Riding fast horses from here, it will take three days to reach Xi Ling Village. We can only pray that Father's health holds out until then.\"","\"What do you mean 'holds out until then'?\" Eldest Brother asked, puzzled.","Mo Jiuye sighed helplessly.","\"Based on my judgment, Father's current condition is very worrisome. What's really threatening his life is not the gu worm in his body, but his already dilapidated health.\"","When they left, although his wife had prepared many emergency items for him, and fortunately there were also heart strengthening pills, otherwise Father probably wouldn't have survived until now.","Although he could discern Father's condition, he didn't know how to treat it. Before seeing He Zhiran, there was no guarantee for Father's life.","This was also the most vexing issue in Mo Jiuye's mind.","The family had finally reunited, yet Father's health was so worrisome.","After hearing Mo Jiuye's words, Second Brother moved to pick Father up, saying, \"What are we waiting for then, let's hurry and take Father down the mountain.\"","Even though it was the dead of night, and the way down the dangerous, treacherous mountain was difficult, he didn't want to delay even a moment that could save Father's life.","Mo Jiuye also had this plan in mind.","\"Yes, let's take Father down the mountain tonight.\"","After speaking, he looked towards Third Brother and Liang Hao sitting on the ground.","\"Third Brother's condition has improved a lot compared to when he was first rescued. I believe he'll be able to move freely by tomorrow morning.\"","Sixth Brother knew that Ninth Younger Brother was worried that on the way down there were poison barriers and toxins that Third Brother and the others would not be able to deal with.","He walked over and patted Mo Jiuye on the shoulder.","\"Ninth Younger Brother, you, Eldest Brother and Second Brother first take Father down the mountain. I'll stay here to look after Third Brother and the others. As soon as they can move, I'll take them and leave together.\"","Mo Jiuye nodded, \"Yes, this is the only thing we can do now.\"","As he spoke, he took out several medicine pills from his clothes and gave them to Sixth Brother, \"These are antidote pills, they'll come in handy when you go down the mountain.\"","Sixth Brother accepted the pills and carefully put them away, \"After you've gone down the mountain and met up with Fifth Brother, hurry back to Xi Ling Village with the fastest speed. We'll see each other back home, brothers.\"","\"Alright.\" Mo Jiuye responded and gave Sixth Brother some other reminders before leaving the mountain with Eldest Brother, Second Brother and Father.","Fortunately he had taken all of the night pearls from the tomb, and left some behind for Third Brother and the others to light up the cave. They also became the most important lighting tools for their descent down the mountain.","With the experience from their climb up, the brothers didn't have much difficulty taking Father down the mountain.","Even so, by the time they met up with Fifth Brother, the sky was already brightening."]},{"number":387,"title":"Chapter 387: Are You a Man or a Ghost","paragraphs":["Wu Ge, responsible for guarding Mr. Si Meng at the foot of the mountain, had no major incidents. After all, the old man was already on the verge of death and couldn't struggle anymore.","The only thing that made people anxious was that Mo Jin Nian and Mo Jiuye had been in the mountains for a whole day without any news coming back, which made Wu Ge uneasy.","At this time, it should be the time when people slept the most soundly, but Wu Ge didn't feel sleepy at all.","He worried that old fox Si Meng would play tricks, but more importantly, he was concerned about the safety of his two brothers.","When he heard faint footsteps coming closer from the mountain and could determine that it was not the two of them, Mo Chongyuan first glanced at Mr. Si Meng, who looked like a dead dog, and then jumped off the carriage.","As the sound got closer and closer, he asked in a deep voice, \"Who goes there?\"","Upon hearing Wu Ge's voice, Mo Jiuye quickly responded, \"Wu Ge, it's me.\"","\"Jiuye, you're back? Is everything going well?\"","Mo Jiuye was eager to save his father, so he didn't have time to explain too much.","\"Wu Ge, I've rescued Father and our two elder brothers. Father is not in a good condition. Let's hurry back to Xiling Village.\"","Upon hearing Mo Jiuye's words, Wu Ge shifted his gaze to the two figures behind him.","By now, the sky was slightly brightening, and the night pearl was of no use. The eldest brother and the second brother had been tormented for many years, and their appearances had changed significantly. For a moment, Wu Ge couldn't recognize them at all.","However, judging from Jiuye's words, Wu Ge guessed that the people behind him were probably their father and brothers.","At this moment, the second brother had already brought their father to Mo Chongyuan's side.","\"Wu Ge, take us to the carriage quickly.\"","Although the second brother's figure had changed, his voice hadn't changed much.","Upon hearing this long-lost voice, tears welled up in Mo Chongyuan's eyes.","\"Is it the second brother?\"","\"It's me.\"","The eldest brother also walked over at this time. He bypassed Mo Jiuye and came to Mo Chongyuan's side, gently patting his shoulder. \"Wu Ge, I'm the eldest brother.\"","\"Eldest brother.\" Although Mo Chongyuan didn't know the condition of his father, he could tell from Jiuye's tone that the situation was urgent. Therefore, he couldn't care too much about his two elder brothers. He just greeted them and led the way towards the carriage.","When they reached the front of the carriage, Wu Ge asked first, \"Jiuye, is that despicable old thing taken care of?\"","Seeing that disgusting old man, Wu Ge felt extremely uncomfortable.","Now that Jiuye had successfully rescued their father and two elder brothers, he no longer had to look at Mr. Si Meng's annoying face all day long.","\"Wu Ge, wait a moment. I'm not sure if he can still be of use.\"","At this moment, Mo Jiuye didn't hold any illusions. He was too worried about his father's condition.","Instead of rushing back to Xiling Village, he wanted to try if Mr. Si Meng could remove the curse on his father.","As he spoke, Mo Jiuye took big strides forward, opened the carriage door, and pulled out Mr. Si Meng, who was like a dead dog.","Then he turned to the second brother and said, \"Second brother, you accompany Father onto the carriage first.\"","Second Brother knew that at this moment, Father needed a more comfortable environment. Compared to being carried outside by himself, Father would be more at ease inside the carriage.","So he nodded and carried Father into the carriage.","Fifth Brother followed suit and jumped in as well.","Although Mr. Si Meng was in the carriage every day, considering the extent to which the Mo brothers hated him, how could he possibly allow him to rest too comfortably?","Therefore, the interior of the carriage was bare and stiff. After Fifth Brother got on, he first tidied it up, laid the quilt that was placed aside, and then gently placed Father on top.","At the same time, he thoughtfully brought some water and tried to feed Father with it.","Outside the carriage, Mo Jiuye sprayed a mouthful of water all over Mr. Si Meng's face.","The old fox, who had felt drowsy, instantly felt much more awake.","Just as he opened his eyes, he saw Mo Jiuye's tall figure standing in front of him, which obviously surprised him.","\"You... are you a human or a ghost?\"","Mr. Si Meng thought that Mo Jiuye would undoubtedly die when he entered the Sixth Hill of Traps. Now that he saw him, the first thing he thought was that he might have also died. To confirm this idea, he asked this question.","Mo Jiuye snorted coldly, \"Based on the things you have done to my Mo family, do you think I would let you die so easily?\"","In fact, Mr. Si Meng asked that question just now because his mind had been drowsy for too long, causing him to be somewhat confused.","After listening to Mo Jiuye's words, he quickly reacted because the pain and weakness in his body were too real.","If he really died, he shouldn't have such feelings.","\"Mo... Mo Jiuye, just kill me!\"","No matter what, Mr. Si Meng couldn't figure it out. How could Mo Jiuye, who entered the Sixth Hill of Traps full of poison, come back alive?","Even if he was curious in his heart, he didn't dare to ask, because in doing so, he would admit that he deliberately sent the Mo brothers to the Sixth Hill of Traps with the intention of taking their lives.","At this moment, Mo Jiuye was concerned about Father's condition and had no interest in playing dumb riddles with the old fox.","\"I'm asking you, is it possible to remove the gu worms in my father's body?\"","After hearing Mo Jiuye's question, Mr. Si Meng's mind froze.","In his opinion, even if the Mo brothers managed to evade the poison traps he set and enter the interior, they wouldn't be able to come out alive, let alone find Mo Qing.","If they were lucky, they might be able to see Mo Family Eldest Son and Second Son, but even then, they would die at the hands of their own blood brothers.","But what did Mo Jiuye ask him?","Mo Jiuye asked him if he could cure Mo Qing of the gu worms?","In that case, did they successfully rescue Mo Qing?","A series of question marks appeared in Mr. Si Meng's mind.","In order to seek answers, he didn't immediately cut off the conversation.","\"The gu worms in your father's body were placed by my own hands, and I control him with my lifebound gu worm. I can naturally remove the worms in his body.\"","Regardless, he planned to stabilize Mo Jiuye first. If he could escape as a result, it would be even better. Even if he couldn't, he could still learn some information.","If Mr. Si Meng had responded with hesitation or shown reluctance to help his father break the curse, Mo Jiuye might have continued to negotiate with him.","However, since this cunning old fox agreed so readily, Mo Jiuye could fully understand his intentions.","The old fox was simply stalling for time or figuring out a way to retrieve his life-saving curse from him and then make a swift escape.","Given the circumstances, Mo Jiuye had no choice but to give up on this almost impossible opportunity to help his father break the curse.","\"If you think you can get your life-saving curse back through this, you can forget about it!\"","At this point, in Mo Jiuye's mind, there was no longer any need to keep Mr. Si Meng around.","Seeing that his intentions were exposed, Mr. Si Meng forced himself to laugh heartily despite his frail body.","\"Hahaha... Mo Jiuye, is it possible that Mo Qing is already at his limits?\""]},{"number":388,"title":"Chapter 388: He's so Cheap.","paragraphs":["Mr. Si Meng paused, noticing that Mo Jiuye was taking a long time to respond, which made him even more satisfied.","It was evident that he had hit the mark; Mo Qing must be on the verge of collapse.","\"Let me tell you, apart from me, no one in this world can remove the Gu worms in his body. Although I couldn't bring you Mo brothers to hell with me, it's worth it to die knowing Mo Qing will accompany me...\"","As he finished speaking, Mr. Si Meng closed his eyes and lay there motionless, preparing for his impending death.","Even with Mo Jiuye's normally steady temperament, it was hard for him to stay calm in this situation.","A prisoner who had persecuted their entire family was now displaying such an attitude at this moment.","\"Do you want to die?\" His voice was so cold that it sent shivers down one's spine.","Mr. Si Meng was no exception. He had been held captive by the Mo brothers for so long, and this was the first time he had heard Mo Jiuye's tone so icy.","He knew in his heart that his time was up.","Well, it was better than enduring the torment while alive. Although he hadn't achieved his wish, the thought of being able to reunite with his beloved soon made it acceptable.","Mo Jiuye did indeed harbor a murderous intent, but he couldn't let the old fox die too easily.","Suddenly, a gleaming dagger appeared in his hand, and then it went straight towards one of Mr. Si Meng's eyes.","With a swift motion, the dagger took out one of Mr. Si Meng's eyeballs.","\"Since you don't want to open your eyes, there's no use keeping this eye.\"","When the eyeball was forcefully removed, even though Mr. Si Meng had mentally prepared himself, he couldn't bear this sudden intense pain.","Where did he find the strength? The sound of his howling echoed through the air, causing birds perched on the trees to scatter.","Second Brother and Fifth Elder Brother, who had just fed their father some water, heard something amiss outside and came out of the carriage.","\"Ninth Brother, what's happening...\"","Before Fifth Elder Brother could finish his sentence, he saw the dagger in Ninth Brother's hand still dripping with blood, with what appeared to be an eyeball hanging from it.","Second Brother and Fifth Elder Brother immediately understood. Ninth Brother was planning to torture the old fox to death.","When it came to tormenting the biggest enemy of the family, Second Brother and Fifth Elder Brother were more than willing. Why should Ninth Brother be the only one to do such a thing?","Fifth Elder Brother also took out a gleaming dagger, and he approached Mr. Si Meng before Second Brother.","With the same swift motion as Mo Jiuye, he plucked out the other eye of the old fox.","Mr. Si Meng had momentarily shown signs of fainting, but when Mo Zhongyuan's blade descended, he regained consciousness once again.","Although his howls continued, they were far less intense than before.","Seeing this, Second Brother stepped forward and took the dagger from Mo Jiuye's hand. He casually scraped it against Mr. Si Meng's body, causing the eyeball hanging from the dagger to roll to the ground.","Then, he swiftly used the dagger to sever all ten of Mr. Si Meng's fingers.","\"This is what you owe our Mo family. Just a few fingers can never make up for it.\"","As he spoke, he began to cut the flesh and skin from Mr. Si Meng's body, one cut at a time.","This could be described as the cruelest punishment of the Great Shun Dynasty, a thousand cuts and ten thousand slashes!","Fifth Elder Brother, seeing the situation, didn't stay idle either. He watched as Mr. Si Meng couldn't bear the pain and even fell into a state of unconsciousness.","How does one suffer when being executed without any perception?","He firmly refused to allow such a situation to occur.","Therefore, Fifth Elder Brother fetched a jug of cold water. Once Mr. Si Meng was about to faint, he would promptly wake him up by splashing water on him.","Second Brother was also very skillful with the knife. He knew where it would cause bleeding, which would lead to a quicker death. Thus, he specifically aimed for places with thick flesh and less bleeding when making incisions.","In order not to delay their journey to Xiling Village, Second Brother deliberately increased his speed.","Although doing so would accelerate the death of Mr. Si Meng, an old cunning fox, there was no other way. After all, their father's life was more important.","Mo Jiuye saw the seamless cooperation between Second Brother and Fifth Elder Brother and realized that he couldn't intervene, so he simply stood aside and watched.","At the same time, he gritted his teeth and said, \"You assist the tyrant and persecute my entire Mo family. It's just desserts that you should die. Do you want to die?","But I won't let you die so easily. I want to make you suffer.\"","Speaking of suffering, Mo Jiuye suddenly remembered that his wife had brought him a packet of itch powder that he hadn't used yet.","He could let the old man experience the painful and itchy sensation once again.","So, he took out the remaining packet of itch powder and mercilessly sprinkled it all over Mr. Si Meng's body.","Mr. Si Meng instantly became both crying and laughing, a sight that brought a sense of relief.","To prevent the old fox from dying too easily, Second Brother and Fifth Elder Brother tormented him for a while before stopping.","They didn't know whether they should bring Mr. Si Meng along on their journey.","\"Ninth Brother, should we take him with us?\" Fifth Elder Brother asked.","Mo Jiuye shook his head. \"It's inconvenient to bring him on the road.\"","Fifth Elder Brother immediately understood Mo Jiuye's meaning and, after exchanging a glance with Second Brother, continued to torture Mr. Si Meng.","Perhaps due to Mr. Si Meng's weak physical condition, he was soon tortured to the point of breathing in more air than he could exhale.","Mo Jiuye knew that the old fox was about to breathe his last breath and quickly reminded them, \"Second Brother, Fifth Elder Brother, cut off his hands, feet, and head. Such a wicked person mustn't be left with a complete corpse.\"","Second Brother wiped the blood off his face and unwillingly said, \"Hmph! Letting him die so quickly is too kind to him.\"","After speaking, the two brothers continued their actions, dismembering the old fox's body and tossing the pieces into the bushes at the side of the road.","Eldest Brother had been staying inside the carriage, taking care of their father. However, he could still hear the commotion outside.","He knew that at this moment, the archenemy who had secretly persecuted the Mo family for years had finally died!","He gently held down his father's arm, which remained in the same position, and whispered, \"Father, can you hear it? The mastermind who persecuted our Mo family is now dead. You must hold on. Mother is still waiting for your return to reunite with her.\"","The brothers outside the carriage quickly tidied up and hurriedly left with the carriage.","This time, Fifth Elder Brother took the reins, while Mo Jiuye and Second Brother rode horses together. Eldest Brother stayed in the carriage to take care of their father.","When they arrived at the gate of Xijing City, the timing was just right.","Mo Jiuye watched as the city gates were opened by two soldiers, and the bustling crowd of people began to enter and exit.","Although there was still a checkpoint at the city gate, Mo Jiuye handed some silver to the gatekeeper soldiers again for convenience, and the carriage passed smoothly.","The weather today wasn't very good, rather gloomy.","Perhaps because the common people were worried about getting caught in the rain while traveling, there weren't many pedestrians on the official road.","The galloping horses covered a distance of about ten miles when a very familiar-looking carriage approached from the opposite direction.","Mo Jiuye took a closer look and found that the carriage and the interior crafted by his wife were almost identical.","Due to the distance, even with Mo Jiuye's sharp eyes, he couldn't clearly see the appearance of the driver, especially since the person was wearing a large straw hat that covered the entire face."]},{"number":389,"title":"Chapter 389: A Slow Poison","paragraphs":["To prove his guess in his heart, Mo Jiuye flew up and quickly came to the front of the carriage with his light work.","Seeing the person coming, Mo Chuhan hurriedly pulled the reins.","He was about to scold the person blocking the way, but he saw a familiar face.","\"Ninth younger brother.\"","\"Eighth older brother, why are you here?\"","Before Mo Jiuye could finish speaking, the carriage door was pushed open from the inside, revealing the face he had been missing day and night for a long time.","\"Husband, I received Xiao Bai's letter and was worried, so I asked eighth older brother to take me to the western border.\"","As she spoke, He Zhiran, with her huge belly, pretended to get out of the carriage.","Mo Jiuye quickly went up to support her.","\"Ranran, your body is weak. How can you travel long distances to get here?\"","Mo Jiuye's words sounded like he was blaming He Zhiran for not knowing how to take care of herself, but he was actually more distressed and ashamed in his heart.","He knew his wife best. She must have heard that they had captured Mr. Si Meng and was going to the western border to rescue her father and brother. She was worried about their physical condition, so she rushed over.","As for why it was the eighth older brother who accompanied her, Mo Jiuye didn't need to ask to know.","Among the nine Mo brothers, the eighth older brother had the most straightforward and gullible personality.","His wife must have taken advantage of the eighth brother's weakness and used some method to trick him into taking her to the western border.","No matter what, his wife seemed to be fine now, which made Mo Jiuye feel a little relieved.","However, his face still looked very ugly.","He Zhiran knew that her actions had worried Mo Jiuye.","\"Husband, after I received the news sent by Xiao Bai, I was worried there might be some things you couldn't resolve, so I fooled the eighth brother into taking me here.\"","She spoke gently, which sounded like a little wife who had done something wrong in Mo Jiuye's ears.","Mo Jiuye had been missing his wife. Seeing her like this now, even if he was angry, it would disappear.","He put his arm around He Zhiran's shoulder and looked down at her bulging belly.","\"Have the children been bothering you lately? Have you been resting well?\"","Seeing that Mo Jiuye was no longer angry, He Zhiran nodded vigorously.","\"They are very obedient. Don't worry!\"","As the couple spoke, the fifth older brother's carriage and the second older brother had arrived near them.","He Zhiran didn't recognize the second older brother, but she could tell from his eyebrows that he must be one of the Mo brothers.","It was obvious that this trip to the western border had yielded great results for Mo Jiuye and his brothers.","Her father was in very poor condition right now. Since his wife had come, even if Mo Jiuye still felt distressed for her, he could not give up his father's life.","He took He Zhiran's hand and briefly introduced her and the second older brother before telling her about his father's condition.","Upon hearing this, He Zhiran immediately went to the carriage where Mo Qing was riding.","\"Let me take a look at father first.\"","With that, she prepared to get on the carriage.","The oldest brother who was taking care of the father inside the carriage also heard the sound outside and opened the carriage door at this time.","Without asking, the woman with the big belly in front of him must be the ninth younger brother's wife.","\"The ninth younger brother said that the ninth younger sister-in-law's medical skills are brilliant. Please take a look at my father.\"","Mo Jiuye had just told her that the one taking care of their father in the carriage was the oldest brother.","\"Big brother, I'll go check on father now.\"","Seeing this, the big brother very tactfully jumped out of the carriage to make room inside.","Mo Jiuye carefully helped He Zhiran onto the carriage.","The first thing that caught her eye was an old man with white hair and skin and bones.","He Zhiran went up and gently pressed Mo Qing's arm that was still shaking back and forth.","Then she put her fingers on his pulse.","Seeing her frowning tighter and tighter, Mo Jiuye asked anxiously, \"Ranran, can father still be saved?\"","He Zhiran retracted her hand with a grave expression.","\"Removing the Gu from father is not a big problem, but you may not know yet that father has been poisoned with a chronic poison.","This kind of poison damages the body very slowly and is not easily noticeable. \"","Mo Jiuye gasped upon hearing this.","\"Ranran, are you saying father is poisoned?\"","He Zhiran knew Mo Jiuye was uncomfortable hearing this news, but she still had to explain it clearly.","\"Although father is poisoned with chronic poison, the toxins have now spread to the area around the heart. You just said the Gu worms in father's body are also near the heart. If my guess is correct, once the toxins come into contact with the Gu worms, father will die immediately.","His current frail state has a lot to do with the poisoning.\"","\"Ranran, is there any good way?\" Mo Jiuye's eyes turned bloodshot as he tightly grasped He Zhiran's arm.","At this question, He Zhiran couldn't answer yet. Father's condition was not very optimistic. Although she still couldn't determine how close the Gu worms and toxins were to each other, judging by father's current condition, he was not suitable for immediate surgery to remove the Gu.","But if the Gu worms were not removed, she worried that they would fuse with the toxins, which would be the same as taking his life directly.","\"Husband, I need to bring father into the space to examine him carefully before I can give you accurate results.\"","Mo Jiuye subconsciously looked outside the carriage.","\"I'll arrange it right away.\"","His wife's space was a huge secret. Entering it on this official road must be done without any flaws.","As he spoke, Mo Jiuye had already jumped off the carriage. He Zhiran didn't hear clearly what he said to several older brothers, and then the carriage slowly started moving.","The carriage swayed for about half an hour before finally stopping.","Mo Jiuye opened the carriage door and came up again.","Through the gap, He Zhiran could see that they had left the official road. Based on the surrounding environment, they should be in the woods near the official road.","\"Ranran, it's safe here. I've also informed my older brothers. They won't disturb you.\"","Mo Jiuye had arranged everything. There was no time to delay. He pulled Mo Qing and He Zhiran into the space together.","She gave Mo Qing a full physical examination.","The results were slightly better than she had imagined.","Through modern medical observation, the chronic poison Mo Qing had was in a state of sticking to the arterial wall.","The toxins did not move randomly with the blood circulation, but progressed in a very regular direction.","This direction was the heart. In other words, her initial judgment was completely correct.","Once the toxins came into contact with the Gu worms near the heart, Mo Qing would come to the end of his life.","He Zhiran had heard of this kind of chronic poison in her previous life. People had tried to use this toxin to treat cerebral hemorrhage patients, but multiple clinical trials failed and it was abandoned.","Since medical professionals in the previous life chose to use this toxin to treat patients, there must be a way to detoxify it.","If she remembered correctly, there was a special serum that could specifically restrain this toxin."]},{"number":390,"title":"Chapter 390: The Nine brothers and Sisters","paragraphs":["Moreover, fortunately, through the recent examination, the toxins and the gu worms in Mo Qing's body were still about 1 cm apart.","According to the spread rate of the toxins, the gu worms and toxins would not converge together for at least a month.","One month would be enough time for He Zhiran to help Mo Qing detoxify, then nourish his body before removing the gu.","Mo Jiuye looked at He Zhiran lost in thought there and asked, “Ranran, how is it?”","He Zhiran gently patted his arm, “The situation is slightly better than expected. I’m going to find medicine to help Father detoxify now.”","The biggest feature of this poison is that the poisoned person cannot have violent exercise, otherwise it would stimulate the spread rate of the toxins.","He Zhiran had just seen Mo Qing’s movements and his curled legs. She could confirm that Mo Qing had been repeating the same actions every day in that tomb, so there shouldn’t have been any violent movements, otherwise his legs would not have become like that.","At present, He Zhiran's plan was that Grandpa Mo was weak and could be nourished slowly, and the gu worms could be surgically removed at any time. The urgent task was to help him detoxify.","Mo Jiuye heard that his wife could detoxify his father and asked happily, “Then what about the gu worms?”","He Zhiran pointed to the location of the gu worms in Mo Qing's body.","\"It's close to the heart, and according to the examination, it can be determined that the hiding place of the gu worms is very deep. There will inevitably be heavy bleeding during the surgery to remove the gu.","With Father's current physical condition, massive bleeding would definitely endanger his life.\"","Mo Jiuye was dumbfounded when he heard He Zhiran say this.","\"Can Father's gu worms not be removed?\"","\"It's not that they can't be removed. First, Father’s body needs to be nourished to a state that can withstand surgery so that it can be done without any risks.\"","Hearing He Zhiran's explanation, Mo Jiuye finally felt a glimmer of hope.","\"Alright, I’ll leave it to Ranran then.\"","At this moment, anything else he said would seem pretentious, even though his heart ached for his pregnant wife’s hardship, it couldn't be helped.","There was no antidote stored in He Zhiran’s medical room space that could detoxify the poison in Mo Qing’s body, so she had to purchase it from Taobao Mall.","She didn’t know if modern times had cancelled the use of this toxin to treat diseases or something else, but there was no such antiserum for sale in Taobao Mall.","He Zhiran thought about it and opened Little Collector’s chat window.","[Hello, I need your help. Please reply as soon as you see this.]","Since asking Little Collector for help several times, the two had often exchanged messages.","Little Collector had also specially set He Zhiran’s messages to give special reminders.","Therefore, as soon as He Zhiran sent the message, she received a reply from the other party.","[I'm here, what do you need help with?]","He Zhiran: [I need an antiserum that is only available at the H City Biological Products Sales.]","Little Collector: [I happen to be on a business trip in H City. Send me the address and I'll go buy it for you now.]","He Zhiran quickly sent Little Collector the detailed address and full name of the antiserum.","[Please, I’m urgently waiting to save someone here.]","Little Collector: [Okay, I'll go buy it for you right away.]","He Zhiran didn’t know how long it would take Little Collector to go out and help buy the antiserum, her phone couldn't receive any messages when she left the space, so she had to wait here.","After all, they had entered the space from inside the carriage. If the brothers became anxious after waiting for a long time and opened the carriage to find no one inside, it would be impossible to explain clearly no matter what.","Therefore, He Zhiran decided to leave the space with Mo Jiuye and his father for the time being and wait in the carriage.","During this time, she would occasionally use her consciousness to enter the space to check if there were any incoming messages from Little Collector.","Not long after they left the space, someone knocked on the carriage door from outside.","\"Ninth Brother, Ninth Sister-in-Law, how is Father's condition?\" It was Eldest Brother's voice.","Although Mo Jiuye had explained very clearly not to let his brothers disturb Ninth Brother and Sister-in-Law while helping Father get treated, such torment was really unbearable.","Especially since they had been inside the carriage for so long without any sound coming out at all, the brothers were even more anxious like ants on a hot pan.","Mo Jiuye reluctantly opened the carriage door slightly to see his brothers all craning their necks towards the carriage.","\"Eldest Brother, Ranran has just finished examining Father and discovered he has been poisoned by a chronic toxin. The situation is not very good.","Ranran is now trying to formulate the antidote. Don't worry for now.\"","Hearing that Father had been poisoned by a chronic toxin was undoubtedly adding insult to injury for the Mo brothers.","Father's condition was already worrying enough, and now he was poisoned...","\"Sister-in-Law, can Father's poison be cured?\"","At this moment, Second Brother couldn't care less about Ninth Brother's urging that Ninth Sister-in-Law was formulating the antidote. He just wanted to know if Father could still survive.","He Zhiran could understand the feelings of the elder brothers. No one could remain calm if their loved one was in mortal danger, otherwise they might as well be an unfeeling machine.","\"I'm trying to formulate the antidote now. If it's successfully formulated, I should be able to cure Father's body.\"","He Zhiran didn't dare make her words too definite. After all, there was no such antiserum for sale in Taobao Mall. If Little Collector couldn't buy it either, wouldn't she have falsely raised everyone's hopes?","Although the brothers didn't understand medicine, they could still see from Father's feeble state that his condition was indeed not optimistic.","Although Sister-in-Law didn't say for certain that she could cure Father, they all understood clearly that she was also doing her best to find a way.","Eldest Brother took the lead and bowed deeply to He Zhiran.","\"Then we'll have to trouble Sister-in-Law.\"","Seeing this, the other brothers followed Eldest Brother's example and sincerely bowed to He Zhiran.","\"Thanks to Sister-in-Law...\"","At the same time, the Mo brothers all had the same guilt as Mo Jiuye.","Their Sister-in-Law was heavily pregnant, and she was carrying the hope of the Mo Family. Not only that, she looked like she would give birth soon.","Yet she had travelled so far to help even in such an awkward state. Ninth Brother was truly blessed to have married such a righteous wife. It was simply a blessing to the entire Mo Family.","Being thanked by so many heroic elder brothers, He Zhiran was also somewhat embarrassed.","She gestured with her hand.","\"We are all one family. Saving Father's life is what I should do. Elders need not be so polite.\"","\"Also, if I get disturbed while formulating the antidote, all my previous efforts would be wasted. So I'll have to trouble the elders to guard this place well.\"","He Zhiran might need to enter the space again soon, so she had to clarify the stakes in advance. Otherwise, if the anxious elder brothers came knocking again, things would get problematic.","Although she didn't say it outright, saying not to let anyone disturb her was something anyone could understand.","\"Sister-in-Law can rest assured. With us brothers here, not to mention people disturbing you, we guarantee that not even a fly will get through.\" Eighth Brother thumped his chest and promised.","At this moment, Eighth Brother still felt somewhat guilty. When he saw Ninth Brother earlier, he realized that he had been fooled by his Sister-in-Law to come to the Western Regions."]},{"number":391,"title":"Chapter 391: Slow Hand","paragraphs":["Fortunately, Ninth Younger Brother's constitution was sturdy, and he was not bothered by fetal qi despite the hardships of travel by boat and carriage, otherwise he would have become the Mo Family's greatest sinner.","Now that Ninth Younger Sister had spoken, forbidding anyone from approaching the carriage, Mo Chuhan would stand guard here diligently for three days and three nights without sleep.","Looking at the silly Eighth Elder Brother, He Zhiran tried hard to restrain her smile.","\"Alright, with elder brothers guarding me, I will definitely be able to calm my heart and research the antidote.\"","Mo Jiuye shut the carriage door again.","At the same time, He Zhiran's consciousness also entered the space to check things out.","It had been two hours now since she spoke with the Little Collector. He planned to look at his phone to see if there was any good news.","As soon as she opened her phone, she saw a message from the Little Collector.","[Fortunately I have not disappointed you. What you wanted has been obtained and can be put up for sale at any time.]","He Zhiran quickly replied: [I see it. Please hurry and put the serum up for sale.]","She received no more messages from the Little Collector, but there was a prompt of a new item in his shop.","He Zhiran quickly went to take a look, and sure enough, it was the serum she needed.","As usual, the asking price was one yuan.","He Zhiran knew that because this serum was so rare, the asking price had always been high.","If she remembered correctly, in her previous life she had gone to H City to help her teacher purchase a vial once, and the asking price at that time was 36,000 yuan for one vial.","36,000 yuan was no small sum even in modern times, and He Zhiran discovered that what the Little Collector was selling her for one yuan was not a single vial, but a whole box of ten vials.","That made the price 360,000 yuan.","In fact, He Zhiran did not know that this serum had already been discontinued in modern times, and the remaining stock had all increased wildly in price.","The ten vials of serum the Little Collector had purchased had cost a full 1 million yuan.","However, when it came to He Zhiran, he would never be stingy.","Although the two of them had a business relationship, they had also helped each other a great deal.","Therefore, he did not feel any heartache at all over the 1 million spent.","He Zhiran did not like taking advantage of others to begin with, and the Little Collector had helped her tremendously as well.","She suddenly remembered the few Night Illuminating Pearls that Mo Jiuye had left in the carriage.","Mo Jiuye had already explained their origins - they had all been secretly taken from Yuan Meng's Tomb.","Although these Night Illuminating Pearls were not as big as the ones they had taken from the Dashun Country Treasury, they were still considered the finest of the finest.","Thus, her consciousness quickly left the space, and she selected the largest one from her bundle to take into the space.","[Thank you for helping me so tremendously. Here is a surprise gift for you.]","After saying this, she smoothly photographed the Night Illuminating Pearl and listed it for sale in the shop.","Taobao appraised the Night Illuminating Pearl to be worth 10 million yuan, but He Zhiran only listed it for 5 million.","Then, she reminded the Little Collector: [This is a one of a kind good item, first come first served.]","After running her shop for a while, and given that all the antiques she sold were genuine, He Zhiran had earned herself a few loyal regular customers.","To prevent the Night Illuminating Pearl from being snapped up by others, she had to give a reminder.","Naturally, when the Little Collector heard there was a good item, he would not hesitate. Knowing He Zhiran was likely very busy on her end, he did not reply but directly purchased it.","Indeed, He Zhiran was very busy. After giving the reminder, she turned off her phone and entered the operating room with the serum the Little Collector had helped purchase.","At the moment, Mo Qing was lying on the operating table. Mo Jiuye had already cleaned his body once over.","However, the position Mo Qing was lying in made one's heart ache upon looking.","He was facing up with his back against the operating table, unable to straighten his legs which remained curled backwards.","He Zhiran had already explained earlier that Mo Qing's bent legs were caused by his bones and muscles deforming and atrophying after maintaining one position for too long.","This condition could slowly recover in the future through physical therapy.","It was only because his wife had a way to treat without endangering his father's life that Mo Jiuye readily accepted the situation.","Mo Qing's arms were still swaying back and forth. Mo Jiuye would periodically help hold them still.","Using this serum would be very painful if the person was conscious during the detoxification process.","Although Mo Qing had sealed away his past memories, he was not completely unconscious.","To spare him from suffering, He Zhiran chose to inject him with some anesthetics.","The anesthetics quickly took effect after entering Mo Qing's body, and he fell into deep sleep.","Next, He Zhiran mixed the serum with a certain amount of saline solution and administered it to Mo Qing intravenously.","After half an hour, all of the serum had been injected, and Mo Qing showed obvious reactions.","One of the arteries at his heart bulged slightly, only noticeable if examining carefully.","He Zhiran was staring at that spot in particular because she knew that symptoms would show during the detoxification process.","She watched as the slight bulge grew bigger, changing from barely noticeable at first to the size of a yellow bean-sized black bump.","As time passed, the little black bump also slowly enlarged, until it finally pierced the skin and became fingernail-sized, with black blood flowing out from the hole.","\"Husband, prepare cotton balls and iodine.\"","Having been He Zhiran's assistant many times now, Mo Jiuye was very adept. At her reminder, it only took a few seconds for him to get the items ready.","With her pregnant belly so large, it was very inconvenient for He Zhiran to bend down. She could only continue instructing Mo Jiuye.","\"Husband, after the black blood has finished flowing out, use the cotton balls and iodine to clean the surface until no more black blood can be seen.\"","The space taken up by this chronic poison in the body was small to begin with, and it was all concentrated in one area.","Therefore, the amount of black blood that flowed out of Mo Qing was not very much either.","This was also the only reason He Zhiran dared to attempt detoxification when he was so weak.","Otherwise, with Mo Qing's current physical condition, if he bled as much as Fifth Elder Brother had during his detox, it would certainly claim his life.","Before even considering whether the detox would succeed, just the excessive blood loss alone could kill him.","Mo Jiuye's technique was very proficient. He carefully helped his father clean away the blood stains from the wound.","Seeing him just about finished, He Zhiran had been thinking to apply some wound-healing medicine to speed up recovery before bandaging it up.","Suddenly, she heard Mo Jiuye cry out in surprise.","\"Ranran, Father, he...\"","From her understanding of Mo Jiuye's disposition, he was extremely steady. For him to make such a sound, something bad must have happened.","Unfortunately, from where she was standing, she could not see Mo Qing's wound clearly. Before Mo Jiuye could even finish speaking, she had swiftly changed positions.","She saw that at the small hole in Mo Qing's body opened up by the toxic blood, there was a fingernail-sized Gu worm going in and out.","That's right, in and out.","Not only was Mo Jiuye shocked by this scene, even He Zhiran was somewhat at a loss."]},{"number":392,"title":"Chapter 392: Father is Awake","paragraphs":["According to reason, once the offspring witch insect sensed danger, it would choose to continue hiding deeper into the human body. However, this offspring witch insect was different. It was like a startled little mouse, poking its head out tentatively, seemingly having lost its sense of direction. Although this phenomenon was unexplainable, on the surface it did not seem to be a bad thing.","\"Husband, prepare a bottle and a pair of forceps.\"","Mo Jiuye instantly understood her meaning. He put aside the cotton ball and iodine tincture in his hand and swiftly fetched the items.","He Zhiran's expression was somewhat solemn. With her hand speed, the chances of successfully clipping the offspring witch insect out from the blood cavity were small. She could only place her hopes on Mo Jiuye. After all, he was a martial artist, so his actions must be faster than hers.","\"Husband, you must be quick with this. Otherwise, I dare not guarantee where the offspring witch insect might burrow to.\"","The location was so close to the heart that if the offspring witch insect escaped towards that direction, the consequences would be unthinkable.","Even with such worries in mind, He Zhiran did not dare to speak it out. At such a critical juncture, she did not want to impose any psychological pressure on Mo Jiuye. If Mo Jiuye became too nervous and slipped up, it would not be worth it.","Mo Jiuye's thin lips were pursed tightly. He stared at the offspring witch insect that was still poking its head out tentatively for a few seconds before taking a deep breath, as if making up his mind about something important.","It was seen that he steadily grasped the forceps. Before He Zhiran could even clearly see his maneuver, the offspring witch insect had already been clipped by the forceps and swiftly placed into the bottle.","The offspring witch insect struggled desperately towards one direction inside the glass bottle.","The attentive He Zhiran noticed that no matter how Mo Jiuye rotated the glass bottle, the offspring witch insect always struggled towards Mo Jiuye's direction.","Seeing the state of the offspring witch insect, He Zhiran had a sudden realization.","\"Husband, isn't the mother witch insect controlling this offspring witch insect on your body?\"","Speaking of the mother witch insect, the witch insects collected from Si Meng were still being carried by Mo Jiuye.","Because the witch insect in his father's body had not been removed yet, Mo Jiuye was worried that if the witch insect controlling the offspring witch insect was not his father's life witch insect, then killing the wrong mother witch insect would be equivalent to indirectly killing his own father.","To be prudent, those mother witch insects had always been carefully kept by Mo Jiuye, not even daring to let them have any mishaps.","Now, seeing his father's situation, being cautious was the right approach.","This offspring witch insect yearned for its mother witch insect so eagerly. If anything unexpected happened to the mother witch insect, this offspring witch insect would likely commit suicide inside his father's body.","At the same time, Mo Jiuye also had another doubt in mind.","That was, he had taken six bottles containing mother witch insects from Si Meng, and he could confirm that those bottles all contained a living mother witch insect.","Now, the witch insects in his father and eldest and second brothers had all been removed. He could also confirm which three mother witch insects were controlling them.","Normally speaking, the offspring witch insects born by the marionette witch insect mother witch insects would live together with the mother witch insects before finding a host.","That meant one porcelain bottle could contain one mother witch insect and one offspring witch insect.","As for the remaining three mother witch insects, Mo Jiuye could confirm that each bottle only contained one mother witch insect.","Where Si Meng had implanted the offspring witch insects was unknown.","Otherwise, after successfully removing the witch insects from his father and brothers, Mo Jiuye could have burned these vile insects to death in one go.","Now, thinking that those three mother witch insects might still be controlling someone else, he temporarily abandoned that idea for now.","However, the three mother witch insects controlling his father and eldest and second brothers could not be kept.","While Mo Jiuye was thinking about these matters, he had already helped his father clean the wound again.","Although the wound was deep, it was not very big and did not require suturing at all. Simply applying medicine and bandaging it would suffice.","After taking care of these, Mo Jiuye directly went outside the medical room without He Zhiran saying anything, and burned those useless witch insects to death.","It would be best for such harmful creatures to be completely erased from this world.","He Zhiran's original plan was to first help Mo Qing detoxify, then remove the witch insect after his body recovered a bit.","She did not expect this offspring witch insect to be so impatient to be reborn that it actually emerged by itself.","After simply examining Mo Qing, He Zhiran discovered that this was a good thing.","Although Mo Qing's body did not show any signs of improvement, it also did not worsen.","It could be said that the offspring witch insect had helped tremendously by sparing Mo Qing the pain of undergoing a second surgery to remove the witch insect.","Now, Mo Qing's vital signs were still normal. He was only severely depleted physically, but his head was not affected much.","Estimated that the anesthetic would wear off in another two hours, He Zhiran took this time to transfuse him with some plasma and nutritional fluids.","Soon, it was around the estimated time for Mo Qing to wake up. He Zhiran brought them to leave the space together.","Not long after Mo Qing was settled in the carriage, he awoke.","First of all, the biggest change with Mo Qing now was that his arms no longer swung back and forth mimicking offering paper money.","Mo Jiuye hurriedly moved closer.","\"Father.\"","Mo Qing's eyelids were a little heavy. He only opened a slit.","The lighting in the carriage was not very good. Also, he had not seen Mo Jiuye for many years.","His impression of Mo Jiuye still remained at his youth. Therefore, seeing this magnified, handsome face before him, Mo Qing was stunned for a moment.","Mo Jiuye could tell his father's state at a glance and knew he might not recognize him.","\"Father, I'm Jiuye. Look closely at me.\"","\"You say you are Jiuye?\" Mo Qing's voice was very soft and somewhat hoarse.","However, both Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran heard his words clearly.","Tears were already welling up in Mo Jiuye's eyes. He nodded with difficulty.","\"Father, I am Jiuye. We haven't seen each other for eight years already.\"","Thinking back eight years ago, Mo Jiuye was still a thirteen-year-old little boy. It was understandable that Mo Qing did not recognize him.","The brothers outside the carriage, in order to let the ninth brother and sister concoct the antidote in peace, stayed close by the carriage without disturbing them.","Therefore, they could completely hear the conversation between Mo Jiuye and his father.","Eldest brother could not wait to open the carriage door.","\"Ninth brother, has Father woken up?\"","Seeing his father's still somewhat unbelieving expression, Mo Jiuye saw his eldest brother as if seeing a savior.","\"Eldest brother, Father is awake. He doesn't recognize me. Please come explain to him that I'm Jiuye.\"","At this moment, eldest brother no longer had the mind to listen to the rest of Mo Jiuye's words. The only words in his mind were \"Father is awake\". Everything else had been automatically ignored by him.","\"Father, you're awake?\"","As for Mo Junrui, Mo Qing could still recognize him. Even though they had not seen each other for many years as father and son, Mo Junrui had already reached adulthood back then. So even if there were any changes to his appearance, it could not be as obvious as Mo Jiuye's change from a youth to an adult.","\"Jun...Junrui...\"","Speaking was still difficult for Mo Qing. The person before his eyes looked identical to his eldest son, but was much more haggard compared to his impressions."]},{"number":393,"title":"Chapter 393: The Daughter-in-law Has Seen her Father","paragraphs":["Mo Qing was somewhat confused about the situation at hand.","Just as he was puzzled, the other brothers outside the carriage also crowded in.","To say they crowded in was an understatement; the already small carriage had become packed to the point where no wind could pass through.","Mo Jiuye could understand his elder brothers' concern for their father, not wanting to drive anyone away.","But he worried that his wife would be squeezed, so he could only helplessly speak up.","\"Elder brothers, you keep Father company. I'll take Ranran out for some fresh air.\"","After speaking, he also gave a signal to his eldest brother, indicating that he should make it clear to Father that he was Mo Jiuye.","At this moment, how could the eldest brother spare any thought for the youngest brother's hint? He quickly shifted his gaze to Father, carefully observing his condition.","Mo Jiuye took Ranran and got off the carriage, leaving a large empty space inside.","The brothers had already surrounded Mo Qing, clamoring for Father.","Mo Qing was still bewildered. How could that young man claim to be Jiuye? His youngest son was only 13 years old, how could he look like that?","And his eldest son, why did he appear much older and haggard?","Just as he was puzzled, Mo Jiacheng also called out to Father.","Mo Qing narrowed his eyes and looked at him. The feeling he got from his second son was the same as his eldest son, old and haggard.","Not only that, they were all wearing coarse linen clothes, completely different from the brocade and jade he imagined.","Looking at Mo Chongyuan and Mo Chuhan who had come closer, they were also wearing coarse linen clothes.","Mo Chongyuan was slightly better off. The last time he saw Father, he was already twenty years old, so he didn't have much change in appearance, except for looking more mature.","But Mo Chuhan was different. He was only two years older than Mo Jiuye and was only fifteen when he last saw Father.","In Mo Qing's eyes, it was still unbelievable.","The brothers kept calling out to Father. Although Mo Qing still had doubts in his heart, seeing tears swirling in their eyes, he could only put his thoughts aside.","He pointed at Mo Chuhan and asked Mo Junrui, \"Junrui, he says he is Chuhan. What's going on?","And just now, there was a young man who claimed to be your ninth brother. He does bear some resemblance to you, but who is he?\"","Upon hearing Father's question, Mo Junrui finally remembered what the ninth brother had said.","\"Father, that really was Jiuye just now. You've been away from home for eight years, and at that time, the ninth brother was still young. It's understandable that you couldn't recognize him.\"","Mo Chuhan, seeing that his eldest brother was only explaining for the ninth brother, quickly stepped forward.","\"Eldest brother, please tell Father that I really am Chuhan.\"","The eldest brother explained as told, \"Father, eight years ago, you were ambushed on the battlefield by a person from the Southern Frontier named Mr. Si Meng. You were drugged and captured by the people from the Southern Frontier.","They even made it seem like you had died in battle and hung your head high on the city wall.","As a result, we all thought you were gone. Later on, one by one, we brothers took over your command.","Except for the ninth brother, all of us fell victim to Mr. Si Meng's schemes and were under his control for many years.","Fortunately, our younger brother Mo Jiuye and his sister Mo Jiumei were wise and persevered through countless hardships to rescue us.","In other words, it has been eight years since our last meeting. Back then, Chuhan and Jiuye were still young, but now they are both married and adults.\"","Mo Junrui gave a simple explanation to his father, without going into too much detail.","His main purpose was to make his father realize a fact: that they, father and son, haven't seen each other for a full eight years.","Although Mo Qing was physically weak, his mind was unaffected.","Although what Mo Junrui said was somewhat bewildering, he was trying hard to accept this reality.","However, there were still many things he couldn't comprehend.","\"Who is this Mr. Si Meng you mentioned? Why does he want to persecute our Mo family? And why do you brothers dress like this now?\"","Mo Qing asked a series of questions in a clear and organized manner.","Answering these questions would take a long time.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran outside the carriage were getting anxious.","After all, Mo Qing had just regained consciousness, and He Zhiran hadn't had a chance to examine him yet.","If they were to talk about all these things, it would probably take until nightfall.","In that case, aside from whether they could help their father with a timely examination, his body would probably not be able to handle it either.","Taking these factors into consideration, Mo Jiuye said to the people inside the carriage:","\"Brothers, Father has just woken up. Let Ruirui help him with an examination first.\"","Hearing that they needed to examine their father's body, which was more important than anything else, the brothers reluctantly left, even though they had a thousand words they wanted to say to their father.","Seeing each of his brothers reluctantly jumping off the carriage, Mo Jiuye carefully helped He Zhiran up.","The shocking things they had just heard forced Mo Qing's mind to work hard, and as a result, he looked a little more spirited than when he first woke up.","But his legs remained curled up, which made people feel sorry for him.","Mo Jiuye called out \"Father\" again and pushed He Zhiran in front of him.","\"Father, this is He Zhiran, the daughter of the He family. I have already married her, do you remember? Our marriage was personally arranged by you.\"","Even though He Zhiran was heavy with child, she didn't forget the proper etiquette when meeting an elder for the first time.","The carriage roof was not high to begin with, and she had been sitting on a nearby seat with bent knees. At this moment, she was already kneeling in front of Mo Qing.","\"Father-in-law, I greet you.\"","While Mo Jiuye was introducing He Zhiran, Mo Qing had been staring at the two of them.","She also noticed that He Zhiran was now pregnant and made an effort to raise her hand.","\"Please rise, Daughter-in-law. I heard what your eldest brother said just now. You have done a lot for the Mo family, and I represent the whole family in expressing our gratitude.\"","Upon hearing his father say \"please rise,\" Mo Jiuye quickly assisted He Zhiran back to her original position.","He Zhiran humbly replied, \"Father-in-law, there's no need to be polite. It is my duty to do all this.\"","She and Mo Jiuye had kicked off their older brothers from the carriage to help Mo Qing with his physical examination, so He Zhiran had no intention of engaging in too much conversation with Mo Qing for the time being.","\"Father, I have some medical skills. Since you just woke up, let me examine your condition first.\"","As she spoke, she already placed her hand on Mo Qing's pulse.","This pulse examination didn't take much time because He Zhiran just wanted to understand the situation after their adoptive father woke up.","She knew that Mo Jiuye and the older brothers outside the carriage were anxious to know the diagnosis results, so she intentionally raised her voice and said:","\"Father's body is currently a bit weak, but there is no life-threatening danger. As long as he takes good care of himself in the future, he will definitely recover completely.\"","He Zhiran wasn't exaggerating. Perhaps it was because Mo Qing had been practicing martial arts for many years, his physical constitution was already much better than an ordinary person's."]},{"number":394,"title":"Chapter 394: Thank you for saving my father's life.","paragraphs":["Although he had suffered inhuman treatment for so many years, it was impossible that his organs had not been damaged, but there was no fatal problem.","At first she was worried that [Mo Qing]'s illness could not be cured because the Gu worm was in a special position. He was worried that [Mo Qing] was too weak to wait until the day the Gu worm was removed.","Just now after giving him plasma and nutrition fluid in the space, it seemed to be absorbed very well, much better than when he first entered the space for examination.","Only [He Zhiran] would dare to make such a diagnosis. If [Mo Qing]'s condition was handed over to the doctors of this era, I'm afraid it would be completely hopeless.","Luckily, the little collector helped to get the antidote to [Mo Qing]'s chronic poison in time.","As for [Mo Qing]'s curled legs, [He Zhiran] did not mention it in front of him.","Unlike his body, as long as he took medicine and adjusted his diet, it would not be difficult to recover.","It would take a lot more time for his legs to truly recover to their original mobility.","She was worried that telling him would affect her father's mood, which would be detrimental to his recovery.","When they returned home, she could help her father recover through acupuncture and physiotherapy. In short, [He Zhiran] was absolutely confident.","After hearing that their father was out of mortal danger, the several elder brothers gathered around again.","Only this time they knew their limits and realized their younger sister was in the carriage, so they just crowded around the carriage door and peered inside.","\"Younger sister, thank you for saving our father's life.\"","As the eldest son of the family, [Mo Junrui] felt it necessary to make clear where the brothers stood, especially since their pregnant younger sister had traveled long distances to help.","If he didn't say thank you, he would feel sorry for all the hardships his younger sister had endured on the boat and carriage.","In the Mo family, the eldest brother had always been the leader of the brothers since childhood. Seeing what the eldest brother did, the other brothers also felt [He Zhiran]'s difficulties and thanked her along with the eldest brother.","[He Zhiran] said this to let everyone understand [Mo Qing]'s physical condition, not to show off.","\"Brothers, you are too polite. Father is relatively stable now. As long as you take good care of him in the future, there will be no problem,\" she said.","If she had to say again that the family did not need to be polite, it would seem pretentious.","She knew the elder brothers were eager to see their father, so she beckoned [Mo Jiuye] to help her down from the carriage and left the space for the father and sons.","And [He Zhiran] also knew clearly that [Mo Jiuye] wanted to stay by his father's side at the moment. After she got off the carriage safely, she sent [Mo Jiuye] back to the carriage.","[Mo Qing] had received too much information in his mind just now, and now he had countless questions to ask.","\"Tell me what happened in the last eight years.\"","When it came to what had happened in the last eight years, among the brothers, [Mo Jiuye] was the clearest, after all, the other brothers had lost consciousness for a period of time during this period.","What they knew was also from listening to [Mo Jiuye].","Therefore, when his father asked, everyone's eyes fell on [Mo Jiuye], waiting for him to tell the story.","[Mo Jiuye] had always thought [Mo Qing] was very powerful, so when he talked about what the Mo family had experienced over the years, he didn't have too many worries.","\"Ever since father was captured by the southerners and your head was hung on the city tower, the elder brothers have gradually taken over your duties...","Finally last year, Emperor Shunwu could no longer restrain himself and took action against our Mo family, first tricking me into the imperial palace and giving me 50 heavy strokes, and the next day issuing an edict to raid and exile my whole Mo family...\"","Anyway it was safe now. The brothers were in no hurry to travel, so [Mo Jiuye] told his father in detail what the Mo family had experienced over the years.","After listening to [Mo Jiuye]'s account, [Mo Qing] was so angry that the veins on his forehead bulged.","At the same time, in his eyes one could also see a trace of disappointment.","After a long silence, he finally said, \"Such an ignorant emperor does not deserve to occupy the throne! But over the years, it has been hard on you brothers, and your mother must have shed no small amount of tears.\"","As the head of a family, no matter how angry [Mo Qing] was inwardly, he could not lose his temper like a junior.","So it took him a long time to speak.","Especially when he thought of his old wife at home, who had not had a peaceful day since marrying him, worrying about him when she was young, and suffering the loss of her husband and sons when she was old.","When he thought of all this, [Mo Qing] felt extremely guilty.","Now he was fortunate to be rescued by his ninth son and daughter-in-law, and the Mo family had now become commoners.","He was lucky to be alive to return, and in the future he would not have to consider national affairs, he just wanted to accompany his old wife and live out their remaining years in peace.","After his daughter-in-law gave birth, he would properly enjoy doting on his grandchild.","Inside the carriage, the father and sons talked about what the Mo family had experienced over the years. [He Zhiran] was also not idle outside the carriage.","Considering [Mo Qing]'s physical condition, she lit a fire outside.","Fortunately, when she went out, she had the foresight to put some pots and food in the carriage.","However, this food would not help [Mo Qing]'s recovery. She could only secretly take things from her space.","She was also not worried about the food being exposed to sunlight. Anyway, [Mo Chuhan] was insensitive. At first when she put food in the carriage, [Mo Chuhan] knew about it.","So [Mo Chuhan] was the best witness.","She had heard from [Mo Jiuye] that [Mo Qing] had lived off the prey on the small hill for so many years.","The main role of the eldest and second elder brothers there was to provide for the three of them.","Of course, in such deep mountains, it could only be hunting.","That meant [Mo Qing] had mainly eaten meat, raw or cooked, for so many years.","His weak physique was related to the chronic poison in his body, and later [Si Meng] was unable to control the Gu worm to restrict [Mo Qing], resulting in him not eating for a long period of time.","Based on this understanding, [He Zhiran] felt that [Mo Qing]'s body was not so deficient that it could not be nourished.","Especially since he had lived on meat for many years, suddenly switching to vegetarianism would probably be too much for his digestive system to take.","Considering all this, [He Zhiran] decided to make a meat-based nourishing soup for him to drink.","After searching in her space for a while, she finally decided to buy a pigeon to make soup, plus some nourishing and flavourful herbs.","The pigeon had been processed and could be cut up immediately to cook.","[He Zhiran] knew that the Mo brothers all wanted to stay by their father's side, so she pretended to call out to [Mo Jiuye].","\"Husband, a pigeon just happened to fall here. It can be used to nourish father.\"","There was already a tacit understanding between her and [Mo Jiuye]. Hearing her say this, he knew what was going on.","\"Brothers, you keep father company first. I'll go out and take a look.\"","Sure enough, as [He Zhiran] had anticipated, with the ninth brother leaving, not one of the elder brothers came to help.","Only this way could the pigeon soup appear openly."]},{"number":395,"title":"Chapter 395: Look who's behind you.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran got off the carriage and saw that He Zhiran was holding a pigeon that had already been processed.","He smiled as he made some audible motions.","\"Okay, caught it, Zhiran you wait, I'll go process it now.\"","With this shout, no one in the carriage doubted.","He Zhiran took the initiative to prepare nutritious pigeon soup for her father, while Mo Jiuye was responsible for everyone else's meals.","After all, they were in the wild, it was good to eat enough, and there was no need to spend much effort on it.","When the husband and wife prepared the meals, it was dusk.","After eating, the sky was almost dark, and their identities were also relatively sensitive, so it was not suitable to stay in the city, so they decided to rest here for one night and set off early the next morning.","Considering that they had left the Western Territory and stayed here to help Mo Qing treat for almost a day,","it was estimated that the cartilage components in the third brother and the others had been eliminated by now, and they should have left Xiaoyueshan and hit the road.","In order to prevent them from missing each other on the road, the fifth brother volunteered to stand on the official road. Once the third brother and the others arrived, everyone would get together and set off immediately.","It was also fortunate for those who rested in the woods. He Zhiran brought some tents they used during their exile when she went out. In this way, everyone did not have to sleep outdoors.","The eldest brother was responsible for taking care of his father, and slept in the carriage with him.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye slept in the carriage she took from Xiling Village.","The second and eighth brothers rested in the tent, and would take turns keeping watch at night to prevent danger.","It was a peaceful night, and as expected, as soon as the cartilage symptoms of the third brother and others improved slightly, they began to go down the mountain, whipping their horses all the way here.","When everyone got together, they simply ate some breakfast and then continued on their way to Xiling Village.","Considering He Zhiran and Mo Qing's health, the carriage traveled very smoothly all the way, so the speed was much slower.","It took a full five days for the party to finally arrive at Xiling Village.","Now the new house of the Mo family has been completely completed, and the furniture has been in place.","Just waiting for Mo Jiuye and his brothers to come back and choose an auspicious day to move in.","Therefore, the Mo family still lived in the rented yard at the moment.","The two carriages slowly drove into Xiling Village. The villagers saw that the Mo family members were driving the carriages. They were used to it.","In their hearts, the Mo family was wealthy, even if they were exiled, they were the existence of rich people.","No one was curious to inquire. All the villagers they met along the way greeted them enthusiastically.","This allowed the eldest brother and second brother who came to Xiling Village for the first time to feel a different feeling.","When they were in the capital before, the Guogong Mansion could be said to be unattainable.","Whoever met them would flatter them for a while. Although it was also a greeting, compared with the simplicity of these villagers, it was completely different.","Unconsciously, the eldest brother and the second brother seemed to have liked it here.","Mo Chuhan drove the carriage at the front and returned to the yard his family rented.","As soon as the carriage arrived at the gate, the seventh brother heard the sound and ran out.","At that time, in the family letter sent by Mo Jiuye, everyone knew the contents clearly, knowing that they had captured Mr. Simeng alive in the capital, and were rushing to the Western Territory.","Although the family members were worried about their trip to the Western Territory, except for the seventh and eighth brothers, no one else came to help. After all, they didn't have much ability. Going there would only add chaos. They could only pray for them to go smoothly.","However, the idea of the seventh and eighth brothers wanting to go to the Western Territories to help was quickly severely stopped by Old Lady Mo.","The two brothers listened to their mother's words. Although they were unwilling, no one dared to act without authorization.","He Zhiran did not dare to reveal the slightest idea of wanting to go to the Western Territory to help. If so, Old Lady Mo would send someone to watch her all day long.","In desperation, He Zhiran could only operate in private, dragging the most simple-minded eighth brother down, and the two made plans to sneak out of the house at night.","The Mo family discovered that He Zhiran and Mo Chuhan were missing when they got up early the next day.","It was He Zhiran who left a note at Old Lady Mo's door.","The content of the note was that she was worried that her father-in-law and two elder brothers were in danger of life in the Western Territory. She understood medicine. Once Mo Jiuye successfully rescued them, she could also help treat them.","As for Mo Chuhan, even though He Zhiran did not write it clearly in the note, Old Lady Mo knew what was going on with her understanding of her son.","It was nothing more than that the silly boy wanted to go to the Western Territories to help eagerly, and was finally persuaded by his sister-in-law's reason, and the two left quietly.","Old Lady Mo was very angry about this. Not for anything else, her daughter-in-law was six months pregnant, and the due date was getting closer and closer. If something went wrong in the Western Territory, as a mother-in-law, she might feel guilty for a lifetime.","However, she also knew her daughter-in-law's temper. No one could stop what she wanted to do.","Therefore, after she and Mo Chuhan left, Old Lady Mo did not send anyone to chase them back. She could only pray for their safety.","Since He Zhiran and Mo Chuhan left home, the whole family was on tenterhooks, afraid that something might happen to He Zhiran.","Seeing Mo Chuhan, the seventh brother came up and punched him hard.","\"Old Eight, you really are getting bolder. Where's the ninth younger sister?\"","Mo Chuhan was beaten, but he didn't dare to get angry. After all, it was too reckless for him to take the ninth younger sister away from home. Fortunately, the ninth younger sister was safe and sound all the way, otherwise he would become a sinner of the Mo family.","He covered his slightly painful abdomen.","\"Seventh brother, I know I'm wrong, but now is not the time to talk about my mistakes. Look who's behind.\"","Hearing him say that, the seventh brother then shifted his attention to the back of the carriage.","At this moment, the eldest brother and the second brother who were riding on horses had come to the front. The two almost dismounted at the same time.","\"Seventh younger brother, don't blame the eighth brother. This time, fortunately, he took the ninth younger sister to the Western Territory, otherwise father would be in danger.\" Seeing that the eighth brother was beaten, the eldest brother helped explain for him reluctantly.","This voice was so familiar to Mo Yuance, and it also had an unreal feeling.","However, he reacted soon, because he heard the familiar voice, and the appearance of the speaker was also extremely familiar.","\"Eldest brother, is it really you?\"","Before the eldest brother could answer, the second brother had already walked up.","He made a casual gesture of smashing his shoulder with his fist.","\"You kid, how can you only see your eldest brother and not see your second brother?\"","\"Second brother.\" Mo Yuance saw his brothers and was so excited that his tone was trembling.","At this time, the third brother also walked over.","\"Okay, our Mo family is finally reunited. Don't block the door anymore. Let's settle father first.\"","When he heard the word father, Mo Yuance was even more excited.","\"Third brother, do you mean father came back with you too?\""]},{"number":396,"title":"Chapter 396: As long as you're both Alive.","paragraphs":["Third Older Brother said somewhat amusedly, “What are you thinking about? Isn’t the reason we brothers went out to search for Father and Eldest and Second Brothers?” Father will naturally come back with us.”","Seeing Mo Yuance still dazed where he stood, Third Older Brother continued, “What are you still dazed for? Go call the family out!”","Reminded by Third Older Brother, Mo Yuance reacted. He didn’t care to ask about his father’s circumstances but turned and ran towards Old Lady Mo’s room, yelling, “Mother, Father and Eldest and Second Brother are back!”","With that yell, not only Old Lady Mo in the room heard clearly, even the few sisters-in-law tending the vegetable garden in the backyard heard it loud and clear.","In the blink of an eye, the door to Old Lady Mo's room was pushed open from inside.","This was also the first time they had seen the old woman move as quick as flying.","\"Yuance, what did you say? Your father and eldest and second brothers are back?\"","Mo Yuance quickly went forward to support her, pointing in the direction of the carriage parked in the yard, \"Mother, look, they are over there!\"","Old Lady Mo's eyes were already wet at this moment, and her vision had become blurred.","However, she could still make out that there were many tall figures standing around the carriage.","She staggered over to the carriage, and two people immediately knelt down before her.","\"Mother, your son has been unfilial and made you worry,\" Eldest and Second Brother said in unison, kowtowing heavily three times to Old Lady Mo.","These were the last two sons the Mo family had found. Old Lady Mo had thought for a time that they would never appear alive again. Now, seeing them alive and well before her, the old woman eventually couldn't hold back her tears.","At the same time, the few sisters-in-law who were working in the backyard also rushed back.","Among them were Eldest Sister-in-law and Second Sister-in-law.","Usually talkative Second Sister-in-law was stunned speechless for the moment, somewhat unbelieving that the man before her was the husband she hadn't seen for many years.","Eldest Sister-in-law just stood in place, covering her face as she wept bitterly.","The other few sisters-in-law were better, although their husbands were all away from home. They were all clear that they were not widows.","Now that Eldest and Second Brother had just returned home, everyone’s attention naturally fell on the two brothers.","At this time, Old Lady Mo had already been supported forward by her seventh son, one hand holding Mo Junrui and the other Mo Jiacheng.","She choked out with difficulty, \"As long as you can come back, as long as you can come back.”","Mo Junrui and Mo Jiacheng took the chance to stand up and direct their gazes at the wives they hadn't seen for years.","When Second Sister-in-law’s gaze met her husband’s, she immediately burst into loud sobs.","At the same time, she staggered over.","\"Husband... sob sob sob... You're finally back alive. Do you know how envious I was of my younger sisters-in-law when I saw they were no longer widows...sob sob sob...\"","Mo Junrui was her son, and also Second Sister-in-law’s husband.","Of course the husband and wife would have a lot to say upon reuniting.","Taking the chance, Old Lady Mo gently patted her two sons’ arms, hinting for them to first go see their wives they hadn’t seen in years.","Mo Jiacheng felt guilty towards his mother for making her endure years of grief over his supposed death. He felt even more guilty towards his wife for making her a widow at a young age.","Considering Father was still in the carriage, Mo Jiacheng decided to first go see his wife while Mother could take the chance to visit Father.","Having received Mother’s hint, Mo Jiacheng strode towards his wife.","Second Sister-in-law threw herself into his arms, crying even louder.","Eldest Sister-in-law was much more composed than Second Sister-in-law. She would always remind herself to set a good example for the family’s daughters-in-law. Therefore, her actions were not as exaggerated as Second Sister-in-law’s. She just strongly suppressed the urge to throw herself into her husband’s arms and slowly walked up to Mo Junrui.","\"Husband...\"","After calling him, Eldest Sister-in-law was already too choked up to speak.","On the contrary, seeing his wife, who was much more haggard than before, Mo Junrui couldn't hold back and stepped forward, sweeping her into his arms.","\"Biting, I'm sorry. I've made you heartbroken all these years.\"","Hearing her husband call her by her maiden name, Eldest Sister-in-law was startled for a moment.","She hadn't heard this term of endearment since news came of her husband's death.","Eldest Sister-in-law completely lost control of her emotions. She collapsed in her husband's arms, wailing loudly, and her fists continuously pounded his chest. It was as if she wanted to vent all the resentment pent up in her heart over the years.","As Eldest and Second Brother tearfully embraced their wives, the other women quietly wept. Mo Hanyue kept by Old Lady Mo's side, wiping away tears while caring for Mother.","Seeing this, the other elder brothers also went to their wives to comfort them.","Mo Jiuye supported He Zhiran as they walked over to Old Lady Mo.","Seeing He Zhiran's huge belly, Old Lady Mo was about to scold them.","But before she could speak, Mo Jiuye quickly said, \"Mother, Father is weak and still in the carriage.\"","Old Lady Mo instantly swallowed back what she was going to say.","\"Hanyue, quickly support your mother to see your father.\"","Mo Jiuye went ahead to the carriage.","\"Mother, I'll carry Father into the room first. You can slowly talk.\"","Old Lady Mo didn't respond to her son's words. Instead, she directly opened the carriage door.","After a few days of recuperation, Mo Qing could now sit for a while.","At this time, he was leaning against the carriage, listening to the sounds of family reunion outside, and his old wife's voice that had become much older than before. For a moment, he didn't know how to face them.","It was all because of his incompetence that such a good family had declined to this state.","The carriage door suddenly opened, sunlight bursting in. Mo Qing squinted slightly.","However, Old Lady Mo and Mo Jiuye could see at a glance that Mo Qing's face was already streaked with tears.","Seeing the emaciated old man in the carriage, Old Lady Mo was startled for a moment.","But she soon recognized him from his brow and eyes.","\"Old Master, is it you?\"","Still, Old Lady Mo couldn't quite believe it. She felt it was real only if the other party acknowledged it.","\"Mistress, I've made you suffer all these years. I'm sorry,\" Mo Qing said with difficulty.","Hearing the familiar yet somewhat aged voice, Old Lady Mo finally believed this was all real.","Now not only were her nine sons alive and well, even her husband, who had been proclaimed dead for so many years, was alive and standing before her.","Old Lady Mo suddenly felt she possessed everything all at once, as if she had returned to the time when the children were young and the family was whole.","\"I'm not suffering... not suffering... As long as you're all alive, that's good...\"","As she spoke, Old Lady Mo could no longer continue. All that could be heard was her sobbing."]},{"number":397,"title":"Chapter 397: Not a few","paragraphs":["Eight years ago, when Mo Hanyue was only eight years old, her only impression of her father was that he was tall and dignified.","Seeing her father again now, she didn't recognize him at all.","However, the kinship from blood made her feel a strange sense of intimacy when she saw the old man in front of her.","The little girl was shy, and seeing Old Lady Mo crying uncontrollably, she held Old Lady Mo's hand as she stood there weeping.","Standing beside them, Mo Jiuye couldn't help shedding tears as he watched the scene.","In order to alleviate the atmosphere, he didn't hurry to carry his father to the room. Instead, he pushed Mo Hanyue forward a little.","He remembered that when Father was at home, what he liked best was Mo Hanyue, his only daughter. One could say he doted on her and pampered her.","Under the present circumstances, letting his sister recognize their father should be the best way to alleviate their grief.","Thinking of this, Mo Jiuye pulled Mo Hanyue over to stand in front of Mo Qing.","\"Dad, look, Hanyue is a young lady now.\"","Sure enough, upon hearing Mo Jiuye's words, Mo Qing's attention quickly fell on Mo Hanyue.","The little girl in front of him had grown into a delicate beauty, with a pair of bright eyes exactly the same as when she was a child.","\"Is this Hanyue? You've already become a young lady. Dad can't hold you anymore.\"","As he spoke, Mo Qing unconsciously glanced at his own legs which were still curled up.","Seeing her father's somewhat awkward manner, Mo Hanyue plucked up her courage and called out, \"Daddy.\"","Hearing his precious daughter call him Daddy, Mo Qing's tears flowed uncontrolled once more.","Seeing her father in tears, Mo Hanyue also lost control. She took a few steps forward, maintaining the closest distance to Mo Qing, and tentatively reached out to touch him.","\"Father... woo... Hanyue missed you so much... woo...\"","Mo Qing braced himself and reached out to grasp his daughter's little hand.","\"Don't cry, Hanyue. From now on, Dad will be with you.\"","When Mo Qing said this, Mo Hanyue cried even harder. Ever since she was little, she didn't have a father. Although her brothers loved and protected her, when she saw her little sisters mention how their father did this and that, she still felt a little sad sometimes.","Moreover, she had never forgotten how her father had doted on her. Seeing her father's decrepit state now, Mo Hanyue felt as if her heart was bleeding.","In her impression, her father had been tall and dignified. Meeting him again now, he had become someone she didn't dare to imagine.","What's more, seeing her father like this made her even more heartbroken.","Mo Hanyue moved forward again and hugged her father's outstretched arm tightly, crying grievously.","Mo Qing felt extremely distressed, and gently stroked her smooth hair with his other hand.","\"Hanyue, be good. From now on, Dad will stay at home and be with our Hanyue.\"","At this moment, Mo Qing still didn't realize that his daughter had already grown up. Moreover, her wedding day was not far off.","In his heart, his Hanyue was still a soft, tender little girl who needed to be doted on.","On the way here, Mo Jiuye and the others had been asking about Father's physical condition. Even though they talked about things at home, they forgot to mention that Mo Hanyue was already betrothed.","Seeing the father and daughter crying so sorrowfully, Old Lady Mo was even more unable to hold back her tears, which fell like rain.","No matter what, their Mo family was finally reunited.","At this moment, Old Lady Mo was not sad but wept for joy. She had not lost her composure.","Seeing her husband and daughter crying so sadly, Old Lady Mo quickly called Mo Jiuye over.","\"Jiuye, quickly carry your father back to the room and let him rest well. I will personally arrange for our Mo family to have a grand reunion banquet today to celebrate properly.\"","Mo Jiuye responded and carried his father into the main room.","As soon as he settled his father down, the whole family crowded in.","The scene before him moved Old Lady Mo, Mo Jiuye and the women of the family the most.","It had been eight years since Mo Qing was reported dead in battle, and the Mo sons had successively died in battle after that.","Until today, no one had imagined that their Mo family could have such a grand reunion.","Seeing this scene, some of the women still couldn't help shedding tears. Their husbands stood beside them to provide comfort.","Old Lady Mo wiped away the tears from the corners of her eyes and said to Mo Qing,","\"Dear husband, after eight long years, our Mo family is finally all here without a single one missing. Don't you have anything to say?\"","After all, Old Lady Mo came from a prominent family, so she still couldn't completely disregard propriety at a time like this.","Mo Qing had been absent from the family for eight years and hadn't participated in so many things that happened during that time.","Now his old wife was asking him to speak, but he really didn't know where to start.","Thinking that it was all thanks to his ninth son and daughter-in-law that the family could reunite, his gaze fell on the young couple.","\"I failed in my duty as the head of this family, and made you grieve for me.","This time, our Mo family is able to be together again, it's all thanks to Jiuye and his wife.","Don't let their young age deceive you. From my observations over the past few days, their bearing and wisdom are far above you elder brothers and sisters-in-law.","Now that I'm old and useless, I only want to keep Old Lady Mo company for the rest of my life, and have the fortune to spend my days doting on grandchildren if you give more to the Mo family.","From now on, this family will be led by Jiuye and his wife. Anyone who dares object will be punished according to family law.\"","As soon as Mo Qing finished speaking, Old Lady Mo couldn't help laughing.","\"Dear husband, where did I say wrong?\"","At this moment, Mo Qing felt a little uneasy. He had announced succession to the public before discussing it with his old wife.","\"Dear husband said nothing wrong. I handed over the leadership of our Mo family to daughter-in-law long ago. Our Mo family is able to be like this today, it's all thanks to their support.","Of course, everyone has made contributions to the family, but our daughter-in-law is clever and capable, she is most suitable to manage the entire Mo family.\"","So that was how it was.","Mo Qing felt rather embarrassed.","He knew his ninth son and daughter-in-law had made outstanding contributions to the Mo family, and wanted to encourage them with this opportunity.","He didn't expect his old wife to have done it before him.","\"In that case, including me, everyone in our Mo family will listen to Jiuye and his wife from now on.\"","No one had any objections to this, especially the elder brothers and sisters-in-law who were originally at home.","They had long witnessed the capabilities of the ninth brother and sister-in-law. Whoever dared disagree, they would be the first to beat him up.","\"Father, Mother, don't worry. From now on, we'll all listen to ninth brother and ninth sister-in-law.\" Everyone responded in chorus.","Just as Old Lady Mo wanted to say something more to this harmonious big family, a series of footsteps were heard coming from outside the door.","Yu Er and Lan Er knew the Mo family was having a reunion today, and the family must have a lot to talk about.","In order to prevent any outsiders from disturbing them, the young sisters had been standing guard at the front gate."]},{"number":398,"title":"Chapter 398: You guys come over here and show me.","paragraphs":["Yu Er was the first to knock on the door, \"Old Lady Mo, Older Brother Tao and the others have arrived.\"","Her meaning was obvious, she was asking if Old Lady Mo would let them in.","Hearing that Tao Ran and the others had come, they were all Mo Qing's former subordinates, so there was no reason to shut them out.","Old Lady Mo got up and said to the doorway, \"Let them in quickly.\"","She believed that when her husband saw these people here, he would definitely be very happy.","No sooner had she finished speaking than the door was pushed open from the outside.","Yes, pushed open.","Tao Ran had just been about to go into town to buy some things when he had just left home and heard the villagers discussing that Mo Jiuye and Mo Chuhan brothers had come back driving two carriages, and there were several people riding tall horses with them.","Mo Jiuye had gone to the capital to find his enemy, Tao Ran and the others knew a little about it.","Hearing that he had returned, none of them had thought that Old Duke could be rescued with the two young masters, they just wanted to come over and see how things were.","Tao Ran didn't go into town either, he called over a group of brothers and ran to the Mo family.","When they arrived at the gate, they happened to see Yan Er and Yu Er guarding there.","Usually, the Mo family didn't have gatekeepers, Tao Ran and the others were very clear about this.","Seeing the two maids guarding the gate strictly, Tao Ran instinctively felt that something big must have happened in the Mo family.","The first thing they thought of was that the Mo family might have encountered something they couldn't solve, or that there was some danger.","Therefore, without waiting for Yan Er to let them in, hearing Old Lady Mo speaking inside, the group of men swarmed in like bees.","Upon entering the room, the group was dumbfounded at once.","Because Mo Junrui and Mo Jiacheng were just turning to look towards the doorway, their eyes met directly.","Tao Ran and the others stood with their mouths agape, and it took them a long time to react.","\"Mas...Master, Second Master?\"","Speaking of the Mo family men, apart from Mo Qing, the two brothers were the ones who had been with these old subordinates the longest.","Mo Junrui strode up to Tao Ran and patted him on the shoulder.","\"Hahaha, it's me, you look much thinner.\"","Mo Jiacheng followed Mo Junrui and walked up to Tao Ran and the others, looking at his brothers for a long time before laughing heartily,","\"Hahaha... I didn't expect that we brothers would have a day to reunite here.\"","Tao Ran said excitedly, \"It really is thanks to Ninth Master, otherwise we brothers would not know how we would be mistreated by that old fox Yuan Meng!\"","Mo Qing was lying on the innermost bed in the room. Hearing the voices of his old subordinates, he was filled with emotion.","He didn't expect that not only had his family suffered such treatment, but so many good brothers who had lived and died with him were also implicated.","At this moment, he was excited to get up and meet these old subordinates, but as soon as he exerted himself, the weakness in his legs spread throughout his body.","Only then did Mo Qing realize that he was now paralyzed in bed.","He sighed helplessly and said loudly, \"Tao Ran, come over and let me take a look at you.\"","Hearing Mo Qing's voice, Tao Ran and the others were stunned again.","Although this voice didn't have the awe-inspiring aura they remembered, it was not unfamiliar to them at all.","\"It's the Old Duke.\" Someone couldn't help but say out loud.","At the same time, the group had already strode towards Mo Qing.","Seeing this, the Mo brothers and female family members automatically gave way.","At the sight of Mo Qing, Tao Ran and the others were stunned for a moment.","If the man in front of them hadn't been sitting on Old Lady Mo's couch, they might have doubted who he really was.","Where was the majestic look of the Old Duke? In Tao Ran's eyes now, he was just an old man in his twilight years.","Not only that, he looked very weak, with white hair, skinny as firewood...","In short, seeing the Old Duke like this made their hearts ache.","Seeing their dumbfounded looks, Mo Qing tried his best to squeeze out a smile and said, \"What's the matter? Just because we haven't seen each other for eight years, you don't recognize me?\"","Likewise, seeing these former subordinates made him feel very bad.","Back then, these people had lived and died with him on the battlefield. He was afraid they would not have enough to eat, so whenever he had some money, he would try to supply them.","Therefore, Tao Ran and the others looked not only strong and healthy, but chubby.","Now looking at them again, they were not only older, but also somewhat thin.","In fact, there was nothing strange about this. When they were rescued, they didn't know how long they had gone without eating. Although they didn't look particularly thin on the outside, it was the toxins in their bodies that were supporting them.","After the poison was cured, their bodies shriveled up in the blink of an eye. In the cave, the several Mo brothers took turns helping them recuperate. Even so, it was impossible to recover all at once.","It had been several months now since they were cured of the poison, and Tao Ran and the others were obviously much better than when they had just been cured.","But the severe malnutrition could not be replenished at once, so their current appearance looked very different in Mo Qing's eyes.","\"Alas... it's been hard on all of you following me.\"","Mo Qing didn't want to say any more. Tao Ran and the others had become his subordinates and suffered this fate. But now he himself was a useless man, he had no standing to offer any compensation.","Thinking of this, his gaze fell again on his curled legs.","Not to mention whether these legs could be cured, for Mo Qing it was the greatest humiliation in his life.","The state of his legs was actually caused by kneeling at Yuan Meng's grave.","If he were still like he was back then, he would surely lead his iron cavalry to raze the south to the ground, to avenge himself and his Mo men who lived and died with him.","But he had to accept reality. Now he was no longer a duke, nor the supreme commander of the three armies, just an ordinary commoner.","Being an ordinary commoner would be good too, he would probably still have to guard against Emperor Shunwu.","The fact that such a big family of Mos had gathered together would sooner or later be known to Emperor Shunwu.","No one among those present understood Emperor Shunwu's temperament better than Mo Qing.","Emperor Shunwu was weak-willed and accustomed to listening to slanderers. Mo Qing guessed that his family's arrest and exile must also have been due to someone speaking ill of them behind the scenes.","Initially, Emperor Shunwu might still have considered how the Mo sons guarded his country, but after listening to such words for too long, Emperor Shunwu would become completely irrational.","If Emperor Shunwu heard that the Mo men were all alive, he would inevitably have some inappropriate ideas again.","Thinking of this, Mo Qing felt it necessary to discuss this matter with everyone, otherwise once Emperor Shunwu really used some sinister means against the Mo family, they would be caught off guard.","Now Mo Qing knew that his ninth son and daughter-in-law were the most capable in the family, so he looked directly at Mo Jiuye."]},{"number":399,"title":"Chapter 399: I Can Work this Out","paragraphs":["\"Mo Jiuye, have you ever thought about what would happen if Emperor Shunwu discovered that all the men of our family are alive?\"","Mo Jiuye had indeed considered this point.","However, he had been busy with the family matters and searching for the whereabouts of his father and brothers during this time. Moreover, he hadn't come up with a good strategy yet, which caused the delay.","Besides, he was always vigilant, watching out for spies sent by Emperor Shunwu or the Southern Border.","He had planned to deal with these issues after rescuing his father and brothers and settling the family down.","Now that his father asked him, Mo Jiuye helplessly shook his head, \"Son hasn't come up with a good solution yet.\"","Mo Qing sighed helplessly upon hearing Mo Jiuye's reply.","Even though he had some plans in mind, it was impossible to carry out such actions without sufficient funds.","He knew that He Zhiran, who had been quiet all along, already had some ideas, and she also guessed some of Mo Qing's thoughts.","\"Father, there's no need to worry about the silver coins. I can find a way to solve that problem.\"","Stealthily raising an army?","What's difficult about that?","Not to mention that she had an endless supply of silver coins in her space, she also possessed powerful weapons.","Raising an army didn't require thousands of soldiers, just about a thousand or eight hundred elite troops would be enough.","Moreover, since the last invasion by the barbarians, she had a thought in mind.","She wanted to wait for Mo Jiuye to return so they could discuss the development of gunpowder.","Once gunpowder was successfully developed, they could create powerful weapons. Although these weapons couldn't compare to the ones in her space, they would be invincible in this era of cold weapons.","Furthermore, there were many men in the Mo family, and they were all righteous individuals. When it came to developing gunpowder, they could assign their own people to do it.","Considering today's presence of Tao Ran and the others, He Zhiran did not mention this idea.","Even so, she made it clear that there was absolutely no problem with the Mo family secretly raising an army.","Moreover, they had purchased a large piece of land and built a camp in a concealed area in the mountains, which allowed them to raise an army without anyone noticing.","In fact, Mo Qing was not the only one who realized this. The Mo brothers were also concerned about raising an army.","Now that their father was the first to bring it up, it meant that this matter needed to be officially put on the agenda.","However, they were well aware of the expenses involved in raising an army, and it was not something that could be achieved with just a small amount of money.","Even if they tried their best to earn money, it was probably impossible for them to raise an army.","Surprisingly, their younger sister Jiu Ye casually said it without any confidence.","Not only that, Jiu Ye also said that there was no need to worry about the silver coins, as she could find a way to solve that problem.","Jiu Ye was indeed good at making money, but they also saw that although the family had daily income, that profit could be considered abundant for ordinary people. If they used that income to raise an army, it would be like a drop in the bucket.","It seemed that Jiu Ye hadn't realized how expensive it was to raise an army, which was why she said such things.","But compared to the ninth brother and sister, they seemed to lack confidence. Currently, they could only live an ordinary life like commoners and probably didn't have the ability to earn even a small amount of money.","However, this matter was crucial and had to be considered.","Lacking the means and solutions, the Mo brothers could only wear a troubled expression and remain silent.","They wanted to see how their usually decisive father planned to arrange things.","The sisters-in-law were perceptive and worried that someone might eavesdrop on such an important family discussion. They pulled Mo Hanyue out of the room and dispersed to stand guard outside.","Only He Zhiran, they all knew that the intelligence and talent of the ninth brother and sister far surpassed those of the Mo brothers. She had to stay and discuss it together.","Inside the hall at this moment, everyone was serious.","Mo Qing scanned the room and finally rested his gaze on Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran.","The one who spoke confidently earlier was the ninth daughter-in-law. However, if he were to ask again at this moment, as the father of the family, he still couldn't bring himself to speak. Therefore, he could only ask Mo Jiuye.","After all, he and He Zhiran were husband and wife, and they communicated the most. It was impossible for a daughter-in-law not to share her thoughts with her husband.","\"Jiuye, what do you think about this matter?\"","Mo Jiuye hadn't been informed about He Zhiran's plan to develop gunpowder, so he hadn't come up with a foolproof solution either.","However, he knew better than anyone about the unlimited money in his wife's possession. In this regard, Mo Jiuye still had confidence.","In addition, he had his own plans to some extent.","\"Father, when Zhiran and I passed through the border on our way to the Southern Frontier, we heard the soldiers who used to follow us talking about their intention to join the Mo family.","Therefore, the issue of personnel can be easily solved.","As for the funds for maintaining the troops, I can come up with a solution.\"","As for the rest, Mo Jiuye hadn't planned it in detail yet.","With He Zhiran's intelligence, she naturally understood that her father-in-law's questions to Mo Jiuye were indirectly asking her.","After Mo Jiuye finished speaking, she added, \"Also, I suggest that we don't have too many troops, preferably not exceeding a thousand.\"","He Zhiran had learned from Mo Jiuye that there were fewer than a thousand soldiers who still followed the Mo family in the South. In her opinion, having a force of less than a thousand was sufficient.","From the perspective of expenses, there was a tenfold difference between maintaining a force of a thousand and ten thousand.","In addition, she considered that if more people were needed, they would have to recruit externally. New recruits wouldn't have a thorough understanding of their background, and if someone with impure intentions managed to infiltrate, it would be a loss.","Upon hearing He Zhiran's words, everyone's gaze focused on her, including Mo Jiuye, and they all felt that her suggestion was somewhat unrealistic.","Mo Qing couldn't hold back and asked, \"Ninth sister, have you forgotten? Some time ago, it was just a group of barbarian people who came to rob us, and their numbers were over five hundred.","Once the barbarian army wants to use this place as a breakthrough to attack, I'm afraid it won't be as simple as five hundred people. Saying they number in the thousands is an understatement.\"","In case we encounter such a situation, we are far from being a thousand people strong. How should we deal with the enemy?\"","The concerns of Mo Chuhan were not unreasonable in the minds of the members of the Mo family.","After all, they all had a military background, and during battles, the number of troops was always a disadvantage.","Back then, Seventh Brother had also participated in that fight at home and understood the severity of the situation.","Being someone who rarely spoke, he couldn't help but raise a question.","\"Ninth Sister, what Eighth Brother said makes sense. Building an army is not child's play.\"","He Zhiran knew that once she uttered such words, she would undoubtedly face the scrutiny of everyone.","With confidence, she explained, \"If I can create a weapon that can single-handedly take on a hundred or even a thousand enemies, would you still consider a thousand people to be few?\"","Upon hearing He Zhiran's words, Mo Jiuye immediately thought of the hand grenades in her space.","He had personally witnessed the power of those things. When he left Southern Border with the Emperor's corpse, he threw a few of them, and he saw countless Southern Border soldiers instantly killed or injured.","That was only because he was trying to escape and hadn't intended to massacre anyone.","If she were to throw a few more, it was feared that the Southern Border camp would no longer exist.","Was Zhiran planning to create such weapons?"]},{"number":400,"title":"Chapter 400: It's Me this time","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye was very enthusiastic about hand grenades.","After truly experiencing their power, he had also tried to research them.","But later, as things got busier, it was temporarily ignored by him.","Now that there were only trusted people in the room, Mo Jiuye also had no scruples about asking.","\"Ran Ran, what kind of weapon are you talking about?\"","He did not say the name of the weapon, but made a gesture of throwing a hand grenade.","Because he was clear in his heart that hand grenades were a product unique to his wife's space. In case what the other person was talking about was not this, wouldn't he expose himself by saying it out.","Now, manufacturing gunpowder was only He Zhiran's preliminary plan. Before it succeeded, she did not want to speak it out too early.","Therefore, she answered more conservatively.","\"I just had an idea, whether it can succeed or not, I have to try it before I know.\"","But she had already made up her mind in her heart. Making gunpowder stuff was not difficult to get, as long as the dosage was grasped.","Although it sounded easy, it was estimated that it would take a lot of twists and turns to produce it. After all, this gunpowder stuff was not to be played with. With a slight carelessness, the people involved in the production could be blown away.","She would have to study it carefully later and strive to do it without any problems.","Mo Qing was confused for a while about what medicine his sister-in-law was selling in her gourd, but he believed her without reservations.","Mo Qing saw that his sister-in-law was talking mysteriously. Even though he was eager to know the details in his heart, he did not dare to inquire in front of so many people.","\"Lady He, the power of the weapon you mentioned is still unknown, and time waits for no one. The reason why I want an army of my own is because I don't know when Emperor Shunwu will take action against us.\"","He knew Emperor Shunwu best. He was already wary of the Mo family to the point of exiling them. Once he learned that the Mo men were still alive, he would probably not sleep well without getting rid of them.","He Zhiran thought for a while and replied, \"I agree with my husband's opinion on training troops. Go to the south and bring back the soldiers who were born and died with the Mo family. That way, there is no need to worry about loyalty.","It can also solve their plight of being ostracized there.","I calculated that rushing on fast horses, this round trip would take at least a month.","In more than a month, I think there will be enough time to research the weapon I mentioned.","If nothing unexpected happens, these soldiers can be equipped with such weapons by the time they arrive in the northwest.\"","He Zhiran had plans that since she suggested having an army of no more than a thousand people, even if she failed to successfully develop gunpowder, she would distribute the hand grenades from her space to everyone.","Giving everyone one first was enough to protect their homes.","That way, she still had enough time to continue researching gunpowder, and sooner or later she would succeed in researching it.","There was no need to worry about the generals either. The medicine men who had returned home had arrived one after another. There were more than 20 people in this room now.","With such an army and her advanced weapons, they would definitely be able to do it without any problems.","Of course, she didn't have any ambitions to fight for power either. The goal was only one - as long as the whole family was safe and sound.","That is to say, she would not choose to provoke others, but if someone bullied them, she would definitely not be soft-handed.","Seeing his ninth sister-in-law's well-reasoned words, the Mo men simply believed in her implicitly.","The third elder brother immediately stood up, \"Since this is the case, I am willing to go to the south to bring those soldiers back.\"","\"Third elder brother, since you came back, you have been collecting information outside all the time. I will go this time.\" The fifth elder brother refused to give in.","The other brothers were equally unwilling to fall behind, and they all rushed to go to the south.","At this time, Mo Qing also saw it.","When he said just now that he wanted his ninth son and daughter-in-law to be in charge of the house, it was nonsense.","Even if he didn't say it, this family would do that.","Wasn't this the case? As soon as his sister-in-law said something, everyone obeyed without asking why.","It seemed that he had very good eyesight. At first glance, he realized that this ninth sister-in-law was extraordinary. Even his arrogant sons obeyed without complaint.","After understanding these things, Mo Qing decided to shut up.","Anyway, he had stated his opinion. He was now a disabled person, so he would not add to the chaos.","The trip to the south was inevitable, and it could not be delayed either. After discussing among the brothers, it was finally decided that the seventh elder brother would go on this trip.","As for making gunpowder, of course, it had to be done by their own people too.","The best person for this in He Zhiran's eyes was the fifth elder brother.","The fifth elder brother was daring and meticulous, and no one could be more suitable.","Of course, the other brothers could also participate, depending on their own wishes.","With things settled, the seventh elder brother would set off for the south tomorrow, but that did not affect the Mo family reunion dinner tonight.","With He Zhiran here, the family would never lack all kinds of good ingredients.","The eighth elder brother had specially gone to the fishing village to buy a lot of seafood that the locals here disliked but the Mo family could make delicious dishes with.","The culinary skills of the sisters-in-law had now been practiced to perfection, but now apart from He Zhiran, the best cook in the Mo family was Yu Er.","This girl usually had no intrigues in her heart and just worked wholeheartedly. She knew that her ninth lady had superb culinary skills. In order to make herself have a skill she could be proud of, whenever He Zhiran cooked, she would follow along to help and learn at the same time.","For the Mo family reunion banquet tonight, Yu Er took over the role of head chef without objection. The sisters-in-law then helped out as sous chefs.","The women worked hard for an afternoon and finally prepared a sumptuous dinner before nightfall.","Similarly, the banquet was set in the main hall where the elderly couple stayed.","Mo Qing returned home in high spirits. Coupled with He Zhiran's conditioning over the past few days, he looked more energetic than ever.","He was carried to the main seat by his sons to sit, with his old wife sitting beside him.","The younger generations then found their own places to sit.","On a nice day like this, with so much delicious food, they naturally asked Fang Chuanzhou, Xie Tianhai and Hu Cong to come over and join them.","As well as Liang Hao, Tao Ran and their group of men.","With them, the hall could not accommodate everyone, so several tables were specially set up in the yard.","Xie Tianhai and Fang Chuanzhou were old acquaintances of Mo Qing. They had pretty good relationships when they were in the capital.","Hu Cong was younger than Mo Qing by some years. Although they did not have much interaction, they both had good impressions of each other.","Mo Qing had also heard of some of their experiences during their exile and felt even closer to Fang Chuanzhou and Xie Tianhai than before.","As for Hu Cong, he suffered the same plight as the Mo family, so Mo Qing sympathized with him even more.","He invited the two old friends and Hu Cong to dine together. Just as everyone was about to start, footsteps came from outside the door.","Nan Rui's voice was very loud.","\"What happy event is it today that it’s so lively?\"","Everyone's gaze turned to the sound source, and they saw Nan Rui supporting Imperial Consort De, smiling and walking into the hall."]}]);
